-- ============================================================
-- roc1: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, Orders 2 to 8, as at 5 November 2026 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a party to a civil action in the Singapore courts (a claimant, a defendant, a third party or an appellant), asking, on facts the party can state,
-- what the party must file or serve, by when, how, what the Court may order, and what follows if the party does not.
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that party would ask.  Nothing here is new law,
-- and no rule is restated: each question builds the modules' inputs from the party's answers and calls the module's own function.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list -- one for each fact the party can state,
-- each with an @desc worded as the party would be asked.
--   * A fact the party may not know is asked as "yes / no / I am not sure"; "I am not sure" becomes NOTHING, and a rule that cannot answer without it answers NOTHING.
--   * A date the party may not have (for example the day to which the time was extended) is asked as a yes/no and a date; the date is ignored when the answer is no.
--   * The Rules keep no list of public holidays.  A question about a period asks for up to two public holidays that fall in or near it;
--     enter 1 January 1900 for a holiday you do not need to give.
--   * A person is asked as a natural person (with an age) or an entity (incorporated or not).
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Rules themselves give; NOTHING means the Rules do not answer on these facts
-- (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (roc1)").  Never read NOTHING as no.
-- Order 3, Rule 2(1) is a caveat on every answer.
--
-- There is no seat for an official.  Where a provision addresses only the Registrar or the Court, the rule is in layer 1 and the party meets it only through
-- the questions below (for example Order 2, rule 6(1); Order 7, rule 2(3); Order 8, rules 4(1), 4(2), 4A(5), 5(4) and 6(4)).

DECLARE `Under Orders 2 to 8, my answer` IS ONE OF
    `Under Orders 2 to 8, yes`
    `Under Orders 2 to 8, no`
    `Under Orders 2 to 8, I am not sure`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the party's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN answer IS A `Under Orders 2 to 8, my answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under Orders 2 to 8, what I say as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `Under Orders 2 to 8, yes` THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Orders 2 to 8, no` THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Orders 2 to 8, I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

GIVEN given IS A BOOLEAN
      date IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Under Orders 2 to 8, a date I may not have` MEANS
    IF given THEN JUST date ELSE NOTHING -- input mapping

GIVEN given IS A BOOLEAN
      amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Under Orders 2 to 8, a number I may not have` MEANS
    IF given THEN JUST amount ELSE NOTHING -- input mapping

GIVEN first IS A DATE
      second IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Court calendar`
`Under Orders 2 to 8, the public holidays I give` MEANS
    `Court calendar` WITH
        `public holidays` IS LIST first, second

GIVEN natural IS A BOOLEAN
      age IS A NUMBER
      incorporated IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Kind of person`
`Under Orders 2 to 8, the person I am asking about` MEANS
    IF natural THEN `Natural person` OF age ELSE Entity OF incorporated

GIVEN length IS A NUMBER
      unit IS A `Time unit`
      direction IS A `Count direction`
GIVETH A Period
`Under Orders 2 to 8, the period I am asking about` MEANS
    Period WITH
        `period length` IS length
        `period unit` IS unit
        `period direction` IS direction

§ `Orders 2 to 8 of the Rules of Court 2021 -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 2 -- the overview: what the claimant, the defendant and the Court may do`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 2, rule 3(1), may I commence an action by filing this document?
GIVEN `document` IS A `Document kind` @desc Which document would you file to commence the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 3(1), may I commence an action by filing this document` IS
    `o 2 r 3(1) a claimant may commence an action by filing that document` `document`

@export Under Order 2, rule 4(2), may the claimant apply for judgment in default?
GIVEN `the defendant fails to file and serve such a notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant fails to file and serve such a notice?
      `the defendant states in the notice that the defendant does not intend to contest the claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant states in the notice that the defendant does not intend to contest the claim?
      `the claimant proves that the originating claim with a statement of claim has been served on the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant proves that the originating claim with a statement of claim has been served on the defendant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 4(2), may the claimant apply for judgment in default` IS
    `o 2 r 4(2) the claimant may apply for judgment in default` `the defendant fails to file and serve such a notice` `the defendant states in the notice that the defendant does not intend to contest the claim` `the claimant proves that the originating claim with a statement of claim has been served on the defendant`

@export Under Order 2, rule 5(1), must the defendant file and serve a defence or an affidavit?
GIVEN `document` IS A `Document kind` @desc Is the action an originating claim or an originating application?
      `the defendant wishes to contest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant wishes to contest?
      `the defendant wishes to introduce evidence in the originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant wishes to introduce evidence in the originating application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 5(1), must the defendant file and serve a defence or an affidavit` IS
    `o 2 r 5(1) the defendant has to file and serve a defence or an affidavit` `document` `the defendant wishes to contest` `the defendant wishes to introduce evidence in the originating application`

@export Under Order 2, rule 5(2), need the defendant file and serve a defence or affidavit on the merits?
GIVEN `the defendant is challenging the jurisdiction of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant is challenging the jurisdiction of the Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 5(2), need the defendant file and serve a defence or affidavit on the merits` IS
    `o 2 r 5(2) the defendant need not file and serve a defence or affidavit on the merits` `the defendant is challenging the jurisdiction of the Court`

@export Under Order 2, rule 5(4), is filing and serving the defence or affidavit treated as submission to the jurisdiction of the Court?
GIVEN `the defence or affidavit states the challenge to jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defence or affidavit states the challenge to jurisdiction?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 5(4), is filing and serving the defence or affidavit treated as submission to the jurisdiction of the Court` IS
    `o 2 r 5(4) the filing and service of the defence or affidavit is treated as submission to the jurisdiction of the Court` `the defence or affidavit states the challenge to jurisdiction`

@export Under Order 2, rule 6(2), may the Court dismiss the action?
GIVEN `no party attends the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that no party attends the case conference?
      `the claimant is absent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant is absent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 6(2), may the Court dismiss the action` IS
    `o 2 r 6(2) the Court may dismiss the action` `no party attends the case conference` `the claimant is absent`

@export Under Order 2, rule 6(3)(a), may the Court dismiss the action for want of service?
GIVEN `the claimant attends the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant attends the case conference?
      `the claimant has not served the originating claim or originating application on the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant has not served the originating claim or originating application on the defendant?
      `the Court is not satisfied that the claimant has taken reasonable steps to effect service expeditiously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court is not satisfied that the claimant has taken reasonable steps to effect service expeditiously?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 6(3)(a), may the Court dismiss the action for want of service` IS
    `o 2 r 6(3)(a) the Court may dismiss the action` `the claimant attends the case conference` `the claimant has not served the originating claim or originating application on the defendant` `the Court is not satisfied that the claimant has taken reasonable steps to effect service expeditiously`

@export Under Order 2, rule 6(4), may the Court give judgment for the claimant at the case conference?
GIVEN `the claimant attends the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant attends the case conference?
      `the defendant is absent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant is absent?
      `the claimant proves that the originating claim or originating application has been served on the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant proves that the originating claim or originating application has been served on the defendant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 6(4), may the Court give judgment for the claimant at the case conference` IS
    `o 2 r 6(4) the Court may give judgment for the claimant` `the claimant attends the case conference` `the defendant is absent` `the claimant proves that the originating claim or originating application has been served on the defendant`

@export Under Order 2, rule 6(5), may the Court take this step when the defence or affidavit has not been filed?
GIVEN `both the claimant and defendant attend the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that both the claimant and defendant attend the case conference?
      `the defendant has not filed and served the defence or affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant has not filed and served the defence or affidavit?
      `document` IS A `Document kind` @desc Is the action an originating claim or an originating application?
      `step` IS A `o 2 r 6(5) the step the Court may take` @desc Which step is in question?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 6(5), may the Court take this step when the defence or affidavit has not been filed` IS
    `o 2 r 6(5) the Court may take that step` `both the claimant and defendant attend the case conference` `the defendant has not filed and served the defence or affidavit` `document` `step`

@export Under Order 2, rule 8, may the Court order the parties to file and exchange affidavits of evidence-in-chief?
GIVEN `pleadings have been filed and served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that pleadings have been filed and served?
      `documents have begun to be exchanged` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that documents have begun to be exchanged?
      `the Court has considered the need for any application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has considered the need for any application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 8, may the Court order the parties to file and exchange affidavits of evidence-in-chief` IS
    `o 2 r 8 the Court may order the parties to file and exchange affidavits of evidence-in-chief` `pleadings have been filed and served` `documents have begun to be exchanged` `the Court has considered the need for any application`

@export Under Order 2, rule 9(3), can I file a pleading after the defence or the defence to counterclaim?
GIVEN `the pleading is after the defence or the defence to counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the pleading is after the defence or the defence to counterclaim?
      `the Court approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court approves?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 9(3), can I file a pleading after the defence or the defence to counterclaim` IS
    `o 2 r 9(3) a pleading after the defence or the defence to counterclaim can be filed` `the pleading is after the defence or the defence to counterclaim` `the Court approves`

@export Under Order 2, rule 9(4), can I file a further affidavit in an originating application?
GIVEN `it is for an originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is for an originating application?
      `the defendant has filed the defendant's affidavit on the merits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant has filed the defendant's affidavit on the merits?
      `the Court approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court approves?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 9(4), can I file a further affidavit in an originating application` IS
    `o 2 r 9(4) a further affidavit can be filed` `it is for an originating application` `the defendant has filed the defendant's affidavit on the merits` `the Court approves`

@export Under Order 2, rule 9(8), may I take out this application?
GIVEN `application` IS A `o 2 r 9(8) the application` @desc What is the application for?
      `it is directed at the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is directed at the case conference?
      `the Court approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court approves?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 9(8), may I take out this application` IS
    `o 2 r 9(8) the application may be taken out` `application` `it is directed at the case conference` `the Court approves`

@export Under Order 2, rule 9(10), may I take out an application on this day?
GIVEN `the day the application is taken out` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the application is taken out?
      `the day the trial commences` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the trial commences?
      `the Court has made its decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court made its decision at the trial?
      `the day the Court makes its decision` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what day? (Give any date if not.)
      `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is a special case?
      `the trial Judge approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the trial Judge approves?
      `a public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of a public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
      `another public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of another public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 9(10), may I take out an application on this day` IS
    `o 2 r 9(10) an application may be taken out on that day` `the day the application is taken out` `the day the trial commences` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, a date I may not have` `the Court has made its decision` `the day the Court makes its decision`) `it is a special case` `the trial Judge approves` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the public holidays I give` `a public holiday in or near the period` `another public holiday in or near the period`)

@export Under Order 2, rule 10(1), may I file an appeal against the Court's decision made in an application?
GIVEN `the law allows an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the law allows an appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 10(1), may I file an appeal against the Court's decision made in an application` IS
    `o 2 r 10(1) an appeal against the Court's decision made in an application may be filed` `the law allows an appeal`

@export Under Order 2, rule 10(7), must I provide security for the costs of the appeal?
GIVEN `the appeal is filed under Division 2 or Division 4 of Order 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the appeal is filed under Division 2 or Division 4 of Order 18?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 10(7), must I provide security for the costs of the appeal` IS
    `o 2 r 10(7) the appellant has to provide security for the costs of the appeal` `the appeal is filed under Division 2 or Division 4 of Order 18`

@export Under Order 2, rule 10(10), may I file this document in the appeal?
GIVEN `the document is other than the parties' written submissions (including any bundle of authorities)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is other than the parties' written submissions (including any bundle of authorities)?
      `the appellate Court approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the appellate Court approves?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 10(10), may I file this document in the appeal` IS
    `o 2 r 10(10) the document may be filed in the appeal` `the document is other than the parties' written submissions (including any bundle of authorities)` `the appellate Court approves`

@export Under Order 2, rule 10(11), may further evidence be admitted on the appeal?
GIVEN `the appellate Court approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the appellate Court approves?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 10(11), may further evidence be admitted on the appeal` IS
    `o 2 r 10(11) further evidence may be admitted` `the appellate Court approves`

@export Under Order 2, rule 12(1), may I file an appeal against the Court's decision after trial or after an originating application is heard?
GIVEN `the law allows an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the law allows an appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 12(1), may I file an appeal against the Court's decision after trial or after an originating application is heard` IS
    `o 2 r 12(1) an appeal against the Court's decision after trial or after an originating application is heard may be filed` `the law allows an appeal`

@export Under Order 2, rule 13(3), is the amount of costs allowed as set out in these Rules?
GIVEN `fixed costs apply under these Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that fixed costs apply under these Rules?
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court otherwise orders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 2, rule 13(3), is the amount of costs allowed as set out in these Rules` IS
    `o 2 r 13(3) the amount of costs allowed is as set out in these Rules` `fixed costs apply under these Rules` `the Court otherwise orders`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 3 -- interpretation, non-compliance, counting time, forms and language`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 3, rule 2(4)(e), may the Court impose a late filing fee?
GIVEN `the document was required to be filed within a period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document was required to be filed within a period?
      `the document remains unfiled after the period expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document remains unfiled after the period expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 3, rule 2(4)(e), may the Court impose a late filing fee` IS
    `o 3 r 2(4)(e) the Court may impose a late filing fee` `the document was required to be filed within a period` `the document remains unfiled after the period expired`

@export Under Order 3, rule 2(4)(e), what late filing fee may the Court impose, in dollars?
GIVEN `the day after which the document is late` IS A DATE @desc What is the day after which the document is late?
      `the day the document is filed` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the document is filed?
      `a public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of a public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
      `another public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of another public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 3, rule 2(4)(e), what late filing fee may the Court impose, in dollars` IS
    `o 3 r 2(4)(e) the late filing fee the Court may impose` `the day after which the document is late` `the day the document is filed` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the public holidays I give` `a public holiday in or near the period` `another public holiday in or near the period`)

@export Under Order 3, rule 2(10), is my application to revoke a judgment or order, or to set aside what was done, taken out in time?
GIVEN `the date the applicant knew or should have known that a ground exists` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the applicant knew or should have known that a ground exists?
      `the date the application is taken out` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the application is taken out?
      `a public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of a public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
      `another public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of another public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
      `the time has been extended or shortened by an order or by consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the time been extended or shortened, by an order of the Court or by consent in writing?
      `the last day of the period as extended or shortened` IS A DATE @desc If it has, what is the last day of the period as extended or shortened? (Give any date if it has not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 3, rule 2(10), is my application to revoke a judgment or order, or to set aside what was done, taken out in time` IS
    `o 3 r 2(10) the application under paragraph (8) is taken out in time` `the date the applicant knew or should have known that a ground exists` `the date the application is taken out` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the public holidays I give` `a public holiday in or near the period` `another public holiday in or near the period`) (`Under Orders 2 to 8, a date I may not have` `the time has been extended or shortened by an order or by consent` `the last day of the period as extended or shortened`)

-- Order 3, rule 3: the counting engine.  The party gives the length and unit of the period the Rules give, whether it is counted after or before the date,
-- and the date it is counted from; the Rules' own method of counting is applied by layer 1.
@export Under Order 3, rule 3, what is the last day for doing an act that must be done within a period of a date?
GIVEN `the length of the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How long is the period the Rules give you, as a number (for example 14)?
      `the unit of the period` IS A `Time unit` @desc In what unit is the period given: days, clear days, working days, weeks, months or hours?
      `the period is counted` IS A `Count direction` @desc Is the period counted after the date, or before the date?
      `the date the period is counted from` IS A DATE @desc From what date is the period counted?
      `a public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of a public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
      `another public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of another public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under Order 3, rule 3, what is the last day for doing an act that must be done within a period of a date` IS
    CONSIDER `o 3 r 3 the period can be counted under this Rule` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the period I am asking about` `the length of the period` `the unit of the period` `the period is counted`)
    WHEN JUST counted THEN
        IF counted
        THEN JUST (`o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the period I am asking about` `the length of the period` `the unit of the period` `the period is counted`) `the date the period is counted from` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the public holidays I give` `a public holiday in or near the period` `another public holiday in or near the period`))
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): Rule 3 does not count this period
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): Rule 3 does not count hours

@export Under Order 3, rule 3, what is the first day on which the act may be done within a period of a date?
GIVEN `the length of the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How long is the period the Rules give you, as a number (for example 14)?
      `the unit of the period` IS A `Time unit` @desc In what unit is the period given: days, clear days, working days, weeks, months or hours?
      `the period is counted` IS A `Count direction` @desc Is the period counted after the date, or before the date?
      `the date the period is counted from` IS A DATE @desc From what date is the period counted?
      `a public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of a public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
      `another public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of another public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under Order 3, rule 3, what is the first day on which the act may be done within a period of a date` IS
    CONSIDER `o 3 r 3 the period can be counted under this Rule` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the period I am asking about` `the length of the period` `the unit of the period` `the period is counted`)
    WHEN JUST counted THEN
        IF counted
        THEN JUST (`o 3 r 3 the first day on which the act may be done` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the period I am asking about` `the length of the period` `the unit of the period` `the period is counted`) `the date the period is counted from` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the public holidays I give` `a public holiday in or near the period` `another public holiday in or near the period`))
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): Rule 3 does not count this period
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): Rule 3 does not count hours

@export Under Order 3, rule 3, is my act in time?
GIVEN `the length of the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How long is the period the Rules give you, as a number (for example 14)?
      `the unit of the period` IS A `Time unit` @desc In what unit is the period given: days, clear days, working days, weeks, months or hours?
      `the period is counted` IS A `Count direction` @desc Is the period counted after the date, or before the date?
      `the date the period is counted from` IS A DATE @desc From what date is the period counted?
      `the day the act is done` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the act done, or on what day do you propose to do it?
      `a public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of a public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
      `another public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of another public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
      `the time has been extended or shortened by an order or by consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the time been extended or shortened, by an order of the Court or by consent in writing?
      `the last day of the period as extended or shortened` IS A DATE @desc If it has, what is the last day of the period as extended or shortened? (Give any date if it has not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 3, rule 3, is my act in time` IS
    `o 3 r 3 the act is in time` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the period I am asking about` `the length of the period` `the unit of the period` `the period is counted`) `the date the period is counted from` `the day the act is done` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the public holidays I give` `a public holiday in or near the period` `another public holiday in or near the period`) (`Under Orders 2 to 8, a date I may not have` `the time has been extended or shortened by an order or by consent` `the last day of the period as extended or shortened`)


-- The yes/no twin of the two questions above: whether the Rules count this kind of period at all (they count days, clear days, working days, weeks and months, not hours).
@export Under Order 3, rule 3, can the Rules count this period?
GIVEN `the length of the period` IS A NUMBER @desc How long is the period the Rules give you, as a number (for example 14)?
      `the unit of the period` IS A `Time unit` @desc In what unit is the period given: days, clear days, working days, weeks, months or hours?
      `the period is counted` IS A `Count direction` @desc Is the period counted after the date, or before the date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 3, rule 3, can the Rules count this period` IS
    `o 3 r 3 the period can be counted under this Rule` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the period I am asking about` `the length of the period` `the unit of the period` `the period is counted`)


@export Under Order 3, rule 4(3), may the period be extended by consent in writing without an order of the Court?
GIVEN `the period is one within which a person is required by these Rules, or by an order, to serve, file or amend a pleading or other document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the period is one within which a person is required by these Rules, or by an order, to serve, file or amend a pleading or other document?
      `the extension is by consent in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the extension by consent in writing?
      `the days by which the period is extended` IS A NUMBER @desc By how many days is the period to be extended?
      `an extension by consent has already been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an extension by consent has already been made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 3, rule 4(3), may the period be extended by consent in writing without an order of the Court` IS
    `o 3 r 4(3) the period may be extended by consent in writing without an order of the Court` `the period is one within which a person is required by these Rules, or by an order, to serve, file or amend a pleading or other document` `the extension is by consent in writing` `the days by which the period is extended` `an extension by consent has already been made`

@export Under Order 3, rule 4, what is the last day of the period as extended or shortened?
GIVEN `the last day under Order 3, Rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day under Order 3, Rule 3?
      `the Court has ordered the period to end on a particular day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered the period to end on a particular day?
      `the day the Court has ordered the period to end` IS A DATE @desc If so, what day? (Give any date if not.)
      `the period was extended by consent in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the period extended by consent in writing?
      `the number of days by which the period was extended by consent in writing` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, by how many days? (Give 0 if it was not.)
      `an extension by consent had already been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an extension by consent had already been made?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under Order 3, rule 4, what is the last day of the period as extended or shortened` IS
    `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened` `the last day under Order 3, Rule 3` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, a date I may not have` `the Court has ordered the period to end on a particular day` `the day the Court has ordered the period to end`) (`Under Orders 2 to 8, a number I may not have` `the period was extended by consent in writing` `the number of days by which the period was extended by consent in writing`) `an extension by consent had already been made`

@export Under Order 3, rule 5(4), are the summons and the affidavit served at least 14 days before the hearing?
GIVEN `the date of the hearing of the summons` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the hearing of the summons?
      `the date the summons and the affidavit are served` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the summons and the affidavit are served?
