-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 4 -- parties, representation, estates and solicitors`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 4, rule 1, may I be a party to proceedings in my own name?
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a natural person (yes), rather than an entity such as a company or an association (no)?
      `the person's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the person, in years? (Give 0 if the person is an entity.)
      `the entity is incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the person is an entity, is it incorporated? (Give no for a natural person.)
      `section 36 of the Civil Law Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that section 36 of the Civil Law Act applies?
      `the entity has the capacity to sue or be sued under any law in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the entity has the capacity to sue or be sued under any law in Singapore or elsewhere?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 4, rule 1, may I be a party to proceedings in my own name` IS
    `o 4 r 1 the person may be a party to proceedings in their own name` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the person I am asking about` `the person is a natural person` `the person's age in years` `the entity is incorporated`) `section 36 of the Civil Law Act applies` `the entity has the capacity to sue or be sued under any law in Singapore or elsewhere`

@export Under Order 4, rule 2(1), must I be represented by a litigation representative?
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a natural person (yes), rather than an entity such as a company or an association (no)?
      `the person's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the person, in years? (Give 0 if the person is an entity.)
      `the entity is incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the person is an entity, is it incorporated? (Give no for a natural person.)
      `section 36 of the Civil Law Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that section 36 of the Civil Law Act applies?
      `the person lacks capacity within the meaning of the Mental Capacity Act in relation to matters concerning the person's property and affairs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person lacks capacity within the meaning of the Mental Capacity Act in relation to matters concerning the person's property and affairs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 4, rule 2(1), must I be represented by a litigation representative` IS
    `o 4 r 2(1) the person must be represented by a litigation representative` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the person I am asking about` `the person is a natural person` `the person's age in years` `the entity is incorporated`) `section 36 of the Civil Law Act applies` `the person lacks capacity within the meaning of the Mental Capacity Act in relation to matters concerning the person's property and affairs`

@export Under Order 4, rule 3(1), must I be represented by a solicitor?
GIVEN `the person is represented by a litigation representative under Rule 2(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is represented by a litigation representative under Rule 2(1)(b)?
      `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a natural person (yes), rather than an entity such as a company or an association (no)?
      `the person's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the person, in years? (Give 0 if the person is an entity.)
      `the entity is incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the person is an entity, is it incorporated? (Give no for a natural person.)
      `the entity has the capacity to sue or be sued under any law in Singapore or elsewhere` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the entity has the capacity to sue or be sued under any law in Singapore or elsewhere?
      `the entity is a registered trade union represented by an officer under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the entity is a registered trade union represented by an officer under paragraph (2)?
      `the Court has given permission under paragraph (3) for an officer to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has given permission under paragraph (3) for an officer to act?
      `the Court has given permission under paragraph (4) for an officer to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has given permission under paragraph (4) for an officer to act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 4, rule 3(1), must I be represented by a solicitor` IS
    `o 4 r 3(1) the person must be represented by a solicitor` `the person is represented by a litigation representative under Rule 2(1)(b)` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the person I am asking about` `the person is a natural person` `the person's age in years` `the entity is incorporated`) `the entity has the capacity to sue or be sued under any law in Singapore or elsewhere` `the entity is a registered trade union represented by an officer under paragraph (2)` `the Court has given permission under paragraph (3) for an officer to act` `the Court has given permission under paragraph (4) for an officer to act`

@export Under Order 4, rule 3(3), may the Court give permission for an officer to act on behalf of the company?
GIVEN `an application is made by a company, variable capital company or limited liability partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an application is made by a company, variable capital company or limited liability partnership?
      `the matter or proceeding is a relevant matter or proceeding to which the applicant is a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the matter or proceeding is a relevant matter or proceeding to which the applicant is a party?
      `the Court is satisfied that the officer has been duly authorised to act on behalf of the applicant in that matter or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court is satisfied that the officer has been duly authorised to act on behalf of the applicant in that matter or proceeding?
      `the Court is satisfied that the officer has sufficient executive or administrative capacity or is a proper person to represent the applicant in that matter or proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court is satisfied that the officer has sufficient executive or administrative capacity or is a proper person to represent the applicant in that matter or proceeding?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 4, rule 3(3), may the Court give permission for an officer to act on behalf of the company` IS
    `o 4 r 3(3) the Court may give permission for an officer to act on behalf of the applicant` `an application is made by a company, variable capital company or limited liability partnership` `the matter or proceeding is a relevant matter or proceeding to which the applicant is a party` `the Court is satisfied that the officer has been duly authorised to act on behalf of the applicant in that matter or proceeding` `the Court is satisfied that the officer has sufficient executive or administrative capacity or is a proper person to represent the applicant in that matter or proceeding`

@export Under Order 4, rule 4(1), may the action be brought against the estate of the deceased?
GIVEN `a defendant has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a defendant has died?
      `a cause of action against the defendant survives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a cause of action against the defendant survives?
      `a grant of probate or letters of administration has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a grant of probate or letters of administration has been made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 4, rule 4(1), may the action be brought against the estate of the deceased` IS
    `o 4 r 4(1) the action may be brought against the estate of the deceased` `a defendant has died` `a cause of action against the defendant survives` `a grant of probate or letters of administration has been made`

@export Under Order 4, rule 4(2)(a), have I applied to the Court as the Rule requires in an action against an estate?
GIVEN `the action is brought against the estate of a deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the action is brought against the estate of a deceased person?
      `the claimant applies for an order appointing a person to represent the estate or, if a grant has been made, an order that the personal representative be made a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant applies for an order appointing a person to represent the estate or, if a grant has been made, an order that the personal representative be made a party?
      `the claimant also applies for an order that the proceedings be carried on against the person appointed or the personal representative as if substituted for the estate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant also applies for an order that the proceedings be carried on against the person appointed or the personal representative as if substituted for the estate?
      `the originating claim or originating application is valid for service on the day of the application` IS A `Under Orders 2 to 8, my answer` @desc Is it the case that the originating claim or originating application is valid for service on the day of the application? (yes, no or I am not sure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 4, rule 4(2)(a), have I applied to the Court as the Rule requires in an action against an estate` IS
    `o 4 r 4(2)(a) the claimant has applied to the Court as required` `the action is brought against the estate of a deceased person` `the claimant applies for an order appointing a person to represent the estate or, if a grant has been made, an order that the personal representative be made a party` `the claimant also applies for an order that the proceedings be carried on against the person appointed or the personal representative as if substituted for the estate` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, what I say as a fact` `the originating claim or originating application is valid for service on the day of the application`)

@export Under Order 4, rule 5(1), does the action continue despite the death or bankruptcy of a party?
GIVEN `a party to an action dies or becomes bankrupt after the action has been commenced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a party to an action dies or becomes bankrupt after the action has been commenced?
      `the cause of action survives` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the cause of action survives?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 4, rule 5(1), does the action continue despite the death or bankruptcy of a party` IS
    `o 4 r 5(1) the action continues despite the death or bankruptcy` `a party to an action dies or becomes bankrupt after the action has been commenced` `the cause of action survives`

@export Under Order 4, rule 6(1), may the persons sue or be sued as a group?
GIVEN `numerous persons have a common interest in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that numerous persons have a common interest in the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 4, rule 6(1), may the persons sue or be sued as a group` IS
    `o 4 r 6(1) the persons may sue or be sued as a group with one or more representing the group` `numerous persons have a common interest in the proceedings`

@export Under Order 4, rule 8(1), must I file and serve a notice of appointment of solicitor?
GIVEN `a party who was not represented by a solicitor decides to appoint a solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a party who was not represented by a solicitor decides to appoint a solicitor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 4, rule 8(1), must I file and serve a notice of appointment of solicitor` IS
    `o 4 r 8(1) the party must file and serve a notice of appointment of solicitor in Form 3 on all the parties` `a party who was not represented by a solicitor decides to appoint a solicitor`

@export Under Order 4, rule 8(3), must I file and serve a notice of change of solicitor?
GIVEN `the party intends to change the party's solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party intends to change the party's solicitor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 4, rule 8(3), must I file and serve a notice of change of solicitor` IS
    `o 4 r 8(3) the party must file and serve a notice of change of solicitor in Form 3 on all the parties` `the party intends to change the party's solicitor`

@export Under Order 4, rule 8(7), must I give notice of an address in Singapore for service?
GIVEN `a party has no solicitor acting for the party on record` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a party has no solicitor acting for the party on record?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 4, rule 8(7), must I give notice of an address in Singapore for service` IS
    `o 4 r 8(7) the party must give notice by letter to all the parties stating an address in Singapore for service` `a party has no solicitor acting for the party on record`

@export Under Order 4, rule 8(8), what address is deemed to be my address for service?
GIVEN `the party fails to comply with paragraph (7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party fails to comply with paragraph (7)?
      `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a natural person (yes), rather than an entity such as a company or an association (no)?
      `the person's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the person, in years? (Give 0 if the person is an entity.)
      `the entity is incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the person is an entity, is it incorporated? (Give no for a natural person.)
GIVETH A `o 4 r 8(8) the deemed address for service`
DECIDE `Under Order 4, rule 8(8), what address is deemed to be my address for service` IS
    `o 4 r 8(8) the address deemed to be the party's address for service` `the party fails to comply with paragraph (7)` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the person I am asking about` `the person is a natural person` `the person's age in years` `the entity is incorporated`)

@export Under Order 4, rule 9(1), may the solicitor apply to the Court for an order declaring that the solicitor has ceased to act?
GIVEN `a solicitor who has acted for a party in a cause or matter has ceased so to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a solicitor who has acted for a party in a cause or matter has ceased so to act?
      `the party has not given notice of change in accordance with Rule 8(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party has not given notice of change in accordance with Rule 8(3)?
      `the party has not given notice of intention to act in person in accordance with Rule 8(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party has not given notice of intention to act in person in accordance with Rule 8(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 4, rule 9(1), may the solicitor apply to the Court for an order declaring that the solicitor has ceased to act` IS
    `o 4 r 9(1) the solicitor may apply to the Court for an order declaring that the solicitor has ceased to act` `a solicitor who has acted for a party in a cause or matter has ceased so to act` `the party has not given notice of change in accordance with Rule 8(3)` `the party has not given notice of intention to act in person in accordance with Rule 8(4)`

