      `the party has reasonable grounds not to make an offer of amicable resolution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party has reasonable grounds not to make an offer of amicable resolution?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 5, rule 1(2), am I to make an offer of amicable resolution before commencing the action` IS
    `o 5 r 1(2) the party is to make an offer of amicable resolution before commencing the action` `the party is about to commence the action` `the party has reasonable grounds not to make an offer of amicable resolution`

@export Under Order 5, rule 1(4), may I reject an offer of amicable resolution?
GIVEN `the person is a party to proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is a party to proceedings?
      `the party has reasonable grounds to reject the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party has reasonable grounds to reject the offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 5, rule 1(4), may I reject an offer of amicable resolution` IS
    `o 5 r 1(4) the party may reject an offer of amicable resolution` `the person is a party to proceedings` `the party has reasonable grounds to reject the offer`

@export Under Order 5, rule 2(2), is my offer open for acceptance as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the parties otherwise agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the parties otherwise agree?
      `the number of days the offer is open for acceptance` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of days the offer is open for acceptance?
      `the period is a reasonable period of time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the period is a reasonable period of time?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 5, rule 2(2), is my offer open for acceptance as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 5 r 2(2) the offer is open for acceptance as required` `the parties otherwise agree` `the number of days the offer is open for acceptance` `the period is a reasonable period of time`

@export Under Order 5, rule 2(3), can the terms of an offer that was not accepted yet be relied upon or made known to the Court?
GIVEN `an offer has been made and not accepted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an offer has been made and not accepted?
      `the Court has determined the merits of the action or appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has determined the merits of the action or appeal?
      `the Court is dealing with the issue of costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court is dealing with the issue of costs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 5, rule 2(3), can the terms of an offer that was not accepted yet be relied upon or made known to the Court` IS
    `o 5 r 2(3) the terms cannot yet be relied upon or made known to the Court` `an offer has been made and not accepted` `the Court has determined the merits of the action or appeal` `the Court is dealing with the issue of costs`

