-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 7 -- service in Singapore`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 7, rule 1(1)(a), may a document be served by personal service?
GIVEN `personal service is expressly required by these Rules or any written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that personal service is expressly required by these Rules or any written law?
      `the Court orders personal service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court orders personal service?
      `the serving party decides to serve personally voluntarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the serving party decides to serve personally voluntarily?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 7, rule 1(1)(a), may a document be served by personal service` IS
    `o 7 r 1(1)(a) a document may be served by personal service` `personal service is expressly required by these Rules or any written law` `the Court orders personal service` `the serving party decides to serve personally voluntarily`

@export Under Order 7, rule 2(1), is personal service effected in this manner?
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a natural person (yes), rather than an entity such as a company or an association (no)?
      `the person's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the person, in years? (Give 0 if the person is an entity.)
      `the entity is incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the person is an entity, is it incorporated? (Give no for a natural person.)
      `manner` IS A `o 7 r 2(1) the manner of personal service` @desc In which manner was the document left?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 7, rule 2(1), is personal service effected in this manner` IS
    `o 7 r 2(1) personal service is effected` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the person I am asking about` `the person is a natural person` `the person's age in years` `the entity is incorporated`) `manner`

@export Under Order 7, rule 3, may ordinary service be effected in this manner?
GIVEN `the person is a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a natural person (yes), rather than an entity such as a company or an association (no)?
      `the person's age in years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old is the person, in years? (Give 0 if the person is an entity.)
      `the entity is incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the person is an entity, is it incorporated? (Give no for a natural person.)
      `manner` IS A `o 7 r 3 the manner of ordinary service` @desc In which manner was the document sent or left?
      `the entity has a registered or principal office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the entity has a registered or principal office?
      `both the serving party and the party to be served act by solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that both the serving party and the party to be served act by solicitor?
      `the solicitor for the party to be served indicated willingness to accept service at a specified fax number and the document is transmitted to that number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the solicitor for the party to be served indicated willingness to accept service at a specified fax number and the document is transmitted to that number?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 7, rule 3, may ordinary service be effected in this manner` IS
    `o 7 r 3 ordinary service may be effected in that manner` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the person I am asking about` `the person is a natural person` `the person's age in years` `the entity is incorporated`) `manner` `the entity has a registered or principal office` `both the serving party and the party to be served act by solicitor` `the solicitor for the party to be served indicated willingness to accept service at a specified fax number and the document is transmitted to that number`

@export Under Order 7, rule 7(1), may I apply to serve the document by substituted service?
GIVEN `the document is required to be served personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is required to be served personally?
      `it is impractical to serve it personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is impractical to serve it personally?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 7, rule 7(1), may I apply to serve the document by substituted service` IS
    `o 7 r 7(1) a party may apply to serve the document by substituted service` `the document is required to be served personally` `it is impractical to serve it personally`

@export Under Order 7, rule 7(3), is substituted service effected within 14 days after the order?
GIVEN `the date of the order of the Court` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the order of the Court?
      `the date substituted service is effected` IS A DATE @desc What is the date substituted service is effected?
      `a public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of a public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
      `another public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of another public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
      `the time has been extended or shortened by an order or by consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the time been extended or shortened, by an order of the Court or by consent in writing?
      `the last day of the period as extended or shortened` IS A DATE @desc If it has, what is the last day of the period as extended or shortened? (Give any date if it has not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 7, rule 7(3), is substituted service effected within 14 days after the order` IS
    `o 7 r 7(3) substituted service is effected within 14 days after the order` `the date of the order of the Court` `the date substituted service is effected` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the public holidays I give` `a public holiday in or near the period` `another public holiday in or near the period`) (`Under Orders 2 to 8, a date I may not have` `the time has been extended or shortened by an order or by consent` `the last day of the period as extended or shortened`)

-- Order 7, rule 8: the day service is deemed to be effected.  The party gives the day and the time of day of service, and how and where it was done.
@export Under Order 7, rule 8, on what day is service deemed to be effected?
GIVEN `the day the document was served` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the document served?
      `the minutes after midnight when it was served` IS A NUMBER @desc At what time of day was it served, as the number of minutes after midnight? (For example 4.30 p.m. is 990; 5 p.m. is 1020.)
      `the method of service` IS A `Method of service` @desc By which method was the document served?
      `the place of service` IS A `Place of service` @desc Was it served in Singapore or out of Singapore?
      `the kind of document served` IS A `Document kind` @desc Which kind of document was served?
      `a written law or another Rule provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law or another Rule provide otherwise for this service?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under Order 7, rule 8, on what day is service deemed to be effected` IS
    `o 7 r 8 the day service is deemed effected` (`Service event` WITH `service of` IS `the kind of document served`, `service method` IS `the method of service`, `service place` IS `the place of service`, `service moment` IS Moment WITH `day of the moment` IS `the day the document was served`, `minutes after midnight` IS `the minutes after midnight when it was served`) `a written law or another Rule provides otherwise`

@export Under Order 7, rule 8, does this Rule deem the day of service?
GIVEN `the day the document was served` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the document served?
      `the minutes after midnight when it was served` IS A NUMBER @desc At what time of day was it served, as the number of minutes after midnight? (For example 4.30 p.m. is 990; 5 p.m. is 1020.)
      `the method of service` IS A `Method of service` @desc By which method was the document served?
      `the place of service` IS A `Place of service` @desc Was it served in Singapore or out of Singapore?
      `the kind of document served` IS A `Document kind` @desc Which kind of document was served?
      `a written law or another Rule provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law or another Rule provide otherwise for this service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 7, rule 8, does this Rule deem the day of service` IS
    `o 7 r 8 this Rule deems the day of service` (`Service event` WITH `service of` IS `the kind of document served`, `service method` IS `the method of service`, `service place` IS `the place of service`, `service moment` IS Moment WITH `day of the moment` IS `the day the document was served`, `minutes after midnight` IS `the minutes after midnight when it was served`) `a written law or another Rule provides otherwise`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 8 -- service out of Singapore`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 8, rule 1(1), may the document be served out of Singapore with the Court's approval?
GIVEN `it can be shown that the Court has the jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it can be shown that the Court has the jurisdiction?
      `it can be shown that the Court is the appropriate court to hear the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it can be shown that the Court is the appropriate court to hear the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 8, rule 1(1), may the document be served out of Singapore with the Court's approval` IS
    `o 8 r 1(1) the document may be served out of Singapore with the Court's approval` `it can be shown that the Court has the jurisdiction` `it can be shown that the Court is the appropriate court to hear the action`

@export Under Order 8, rule 1, is the Court's approval not required to serve the document out of Singapore?
GIVEN `service out of Singapore is allowed under a contract between the parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that service out of Singapore is allowed under a contract between the parties?
      `the document is a court document other than the originating process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is a court document other than the originating process?
      `the Court's approval has been granted for service of the originating process out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court's approval has been granted for service of the originating process out of Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 8, rule 1, is the Court's approval not required to serve the document out of Singapore` IS
    `o 8 r 1 the Court's approval is not required to serve the document out of Singapore` `service out of Singapore is allowed under a contract between the parties` `the document is a court document other than the originating process` `the Court's approval has been granted for service of the originating process out of Singapore`

@export Under Order 8, rule 2(1), may service out of Singapore be effected in this manner?
GIVEN `the Court's approval has been obtained under Rule 1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court's approval has been obtained under Rule 1(2)?
      `manner` IS A `o 8 r 2(1) the manner of service out of Singapore` @desc In which manner is service to be effected?
      `the Hague Service Convention governs service in the foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Hague Service Convention governs service in the foreign country?
      `another Civil Procedure Convention governs service in the foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that another Civil Procedure Convention governs service in the foreign country?
      `the foreign government is willing to effect service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the foreign government is willing to effect service?
      `the foreign judicial authority is willing to effect service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the foreign judicial authority is willing to effect service?
      `the receiving Contracting State has made an objection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the receiving Contracting State has made an objection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 8, rule 2(1), may service out of Singapore be effected in this manner` IS
    `o 8 r 2(1) service out of Singapore may be effected in that manner` `the Court's approval has been obtained under Rule 1(2)` `manner` `the Hague Service Convention governs service in the foreign country` `another Civil Procedure Convention governs service in the foreign country` `the foreign government is willing to effect service` `the foreign judicial authority is willing to effect service` `the receiving Contracting State has made an objection`

@export Under Order 8, rule 2(4), must the document be accompanied by a translation?
GIVEN `the originating process or court document is to be served outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the originating process or court document is to be served outside Singapore?
      `the official language or one of the official languages is English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the official language or one of the official languages is English?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 8, rule 2(4), must the document be accompanied by a translation` IS
    `o 8 r 2(4) the document must be accompanied by a translation` `the originating process or court document is to be served outside Singapore` `the official language or one of the official languages is English`

@export Under Order 8, rule 4A(1), does Rule 4A apply to the service?
GIVEN `the service is under Article 3 of the Hague Service Convention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the service is under Article 3 of the Hague Service Convention?
      `the document is an originating process or other court document required in connection with civil proceedings in respect of a civil or commercial matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is an originating process or other court document required in connection with civil proceedings in respect of a civil or commercial matter?
      `the person to be served is a State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person to be served is a State?
      `the person to be served is in a Contracting State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person to be served is in a Contracting State?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 8, rule 4A(1), does Rule 4A apply to the service` IS
    `o 8 r 4A(1) this Rule applies to the service` `the service is under Article 3 of the Hague Service Convention` `the document is an originating process or other court document required in connection with civil proceedings in respect of a civil or commercial matter` `the person to be served is a State` `the person to be served is in a Contracting State`

@export Under Order 8, rule 7(2), are the expenses paid within 14 days after the request?
GIVEN `the solicitor is requested to pay the expenses` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the solicitor is requested to pay the expenses?
      `the date of the request` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the request?
      `the date the expenses are paid` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the expenses are paid?
      `a public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of a public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
      `another public holiday in or near the period` IS A DATE @desc Give the date of another public holiday that falls in or near the period (1 January 1900 if there is none).
      `the time has been extended or shortened by an order or by consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the time been extended or shortened, by an order of the Court or by consent in writing?
      `the last day of the period as extended or shortened` IS A DATE @desc If it has, what is the last day of the period as extended or shortened? (Give any date if it has not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 8, rule 7(2), are the expenses paid within 14 days after the request` IS
    `o 8 r 7(2) the expenses are paid within 14 days after the request` `the solicitor is requested to pay the expenses` `the date of the request` `the date the expenses are paid` (`Under Orders 2 to 8, the public holidays I give` `a public holiday in or near the period` `another public holiday in or near the period`) (`Under Orders 2 to 8, a date I may not have` `the time has been extended or shortened by an order or by consent` `the last day of the period as extended or shortened`)

-- ============================================================
-- roc2: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021 -- THE SEAT LAYER for Orders 9 to 14.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the page that Singapore Statutes Online labelled "Current version as at 05 Nov 2026".
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a party to a civil action in the Singapore courts (a claimant, a defendant, a third party or an appellant), asking on facts the
-- party can state what must be filed or served, by when, how, at what cost, what the Court may order, and what follows if it is not done.
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that party would ask.
-- Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question calls one layer-1 function (or, for a rule that is gathered from
-- several limbs or that is "subject to" another rule, calls the limb functions and passes their answers in).
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list the Rules give -- one for each fact
-- the party can state, each with an @desc worded as the party would be asked.  The MAYBE inputs of the gathering rules in layer 1 are never
-- asked of the party: the question calls the limb rules itself and passes their answers in, so the party states only the plain facts.
-- THE DAYS.  The count of a period is Order 3, rule 3 (another part of the encoding).  A question about a period asks for the day on which
-- the period ends ("the last day for doing the act") or begins ("the earliest day for doing the act"), counted as that rule provides.
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Rules themselves give; NOTHING means the Rules do not answer on these
-- facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (roc2)").  Never read NOTHING as no.  By Order 3, rule 2(1), unless the context otherwise requires,
-- every requirement in the Rules is subject to the Court's discretion to order otherwise in the interests of justice; no answer here says that discretion is absent.
-- There is no seat for an official.  Where a rule addresses the Court or the Registrar, the question is what the Court may do or must do
-- in the party's case.

§ `The Rules of Court 2021, Orders 9 to 14 -- my questions as a party to a civil action`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 9, Rule 1 -- general matters`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 9, rule 1(1), how many weeks after the originating claim or originating application is issued is the case conference to be held?
GIVEN `place of service` IS A `Place of service` @desc Is the defendant to be served in Singapore, or is the originating claim or originating application to be served out of Singapore?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 1(1), how many weeks after the originating claim or originating application is issued is the case conference to be held` IS
    (`o 9 r 1(1) the period before the case conference` `place of service`)'s `period length`

@export Under Order 9, rule 1(1), on what date is the case conference to be held?
GIVEN `place of service` IS A `Place of service` @desc Is the defendant to be served in Singapore, or is the originating claim or originating application to be served out of Singapore?
      `the day the originating claim or originating application is issued` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the originating claim or originating application is issued? (a date)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 1(1), on what date is the case conference to be held` IS
    `o 9 r 1(1) the day on which the case conference is to be held` `place of service` `the day the originating claim or originating application is issued`

@export Under Order 9, rule 1(2), may the Court hold a case conference earlier or later than the time stated in paragraph (1)?
GIVEN `a party asks for the case conference to be held earlier or later` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a party asks for the case conference to be held earlier or later?
      `the Court acts on its own accord` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court acts on its own accord?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 1(2), may the Court hold a case conference earlier or later than the time stated in paragraph (1)` IS
    `o 9 r 1(2) the Court may hold a case conference earlier or later than the time stated in paragraph (1)` `a party asks for the case conference to be held earlier or later` `the Court acts on its own accord`

@export Under Order 9, rule 1(4), who conducts the case conference?
GIVEN `the Registrar has referred the matter to a Judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar has referred the matter to a Judge?
GIVETH A `Decision maker`
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 1(4), who conducts the case conference` IS
    `o 9 r 1(4) who conducts the case conference` `the Registrar has referred the matter to a Judge`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 9, Rule 4 -- absence of parties`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 9, rule 4(1), may the Court dismiss the action?
GIVEN `no party attends the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that no party attends the case conference?
      `the claimant is absent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant is absent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 4(1), may the Court dismiss the action` IS
    `o 9 r 4(1) the Court may dismiss the action` `no party attends the case conference` `the claimant is absent`

@export Under Order 9, rule 4(2), may the Court give judgment for the claimant?
GIVEN `the claimant attends the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant attends the case conference?
      `the defendant is absent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant is absent?
      `proof of service of the originating claim or originating application on the defendant is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that proof of service of the originating claim or originating application on the defendant is given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 4(2), may the Court give judgment for the claimant` IS
    `o 9 r 4(2) the Court may give judgment for the claimant` `the claimant attends the case conference` `the defendant is absent` `proof of service of the originating claim or originating application on the defendant is given`

@export Under Order 9, rule 4(3), may the Court set aside or vary the dismissal or default judgment?
GIVEN `the dismissal or default judgment was given under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the dismissal or default judgment was given under this Rule?
      `there were valid reasons for the absence of the defaulting party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that there were valid reasons for the absence of the defaulting party?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 4(3), may the Court set aside or vary the dismissal or default judgment` IS
    `o 9 r 4(3) the Court may set aside or vary the dismissal or default judgment` `the dismissal or default judgment was given under this Rule` `there were valid reasons for the absence of the defaulting party`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 9, Rule 5 -- failure to serve originating process`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 9, rule 5(1)(a), may the Court dismiss the action?
GIVEN `the claimant attends the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant attends the case conference?
      `the claimant has not served the originating claim or originating application on the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant has not served the originating claim or originating application on the defendant?
      `the Court is not satisfied that the claimant has taken reasonable steps to effect service expeditiously` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court is not satisfied that the claimant has taken reasonable steps to effect service expeditiously?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 5(1)(a), may the Court dismiss the action` IS
    `o 9 r 5(1)(a) the Court may dismiss the action` `the claimant attends the case conference` `the claimant has not served the originating claim or originating application on the defendant` `the Court is not satisfied that the claimant has taken reasonable steps to effect service expeditiously`

@export Under Order 9, rule 5(1)(b), may the Court make this order?
GIVEN `the claimant attends the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant attends the case conference?
      `the claimant has not served the originating claim or originating application on the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant has not served the originating claim or originating application on the defendant?
      `order` IS A `o 9 r 5(1)(b) an order the Court may make` @desc Which of these is an order the Court may make?
      `it is necessary to extend the validity of the originating process` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is necessary to extend the validity of the originating process?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 5(1)(b), may the Court make this order` IS
    `o 9 r 5(1)(b) the Court may make this order` `the claimant attends the case conference` `the claimant has not served the originating claim or originating application on the defendant` `order` `it is necessary to extend the validity of the originating process`

@export Under Order 9, rule 5(1)(b)(i), how many days after the date of the first case conference does the Court allow the claimant to serve the originating process or apply for substituted service?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 5(1)(b)(i), how many days after the date of the first case conference does the Court allow the claimant to serve the originating process or apply for substituted service` IS
    (`o 9 r 5(1)(b)(i) fourteen days`)'s `period length`

@export Under Order 9, rule 5(1)(b)(i), is the originating process served within 14 days after the first case conference?
GIVEN `the date the originating process is served` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the originating process is served? (a date)
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted as Order 3, rule 3 provides? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 5(1)(b)(i), is the originating process served within 14 days after the first case conference` IS
    `o 9 r 5(1)(b)(i) the originating process is served within 14 days after the first case conference` `the date the originating process is served` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

@export Under Order 9, rule 5(1)(b)(ii), is the application for substituted service made within that time?
GIVEN `the date the application for substituted service is made` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the application for substituted service is made? (a date)
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted as Order 3, rule 3 provides? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 5(1)(b)(ii), is the application for substituted service made within that time` IS
    `o 9 r 5(1)(b)(ii) the application for substituted service is made within that time` `the date the application for substituted service is made` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

@export Under Order 9, rule 5(2), may the Court dismiss the action?
GIVEN `the claimant fails to serve the originating process by the second case conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant fails to serve the originating process by the second case conference?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 5(2), may the Court dismiss the action` IS
    `o 9 r 5(2) the Court may dismiss the action` `the claimant fails to serve the originating process by the second case conference`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 9, Rule 6 -- failure to file and serve defence in originating claim`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 9, rule 6(1), may the Court enter judgment against the defendant in default of a defence?
GIVEN `the action is an originating claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the action is an originating claim?
      `the claimant and the defendant both attend the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant and the defendant both attend the case conference?
      `no defence is served by the first case conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that no defence is served by the first case conference?
      `the time for filing and serving a defence has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the time for filing and serving a defence has expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 6(1), may the Court enter judgment against the defendant in default of a defence` IS
    `o 9 r 6(1) the Court may enter judgment against the defendant in default of a defence` `the action is an originating claim` `the claimant and the defendant both attend the case conference` `no defence is served by the first case conference` `the time for filing and serving a defence has expired`

@export Under Order 9, rule 6(2), may the Court set aside or vary the default judgment?
GIVEN `the judgment is a default judgment entered under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the judgment is a default judgment entered under paragraph (1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 6(2), may the Court set aside or vary the default judgment` IS
    `o 9 r 6(2) the Court may set aside or vary the default judgment` `the judgment is a default judgment entered under paragraph (1)`

@export Under Order 9, rule 6(3), may the Court extend time for the defendant to serve the defence after the first case conference?
GIVEN `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is a special case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 6(3), may the Court extend time for the defendant to serve the defence after the first case conference` IS
    `o 9 r 6(3) the Court may extend time for the defendant to serve the defence after the first case conference` `it is a special case`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 9, Rule 7 -- challenges to jurisdiction of Court`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 9, rule 7(2)(a), how many days after the date of the case conference must the defendant challenging the jurisdiction file and serve the application and affidavit?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 7(2)(a), how many days after the date of the case conference must the defendant challenging the jurisdiction file and serve the application and affidavit` IS
    (`o 9 r 7(2)(a) fourteen days`)'s `period length`

@export Under Order 9, rule 7(2)(a), does the defendant file and serve the application and affidavit in time?
GIVEN `the date the defendant files and serves the application and affidavit` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the defendant files and serves the application and affidavit? (a date)
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted as Order 3, rule 3 provides? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 7(2)(a), does the defendant file and serve the application and affidavit in time` IS
    `o 9 r 7(2)(a) the defendant files and serves the application and affidavit in time` `the date the defendant files and serves the application and affidavit` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

@export Under Order 9, rule 7(2)(b), how many days after that must the claimant file and serve any affidavit in reply?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 7(2)(b), how many days after that must the claimant file and serve any affidavit in reply` IS
    (`o 9 r 7(2)(b) fourteen days thereafter`)'s `period length`

@export Under Order 9, rule 7(2)(b), does the claimant file and serve the affidavit in reply in time?
GIVEN `the date the claimant files and serves the affidavit in reply` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the claimant files and serves the affidavit in reply? (a date)
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted as Order 3, rule 3 provides? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 7(2)(b), does the claimant file and serve the affidavit in reply in time` IS
    `o 9 r 7(2)(b) the claimant files and serves the affidavit in reply in time` `the date the claimant files and serves the affidavit in reply` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

@export Under Order 9, rule 7(2)(c), is the hearing fixed within 14 days after all affidavits have been filed and served?
GIVEN `the date fixed for the hearing` IS A DATE @desc What is the date fixed for the hearing? (a date)
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted as Order 3, rule 3 provides? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 7(2)(c), is the hearing fixed within 14 days after all affidavits have been filed and served` IS
    `o 9 r 7(2)(c) the hearing is fixed within 14 days after all affidavits have been filed and served` `the date fixed for the hearing` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 9, Rule 9 -- single application pending trial`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 9, rule 9(5), how many days after the date of the case conference must the applying party file and serve the application and supporting affidavit?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 9(5), how many days after the date of the case conference must the applying party file and serve the application and supporting affidavit` IS
    (`o 9 r 9(5) twenty-one days`)'s `period length`

@export Under Order 9, rule 9(5), does the party file and serve in time?
GIVEN `party` IS A `o 9 r 9(5) party to the single application` @desc Which of these is the party to the single application?
      `the date the party files and serves` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the party files and serves? (a date)
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted as Order 3, rule 3 provides? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 9(5), does the party file and serve in time` IS
    `o 9 r 9(5) the party files and serves in time` `party` `the date the party files and serves` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

@export Under Order 9, rule 9(10), may an application be taken out?
GIVEN `the date of the application` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the application? (a date)
      `o 3 r 3 the day 14 days before the commencement of the trial` IS A DATE @desc What is the the day 14 days before the commencement of the trial, counted as Order 3, rule 3 provides? (a date)
      `the Court has determined the merits of the action by the date of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has determined the merits of the action by the date of the application?
      `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is a special case?
      `the trial Judge approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the trial Judge approves?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 9(10), may an application be taken out` IS
    `o 9 r 9(10) an application may be taken out` `the date of the application` `o 3 r 3 the day 14 days before the commencement of the trial` `the Court has determined the merits of the action by the date of the application` `it is a special case` `the trial Judge approves`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 9, Rule 10 -- adding and removing of parties`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 9, rule 10(2), may the person proceed in this way?
