-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 9, Rule 12 -- security for costs`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 9, rule 12(1), may the defendant apply for security for the defendant's costs?
GIVEN `the claimant is ordinarily resident out of the jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant is ordinarily resident out of the jurisdiction?
      `the claimant is a nominal claimant suing for some other person's benefit and not in a representative capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant is a nominal claimant suing for some other person's benefit and not in a representative capacity?
      `the claimant is being funded by a non-party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant is being funded by a non-party?
      `there is reason to believe that the claimant will be unable to pay the defendant's costs if ordered to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that there is reason to believe that the claimant will be unable to pay the defendant's costs if ordered to do so?
      `the claimant has not stated or has incorrectly stated the claimant's address in the originating claim or originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant has not stated or has incorrectly stated the claimant's address in the originating claim or originating application?
      `the claimant has changed the claimant's address during the course of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant has changed the claimant's address during the course of the proceedings?
      `the claimant did so to evade the consequences of the litigation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant did so to evade the consequences of the litigation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 12(1), may the defendant apply for security for the defendant's costs` IS
    `o 9 r 12(1) the defendant may apply for security for the defendant's costs` (`o 9 r 12(1)(a) the defendant may apply for security for costs because the claimant is ordinarily resident out of the jurisdiction` `the claimant is ordinarily resident out of the jurisdiction`) (`o 9 r 12(1)(b) the defendant may apply for security for costs because the claimant is a nominal claimant or is funded by a non-party` `the claimant is a nominal claimant suing for some other person's benefit and not in a representative capacity` `the claimant is being funded by a non-party` `there is reason to believe that the claimant will be unable to pay the defendant's costs if ordered to do so`) (`o 9 r 12(1)(c) the defendant may apply for security for costs because of the claimant's address` `the claimant has not stated or has incorrectly stated the claimant's address in the originating claim or originating application` `the claimant has changed the claimant's address during the course of the proceedings` `the claimant did so to evade the consequences of the litigation`)

@export Under Order 9, rule 12(3), may the defendant apply for security for the defendant's costs to be provided by a non-party?
GIVEN `the non-party has assigned that non-party's right in the action to the claimant in return for a share of any money or property which the claimant may recover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the non-party has assigned that non-party's right in the action to the claimant in return for a share of any money or property which the claimant may recover?
      `the non-party has contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant's costs in return for a share of any money or property which the claimant may recover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the non-party has contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant's costs in return for a share of any money or property which the claimant may recover?
      `the non-party has contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant's costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the non-party has contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant's costs?
      `the non-party actively instigates or encourages the claimant to maintain the claimant's action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the non-party actively instigates or encourages the claimant to maintain the claimant's action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 12(3), may the defendant apply for security for the defendant's costs to be provided by a non-party` IS
    `o 9 r 12(3) the defendant may apply for security for the defendant's costs to be provided by a non-party` (`o 9 r 12(3)(a) the defendant may apply for security for costs from the non-party who assigned a right in the action` `the non-party has assigned that non-party's right in the action to the claimant in return for a share of any money or property which the claimant may recover`) (`o 9 r 12(3)(b) the defendant may apply for security for costs from the non-party who contributed in return for a share` `the non-party has contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant's costs in return for a share of any money or property which the claimant may recover`) (`o 9 r 12(3)(c) the defendant may apply for security for costs from the non-party who contributed and instigates the action` `the non-party has contributed or agreed to contribute to the claimant's costs` `the non-party actively instigates or encourages the claimant to maintain the claimant's action`)

@export Under Order 9, rule 12(4), is the application for an order under paragraph (3) made as required?
GIVEN `the application is made by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is made by summons?
      `the summons is served on the non-party personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the summons is served on the non-party personally?
      `the summons is served on every party to the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the summons is served on every party to the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 9, rule 12(4), is the application for an order under paragraph (3) made as required` IS
    `o 9 r 12(4) the application for an order under paragraph (3) is made as required` `the application is made by summons` `the summons is served on the non-party personally` `the summons is served on every party to the proceedings`

