§§ `Order 10, Rule 1 -- third party notice`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 10, rule 1(1), may the defendant issue a third party notice against a person who is not already a party?
GIVEN `the defendant claims against a person not already a party to the action any contribution or indemnity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant claims against a person not already a party to the action any contribution or indemnity?
      `the defendant claims against such a person a relief or remedy relating to or connected with the original subject matter of the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant claims against such a person a relief or remedy relating to or connected with the original subject matter of the action?
      `that relief or remedy is substantially the same as some relief or remedy claimed by the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that that relief or remedy is substantially the same as some relief or remedy claimed by the claimant?
      `the defendant requires that a question or issue be determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant requires that a question or issue be determined?
      `the question or issue relates to or is connected with the original subject matter of the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the question or issue relates to or is connected with the original subject matter of the action?
      `it is to be determined as between either or both of the claimant and the defendant and a person not already a party to the action as well as between the claimant and the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is to be determined as between either or both of the claimant and the defendant and a person not already a party to the action as well as between the claimant and the defendant?
      `the defendant has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so under these Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so under these Rules?
      `the Court has given the defendant permission to issue a third party notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has given the defendant permission to issue a third party notice?
      `the action was begun by` IS A `Document kind` @desc How was the action begun: by an originating claim or by an originating application (or some other way)?
      `the defendant issues the third party notice before serving the defendant's defence on the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant issues the third party notice before serving the defendant's defence on the claimant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 10, rule 1(1), may the defendant issue a third party notice against a person who is not already a party` IS
    `o 10 r 1(1) the defendant may issue a third party notice` (`o 10 r 1(1)(a) the defendant claims against a person not already a party any contribution or indemnity` `the defendant claims against a person not already a party to the action any contribution or indemnity`) (`o 10 r 1(1)(b) the defendant claims against a person not already a party a relief or remedy connected with the action` `the defendant claims against such a person a relief or remedy relating to or connected with the original subject matter of the action` `that relief or remedy is substantially the same as some relief or remedy claimed by the claimant`) (`o 10 r 1(1)(c) the defendant requires a question or issue to be determined also as against a person not already a party` `the defendant requires that a question or issue be determined` `the question or issue relates to or is connected with the original subject matter of the action` `it is to be determined as between either or both of the claimant and the defendant and a person not already a party to the action as well as between the claimant and the defendant`) `the defendant has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so under these Rules` (`o 10 r 1(2) the defendant may issue a third party notice` `the Court has given the defendant permission to issue a third party notice` `the action was begun by` `the defendant issues the third party notice before serving the defendant's defence on the claimant`)

@export Under Order 10, rule 1(3), is the person a third party?
GIVEN `a third party notice is served on the person against whom it is issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a third party notice is served on the person against whom it is issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 10, rule 1(3), is the person a third party` IS
    `o 10 r 1(3) the person is a third party` `a third party notice is served on the person against whom it is issued`

