§§ `Order 10, Rule 4 -- third party directions`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 10, rule 4(1), must the defendant apply to the Court for directions?
GIVEN `the defendant has issued a third party notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant has issued a third party notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 10, rule 4(1), must the defendant apply to the Court for directions` IS
    `o 10 r 4(1) the defendant must apply to the Court for directions` `the defendant has issued a third party notice`

@export Under Order 10, rule 4(2)(a), how many days after the third party files and serves the notice of intention to contest or not contest may the third party apply for directions?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 10, rule 4(2)(a), how many days after the third party files and serves the notice of intention to contest or not contest may the third party apply for directions` IS
    (`o 10 r 4(2)(a) fourteen days after the third party files and serves the notice of intention to contest or not contest`)'s `period length`

@export Under Order 10, rule 4(2), may the third party apply?
GIVEN `no summons is served on the third party under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that no summons is served on the third party under paragraph (1)?
      `the action was begun by` IS A `Document kind` @desc How was the action begun: by an originating claim or by an originating application (or some other way)?
      `the date of the third party's application` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the third party's application? (a date)
      `o 3 r 3 the earliest day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest day for doing the act, counted as Order 3, rule 3 provides? (a date)
      `the application is by summons in Form 23 served on all the other parties to the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is by summons in Form 23 served on all the other parties to the action?
      `thing` IS A `o 10 r 4(2) what the third party may apply for` @desc Which of these is what the third party may apply for?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 10, rule 4(2), may the third party apply` IS
    `o 10 r 4(2) the third party may apply` `no summons is served on the third party under paragraph (1)` `the action was begun by` `the date of the third party's application` `o 3 r 3 the earliest day for doing the act` `the application is by summons in Form 23 served on all the other parties to the action` `thing`

@export Under Order 10, rule 4(3), may the Court make this order?
GIVEN `an application for directions under this Rule is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an application for directions under this Rule is made?
      `order` IS A `o 10 r 4(3) an order the Court may make on the application for directions` @desc Which of these is an order the Court may make on the application for directions?
      `the liability of the third party to the defendant who issued the third party notice is established on the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the liability of the third party to the defendant who issued the third party notice is established on the hearing?
      `the claimant has signed judgment against the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant has signed judgment against the defendant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 10, rule 4(3), may the Court make this order` IS
    `o 10 r 4(3) the Court may make this order` `an application for directions under this Rule is made` `order` `the liability of the third party to the defendant who issued the third party notice is established on the hearing` `the claimant has signed judgment against the defendant`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 10, Rule 5 -- default of third party, etc.`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 10, rule 5(1), is the third party in default?
GIVEN `the third party is required by these Rules to file and serve a notice of intention to contest or not contest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the third party is required by these Rules to file and serve a notice of intention to contest or not contest?
      `the third party has filed and served the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the third party has filed and served the notice?
      `the third party has been ordered to serve a defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the third party has been ordered to serve a defence?
      `the third party has served the defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the third party has served the defence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 10, rule 5(1), is the third party in default` IS
    `o 10 r 5(1) the third party is in default` `the third party is required by these Rules to file and serve a notice of intention to contest or not contest` `the third party has filed and served the notice` `the third party has been ordered to serve a defence` `the third party has served the defence`

@export Under Order 10, rule 5(1)(a), is the third party deemed to admit any claim stated in the third party notice?
GIVEN `the third party is in default under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the third party is in default under paragraph (1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 10, rule 5(1)(a), is the third party deemed to admit any claim stated in the third party notice` IS
    `o 10 r 5(1)(a) the third party is deemed to admit any claim stated in the third party notice` `the third party is in default under paragraph (1)`

@export Under Order 10, rule 5(1)(b), may the defendant enter judgment against the third party?
GIVEN `the third party is in default under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the third party is in default under paragraph (1)?
      `judgment in default is given against the defendant in the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that judgment in default is given against the defendant in the action?
      `that judgment has been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that that judgment has been satisfied?
      `the Court has given permission to enter judgment before satisfaction of that judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has given permission to enter judgment before satisfaction of that judgment?
      `relief` IS A `o 10 r 5(1)(b) a relief the defendant claims in the third party notice` @desc Which of these is a relief the defendant claims in the third party notice?
      `the Court has given permission to enter judgment in respect of any other relief or remedy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has given permission to enter judgment in respect of any other relief or remedy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 10, rule 5(1)(b), may the defendant enter judgment against the third party` IS
    `o 10 r 5(1)(b) the defendant may enter judgment against the third party` `the third party is in default under paragraph (1)` `judgment in default is given against the defendant in the action` `that judgment has been satisfied` `the Court has given permission to enter judgment before satisfaction of that judgment` `relief` `the Court has given permission to enter judgment in respect of any other relief or remedy`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 10, Rule 7 -- judgment between defendant and third party`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 10, rule 7(2), may an enforcement order be issued against the third party?
GIVEN `judgment is given against the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that judgment is given against the defendant?
      `judgment is given for the defendant against the third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that judgment is given for the defendant against the third party?
      `the judgment against the defendant has been satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the judgment against the defendant has been satisfied?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has given permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 10, rule 7(2), may an enforcement order be issued against the third party` IS
    `o 10 r 7(2) an enforcement order may be issued against the third party` `judgment is given against the defendant` `judgment is given for the defendant against the third party` `the judgment against the defendant has been satisfied` `the Court has given permission`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 10, Rule 8 -- claims and issues between defendant and some other party (O. 10, r. 8)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 10, rule 8(1), may the defendant issue and serve a notice on a person who is already a party without permission?
GIVEN `the defendant claims against a person who is already a party to the action any contribution or indemnity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant claims against a person who is already a party to the action any contribution or indemnity?
      `the defendant claims against such a person a relief or remedy relating to or connected with the original subject matter of the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant claims against such a person a relief or remedy relating to or connected with the original subject matter of the action?
      `that relief or remedy is substantially the same as some relief or remedy claimed by the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that that relief or remedy is substantially the same as some relief or remedy claimed by the claimant?
      `the defendant requires that a question or issue be determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant requires that a question or issue be determined?
      `the question or issue relates to or is connected with the original subject matter of the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the question or issue relates to or is connected with the original subject matter of the action?
      `it is to be determined as between either or both of the claimant and the defendant and some other person who is already a party to the action as well as between the claimant and the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is to be determined as between either or both of the claimant and the defendant and some other person who is already a party to the action as well as between the claimant and the defendant?
      `the defendant has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so under these Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the defendant has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so under these Rules?
      `the claim could be made by the defendant by counterclaim in the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claim could be made by the defendant by counterclaim in the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 10, rule 8(1), may the defendant issue and serve a notice on a person who is already a party without permission` IS
    `o 10 r 8(1) the defendant may issue and serve a notice on the person without permission` (`o 10 r 8(1)(a) the defendant claims against a person already a party any contribution or indemnity` `the defendant claims against a person who is already a party to the action any contribution or indemnity`) (`o 10 r 8(1)(b) the defendant claims against a person already a party a relief or remedy connected with the action` `the defendant claims against such a person a relief or remedy relating to or connected with the original subject matter of the action` `that relief or remedy is substantially the same as some relief or remedy claimed by the claimant`) (`o 10 r 8(1)(c) the defendant requires a question or issue to be determined also as against another party` `the defendant requires that a question or issue be determined` `the question or issue relates to or is connected with the original subject matter of the action` `it is to be determined as between either or both of the claimant and the defendant and some other person who is already a party to the action as well as between the claimant and the defendant`) `the defendant has filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest if required to do so under these Rules` (`o 10 r 8(2) paragraph (1) applies in relation to the claim` `the claim could be made by the defendant by counterclaim in the action`)

@export Under Order 10, rule 8(4), how many days after service of the notice on the person may the person apply?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 10, rule 8(4), how many days after service of the notice on the person may the person apply` IS
    (`o 10 r 8(4) fourteen days after service of the notice on the person`)'s `period length`

@export Under Order 10, rule 8(4), may the person apply?
GIVEN `no summons under Rule 4(1) is served on the person on whom a notice has been served under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that no summons under Rule 4(1) is served on the person on whom a notice has been served under this Rule?
      `the date of the person's application` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the person's application? (a date)
      `o 3 r 3 the earliest day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the earliest day for doing the act, counted as Order 3, rule 3 provides? (a date)
      `the application is by summons in Form 23 served on all the other parties to the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is by summons in Form 23 served on all the other parties to the action?
      `thing` IS A `o 10 r 4(2) what the third party may apply for` @desc Which of these is what the third party may apply for?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 10, rule 8(4), may the person apply` IS
    `o 10 r 8(4) the person may apply` `no summons under Rule 4(1) is served on the person on whom a notice has been served under this Rule` `the date of the person's application` `o 3 r 3 the earliest day for doing the act` `the application is by summons in Form 23 served on all the other parties to the action` `thing`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 10, Rule 9 -- claims by third and subsequent parties`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 10, rule 9(3), may the third party issue a notice under Rule 1?
GIVEN `the Court has given the third party permission to issue a notice under Rule 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has given the third party permission to issue a notice under Rule 1?
      `the action in question was begun by` IS A `Document kind` @desc How was the action begun: by an originating claim or by an originating application (or some other way)?
      `the date the third party issues the notice` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the third party issues the notice? (a date)
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted as Order 3, rule 3 provides? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 10, rule 9(3), may the third party issue a notice under Rule 1` IS
    `o 10 r 9(3) the third party may issue a notice under Rule 1` `the Court has given the third party permission to issue a notice under Rule 1` `the action in question was begun by` `the date the third party issues the notice` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 11, Rule 2 -- order for production`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 11, rule 2(1), may the Court order the parties to exchange a list of and a copy of the documents?
GIVEN `the order is made at a case conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the order is made at a case conference?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 11, rule 2(1), may the Court order the parties to exchange a list of and a copy of the documents` IS
    `o 11 r 2(1) the Court may order the parties to exchange a list of and a copy of the documents` `the order is made at a case conference`

@export Under Order 11, rule 2(1), how many days after the date of the case conference must the parties exchange the list and copies of the documents?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 11, rule 2(1), how many days after the date of the case conference must the parties exchange the list and copies of the documents` IS
    (`o 11 r 2(1) fourteen days after the date of the case conference`)'s `period length`

@export Under Order 11, rule 2(1), do the parties exchange the list and the copies in time?
GIVEN `the date the parties exchange the list and the copies` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the parties exchange the list and the copies? (a date)
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted as Order 3, rule 3 provides? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 11, rule 2(1), do the parties exchange the list and the copies in time` IS
    `o 11 r 2(1) the parties exchange the list and the copies in time` `the date the parties exchange the list and the copies` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

@export Under Order 11, rule 2(2), is a document a known adverse document?
GIVEN `the party knows that the document is adverse to the party's case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party knows that the document is adverse to the party's case?
      `the party ought reasonably to know that the document is adverse to the party's case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party ought reasonably to know that the document is adverse to the party's case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 11, rule 2(2), is a document a known adverse document` IS
    `o 11 r 2(2) a document is a known adverse document` `the party knows that the document is adverse to the party's case` `the party ought reasonably to know that the document is adverse to the party's case`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 11, Rule 3 -- production of requested documents`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 11, rule 3(1), may the Court order any party to produce the requested documents?
GIVEN `the requested documents are in the party's possession or control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the requested documents are in the party's possession or control?
      `the requesting party properly identifies the requested documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the requesting party properly identifies the requested documents?
      `the requesting party shows that the requested documents are material to the issues in the case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the requesting party shows that the requested documents are material to the issues in the case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 11, rule 3(1), may the Court order any party to produce the requested documents` IS
    `o 11 r 3(1) the Court may order any party to produce the requested documents` `the requested documents are in the party's possession or control` `the requesting party properly identifies the requested documents` `the requesting party shows that the requested documents are material to the issues in the case`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 11, Rule 4 -- court’s power to order production of documents`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 11, rule 4, may the Court of its own accord order a party or non-party to produce a copy of the document?
GIVEN `the document is in the person's possession or control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is in the person's possession or control?
      `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is a special case?
      `the document merely leads a party on a train of inquiry to other documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document merely leads a party on a train of inquiry to other documents?
      `the document is part of a party's private or internal correspondence, whether in paper form or in an electronic format` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is part of a party's private or internal correspondence, whether in paper form or in an electronic format?
      `the correspondence is a known adverse document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the correspondence is a known adverse document?
      `a written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a written law provides otherwise?
      `the document is subject to any privilege` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is subject to any privilege?
      `its production would be contrary to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that its production would be contrary to the public interest?
      `the document was at any time subject to any privilege` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document was at any time subject to any privilege?
      `the party entitled to the privilege consents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party entitled to the privilege consents?
      `the Court approves` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court approves?
      `the party is required by an order made by the Court under this Order to produce documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party is required by an order made by the Court under this Order to produce documents?
      `the ground is that the document is confidential` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the ground is that the document is confidential?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 11, rule 4, may the Court of its own accord order a party or non-party to produce a copy of the document` IS
    `o 11 r 4 the Court may order any party or non-party to produce a copy of the document` `the document is in the person's possession or control` (`o 11 r 5 the Court may order the production of the document` (`o 11 r 5(1) the Court may order production of the document` `it is a special case` `the document merely leads a party on a train of inquiry to other documents`) (`o 11 r 5(2) the Court may order the production of the document` `the document is part of a party's private or internal correspondence, whether in paper form or in an electronic format` `it is a special case` `the correspondence is a known adverse document`) (`o 11 r 5(3) the Court may order the production of the document` `a written law provides otherwise` `the document is subject to any privilege` `its production would be contrary to the public interest`)) (`o 11 r 8(1) the document may be relied on` `the document was at any time subject to any privilege` `the party entitled to the privilege consents` `the Court approves`) (`o 11 r 9(1) the party may withhold or object to the production of the document on this ground` `the party is required by an order made by the Court under this Order to produce documents` `the ground is that the document is confidential`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 11, Rule 5 -- no order for production of certain documents`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 11, rule 5, may the Court order the production of the document?
GIVEN `it is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is a special case?
      `the document merely leads a party on a train of inquiry to other documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document merely leads a party on a train of inquiry to other documents?
      `the document is part of a party's private or internal correspondence, whether in paper form or in an electronic format` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is part of a party's private or internal correspondence, whether in paper form or in an electronic format?
      `the correspondence is a known adverse document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the correspondence is a known adverse document?
      `a written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a written law provides otherwise?
      `the document is subject to any privilege` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is subject to any privilege?
      `its production would be contrary to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that its production would be contrary to the public interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 11, rule 5, may the Court order the production of the document` IS
    `o 11 r 5 the Court may order the production of the document` (`o 11 r 5(1) the Court may order production of the document` `it is a special case` `the document merely leads a party on a train of inquiry to other documents`) (`o 11 r 5(2) the Court may order the production of the document` `the document is part of a party's private or internal correspondence, whether in paper form or in an electronic format` `it is a special case` `the correspondence is a known adverse document`) (`o 11 r 5(3) the Court may order the production of the document` `a written law provides otherwise` `the document is subject to any privilege` `its production would be contrary to the public interest`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 11, Rule 6 -- continuing duty to produce`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 11, rule 6, does the party required to produce the documents remain under a duty to produce further documents?
GIVEN `the Court makes an order under Rule 2, 3 or 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court makes an order under Rule 2, 3 or 4?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 11, rule 6, does the party required to produce the documents remain under a duty to produce further documents` IS
    `o 11 r 6 the party required to produce the documents remains under a duty to produce further documents` `the Court makes an order under Rule 2, 3 or 4`

@export Under Order 11, rule 6, how many days after a document comes into the party's possession or control must the party produce it?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 11, rule 6, how many days after a document comes into the party's possession or control must the party produce it` IS
    (`o 11 r 6 fourteen days after the document comes into the party's possession or control`)'s `period length`

@export Under Order 11, rule 6, does the party produce the document in time?
GIVEN `the date the party produces the document` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the party produces the document? (a date)
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted as Order 3, rule 3 provides? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 11, rule 6, does the party produce the document in time` IS
    `o 11 r 6 the party produces the document in time` `the date the party produces the document` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 11, Rule 7 -- non‑compliance with production order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 11, rule 7, if a party fails to comply with an order made under Order 11, may the Court do this?
GIVEN `a party fails to comply with an order made by the Court under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a party fails to comply with an order made by the Court under this Order?
      `thing` IS A `o 11 r 7 a thing the Court may do` @desc Which of these is a thing the Court may do?
      `the order has been served on that party's solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the order has been served on that party's solicitor?
      `that party shows that that party was not notified or did not know about the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that that party shows that that party was not notified or did not know about the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 11, rule 7, if a party fails to comply with an order made under Order 11, may the Court do this` IS
    `o 11 r 7 the Court may do this` `a party fails to comply with an order made by the Court under this Order` `thing` `the order has been served on that party's solicitor` `that party shows that that party was not notified or did not know about the order`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 11, Rule 9 -- confidential documents`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 11, rule 9(1), may the party withhold or object to the production of the document on this ground?
GIVEN `the party is required by an order made by the Court under this Order to produce documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party is required by an order made by the Court under this Order to produce documents?
      `the ground is that the document is confidential` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the ground is that the document is confidential?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 11, rule 9(1), may the party withhold or object to the production of the document on this ground` IS
    `o 11 r 9(1) the party may withhold or object to the production of the document on this ground` `the party is required by an order made by the Court under this Order to produce documents` `the ground is that the document is confidential`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 11, Rule 12 -- inspection of original of document produced`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 11, rule 12(2), how many days after the request must the inspection take place?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 11, rule 12(2), how many days after the request must the inspection take place` IS
    (`o 11 r 12(2) fourteen days after the request`)'s `period length`

@export Under Order 11, rule 12(2), does the inspection take place in time?
GIVEN `the parties otherwise agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the parties otherwise agree?
      `the date the inspection takes place` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the inspection takes place? (a date)
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted as Order 3, rule 3 provides? (a date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 11, rule 12(2), does the inspection take place in time` IS
    `o 11 r 12(2) the inspection takes place in time` `the parties otherwise agree` `the date the inspection takes place` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

