-- ============================================================
-- roc3: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026 -- THE SEAT LAYER for Orders 15 to 18 (roc3).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a party to a civil action in the Singapore courts -- a claimant, a defendant, a third party or an appellant -- asking, on
-- facts they can state, what they must file or serve, by when, how, at what cost, what the Court may order, and what follows if
-- they do not.  This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above as the questions that person
-- would ask.  Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question calls one layer-1 rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a date, a number, or a choice from a list -- one for each fact the
-- person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.  A fact that may not have happened yet (a notice
-- not yet served) is asked as a yes/no and, if yes, a date; the layer-1 rule receives it as a MAYBE DATE.
--   * "the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3" is the one input every deadline question needs.  The Rules
--     count their own periods in Order 3, rule 3 (which is not among this part's ranges), so the person, or their solicitor,
--     says what that last day is; this layer does not count days.  Order 3, rule 2(1) is not applied.
--   * Order 15, rule 15 and Order 18, rule 29 ask for facts about permissions and orders the Court has given; the person states them.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Rules themselves give; NOTHING means the Rules do not answer
-- on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- There is no seat for an official: where a rule addresses only an official (the Registrar, a District Judge, a Magistrate
-- certifying grounds of decision), it is encoded in layer 1 and the person meets it only through the questions below.

§ `Orders 15 to 18 of the Rules of Court 2021 -- my questions as a party`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Order 15 -- Court hearings and evidence`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `Order 15, rule 1`

@export Under Order 15, rule 1(1), must my matter be heard in chambers?
GIVEN `the kind of matter` IS A `o 15 r 1 kind of matter` @desc Which kind of matter is yours?
      `a written law or the practice directions provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a written law or the practice directions provide otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 1(1), must my matter be heard in chambers` IS
    `o 15 r 1(1) the matter must be heard in chambers` `the kind of matter` `a written law or the practice directions provide otherwise`

@export Under Order 15, rule 1(3), must my application or appeal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal be heard in open court?
GIVEN `the kind of matter` IS A `o 15 r 1 kind of matter` @desc Which kind of matter is yours?
      `the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal has otherwise ordered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 1(3), must my application or appeal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal be heard in open court` IS
    `o 15 r 1(3) the matter must be heard in open court` `the kind of matter` `the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal has otherwise ordered`

§§ `Order 15, rule 3`

@export Under Order 15, rule 3(1), am I attending my hearing as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the party is legally represented` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are legally represented?
      `the party attends in person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you attend in person?
      `the party attends by a solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you attend by a solicitor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 3(1), am I attending my hearing as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 15 r 3(1) the party attends as the Rule requires` `the party is legally represented` `the party attends in person` `the party attends by a solicitor`

@export Under Order 15, rule 3(2), may the Court dismiss my application, action or appeal, or make another order against me, if I do not attend?
GIVEN `the party fails to attend the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you fail to attend the hearing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 3(2), may the Court dismiss my application, action or appeal, or make another order against me, if I do not attend` IS
    `o 15 r 3(2) the Court may dismiss the party's application, action or appeal or make any other appropriate order against the party` `the party fails to attend the hearing`

§§ `Order 15, rule 4`

@export Under Order 15, rule 4(1), may I ask the Registrar for an order to attend court or to produce documents in Form 29?
GIVEN `the person is a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 4(1), may I ask the Registrar for an order to attend court or to produce documents in Form 29` IS
    `o 15 r 4(1) the person may request the Registrar to issue an order to attend court or to produce documents in Form 29` `the person is a party`

@export Under Order 15, rule 4(3), have I served my order to attend court or to produce documents on the witness in the way and in time the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the order is served by the requesting party on the witness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order is served by you on the witness?
      `the service is personal service in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the service is personal service in Singapore?
      `the date of service` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of service?
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 4(3), have I served my order to attend court or to produce documents on the witness in the way and in time the Rule requires` IS
    `o 15 r 4(3) the order is served in the way and in time the Rule requires` `the order is served by the requesting party on the witness` `the service is personal service in Singapore` `the date of service` `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

@export Under Order 15, rule 4(9), is a witness who complies with my order entitled to claim reasonable compensation from me?
GIVEN `the witness complies with an order to attend court or an order to produce documents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the witness complies with an order to attend court or an order to produce documents?
      `the witness has made a request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the witness has made a request?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 4(9), is a witness who complies with my order entitled to claim reasonable compensation from me` IS
    `o 15 r 4(9) the witness is entitled to claim reasonable compensation for time and expenses from the requesting party` `the witness complies with an order to attend court or an order to produce documents` `the witness has made a request`

§§ `Order 15, rule 5`

@export Under Order 15, rule 5(3), have I applied for a letter of request as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the application is made by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application is made by summons?
      `the summons is supported by an affidavit setting out the basis for the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the summons is supported by an affidavit setting out the basis for the application?
      `the affidavit encloses a copy of each document the applicant intends to file in the Registry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the affidavit encloses a copy of each document you intend to file in the Registry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 5(3), have I applied for a letter of request as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 15 r 5(3) the application is made as the Rule requires` `the application is made by summons` `the summons is supported by an affidavit setting out the basis for the application` `the affidavit encloses a copy of each document the applicant intends to file in the Registry`

§§ `Order 15, rule 6`

@export Under Order 15, rule 6(1), may I attend the hearing?
GIVEN `the hearing is in open court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the hearing is in open court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 6(1), may I attend the hearing` IS
    `o 15 r 6(1) the person may attend the hearing` `the hearing is in open court`

§§ `Order 15, rule 8`

@export Under Order 15, rule 8(8), may I cross-examine the claimant and the claimant's witnesses?
GIVEN `the person is the defendant or another party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are the defendant or another party?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 8(8), may I cross-examine the claimant and the claimant's witnesses` IS
    `o 15 r 8(8) the person may cross-examine the claimant and the claimant's witnesses` `the person is the defendant or another party`

@export Under Order 15, rule 8(11), may I, as the defendant, make a submission of No case to answer?
GIVEN `it is the conclusion of the claimant's case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is the conclusion of the claimant's case?
      `the defendant will not be giving evidence by himself or herself or through the defendant's witnesses even if the Court rules against the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you will not be giving evidence by himself or herself or through your witnesses even if the Court rules against you?
      `the defendant does not have a counterclaim arising out of substantially the same facts as the claimant's case or withdraws it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you do not have a counterclaim arising out of substantially the same facts as the claimant's case or withdraws it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 8(11), may I, as the defendant, make a submission of No case to answer` IS
    `o 15 r 8(11) the defendant may make a submission of No case to answer` `it is the conclusion of the claimant's case` `the defendant will not be giving evidence by himself or herself or through the defendant's witnesses even if the Court rules against the defendant` `the defendant does not have a counterclaim arising out of substantially the same facts as the claimant's case or withdraws it`

§§ `Order 15, rule 11`

@export Under Order 15, rule 11(8), may I apply for a certified transcript of the official record of the hearing?
GIVEN `the party has paid the relevant fees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have paid the relevant fees?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 11(8), may I apply for a certified transcript of the official record of the hearing` IS
    `o 15 r 11(8) the party may apply for a certified transcript of the official record of the hearing` `the party has paid the relevant fees`

@export Under Order 15, rule 11(9), may I claim the cost of a certified transcript as an item of disbursement?
GIVEN `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has otherwise ordered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 11(9), may I claim the cost of a certified transcript as an item of disbursement` IS
    `o 15 r 11(9) the costs of producing a certified transcript may be claimed as an item of disbursement` `the Court has otherwise ordered`

§§ `Order 15, rule 12`

@export Under Order 15, rule 12(2), am I entitled to a copy of the Court's decision?
GIVEN `the decision was given in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the decision was given in writing?
      `the relevant charges have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the relevant charges have been paid?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 12(2), am I entitled to a copy of the Court's decision` IS
    `o 15 r 12(2) the parties are entitled to a copy of the decision` `the decision was given in writing` `the relevant charges have been paid`

§§ `Order 15, rule 15`

@export Under Order 15, rule 15(4), did I apply for directions on the assessment of damages in time?
GIVEN `the date the party entitled to the benefit of the judgment applied to the Court for directions` IS A DATE @desc On what date did this happen: you entitled to the benefit of the judgment applied to the Court for directions?
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 15(4), did I apply for directions on the assessment of damages in time` IS
    `o 15 r 15(4) the application for directions is made in time` `the date the party entitled to the benefit of the judgment applied to the Court for directions` `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

@export Under Order 15, rule 15(5), did I serve my notice of appointment for the assessment of damages in time?
GIVEN `the date the notice of appointment was served on the party against whom the judgment is given` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of appointment served on you against whom the judgment is given?
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 15(5), did I serve my notice of appointment for the assessment of damages in time` IS
    `o 15 r 15(5) the notice of appointment is served in time` `the date the notice of appointment was served on the party against whom the judgment is given` `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

§§ `Order 15, rule 16`

@export Under Order 15, rule 16(3), may my affidavit of evidence-in-chief be used?
GIVEN `the maker attends Court for cross-examination` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you attend Court for cross-examination?
      `the parties otherwise agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the parties otherwise agree?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 16(3), may my affidavit of evidence-in-chief be used` IS
    `o 15 r 16(3) the affidavit of evidence-in-chief may be used` `the maker attends Court for cross-examination` `the parties otherwise agree`

@export Under Order 15, rule 16(6), did I give my notice of objection to the other side's affidavits in time?
GIVEN `the notice was given by filing and serving the form specified in the practice directions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice was given by filing and serving the form specified in the practice directions?
      `the date the notice was filed and served` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice filed and served?
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 16(6), did I give my notice of objection to the other side's affidavits in time` IS
    `o 15 r 16(6) the notice of objection is given in time` `the notice was given by filing and serving the form specified in the practice directions` `the date the notice was filed and served` `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

§§ `Order 15, rule 19`

@export Under Order 15, rule 19(1), is my affidavit in the form the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the affidavit is in Form 31` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the affidavit is in Form 31?
      `the text is set out in consecutively numbered paragraphs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the text is set out in consecutively numbered paragraphs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 19(1), is my affidavit in the form the Rule requires` IS
    `o 15 r 19(1) the affidavit is in the form the Rule requires` `the affidavit is in Form 31` `the text is set out in consecutively numbered paragraphs`

§§ `Order 15, rule 20`

@export Under Order 15, rule 20, may I make an affidavit?
GIVEN `the person is legally competent to give evidence in court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are legally competent to give evidence in court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 20, may I make an affidavit` IS
    `o 15 r 20 the person may make an affidavit` `the person is legally competent to give evidence in court`

§§ `Order 15, rule 25`

@export Under Order 15, rule 25(2), may my affidavit contain this matter?
GIVEN `the matter is vulgar or insulting words` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the matter is vulgar or insulting words?
      `those words are in issue in the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that those words are in issue in the action?
      `the matter is intended to offend or to belittle any person or entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the matter is intended to offend or to belittle any person or entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 25(2), may my affidavit contain this matter` IS
    `o 15 r 25(2) the affidavit may contain the matter` `the matter is vulgar or insulting words` `those words are in issue in the action` `the matter is intended to offend or to belittle any person or entity`

§§ `Order 15, rule 26`

@export Under Order 15, rule 26(1), may I alter my affidavit?
GIVEN `the affidavit has been affirmed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the affidavit has been affirmed?
      `the affidavit has been filed in Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the affidavit has been filed in Court?
      `the affidavit is re-affirmed before a commissioner for oaths` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the affidavit is re-affirmed before a commissioner for oaths?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 26(1), may I alter my affidavit` IS
    `o 15 r 26(1) the affidavit may be altered` `the affidavit has been affirmed` `the affidavit has been filed in Court` `the affidavit is re-affirmed before a commissioner for oaths`

§§ `Order 15, rule 27`

@export Under Order 15, rule 27(1), must I annex a copy of the document my affidavit refers to?
GIVEN `the affidavit refers to a document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the affidavit refers to a document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 27(1), must I annex a copy of the document my affidavit refers to` IS
    `o 15 r 27(1) a copy of the document must be annexed to the affidavit` `the affidavit refers to a document`

§§ `Order 15, rule 29`

@export Under Order 15, rule 29, must I give notice of my intention to use an affidavit filed in previous proceedings and serve it on every other party?
GIVEN `the party intends to use in any proceedings an affidavit filed in previous proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you intend to use in any proceedings an affidavit filed in previous proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 15, rule 29, must I give notice of my intention to use an affidavit filed in previous proceedings and serve it on every other party` IS
    `o 15 r 29 the party must give notice of the intention to use the affidavit and serve it on every other party` `the party intends to use in any proceedings an affidavit filed in previous proceedings`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Order 16 -- Withdrawal and discontinuance`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `Order 16, rule 1`

@export Under Order 16, rule 1, may I withdraw my notice of intention to contest or not contest?
GIVEN `the party has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has given permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 16, rule 1, may I withdraw my notice of intention to contest or not contest` IS
    `o 16 r 1 the party may withdraw the notice of intention to contest or not contest` `the party has filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action` `the Court has given permission`

§§ `Order 16, rule 2`

@export Under Order 16, rule 2(1), may I, as the claimant, discontinue the action or withdraw a claim without the permission of the Court?
GIVEN `the action was begun by originating claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the action was begun by originating claim?
      `has happened: the date a notice in Form 32 was served on the defendant concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a notice in Form 32 been served on the defendant concerned?
      `date of: the date a notice in Form 32 was served on the defendant concerned` IS A DATE @desc On what date was a notice in Form 32 served on the defendant concerned? (Give any date if it has not happened.)
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 16, rule 2(1), may I, as the claimant, discontinue the action or withdraw a claim without the permission of the Court` IS
    `o 16 r 2(1) the claimant may discontinue the action or withdraw a claim without the permission of the Court` `the action was begun by originating claim` (IF `has happened: the date a notice in Form 32 was served on the defendant concerned` THEN JUST `date of: the date a notice in Form 32 was served on the defendant concerned` ELSE NOTHING) `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

@export Under Order 16, rule 2(2)(a), may I, as the defendant, withdraw my defence without the permission of the Court?
GIVEN `the defendant has filed a defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have filed a defence?
      `a notice in Form 32 was served on the claimant or other party concerned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a notice in Form 32 was served on the claimant or other party concerned?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 16, rule 2(2)(a), may I, as the defendant, withdraw my defence without the permission of the Court` IS
    `o 16 r 2(2)(a) the defendant may withdraw the defence or any part of it without the permission of the Court` `the defendant has filed a defence` `a notice in Form 32 was served on the claimant or other party concerned`

@export Under Order 16, rule 2(5), may the action be withdrawn without the permission of the Court because we all consent?
GIVEN `all the parties to the action consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that all the parties to the action consent?
      `the trial has begun` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trial has begun?
      `a written consent to the action being withdrawn signed by all the parties is produced to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a written consent to the action being withdrawn signed by all the parties is produced to the Registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 16, rule 2(5), may the action be withdrawn without the permission of the Court because we all consent` IS
    `o 16 r 2(5) the action may be withdrawn without the permission of the Court on the consent of all the parties` `all the parties to the action consent` `the trial has begun` `a written consent to the action being withdrawn signed by all the parties is produced to the Registrar`

§§ `Order 16, rule 3`

@export Under Order 16, rule 3(1), may I discontinue the action or counterclaim without the permission of the Court?
GIVEN `Rule 2 provides for the discontinuance or withdrawal without the permission of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that Rule 2 provides for the discontinuance or withdrawal without the permission of the Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 16, rule 3(1), may I discontinue the action or counterclaim without the permission of the Court` IS
    `o 16 r 3(1) a party may discontinue the action or counterclaim or withdraw a claim without the permission of the Court` `Rule 2 provides for the discontinuance or withdrawal without the permission of the Court`

§§ `Order 16, rule 2`

@export Under Order 16, rule 2(7), is my action, cause or matter deemed to have been discontinued because nothing has been done in it for more than a year?
GIVEN `a party has taken a step or proceeding in the action, cause or matter that appears from the records maintained by the Court within the one year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have taken a step or proceeding in the action, cause or matter that appears from the records maintained by the Court within the one year?
      `the action, cause or matter has been stayed pursuant to an order of court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the action, cause or matter has been stayed pursuant to an order of court?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 16, rule 2(7), is my action, cause or matter deemed to have been discontinued because nothing has been done in it for more than a year` IS
    `o 16 r 2(7) the action, cause or matter is deemed to have been discontinued` `a party has taken a step or proceeding in the action, cause or matter that appears from the records maintained by the Court within the one year` `the action, cause or matter has been stayed pursuant to an order of court` `the date I am asking about` `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

§§ `Order 16, rule 4`

@export Under Order 16, rule 4, is the earlier discontinuance a defence to the new action brought against me for the same cause of action?
GIVEN `the party discontinued, is deemed to have discontinued, or withdrew a particular claim in, an action or counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you discontinued, is deemed to have discontinued, or withdrew a particular claim in, an action or counterclaim?
      `the subsequent action is for the same, or substantially the same, cause of action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the subsequent action is for the same, or substantially the same, cause of action?
      `the Court imposed terms in granting permission under Rule 3 that bear on the point` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court imposed terms in granting permission under Rule 3 that bear on the point?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 16, rule 4, is the earlier discontinuance a defence to the new action brought against me for the same cause of action` IS
    `o 16 r 4 the discontinuance is a defence to a subsequent action for the same cause of action` `the party discontinued, is deemed to have discontinued, or withdrew a particular claim in, an action or counterclaim` `the subsequent action is for the same, or substantially the same, cause of action` `the Court imposed terms in granting permission under Rule 3 that bear on the point`

§§ `Order 16, rule 5`

@export Under Order 16, rule 5, may the Court stay the new action I have brought until I have paid the costs of the discontinued one?
GIVEN `the party discontinued, is deemed to have discontinued, or withdrew a particular claim in, an action or counterclaim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you discontinued, is deemed to have discontinued, or withdrew a particular claim in, an action or counterclaim?
      `the party is liable to pay another party's costs of the action or counterclaim or the costs occasioned by the claim withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are liable to pay another party's costs of the action or counterclaim or the costs occasioned by the claim withdrawn?
      `before payment of those costs the party brings an action for the same, or substantially the same, cause of action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that before payment of those costs you bring an action for the same, or substantially the same, cause of action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 16, rule 5, may the Court stay the new action I have brought until I have paid the costs of the discontinued one` IS
    `o 16 r 5 the Court may order the proceedings in the subsequent action to be stayed until the costs are paid` `the party discontinued, is deemed to have discontinued, or withdrew a particular claim in, an action or counterclaim` `the party is liable to pay another party's costs of the action or counterclaim or the costs occasioned by the claim withdrawn` `before payment of those costs the party brings an action for the same, or substantially the same, cause of action`

