§ `Order 18 -- Appeals`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

§§ `Order 18, rule 3`

@export Under Order 18, rule 3(1), is the time for my appeal, or my application for permission to appeal, still held back from starting to run?
GIVEN `the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in the application, including costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in the application, including costs?
      `a written law, paragraph (1A) or paragraph (2) provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a written law, paragraph (1A) or paragraph (2) provides otherwise?
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has otherwise ordered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 3(1), is the time for my appeal, or my application for permission to appeal, still held back from starting to run` IS
    `o 18 r 3(1) the time for filing an appeal or an application for permission to appeal is still barred from starting to run` `the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in the application, including costs` `a written law, paragraph (1A) or paragraph (2) provides otherwise` `the Court has otherwise ordered`

§§ `Order 18, rule 4`

@export Under Order 18, rule 4(1), may I file an appeal for this application?
GIVEN `the party has already filed an appeal for the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have already filed an appeal for the application?
      `paragraph (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that paragraph (2) applies?
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has otherwise ordered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 4(1), may I file an appeal for this application` IS
    `o 18 r 4(1) the party may file another appeal for the application` `the party has already filed an appeal for the application` `paragraph (2) applies` `the Court has otherwise ordered`

§§ `Order 18, rule 6`

@export Under Order 18, rule 6(1), does my appeal stay enforcement of the lower Court's decision?
GIVEN `the lower Court or the appellate Court has directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the lower Court or the appellate Court has directed otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 6(1), does my appeal stay enforcement of the lower Court's decision` IS
    `o 18 r 6(1) the appeal operates as a stay of enforcement or of proceedings under the decision of the lower Court` `the lower Court or the appellate Court has directed otherwise`

§§ `Order 18, rule 8`

@export Under Order 18, rule 8(3), may I make oral submissions at the hearing of the appeal?
GIVEN `the appellate Court has ordered those oral submissions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appellate Court has ordered those oral submissions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 8(3), may I make oral submissions at the hearing of the appeal` IS
    `o 18 r 8(3) the party may make oral submissions at the hearing of the appeal` `the appellate Court has ordered those oral submissions`

§§ `Order 18, rule 9`

@export Under Order 18, rule 9(3), may the appellate Court restore my appeal for rehearing after I was absent?
GIVEN `the application is made by the absent party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application is made by you?
      `the application was filed and served in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application was filed and served in time?
      `the absent party shows good reason for the absence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you show good reason for the absence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 9(3), may the appellate Court restore my appeal for rehearing after I was absent` IS
    `o 18 r 9(3) the Court may restore the appeal for rehearing` `the application is made by the absent party` `the application was filed and served in time` `the absent party shows good reason for the absence`

§§ `Order 18, rule 12`

@export Under Order 18, rule 12(1), may I withdraw my appeal or application?
GIVEN `the appeal or application has already been heard or dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appeal or application has already been heard or dealt with?
      `the notice of withdrawal in Form 34 is filed and served on all the parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice of withdrawal in Form 34 is filed and served on all the parties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 12(1), may I withdraw my appeal or application` IS
    `o 18 r 12(1) the appellant may withdraw the appeal or the applicant may withdraw the application` `the appeal or application has already been heard or dealt with` `the notice of withdrawal in Form 34 is filed and served on all the parties`

§§ `Order 18, rule 15`

@export Under Order 18, rule 15, did I file and serve my notice of appeal against the Registrar's decision in time?
GIVEN `the party intends to appeal to a District Judge against a decision of the Registrar of the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you intend to appeal to a District Judge against a decision of the Registrar of the State Courts?
      `the notice of appeal is in Form 35 and is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice of appeal is in Form 35 and is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
      `the date the notice of appeal in Form 35 was filed and served` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of appeal in Form 35 filed and served?
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 15, did I file and serve my notice of appeal against the Registrar's decision in time` IS
    `o 18 r 15 the notice of appeal in Form 35 is filed and served in time` `the party intends to appeal to a District Judge against a decision of the Registrar of the State Courts` `the notice of appeal is in Form 35 and is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` `the date the notice of appeal in Form 35 was filed and served` `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

§§ `Order 18, rule 17`

@export Under Order 18, rule 17(1), did I file and serve my notice of appeal to the General Division in time?
GIVEN `the party intends to appeal against a decision of a District Judge or Magistrate or against a decision of a District Judge hearing an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you intend to appeal against a decision of a District Judge or Magistrate or against a decision of a District Judge hearing an appeal?
      `the notice of appeal is in Form 35 and is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice of appeal is in Form 35 and is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
      `the date the notice of appeal in Form 35 was filed and served` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of appeal in Form 35 filed and served?
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 17(1), did I file and serve my notice of appeal to the General Division in time` IS
    `o 18 r 17(1) the notice of appeal in Form 35 is filed and served in time` `the party intends to appeal against a decision of a District Judge or Magistrate or against a decision of a District Judge hearing an appeal` `the notice of appeal is in Form 35 and is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` `the date the notice of appeal in Form 35 was filed and served` `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

§§ `Order 18, rule 19`

@export Under Order 18, rule 19(1), did I apply to the District Judge or Magistrate for permission to appeal in time?
GIVEN `permission to appeal is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that permission to appeal is required?
      `the application is served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application is served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
      `the date the application was made and served` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the application made and served?
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 19(1), did I apply to the District Judge or Magistrate for permission to appeal in time` IS
    `o 18 r 19(1) the application for permission to the District Judge or Magistrate is made and served in time` `permission to appeal is required` `the application is served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` `the date the application was made and served` `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

§§ `Order 18, rule 20`

@export Under Order 18, rule 20(1), have I provided security for the respondent's costs and filed the certificate in Form 36 at the right time?
GIVEN `the appellant has provided security for the respondent's costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have provided security for the respondent's costs?
      `the certificate for security for costs in Form 36 is filed at the time of filing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate for security for costs in Form 36 is filed at the time of filing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 20(1), have I provided security for the respondent's costs and filed the certificate in Form 36 at the right time` IS
    `o 18 r 20(1) the appellant has provided security and filed the certificate in Form 36 at the time of filing` `the appellant has provided security for the respondent's costs` `the certificate for security for costs in Form 36 is filed at the time of filing`

@export Under Order 18, rule 20(5), is the security I provided on my appeal to the General Division the amount the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the kind of action appealed from` IS A `o 18 r 20(5) kind of action appealed from` @desc Which kind of action appealed from is yours?
      `amount` IS A NUMBER @desc What is amount?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 20(5), is the security I provided on my appeal to the General Division the amount the Rule requires` IS
    `o 18 r 20(5) the security is in the amount required` `the kind of action appealed from` `amount`

§§ `Order 18, rule 21`

@export Under Order 18, rule 21(5), did I file and serve my written submissions on the appeal in time?
GIVEN `the date the written submissions were filed and served` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the written submissions filed and served?
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 21(5), did I file and serve my written submissions on the appeal in time` IS
    `o 18 r 21(5) the written submissions are filed and served in time` `the date the written submissions were filed and served` `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

@export Under Order 18, rule 21(12), is my appeal deemed withdrawn because I did not file my written submissions in time?
GIVEN `the appellant fails to file and serve the written submissions within the specified time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you fail to file and serve the written submissions within the specified time?
      `the appellate Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appellate Court has otherwise ordered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 21(12), is my appeal deemed withdrawn because I did not file my written submissions in time` IS
    `o 18 r 21(12) the appeal is deemed withdrawn` `the appellant fails to file and serve the written submissions within the specified time` `the appellate Court has otherwise ordered`

§§ `Order 18, rule 27`

@export Under Order 18, rule 27(1), did I file and serve my notice of appeal to the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal in time?
GIVEN `the party intends to appeal to the appellate Court against the decision of the lower Court hearing an application or an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you intend to appeal to the appellate Court against the decision of the lower Court hearing an application or an appeal?
      `the notice of appeal is in Form 35 and is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice of appeal is in Form 35 and is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
      `the date the notice of appeal in Form 35 was filed and served` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the notice of appeal in Form 35 filed and served?
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 27(1), did I file and serve my notice of appeal to the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal in time` IS
    `o 18 r 27(1) the notice of appeal in Form 35 is filed and served in time` `the party intends to appeal to the appellate Court against the decision of the lower Court hearing an application or an appeal` `the notice of appeal is in Form 35 and is filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` `the date the notice of appeal in Form 35 was filed and served` `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

§§ `Order 18, rule 29`

@export Under Order 18, rule 29(1), did I apply to the appellate Court for permission to appeal in time?
GIVEN `permission to appeal against a decision is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that permission to appeal against a decision is required?
      `paragraph (2), (3) or (4) or a written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that paragraph (2), (3) or (4) or a written law provides otherwise?
      `the application and the documents mentioned in paragraph (7) are filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application and the documents mentioned in paragraph (7) are filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
      `the date the application was filed and served` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the application filed and served?
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 29(1), did I apply to the appellate Court for permission to appeal in time` IS
    `o 18 r 29(1) the application for permission to the appellate Court is made in time` `permission to appeal against a decision is required` `paragraph (2), (3) or (4) or a written law provides otherwise` `the application and the documents mentioned in paragraph (7) are filed and served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` `the date the application was filed and served` `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

@export Under Order 18, rule 29(7), have I filed my written submissions and bundle of authorities with my application for permission to appeal?
GIVEN `a party applies for permission under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you apply for permission under this Rule?
      `written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities are filed at the time of filing the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities are filed at the time of filing the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 29(7), have I filed my written submissions and bundle of authorities with my application for permission to appeal` IS
    `o 18 r 29(7) the documents mentioned in paragraph (7) are filed with the application` `a party applies for permission under this Rule` `written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities are filed at the time of filing the application`

@export Under Order 18, rule 29(8), did I file and serve my written submissions opposing the application for permission in time?
GIVEN `a party wishes to oppose an application for permission under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you wish to oppose an application for permission under this Rule?
      `the written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities are filed and served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities are filed and served?
      `the date the written submissions and any bundles were filed and served` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the written submissions and any bundles filed and served?
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 29(8), did I file and serve my written submissions opposing the application for permission in time` IS
    `o 18 r 29(8) the opposing party's written submissions are filed and served in time` `a party wishes to oppose an application for permission under this Rule` `the written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities are filed and served` `the date the written submissions and any bundles were filed and served` `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

§§ `Order 18, rule 30`

@export Under Order 18, rule 30(5), is the security I provided the amount the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the amount of the security` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the security?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 30(5), is the security I provided the amount the Rule requires` IS
    `o 18 r 30(5) the security is in the amount required` `the amount of the security`

§§ `Order 18, rule 33`

@export Under Order 18, rule 33(5), did I file and serve my written submissions on the appeal to the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal in time?
GIVEN `the date the written submissions were filed and served` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the written submissions filed and served?
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 33(5), did I file and serve my written submissions on the appeal to the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal in time` IS
    `o 18 r 33(5) the written submissions are filed and served in time` `the date the written submissions were filed and served` `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

§§ `Order 18, rule 35`

@export Under Order 18, rule 35(4), did I file and serve my affidavit in reply to the application in time?
GIVEN `Rule 29(15) provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that Rule 29(15) provides otherwise?
      `the party wishes to file an affidavit in reply to the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you wish to file an affidavit in reply to the application?
      `the date the affidavit in reply was filed and served` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the affidavit in reply filed and served?
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 35(4), did I file and serve my affidavit in reply to the application in time` IS
    `o 18 r 35(4) the affidavit in reply is filed and served in time` `Rule 29(15) provides otherwise` `the party wishes to file an affidavit in reply to the application` `the date the affidavit in reply was filed and served` `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

@export Under Order 18, rule 35(9), is the security I provided with my application the amount the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the amount of the security` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of the security?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 35(9), is the security I provided with my application the amount the Rule requires` IS
    `o 18 r 35(9) the security is in the amount required` `the amount of the security`

§§ `Order 18, rule 37`

@export Under Order 18, rule 37(1), did I file and serve my written submissions on the application in time?
GIVEN `another provision of these Rules or any other written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that another provision of these Rules or any other written law provides otherwise?
      `the appellate Court has otherwise directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appellate Court has otherwise directed?
      `the applicant and the opposing party file and serve written submissions (if any) and any bundle of authorities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you and the opposing party file and serve written submissions (if any) and any bundle of authorities?
      `the date the written submissions were filed and served` IS A DATE @desc On what date were the written submissions filed and served?
      `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted under Order 3, rule 3 of the Rules of Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 18, rule 37(1), did I file and serve my written submissions on the application in time` IS
    `o 18 r 37(1) the written submissions and bundles of authorities are filed and served in time` `another provision of these Rules or any other written law provides otherwise` `the appellate Court has otherwise directed` `the applicant and the opposing party file and serve written submissions (if any) and any bundle of authorities` `the date the written submissions were filed and served` `the last day for doing this, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

-- ============================================================
-- roc4: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 19 (APPEALS) -- THE SEAT LAYER (part roc4).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a party to a civil action in the Singapore courts (a claimant, a defendant, a third party or an appellant) who is appealing,
-- or is answering an appeal, or is asking the appellate Court for something in an appeal.
-- This layer phrases the rules of Order 19, already encoded in the layer-1 modules imported above, as the questions that person asks:
-- what must I file or serve, by when, how, at what cost, what may the Court order, and what follows if I do not.
-- Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question calls a layer-1 rule.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs (yes or no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list), one for each fact the person can state.
-- The records and MAYBE inputs the layer-1 modules expect are built in the wiring functions below, from those answers.
--   * TIME.  Order 19 counts its periods under Order 3, rule 3, and a Court may extend or shorten a time under Order 3, rule 4.
--     Those two rules are not in this part.  Where a question turns on a period, you give "your last day for this step" (the last day after the Order 3 count and any change by the Court);
--     the question compares the date you did the step with it.  That one answer stands for both seams (`o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` and `o 3 r 4 the last day as extended or shortened`):
--     the rule uses the changed day when there is one and the counted day when there is not, so passing the effective day as the counted day and "no change" is the same comparison.
--   * FEES.  The fee for pages in excess of a page limit is in the Fourth Schedule (part roc12).  You give the fee that Schedule sets for the document, in dollars.
--   * BORROWED FACTS.  Sections of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act and of the Medical Registration Act are not among the sources; each is asked as a yes or no fact named for the section.
--   * SECURITY FOR COSTS in the Court of Appeal, the Appellate Division and applications, and the costs the Court orders, are amounts you give.  The Order itself fixes the amount of the security.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers Order 19 itself gives: JUST FALSE is the text's own "no" (a condition or a period the text fixes in its own words, a flat negative, a definition that "means").
-- NOTHING means Order 19 does not answer on these facts: it is silent, it lists without closing the list, it limits a grant in its own wording and the case falls outside,
-- or it points to an order, direction, power or written law that is not among the sources.  Never read NOTHING as no.
-- See NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (roc4)".
--
-- There is no seat for an official.  Where a provision addresses only the Court, the Registrar or the Registry, its rule is in layer 1,
-- and the person meets it here only as what it means for them: what the Court may order against them or in their favour, what they must be given, and by when.
--
-- QUESTION NAMES begin "Under Order 19, rule N," so that no two parts of the Rules can share a name.  Wiring functions begin "o 19 seat".

DECLARE `o 19 seat what my matter is` IS ONE OF
    `o 19 seat an appeal against a judgment`
    `o 19 seat an appeal from a tribunal`
    `o 19 seat an application to the appellate Court relating to an appeal`
    `o 19 seat an appeal against a Disciplinary Tribunal decision under the Medical Registration Act`
    `o 19 seat something else`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN court IS A `Court level`
      who IS A `Decision maker`
      what IS A `o 19 r 3 kind of decision`
      began IS A `Document kind`
      damages IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against`
`o 19 seat my judgment` MEANS
    `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF court, who, what, began, damages -- input mapping

GIVEN kind IS A `o 19 seat what my matter is`
      court IS A `Court level`
      who IS A `Decision maker`
      what IS A `o 19 r 3 kind of decision`
      began IS A `Document kind`
      damages IS A BOOLEAN
      `to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `pursuant to a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `relating to an appeal in paragraphs (a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `o 19 r 1 matter`
`o 19 seat my matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `o 19 seat an appeal against a judgment` THEN `o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` (`o 19 seat my judgment` court who what began damages) -- input mapping
    WHEN `o 19 seat an appeal from a tribunal` THEN `o 19 r 1 an appeal from a tribunal` `to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `pursuant to a written law` -- input mapping
    WHEN `o 19 seat an application to the appellate Court relating to an appeal` THEN `o 19 r 1 an application to the appellate Court` `relating to an appeal in paragraphs (a) to (d)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `o 19 seat an appeal against a Disciplinary Tribunal decision under the Medical Registration Act` THEN `o 19 r 1 an appeal against an order or decision of a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act` -- input mapping
    WHEN `o 19 seat something else` THEN `o 19 r 1 any other matter` -- input mapping

GIVEN from IS A `Court level`
      to IS A `Court level`
      tribunal IS A BOOLEAN
      mra IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `o 19 r 2 route of appeal`
`o 19 seat my route of appeal` MEANS
    `o 19 r 2 route of appeal` OF from, to, tribunal, mra -- input mapping

-- A date from an answer of yes or no and a date: the date counts only if the answer is yes.
GIVEN yes IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 19 seat the date if it happened` MEANS
    IF yes THEN JUST day ELSE NOTHING -- input mapping

-- An amount that is a cost the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent: 0 means none ordered.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`o 19 seat the costs ordered if any` MEANS
    IF amount GREATER THAN 0 THEN JUST amount ELSE NOTHING -- input mapping

-- A moment from a date, an hour (0 to 23) and a minute (0 to 59).
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      hour IS A NUMBER
      minute IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Moment
`o 19 seat the moment` MEANS
    Moment OF day, ((hour TIMES 60) PLUS minute) -- input mapping

GIVEN yes IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
      hour IS A NUMBER
      minute IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE Moment
`o 19 seat the moment if it happened` MEANS
    IF yes THEN JUST (`o 19 seat the moment` day hour minute) ELSE NOTHING -- input mapping

§ `Order 19 -- Appeals -- my questions`

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 19, Division 1 -- General (rules 1 to 12)`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- application of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 1, does Order 19 apply to my matter?
GIVEN `what my matter is` IS A `o 19 seat what my matter is` @desc What are you asking about: an appeal against a judgment, an appeal from a tribunal, an application to the appellate Court relating to an appeal, an appeal against a Disciplinary Tribunal decision under the Medical Registration Act, or something else?
      `the court that gave the judgment` IS A `Court level` @desc Which court gave the judgment you are appealing against?
      `who gave the judgment` IS A `Decision maker` @desc Who gave the judgment: the court itself, a Judge, a District Judge, a Magistrate or the Registrar?
      `what the judgment was given in` IS A `o 19 r 3 kind of decision` @desc What kind of decision is it: a trial, a case decided at trial in the absence of a party, after damages were assessed or accounts taken, a committal order for contempt, a prerogative order, an appeal against one of those, or any other decision?
      `how my proceedings began` IS A `Document kind` @desc How did the proceedings begin: with an originating claim or an originating application (or another document)?
      `a District Judge assessed damages or took accounts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the damages assessed or the accounts taken by a District Judge?
      `the tribunal appeal goes to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your matter is an appeal from a tribunal, does it go to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal?
      `the tribunal appeal is under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your matter is an appeal from a tribunal, is it brought under a written law?
      `my application relates to an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your matter is an application, does it relate to an appeal against a judgment, an appeal from a tribunal, or an appeal against a Disciplinary Tribunal decision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 1, does Order 19 apply to my matter` IS
    `o 19 r 1 this Order applies` (`o 19 seat my matter` `what my matter is` `the court that gave the judgment` `who gave the judgment` `what the judgment was given in` `how my proceedings began` `a District Judge assessed damages or took accounts` `the tribunal appeal goes to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `the tribunal appeal is under a written law` `my application relates to an appeal`)


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- how this Order is divided`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 2, which Division of Order 19 deals with my appeal?
GIVEN `the court I am appealing from` IS A `Court level` @desc From which court are you appealing?
      `the court I am appealing to` IS A `Court level` @desc To which court are you appealing?
      `my appeal is from a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal from a tribunal (and not from a court)?
      `my appeal is from a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against a decision or order of a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act?
GIVETH A `o 19 r 2 Division`
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 2, which Division of Order 19 deals with my appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 2 the Division that concerns the appeal` (`o 19 seat my route of appeal` `the court I am appealing from` `the court I am appealing to` `my appeal is from a tribunal` `my appeal is from a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 2(1), does a written law on the right to appeal or on permission to appeal take priority over this Order?
GIVEN `a written law on the right to appeal or on permission to appeal applies to my case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law (an Act or subsidiary legislation, not these Rules) deal with the right to appeal in your case, or with a requirement to apply for permission to appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 2(1), does a written law on the right to appeal or on permission to appeal take priority over this Order` IS
    `o 19 r 2(1) this Order yields to a written law on the right to appeal or on permission to appeal` `a written law on the right to appeal or on permission to appeal applies to my case`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 3 -- meanings of words in this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 3, is the decision I am appealing against a "judgment" for the purposes of Order 19?
GIVEN `it was given by the lower Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the decision given by the lower Court (the court you are appealing from)?
      `what the judgment was given in` IS A `o 19 r 3 kind of decision` @desc What kind of decision is it: a trial, a case decided at trial in the absence of a party, after damages were assessed or accounts taken, a committal order for contempt, a prerogative order, an appeal against one of those, or any other decision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 3, is the decision I am appealing against a "judgment" for the purposes of Order 19` IS
    `o 19 r 3 a decision is a judgment` `it was given by the lower Court` `what the judgment was given in`

@export Under Order 19, rule 3, is this document part of the record of appeal?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `o 19 r 3 document` @desc Which document are you asking about?
      `it is relevant to the matter decided and the nature of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it relevant to the matter decided and to the nature of the appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 3, is this document part of the record of appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of appeal` `the document` `it is relevant to the matter decided and the nature of the appeal`

@export Under Order 19, rule 3, is this document part of a core bundle of documents?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `o 19 r 3 document` @desc Which document are you asking about?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 3, is this document part of a core bundle of documents` IS
    `o 19 r 3 a document is part of a core bundle of documents` `the document`

@export Under Order 19, rule 3, is this document part of the record of proceedings?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `o 19 r 3 document` @desc Which document are you asking about?
      `the appeal is from the General Division, the District Court or the Magistrate's Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal from the General Division, the District Court or the Magistrate's Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 3, is this document part of the record of proceedings` IS
    `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of proceedings` `the document` `the appeal is from the General Division, the District Court or the Magistrate's Court`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 4 -- when time for filing the notice of appeal starts to run`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Only for an appeal from the District Court or the Magistrate's Court after a trial: the form asks "Was there a trial?" before showing this group.

@export Under Order 19, rule 4, from what date does the time for filing my notice of appeal run?
GIVEN `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the lower Court hear and determine all the matters in the trial other than costs?
      `the lower Court has heard and determined the issue of costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs?
      `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` IS A DATE @desc If it has, on what date? (Give any date if it has not.)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
      `a written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law (not these Rules) provide otherwise for when time starts to run?
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 4, from what date does the time for filing my notice of appeal run` IS
    `o 19 r 4 the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` (`o 19 seat the date if it happened` `the lower Court has heard and determined the issue of costs` `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs`) `the date I am asking about` `a written law provides otherwise` `the Court otherwise orders`

@export Under Order 19, rule 4(1), has the time for filing my notice of appeal started to run?
GIVEN `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the lower Court hear and determine all the matters in the trial other than costs?
      `the lower Court has heard and determined the issue of costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs?
      `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` IS A DATE @desc If it has, on what date? (Give any date if it has not.)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
      `a written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law (not these Rules) provide otherwise for when time starts to run?
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 4(1), has the time for filing my notice of appeal started to run` IS
    `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing has started to run` `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` (`o 19 seat the date if it happened` `the lower Court has heard and determined the issue of costs` `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs`) `the date I am asking about` `a written law provides otherwise` `the Court otherwise orders`

@export Under Order 19, rule 4(1), is it too early for the time for filing my notice of appeal to run?
GIVEN `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the lower Court hear and determine all the matters in the trial other than costs?
      `the lower Court has heard and determined the issue of costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs?
      `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` IS A DATE @desc If it has, on what date? (Give any date if it has not.)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
      `a written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law (not these Rules) provide otherwise for when time starts to run?
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 4(1), is it too early for the time for filing my notice of appeal to run` IS
    `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing cannot yet start to run` `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the trial` (`o 19 seat the date if it happened` `the lower Court has heard and determined the issue of costs` `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs`) `the date I am asking about` `a written law provides otherwise` `the Court otherwise orders`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 5 -- intervening in an appeal`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 5(1), may I apply to intervene in the appeal?
GIVEN `I am a party in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you already a party in the appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 5(1), may I apply to intervene in the appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 5(1) a person may apply to intervene in the appeal with the permission of the appellate Court` `I am a party in the appeal`

@export Under Order 19, rule 5(2), have I filed and served my application to intervene as required?
GIVEN `I filed my application for permission to intervene` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you filed your application for permission to intervene?
      `I filed the supporting affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you filed the supporting affidavit?
      `I served both on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you served both on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 5(2), have I filed and served my application to intervene as required` IS
    `o 19 r 5(2) the application and the supporting affidavit are filed and served as required` `I filed my application for permission to intervene` `I filed the supporting affidavit` `I served both on all parties who have an interest in the appeal`

@export Under Order 19, rule 5(3), does my affidavit have to set out my interest in the appeal?
GIVEN `my affidavit sets out my interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your supporting affidavit set out your interest in the appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 5(3), does my affidavit have to set out my interest in the appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 5(3) the supporting affidavit sets out the applicant's interest` `my affidavit sets out my interest in the appeal`

@export Under Order 19, rule 5(4), may the Court make my permission to intervene subject to conditions?
GIVEN `the appellate Court grants me permission to intervene` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appellate Court granted you permission to intervene?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 5(4), may the Court make my permission to intervene subject to conditions` IS
    `o 19 r 5(4) the appellate Court may impose conditions on the permission to intervene` `the appellate Court grants me permission to intervene`

@export Under Order 19, rule 5(4), may the Court order me, as an intervener, to give security for costs?
GIVEN `the appellate Court grants me permission to intervene` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appellate Court granted you permission to intervene?
      `the condition orders me to give security for costs to any or all of the parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the condition order you to provide security for costs to any or all of the parties in the appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 5(4), may the Court order me, as an intervener, to give security for costs` IS
    `o 19 r 5(4) the condition of security for costs may be imposed on an intervening party` `the appellate Court grants me permission to intervene` `the condition orders me to give security for costs to any or all of the parties`


