DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 14(2), may the General Division extend the time for my notice of appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 14(2) the General Division may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal` `I apply`

@export Under Order 19, rule 14(2), may the lower Court extend the time for my notice of appeal?
GIVEN `I apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for the extension?
      `I apply before the time expires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply before the time expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 14(2), may the lower Court extend the time for my notice of appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 14(2) the lower Court may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal` `I apply` `I apply before the time expires`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 15 -- permission to appeal`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Only where permission to appeal is required: the form asks "Do you need permission to appeal?" before showing this group.

@export Under Order 19, rule 15(1), within how many days must I apply to the lower Court for permission to appeal?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 15(1), within how many days must I apply to the lower Court for permission to appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 15(1) the period for the application for permission to the lower Court`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 19, rule 15(1), have I applied to the lower Court for permission to appeal as required?
GIVEN `permission to appeal is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is permission to appeal required?
      `I made the application to the lower Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the application to the lower Court (and not to another court)?
      `I served the application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve the application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
      `the date I made the application to the lower Court` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the application to the lower Court?
      `the date I served the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the application?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the Rules give you for this step? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 directs, and if the Court extended or shortened the time under Order 3, rule 4, give the changed last day.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 15(1), have I applied to the lower Court for permission to appeal as required` IS
    `o 19 r 15(1) the application for permission to the lower Court is made and served as required` `permission to appeal is required` `I made the application to the lower Court` `I served the application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` `the date I made the application to the lower Court` `the date I served the application` `my last day` NOTHING

@export Under Order 19, rule 15(2), within how many days must I apply to the General Division for permission to appeal?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 15(2), within how many days must I apply to the General Division for permission to appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 15(2) the period for the application for permission to the General Division`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 19, rule 15(2), have I applied to the General Division for permission to appeal as required?
GIVEN `the lower Court did not grant me permission to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the lower Court refuse to grant you permission to appeal?
      `I served the application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve the application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
      `the date I made the application to the General Division` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the application to the General Division?
      `the date I served the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the application?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the Rules give you for this step? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 directs, and if the Court extended or shortened the time under Order 3, rule 4, give the changed last day.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 15(2), have I applied to the General Division for permission to appeal as required` IS
    `o 19 r 15(2) the application for permission to the General Division is made and served as required` `the lower Court did not grant me permission to appeal` `I served the application on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` `the date I made the application to the General Division` `the date I served the application` `my last day` NOTHING

@export Under Order 19, rule 15(3), within how many days must I file and serve my notice of appeal once permission is granted?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 15(3), within how many days must I file and serve my notice of appeal once permission is granted` IS
    `o 19 r 15(3) the period for the notice of appeal after permission is granted`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 19, rule 15(3), once permission is granted, have I filed and served my notice of appeal as required?
GIVEN `permission to appeal is granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has permission to appeal been granted?
      `my notice of appeal is in Form 35` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your notice of appeal in Form 35?
      `I served it on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve it on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
      `the date I filed the notice of appeal` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the notice of appeal?
      `the date I served the notice of appeal` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the notice of appeal?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the Rules give you for this step? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 directs, and if the Court extended or shortened the time under Order 3, rule 4, give the changed last day.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 15(3), once permission is granted, have I filed and served my notice of appeal as required` IS
    `o 19 r 15(3) the notice of appeal after permission is filed and served as required` `permission to appeal is granted` `my notice of appeal is in Form 35` `I served it on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` `the date I filed the notice of appeal` `the date I served the notice of appeal` `my last day` NOTHING

@export Under Order 19, rule 15(4), may the General Division extend the time for my application for permission to appeal?
GIVEN `I apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for the extension?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 15(4), may the General Division extend the time for my application for permission to appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 15(4) the General Division may extend the time for filing and serving an application for permission to appeal` `I apply`

@export Under Order 19, rule 15(4), may the lower Court extend the time for my application for permission to appeal?
GIVEN `I apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for the extension?
      `I apply before the time expires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply before the time expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 15(4), may the lower Court extend the time for my application for permission to appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 15(4) the lower Court may extend the time for filing and serving an application for permission to appeal` `I apply` `I apply before the time expires`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 16 -- security for costs`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 16(1), have I given security for costs and filed the certificate as required?
GIVEN `I have provided security for the respondent's costs of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided security for the respondent's costs of the appeal?
      `I have filed the certificate for security for costs in Form 36` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you filed the certificate for security for costs in Form 36?
      `I did both when I filed the notice of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do both at the time you filed the notice of appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 16(1), have I given security for costs and filed the certificate as required` IS
    `o 19 r 16(1) the appellant has provided security for costs and filed the certificate as required` `I have provided security for the respondent's costs of the appeal` `I have filed the certificate for security for costs in Form 36` `I did both when I filed the notice of appeal`

@export Under Order 19, rule 16(2), need all the appellants give only one set of security?
GIVEN `there is more than one appellant in the same appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there more than one appellant in the same appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 16(2), need all the appellants give only one set of security` IS
    `o 19 r 16(2) the appellants need to provide only one set of security for the appeal` `there is more than one appellant in the same appeal`

@export Under Order 19, rule 16(3), must I give security for each respondent or each set of respondents?
GIVEN `there is more than one respondent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there more than one respondent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 16(3), must I give security for each respondent or each set of respondents` IS
    `o 19 r 16(3) the appellant must provide security for each respondent or each set of respondents` `there is more than one respondent`

@export Under Order 19, rule 16(3), how many sets of security must I give?
GIVEN `the number of respondents` IS A NUMBER @desc How many respondents are there? Count each respondent, even where two or more are represented by the same firm of solicitors.
      `the number of sets of respondents, where respondents represented by the same firm of solicitors are one set` IS A NUMBER @desc How many sets of respondents are there, counting respondents represented by the same firm of solicitors as one set?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 16(3), how many sets of security must I give` IS
    `o 19 r 16(3) the number of sets of security the appellant must provide` `the number of respondents` `the number of sets of respondents, where respondents represented by the same firm of solicitors are one set`

@export Under Order 19, rule 16(4), is my security in a form the Rules allow?
GIVEN `the form of my security` IS A `o 19 r 16(4) form of security` @desc In what form is your security: a solicitor's undertaking in Form 37, a deposit in the Registry or with the Accountant-General, or any other form?
      `the undertaking is filed and served on the respondent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a solicitor's undertaking, is it filed and served on the respondent?
      `the form is acceptable to the parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is another form, is it acceptable to the parties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 16(4), is my security in a form the Rules allow` IS
    `o 19 r 16(4) the security is in a form the text allows` `the form of my security` `the undertaking is filed and served on the respondent` `the form is acceptable to the parties`

@export Under Order 19, rule 16(5), how much security must I give?
GIVEN `the court whose judgment I am appealing against` IS A `Court level` @desc Which court gave the judgment you are appealing against: the Magistrate's Court or the District Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 16(5), how much security must I give` IS
    `o 19 r 16(5) the amount of security the appellant must provide` `the court whose judgment I am appealing against`

@export Under Order 19, rule 16(5), is the security I gave the right amount?
GIVEN `the court whose judgment I am appealing against` IS A `Court level` @desc Which court gave the judgment you are appealing against: the Magistrate's Court or the District Court?
      `the amount of security I provided` IS A NUMBER @desc How much security did you provide, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 16(5), is the security I gave the right amount` IS
    `o 19 r 16(5) the security is in the amount the text requires` `the court whose judgment I am appealing against` `the amount of security I provided`

@export Under Order 19, rule 16(6), may I apply to vary or waive the amount of security?
GIVEN `I am a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 16(6), may I apply to vary or waive the amount of security` IS
    `o 19 r 16(6) a party may apply to the appellate Court to vary or waive the amount of security` `I am a party`

@export Under Order 19, rule 16(7), may the Court order me to give further security for costs?
GIVEN `the order is for further security for costs to be given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order one for further security for costs to be given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 16(7), may the Court order me to give further security for costs` IS
    `o 19 r 16(7) the appellate Court may order further security for costs to be given` `the order is for further security for costs to be given`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(3), within how many weeks must written grounds of decision be issued before the appellant must apply to proceed?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(3), within how many weeks must written grounds of decision be issued before the appellant must apply to proceed` IS
    `o 19 r 17(3) the period for written grounds of decision`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(4), within how many days must the appellant file and serve the appellant's documents?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(4), within how many days must the appellant file and serve the appellant's documents` IS
    `o 19 r 17(4) the period for the appellant's documents`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(8), within how many days must the respondent file and serve the respondent's documents?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(8), within how many days must the respondent file and serve the respondent's documents` IS
    `o 19 r 17(8) the period for the respondent's documents`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(10), within how many days must the appellant file and serve the Reply and the other reply documents?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(10), within how many days must the appellant file and serve the Reply and the other reply documents` IS
    `o 19 r 17(10) the period for the appellant's reply documents`'s `period length`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 17 -- documents to be filed`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(1), must the lower Court issue its written grounds of decision?
GIVEN `the notice of appeal has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the notice of appeal been filed?
      `the lower Court has already issued its written grounds of decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the lower Court already issued its written grounds of decision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(1), must the lower Court issue its written grounds of decision` IS
    `o 19 r 17(1) the lower Court must issue its written grounds of decision` `the notice of appeal has been filed` `the lower Court has already issued its written grounds of decision`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(2), will the Registry notify me that the record of proceedings is ready for collection?
GIVEN `the record of proceedings is ready for collection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the record of proceedings ready for collection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(2), will the Registry notify me that the record of proceedings is ready for collection` IS
    `o 19 r 17(2) the Registry must notify the parties that the record of proceedings is ready for collection` `the record of proceedings is ready for collection`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(3), have 12 weeks passed after filing the notice of appeal with no written grounds of decision?
GIVEN `the written grounds of decision have been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the written grounds of decision been issued?
      `the date the written grounds of decision were issued` IS A DATE @desc If they have been issued, on what date? (Give any date if they have not.)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the 12 weeks after the date of filing the notice of appeal, counted as Order 3, rule 3 directs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(3), have 12 weeks passed after filing the notice of appeal with no written grounds of decision` IS
    `o 19 r 17(3) no written grounds of decision are issued within 12 weeks` (`o 19 seat the date if it happened` `the written grounds of decision have been issued` `the date the written grounds of decision were issued`) `the date I am asking about` `my last day`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(3)(a), must I, as appellant, apply in writing to the Registrar to proceed with the appeal?
GIVEN `no written grounds of decision are issued within 12 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have 12 weeks passed after filing the notice of appeal with no written grounds of decision issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(3)(a), must I, as appellant, apply in writing to the Registrar to proceed with the appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 17(3)(a) the appellant must apply in writing to the Registrar to proceed with the appeal and for a copy of the record of proceedings` `no written grounds of decision are issued within 12 weeks`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(3)(b), may the respondent apply to proceed or give me 14 days' written notice of intention to strike out my appeal?
GIVEN `no written grounds of decision are issued within 12 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have 12 weeks passed after filing the notice of appeal with no written grounds of decision issued?
      `the appellant has failed to apply as sub-paragraph (a) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appellant failed to apply in writing to the Registrar to proceed with the appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(3)(b), may the respondent apply to proceed or give me 14 days' written notice of intention to strike out my appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 17(3)(b) the respondent may apply in writing to the Registrar to proceed or give 14 days' written notice of intention to strike out the appeal` `no written grounds of decision are issued within 12 weeks` `the appellant has failed to apply as sub-paragraph (a) requires`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(3)(c), may the respondent apply to strike out my appeal?
GIVEN `the respondent has given the appellant 14 days' written notice of intention to strike out the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the respondent given the appellant 14 days' written notice of intention to strike out the appeal?
      `the 14 days' notice period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the 14 days' notice period expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(3)(c), may the respondent apply to strike out my appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 17(3)(c) the respondent may apply to strike out the appeal` `the respondent has given the appellant 14 days' written notice of intention to strike out the appeal` `the 14 days' notice period has expired`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(4), did I file and serve this document of the appellant's in time?
GIVEN `which document` IS A `o 19 r 17(4) document` @desc Which of the appellant's documents are you asking about: the record of appeal, the appellant's Case, the appellant's core bundle of documents or the appellant's bundle of authorities?
      `the written judgment or grounds of decision and the extracted order of the lower Court are in a separate volume` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is the core bundle: are the written judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court (if any) and the extracted order in a separate volume?
      `the date I filed the document` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the document?
      `the date I served the document` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the document?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the Rules give you for this step? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 directs, and if the Court extended or shortened the time under Order 3, rule 4, give the changed last day.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(4), did I file and serve this document of the appellant's in time` IS
    `o 19 r 17(4) the appellant's document is filed and served in time` `which document` `the written judgment or grounds of decision and the extracted order of the lower Court are in a separate volume` `the date I filed the document` `the date I served the document` `my last day` NOTHING

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(5), is my appeal deemed withdrawn?
GIVEN `I failed to file and serve the record of appeal, the core bundle of documents or the appellant's Case within the specified time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to file and serve the record of appeal, the core bundle of documents or the appellant's Case within the specified time?
      `the appellate Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(5), is my appeal deemed withdrawn` IS
    `o 19 r 17(5) the appeal is deemed withdrawn` `I failed to file and serve the record of appeal, the core bundle of documents or the appellant's Case within the specified time` `the appellate Court otherwise orders`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(6), must the security for costs be paid out and the undertaking discharged where my appeal is deemed withdrawn?
GIVEN `my appeal is deemed withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal deemed withdrawn?
      `all the parties to the appeal consent to the payment of the security for costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the parties to the appeal consent to the payment of the security for costs?
      `the document signifying the consent, signed by the parties, is filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the document signifying the consent, signed by the parties, been filed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(6), must the security for costs be paid out and the undertaking discharged where my appeal is deemed withdrawn` IS
    `o 19 r 17(6) the security for costs must be paid and the solicitor's undertaking is discharged` `my appeal is deemed withdrawn` `all the parties to the appeal consent to the payment of the security for costs` `the document signifying the consent, signed by the parties, is filed`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(7)(a), may I request directions in writing on outstanding issues after my appeal is deemed withdrawn?
GIVEN `my appeal is deemed withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal deemed withdrawn?
      `there are outstanding issues as to costs or other matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there outstanding issues as to costs or other matters?
      `the date I made the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the request?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the Rules give you for this step? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 directs, and if the Court extended or shortened the time under Order 3, rule 4, give the changed last day.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(7)(a), may I request directions in writing on outstanding issues after my appeal is deemed withdrawn` IS
    `o 19 r 17(7)(a) the appellant or a party may request in writing to the General Division for directions on those issues` `my appeal is deemed withdrawn` `there are outstanding issues as to costs or other matters` `the date I made the request` `my last day` NOTHING

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(7)(b), may I make oral arguments in that request?
GIVEN `the appellate Court otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court directed otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(7)(b), may I make oral arguments in that request` IS
    `o 19 r 17(7)(b) oral arguments may be made in the request` `the appellate Court otherwise directs`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(7)(c), may the Registrar give directions on written submissions for that request?
GIVEN `the Registrar has received a request under sub-paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Registrar received a request under sub-paragraph (a)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(7)(c), may the Registrar give directions on written submissions for that request` IS
    `o 19 r 17(7)(c) the Registrar of the Supreme Court may give directions on the making of written submissions for the request` `the Registrar has received a request under sub-paragraph (a)`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(8), did the respondent file and serve this document in time?
GIVEN `which document` IS A `o 19 r 17(8) document` @desc Which of the respondent's documents are you asking about: the respondent's Case, the respondent's core bundle of documents or the respondent's bundle of authorities?
      `a core bundle of documents is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is the core bundle: is a core bundle of documents necessary?
      `the date I filed the document` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the document?
      `the date I served the document` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the document?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the Rules give you for this step? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 directs, and if the Court extended or shortened the time under Order 3, rule 4, give the changed last day.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(8), did the respondent file and serve this document in time` IS
    `o 19 r 17(8) the respondent's document is filed and served in time` `which document` `a core bundle of documents is necessary` `the date I filed the document` `the date I served the document` `my last day` NOTHING

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(9), is the respondent barred from making submissions at the hearing?
GIVEN `the respondent failed to file and serve the respondent's Case within the specified time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the respondent fail to file and serve the respondent's Case within the specified time?
      `the appellate Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(9), is the respondent barred from making submissions at the hearing` IS
    `o 19 r 17(9) the respondent is barred from making submissions at the hearing of the appeal` `the respondent failed to file and serve the respondent's Case within the specified time` `the appellate Court otherwise orders`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(10), did the appellant file and serve this reply document in time?
GIVEN `which document` IS A `o 19 r 17(10) document` @desc Which document are you asking about: the appellant's Reply, the second core bundle or the appellant's second bundle of authorities?
      `the document is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there such a document: is there a Reply, is the second core bundle necessary, or is there a second bundle of authorities?
      `the date I filed the document` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the document?
      `the date I served the document` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the document?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the Rules give you for this step? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 directs, and if the Court extended or shortened the time under Order 3, rule 4, give the changed last day.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(10), did the appellant file and serve this reply document in time` IS
    `o 19 r 17(10) the appellant's reply document is filed and served in time` `which document` `the document is required` `the date I filed the document` `the date I served the document` `my last day` NOTHING

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(11), may all the appellants join in one Case and one Reply?
GIVEN `there is more than one appellant in an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there more than one appellant in the appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(11), may all the appellants join in one Case and one Reply` IS
    `o 19 r 17(11) all the appellants may join in one appellants' Case and in one appellants' Reply` `there is more than one appellant in an appeal`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(12), may all the respondents join in one Case?
GIVEN `there is more than one respondent in an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there more than one respondent in the appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(12), may all the respondents join in one Case` IS
    `o 19 r 17(12) all the respondents may join in one respondents' Case` `there is more than one respondent in an appeal`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(13), must I file a separate Case if my interest in the appeal is passive?
GIVEN `my interest in the appeal is passive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your interest in the appeal passive (for example, as a stakeholder, a trustee or an executor)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(13), must I file a separate Case if my interest in the appeal is passive` IS
    `o 19 r 17(13) a party with a passive interest is required to file a separate Case` `my interest in the appeal is passive`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(13), have I ensured that my passive position is explained in one of the Cases?
GIVEN `my interest in the appeal is passive` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your interest in the appeal passive (for example, as a stakeholder, a trustee or an executor)?
      `my position is explained in one of the Cases filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your position explained in one of the Cases filed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(13), have I ensured that my passive position is explained in one of the Cases` IS
    `o 19 r 17(13) the passive party has ensured that its position is explained in one of the Cases` `my interest in the appeal is passive` `my position is explained in one of the Cases filed`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(14), may the appellant and the respondent seek directions to file a joint Case?
GIVEN `there are special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there special circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(14), may the appellant and the respondent seek directions to file a joint Case` IS
    `o 19 r 17(14) the appellant and the respondent may seek directions from the General Division to file a joint Case` `there are special circumstances`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(15), must we try to agree on a single Case for each party and on the timelines?
GIVEN `the appeals are related appeals to be heard together` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there 2 or more  appeals to be heard together?
      `we have tried to agree on filing a single Case for each party and on the timelines` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties tried to agree on filing a single Case for each party and on the timelines?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(15), must we try to agree on a single Case for each party and on the timelines` IS
    `o 19 r 17(15) the parties have tried to agree on a single Case for each party and on the timelines` `the appeals are related appeals to be heard together` `we have tried to agree on filing a single Case for each party and on the timelines`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(16), where we cannot agree, must we request a case conference or seek directions?
GIVEN `we are unable to agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the parties unable to agree on a single Case for each party and the timelines?
      `we have requested a case conference or sought directions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties requested in writing a case conference before the Court, or sought directions from it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(16), where we cannot agree, must we request a case conference or seek directions` IS
    `o 19 r 17(16) the parties have requested a case conference or sought directions` `we are unable to agree` `we have requested a case conference or sought directions`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(17), where we have agreed, must we tell the Registrar the timelines and seek approval?
GIVEN `we have agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties agreed on a single Case for each party and the timelines?
      `we have informed the Registrar in writing of the timelines and sought the Court's approval` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties informed the Registrar in writing of the timelines agreed, and sought the Court's approval of them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(17), where we have agreed, must we tell the Registrar the timelines and seek approval` IS
    `o 19 r 17(17) the parties have informed the Registrar of the agreed timelines and sought approval` `we have agreed` `we have informed the Registrar in writing of the timelines and sought the Court's approval`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(18), must we file a joint record of appeal?
GIVEN `there are 2 or more appeals arising from the same judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there 2 or more appeals arising from the same judgment?
      `we have filed a joint record of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the parties filed a joint record of appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(18), must we file a joint record of appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 17(18) the parties have filed a joint record of appeal` `there are 2 or more appeals arising from the same judgment` `we have filed a joint record of appeal`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(19), may I file a document other than those the Rule sets out?
GIVEN `the appellate Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(19), may I file a document other than those the Rule sets out` IS
    `o 19 r 17(19) a document other than those set out in this Rule may be filed` `the appellate Court otherwise orders`

@export Under Order 19, rule 17(20), may I file written submissions or skeletal arguments before or at the appeal?
GIVEN `the appellate Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 17(20), may I file written submissions or skeletal arguments before or at the appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 17(20) written submissions or skeletal arguments may be filed before or at the appeal` `the appellate Court otherwise orders`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 18 -- appellant's Case, respondent's Case and appellant's Reply`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 18(1), does my Case as appellant contain what it must contain?
GIVEN `my Case has a succinct summary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain a succinct summary of the facts, the decision of the lower Court, the contentions to be made at the appeal and the orders sought?
      `my Case has detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues, including the relevant authorities, highlighting any new points not raised in the lower Court?
      `my Case has references in the right-hand margin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case have references in the right-hand margin to the relevant pages in the record of appeal and your core bundle of documents?
      `my Case has submissions on the appropriate costs orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain submissions on the appropriate costs orders to be made on appeal?
      `my Case has submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements that should be awarded in respect of all parties to the appeal?
      `my Case has the name and signature of my solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case carry the name and signature of your solicitor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 18(1), does my Case as appellant contain what it must contain` IS
    `o 19 r 18(1) the appellant's Case contains what it must contain` (`o 19 r 18(1) the appellant's Case` `my Case has a succinct summary` `my Case has detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues` `my Case has references in the right-hand margin` `my Case has submissions on the appropriate costs orders` `my Case has submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements` `my Case has the name and signature of my solicitor`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 18(2), does my Case as respondent contain what it must contain?
GIVEN `the respondent's Case has a succinct summary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain a succinct summary of the contentions to be made at the appeal and the orders sought?
      `the respondent's Case has detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues, including the relevant authorities, highlighting any new points not raised in the lower Court?
      `the respondent's Case has references in the right-hand margin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case have references in the right-hand margin to the relevant pages in the record of appeal and your core bundle of documents (if any)?
      `I intend to submit that the lower Court's decision should be varied or affirmed on other grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you intend to submit that the lower Court's decision should be varied (where you have not appealed) or affirmed on grounds other than those the lower Court relied on?
      `the Case sets out those submissions and the reasons for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does your Case state those submissions and the reasons for them?
      `the respondent's Case has submissions on the appropriate costs orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain submissions on the appropriate costs orders to be made on appeal?
      `the respondent's Case has submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements that should be awarded in respect of all parties to the appeal?
      `the respondent's Case has the name and signature of the respondent's solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case carry the name and signature of your solicitor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 18(2), does my Case as respondent contain what it must contain` IS
    `o 19 r 18(2) the respondent's Case contains what it must contain` (`o 19 r 18(2) the respondent's Case` `the respondent's Case has a succinct summary` `the respondent's Case has detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues` `the respondent's Case has references in the right-hand margin` `I intend to submit that the lower Court's decision should be varied or affirmed on other grounds` `the Case sets out those submissions and the reasons for them` `the respondent's Case has submissions on the appropriate costs orders` `the respondent's Case has submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements` `the respondent's Case has the name and signature of the respondent's solicitor`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 18(3), am I barred from making the submissions in paragraph (2)(d)?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with the requirements in paragraph (2)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with the requirements in paragraph (2)(d) (stating that you will submit the decision should be varied or affirmed on other grounds, and your reasons)?
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 18(3), am I barred from making the submissions in paragraph (2)(d)` IS
    `o 19 r 18(3) the respondent is barred from making the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` `I failed to comply with the requirements in paragraph (2)(d)` `the Court otherwise orders`

@export Under Order 19, rule 18(4), does my Reply as appellant contain what it must contain?
GIVEN `my Reply has detailed submissions in reply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Reply contain your detailed submissions in reply to the respondent's submissions?
      `my Reply has references in the right-hand margin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Reply have references in the right-hand margin to the relevant pages in the record of appeal and the core bundles?
      `my Reply has the name and signature of my solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Reply carry the name and signature of your solicitor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 18(4), does my Reply as appellant contain what it must contain` IS
    `o 19 r 18(4) the appellant's Reply contains what it must contain` (`o 19 r 18(4) the appellant's Reply` `my Reply has detailed submissions in reply` `my Reply has references in the right-hand margin` `my Reply has the name and signature of my solicitor`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 18(5), does my Case or Reply contain everything I intend to put forward?
GIVEN `it contains everything that I intend to put forward and is prepared on the basis that there will be no need to supplement or to elaborate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain everything you intend to put forward at the appeal, and is it prepared on the basis that there will be no need to supplement or to elaborate on any points made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 18(5), does my Case or Reply contain everything I intend to put forward` IS
    `o 19 r 18(5) the Case or Reply contains everything the party intends to put forward` `it contains everything that I intend to put forward and is prepared on the basis that there will be no need to supplement or to elaborate`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 19 -- page limits`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 19(1), what is the page limit for a Case or Reply?
GIVEN `which document` IS A `o 19 r 19(1) document` @desc Which document: the appellant's Case, the respondent's Case or the appellant's Reply?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 19(1), what is the page limit for a Case or Reply` IS
    `o 19 r 19(1) the page limit` `which document`

@export Under Order 19, rule 19(1), is my Case or Reply within the page limit?
GIVEN `which document` IS A `o 19 r 19(1) document` @desc Which document: the appellant's Case, the respondent's Case or the appellant's Reply?
      `the number of pages` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pages is the document?
      `the General Division otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division ordered otherwise on the page limit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 19(1), is my Case or Reply within the page limit` IS
    `o 19 r 19(1) the document is within the page limit` `which document` `the number of pages` `the General Division otherwise orders`

@export Under Order 19, rule 19(2), what is the page limit for a core bundle?
GIVEN `which document` IS A `o 19 r 19(2) document` @desc Which document: the appellant's core bundle of documents, the respondent's core bundle of documents or the second core bundle?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 19(2), what is the page limit for a core bundle` IS
    `o 19 r 19(2) the page limit` `which document`

@export Under Order 19, rule 19(2), is my core bundle within the page limit?
GIVEN `which document` IS A `o 19 r 19(2) document` @desc Which document: the appellant's core bundle of documents, the respondent's core bundle of documents or the second core bundle?
      `the number of pages` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pages is the document?
      `the General Division otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division ordered otherwise on the page limit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 19(2), is my core bundle within the page limit` IS
    `o 19 r 19(2) the document is within the page limit` `which document` `the number of pages` `the General Division otherwise orders`

@export Under Order 19, rule 19(3), may the Court allow me to exceed the page limit?
GIVEN `there are special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there special circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 19(3), may the Court allow me to exceed the page limit` IS
    `o 19 r 19(3)(a) the General Division may allow the page limit to be exceeded` `there are special circumstances`

@export Under Order 19, rule 19(3), must I pay fees for the pages in excess of the page limit?
GIVEN `the Court allows the page limit to be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court allowed the page limit to be exceeded?
      `the Court waives the fees under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise on the fees, under paragraph (4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 19(3), must I pay fees for the pages in excess of the page limit` IS
    `o 19 r 19(3)(b) the fees and additional fees for the pages in excess are payable` `the Court allows the page limit to be exceeded` `the Court waives the fees under paragraph (4)`

@export Under Order 19, rule 19(3), how much must I pay for the pages in excess of the page limit?
GIVEN `the Court allows the page limit to be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court allowed the page limit to be exceeded?
      `the Court waives the fees under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise on the fees, under paragraph (4)?
      `the fee for the pages in excess` IS A NUMBER @desc What fee does the Fourth Schedule set for the pages in excess of the limit, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 19(3), how much must I pay for the pages in excess of the page limit` IS
    `o 19 r 19(3)(b) the amount payable for the pages in excess` `the Court allows the page limit to be exceeded` `the Court waives the fees under paragraph (4)` `the fee for the pages in excess`

@export Under Order 19, rule 19(4), may I ask the Court to waive, refund, defer or apportion the fees for the pages in excess?
GIVEN `I apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying to the Court to waive, refund, defer or apportion the fees?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 19(4), may I ask the Court to waive, refund, defer or apportion the fees for the pages in excess` IS
    `o 19 r 19(4) the General Division may waive, refund, defer or apportion the payment of the fees` `I apply`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 20 -- payment out of security for costs and release of undertaking`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 20(1), do I need an order from the Court for this Rule to apply?
GIVEN `the Court has made an order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court made an order about payment out of the security?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 20(1), do I need an order from the Court for this Rule to apply` IS
    `o 19 r 20(1) an order from the Court is needed for this Rule to apply` `the Court has made an order`

@export Under Order 19, rule 20(2), must the security for costs be paid to the respondent towards the costs ordered?
GIVEN `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did the General Division order the appellant to pay the respondent in costs, in dollars? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 20(2), must the security for costs be paid to the respondent towards the costs ordered` IS
    `o 19 r 20(2) the security for costs must be paid to the respondent towards the costs ordered` (`o 19 seat the costs ordered if any` `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 20(2), how much of the security is paid to the respondent?
GIVEN `the security for costs provided` IS A NUMBER @desc How much security for costs was provided, in dollars?
      `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did the General Division order the appellant to pay the respondent in costs, in dollars? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 20(2), how much of the security is paid to the respondent` IS
    `o 19 r 20(2) the amount of the security paid to the respondent` `the security for costs provided` (`o 19 seat the costs ordered if any` `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 20(2), how much of the security is paid back to the appellant?
GIVEN `the security for costs provided` IS A NUMBER @desc How much security for costs was provided, in dollars?
      `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did the General Division order the appellant to pay the respondent in costs, in dollars? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 20(2), how much of the security is paid back to the appellant` IS
    `o 19 r 20(2) the balance of the security paid to the appellant` `the security for costs provided` (`o 19 seat the costs ordered if any` `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 20(3), must the security be paid to the appellant and the appellant's solicitor be released from the undertaking?
GIVEN `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did the General Division order the appellant to pay the respondent in costs, in dollars? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 20(3), must the security be paid to the appellant and the appellant's solicitor be released from the undertaking` IS
    `o 19 r 20(3) the security for costs must be paid to the appellant and the appellant's solicitor is released from any undertaking` (`o 19 seat the costs ordered if any` `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent`)


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 21 -- further arguments`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 21, may the parties make further arguments after the hearing or the decision?
GIVEN `the General Division has heard the appeal and reserved its decision, or has given its decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division heard the appeal and reserved its decision, or given its decision in the appeal?
      `the General Division otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division directed otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 21, may the parties make further arguments after the hearing or the decision` IS
    `o 19 r 21 further arguments from the parties are allowed` `the General Division has heard the appeal and reserved its decision, or has given its decision` `the General Division otherwise directs`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 22 -- notifying the State Courts`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 22, must I file a certified copy of the General Division's judgment or order with the Registrar of the State Courts?
GIVEN `I have filed a certified copy of the General Division's judgment or order with the Registrar of the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you filed a certified copy of the General Division's judgment or order with the Registrar of the State Courts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 22, must I file a certified copy of the General Division's judgment or order with the Registrar of the State Courts` IS
    `o 19 r 22 the appellant has notified the Registrar of the State Courts of the General Division's judgment or order` `I have filed a certified copy of the General Division's judgment or order with the Registrar of the State Courts`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 23 -- enforcement in the State Courts`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 23, must I take a step to enforce the judgment or order in the State Courts?
GIVEN `the judgment or order has been the subject matter of an appeal under Division 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the judgment or order been the subject matter of an appeal under Division 2?
      `the step for enforcement is taken in the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the step for enforcement taken in the State Courts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 23, must I take a step to enforce the judgment or order in the State Courts` IS
    `o 19 r 23 the step for enforcement is taken in the right court` `the judgment or order has been the subject matter of an appeal under Division 2` `the step for enforcement is taken in the State Courts`


-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 19, Division 3 -- Appeals from the General Division to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal, etc. (rules 24 to 40)`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 24 -- scope of this Division`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 24, does Division 3 apply to my appeal or application?
GIVEN `the court I am appealing from` IS A `Court level` @desc From which court are you appealing?
      `the court I am appealing to` IS A `Court level` @desc To which court are you appealing?
      `my appeal is from a tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal from a tribunal (and not from a court)?
      `my appeal is from a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal against a decision or order of a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act?
      `my application is to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are making an application: is it to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal?
      `it relates to an appeal against a judgment of the General Division or the Appellate Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are making an application: does it relate to an appeal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal against a judgment of the General Division, or to the Court of Appeal against a judgment of the Appellate Division?
      `my tribunal appeal is under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If your appeal is from a tribunal: is it brought under a written law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 24, does Division 3 apply to my appeal or application` IS
    `o 19 r 24 this Division applies` (`o 19 seat my route of appeal` `the court I am appealing from` `the court I am appealing to` `my appeal is from a tribunal` `my appeal is from a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act`) `my application is to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `it relates to an appeal against a judgment of the General Division or the Appellate Division` `my tribunal appeal is under a written law`

@export Under Order 19, rule 24(e), does Division 3 apply to my tribunal appeal without modification?
GIVEN `the appellate Court has directed modifications` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appellate Court directed modifications?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 24(e), does Division 3 apply to my tribunal appeal without modification` IS
    `o 19 r 24(e) this Division applies to the tribunal appeal without modification` `the appellate Court has directed modifications`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 25 -- bringing of appeal`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 25(1), within how many days must I file and serve my notice of appeal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 25(1), within how many days must I file and serve my notice of appeal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 25(1)(a) the period for the notice of appeal`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 19, rule 25(1), from what date do the 28 days for my notice of appeal run?
GIVEN `a request for further arguments has been made under section 29B(2) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a request for further arguments been made under section 29B(2) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act?
      `the date of the lower Court's judgment` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the lower Court's judgment?
      `I know the date mentioned in section 29B(4)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If a request was made: do you know the date mentioned in section 29B(4)(b) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act?
      `the date mentioned in section 29B(4)(b)` IS A DATE @desc If you know it, what is that date? (Give any date if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 25(1), from what date do the 28 days for my notice of appeal run` IS
    `o 19 r 25(1) the date after which the 28 days for the notice of appeal run` `a request for further arguments has been made under section 29B(2) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act` `the date of the lower Court's judgment` (`o 19 seat the date if it happened` `I know the date mentioned in section 29B(4)(b)` `the date mentioned in section 29B(4)(b)`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 25(1), have I filed and served my notice of appeal as required?
GIVEN `my notice of appeal is in Form 35` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your notice of appeal in Form 35?
      `I served it on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve it on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
      `the date I filed the notice of appeal` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the notice of appeal?
      `the date I served the notice of appeal` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the notice of appeal?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the Rules give you for this step? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 directs, and if the Court extended or shortened the time under Order 3, rule 4, give the changed last day.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 25(1), have I filed and served my notice of appeal as required` IS
    `o 19 r 25(1) the notice of appeal is filed and served as required` `my notice of appeal is in Form 35` `I served it on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` `the date I filed the notice of appeal` `the date I served the notice of appeal` `my last day` NOTHING

@export Under Order 19, rule 25(2), may the appellate Court extend the time for my notice of appeal?
GIVEN `I apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for the extension?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 25(2), may the appellate Court extend the time for my notice of appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 25(2) the appellate Court may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal` `I apply`

@export Under Order 19, rule 25(2), may the lower Court extend the time for my notice of appeal?
GIVEN `I apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you applied for the extension?
      `I apply before the time expires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply before the time expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 25(2), may the lower Court extend the time for my notice of appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 25(2) the lower Court may extend the time for filing and serving the notice of appeal` `I apply` `I apply before the time expires`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 26 -- permission to appeal`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Only where permission to appeal is required: the form asks "Do you need permission to appeal?" before showing this group.

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(1), within how many days must I apply for permission to appeal?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(1), within how many days must I apply for permission to appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 26(1) the period for the application for permission`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(1), have I applied for permission to appeal as required?
GIVEN `permission to appeal is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is permission to appeal required?
      `I made the application to the appellate Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the application to the appellate Court (and not to another court)?
      `a request for further arguments has been made under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a request for further arguments been made under paragraph (2)?
      `a written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law (not these Rules) provide otherwise?
      `I filed written submissions and any bundle of authorities with the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities with the application?
      `I served the application and those documents on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve the application and those documents on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
      `the date I filed the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the application?
      `the date I served the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the application?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the Rules give you for this step? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 directs, and if the Court extended or shortened the time under Order 3, rule 4, give the changed last day.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(1), have I applied for permission to appeal as required` IS
    `o 19 r 26(1) the application for permission is filed and served as required` `permission to appeal is required` `I made the application to the appellate Court` `a request for further arguments has been made under paragraph (2)` `a written law provides otherwise` `I filed written submissions and any bundle of authorities with the application` `I served the application and those documents on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` `the date I filed the application` `the date I served the application` `my last day` NOTHING

-- The first limb is read as a request made before the earliest of the three times, and the 15th day as starting at its first minute (fork F5 in NOTES.md).
@export Under Order 19, rule 26(2), may the Judge who made the decision hear further arguments?
GIVEN `permission to appeal against the decision is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is permission to appeal against the decision required?
      `a party or the Judge requested further arguments under section 29B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did any party to the hearing, or the Judge, request further arguments under section 29B of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act?
      `the date of the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the request made?
      `the hour of the request` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour (0 to 23) was it made?
      `the minute of the request` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute (0 to 59) of that hour was it made?
      `the date the decision was made` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the decision made?
      `the judgment or order has been extracted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the judgment or order relating to the decision been extracted?
      `the date it was extracted` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Give any date if not.)
      `the hour it was extracted` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour (0 to 23)?
      `the minute it was extracted` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute (0 to 59)?
      `an application for permission to appeal has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for permission to appeal against the decision been filed?
      `the date it was filed` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Give any date if not.)
      `the hour it was filed` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour (0 to 23)?
      `the minute it was filed` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute (0 to 59)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(2), may the Judge who made the decision hear further arguments` IS
    `o 19 r 26(2) the Judge who made the decision may hear further arguments` `permission to appeal against the decision is required` `a party or the Judge requested further arguments under section 29B` (`o 19 seat the moment` `the date of the request` `the hour of the request` `the minute of the request`) (`o 19 seat the moment if it happened` `the judgment or order has been extracted` `the date it was extracted` `the hour it was extracted` `the minute it was extracted`) `the date the decision was made` (`o 19 seat the moment if it happened` `an application for permission to appeal has been filed` `the date it was filed` `the hour it was filed` `the minute it was filed`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(3), is it too early to file my application for permission to appeal?
GIVEN `a request for further arguments has been made under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a request for further arguments been made under paragraph (2)?
      `the Judge has disposed of the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Judge affirmed, varied or set aside the decision after hearing further arguments, or certified (or is deemed to have certified) that no further arguments are required?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(3), is it too early to file my application for permission to appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 26(3)(a) the application for permission to appeal cannot yet be filed against the decision` `a request for further arguments has been made under paragraph (2)` `the Judge has disposed of the request`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(3), may I file my application for permission to appeal against the decision?
GIVEN `a request for further arguments has been made under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a request for further arguments been made under paragraph (2)?
      `the Judge has disposed of the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Judge affirmed, varied or set aside the decision after hearing further arguments, or certified (or is deemed to have certified) that no further arguments are required?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(3), may I file my application for permission to appeal against the decision` IS
    `o 19 r 26(3)(a) the application for permission to appeal may be filed against the decision` `a request for further arguments has been made under paragraph (2)` `the Judge has disposed of the request`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(3), from what date do the 14 days for my application run after further arguments?
GIVEN `the Judge affirmed, varied or set aside the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Judge affirm, vary or set aside the decision after hearing further arguments?
      `the date the Judge did so` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Give any date if not.)
      `the Judge certified that no further arguments are required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Judge certify (or is the Judge deemed to have certified) that no further arguments are required?
      `the date the Judge certified` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Give any date if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(3), from what date do the 14 days for my application run after further arguments` IS
    `o 19 r 26(3)(b) the date after which the 14 days for the application run` (`o 19 seat the date if it happened` `the Judge affirmed, varied or set aside the decision` `the date the Judge did so`) (`o 19 seat the date if it happened` `the Judge certified that no further arguments are required` `the date the Judge certified`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(3), have I applied for permission to appeal in time after further arguments?
GIVEN `a request for further arguments has been made under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a request for further arguments been made under paragraph (2)?
      `I filed written submissions and any bundle of authorities with the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities with the application?
      `I served the application and those documents on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve the application and those documents on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
      `the date I filed the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the application?
      `the date I served the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the application?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the Rules give you for this step? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 directs, and if the Court extended or shortened the time under Order 3, rule 4, give the changed last day.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(3), have I applied for permission to appeal in time after further arguments` IS
    `o 19 r 26(3)(b) the application for permission is filed and served as required after further arguments` `a request for further arguments has been made under paragraph (2)` `I filed written submissions and any bundle of authorities with the application` `I served the application and those documents on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` `the date I filed the application` `the date I served the application` `my last day` NOTHING

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(4), do paragraphs (2) and (3) affect section 29B of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act?
GIVEN `paragraph (2) or (3) is applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is paragraph (2) or (3) being applied?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(4), do paragraphs (2) and (3) affect section 29B of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act` IS
    `o 19 r 26(4) paragraphs (2) and (3) affect section 29B of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act` `paragraph (2) or (3) is applied`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(5), may the Court of Appeal grant permission to appeal against a decision of the Appellate Division?
GIVEN `permission to appeal under section 47(1) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is permission to appeal under section 47(1) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act required?
      `the appeal will raise a point of law of public importance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the appeal raise a point of law of public importance?
      `it is appropriate for the Court of Appeal to hear a further appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it appropriate for the Court of Appeal to hear a further appeal, having regard to all relevant matters?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(5), may the Court of Appeal grant permission to appeal against a decision of the Appellate Division` IS
    `o 19 r 26(5) the Court of Appeal may grant permission to appeal against a decision of the Appellate Division` `permission to appeal under section 47(1) of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act is required` `the appeal will raise a point of law of public importance` `it is appropriate for the Court of Appeal to hear a further appeal`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(5), may the Court of Appeal have regard to this matter in deciding whether to hear a further appeal?
GIVEN `which matter` IS A `o 19 r 26(5)(b) matter the Court of Appeal considers` @desc Which matter: whether a decision of the Court of Appeal is required to resolve the point of law, whether the interests of the administration of justice require its consideration, or any other relevant matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(5), may the Court of Appeal have regard to this matter in deciding whether to hear a further appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 26(5)(b) the Court of Appeal may have regard to the matter` `which matter`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(6), may I apply to the other appellate Court for permission to appeal?
GIVEN `I applied to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal for permission to appeal within the time provided under Rule 26?
      `that court decided that the other court is the one to give permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did that court decide that the court from which permission must be obtained is the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division (the other one)?
      `the date I applied to the other court` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you applying to the other court?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the Rules give you for this step? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 directs, and if the Court extended or shortened the time under Order 3, rule 4, give the changed last day.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(6), may I apply to the other appellate Court for permission to appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 26(6) the party may apply to the relevant appellate Court for permission to appeal` `I applied to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal in time` `that court decided that the other court is the one to give permission` `the date I applied to the other court` `my last day` NOTHING

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(7), have I filed and served the documents that go with my application for permission?
GIVEN `I filed written submissions with the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file written submissions with the application, at the time of filing it?
      `I filed any accompanying bundle of authorities with the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file any accompanying bundle of authorities with the application?
      `I served the application and the documents on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve the application, the written submissions and any bundles on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(7), have I filed and served the documents that go with my application for permission` IS
    `o 19 r 26(7) the documents mentioned are filed and served with the application` `I filed written submissions with the application` `I filed any accompanying bundle of authorities with the application` `I served the application and the documents on all parties who have an interest in the appeal`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(7), may I file a bundle of documents with my application?
GIVEN `I filed a bundle of documents relevant to the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file a bundle of the documents relevant to the application that were filed in the proceedings below?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(7), may I file a bundle of documents with my application` IS
    `o 19 r 26(7)(b) the applicant may file a bundle of documents with the application` `I filed a bundle of documents relevant to the application`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(8), have I filed and served my opposing submissions as required?
GIVEN `I wish to oppose the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you wish to oppose the application for permission?
      `I filed and served written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file and serve written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities?
      `the date I filed my submissions` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file my submissions?
      `the date I served my submissions` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve my submissions?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the Rules give you for this step? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 directs, and if the Court extended or shortened the time under Order 3, rule 4, give the changed last day.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(8), have I filed and served my opposing submissions as required` IS
    `o 19 r 26(8) the opposing party's submissions are filed and served as required` `I wish to oppose the application` `I filed and served written submissions and any accompanying bundle of authorities` `the date I filed my submissions` `the date I served my submissions` `my last day` NOTHING

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(8), may I file a bundle of documents with my opposing submissions?
GIVEN `I filed and served a bundle of documents relevant to the application with my submissions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file and serve a bundle of the documents relevant to the application, together with your written submissions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(8), may I file a bundle of documents with my opposing submissions` IS
    `o 19 r 26(8)(b) the opposing party may file and serve a bundle of documents with its submissions` `I filed and served a bundle of documents relevant to the application with my submissions`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(9), must the application and the documents be served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
GIVEN `they were served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the application, written submissions, any accompanying bundles of authorities and bundles of documents served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(9), must the application and the documents be served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 26(9) the application and the accompanying documents are served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` `they were served on all parties who have an interest in the appeal`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(10), are my written submissions within the page limit and in the form specified?
GIVEN `the number of pages` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pages are the written submissions?
      `the appellate Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appellate Court ordered otherwise on the page limit?
      `the submissions are in the form specified in any practice directions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the submissions in the form specified in any practice directions issued by the Registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(10), are my written submissions within the page limit and in the form specified` IS
    `o 19 r 26(10) the written submissions are within the page limit and in the form specified` `the number of pages` `the appellate Court otherwise orders` `the submissions are in the form specified in any practice directions`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(11), is my bundle of documents within the page limit?
GIVEN `the number of pages` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pages is the bundle of documents?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(11), is my bundle of documents within the page limit` IS
    `o 19 r 26(11) the bundle of documents is within the page limit` `the number of pages`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(12), may the appellate Court allow my written submissions to exceed the page limit?
GIVEN `there are special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there special circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(12), may the appellate Court allow my written submissions to exceed the page limit` IS
    `o 19 r 26(12)(a) the appellate Court may allow the page limit for the written submissions to be exceeded` `there are special circumstances`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(12), must I pay fees for the pages in excess of the page limit?
GIVEN `the Court allows the page limit to be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court allowed the page limit to be exceeded?
      `the Court waives the fees under paragraph (13)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise on the fees, under paragraph (13)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(12), must I pay fees for the pages in excess of the page limit` IS
    `o 19 r 26(12)(b) the fees and additional fees for the pages in excess are payable` `the Court allows the page limit to be exceeded` `the Court waives the fees under paragraph (13)`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(12), how much must I pay for the pages in excess of the page limit?
GIVEN `the Court allows the page limit to be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court allowed the page limit to be exceeded?
      `the Court waives the fees under paragraph (13)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise on the fees, under paragraph (13)?
      `the fee for the pages in excess` IS A NUMBER @desc What fee does the Fourth Schedule set for the pages in excess of the limit, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(12), how much must I pay for the pages in excess of the page limit` IS
    `o 19 r 26(12)(b) the amount payable for the pages in excess` `the Court allows the page limit to be exceeded` `the Court waives the fees under paragraph (13)` `the fee for the pages in excess`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(13), may I ask the Court to waive, refund, defer or apportion the fees?
GIVEN `I apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying to the Court to waive, refund, defer or apportion the fees?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(13), may I ask the Court to waive, refund, defer or apportion the fees` IS
    `o 19 r 26(13) the appellate Court may waive, refund, defer or apportion the payment of the fees` `I apply`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(14), may I file more than one set of submissions for a party or parties represented by the same firm?
GIVEN `the appellate Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appellate Court ordered otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(14), may I file more than one set of submissions for a party or parties represented by the same firm` IS
    `o 19 r 26(14) more than one set of submissions may be filed for a party or a set of parties represented by the same firm of solicitors` `the appellate Court otherwise orders`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(15), may I file an affidavit in my application for permission to appeal?
GIVEN `the appellate Court gives permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appellate Court given permission to file an affidavit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(15), may I file an affidavit in my application for permission to appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 26(15) an affidavit may be filed in an application for permission to appeal` `the appellate Court gives permission`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(16), may I make oral arguments in an application for permission to appeal?
GIVEN `the appellate Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appellate Court ordered otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(16), may I make oral arguments in an application for permission to appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 26(16) oral arguments may be made in an application for permission to appeal` `the appellate Court otherwise orders`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(17), within how many days must I file and serve my notice of appeal once permission is granted?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(17), within how many days must I file and serve my notice of appeal once permission is granted` IS
    `o 19 r 26(17) the period for the notice of appeal after permission is granted`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(17), once permission is granted, have I filed and served my notice of appeal as required?
GIVEN `permission to appeal is granted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has permission to appeal been granted?
      `my notice of appeal is in Form 35` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your notice of appeal in Form 35?
      `I served it on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve it on all parties who have an interest in the appeal?
      `the date I filed the notice of appeal` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the notice of appeal?
      `the date I served the notice of appeal` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the notice of appeal?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the Rules give you for this step? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 directs, and if the Court extended or shortened the time under Order 3, rule 4, give the changed last day.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(17), once permission is granted, have I filed and served my notice of appeal as required` IS
    `o 19 r 26(17) the notice of appeal after permission is filed and served as required` `permission to appeal is granted` `my notice of appeal is in Form 35` `I served it on all parties who have an interest in the appeal` `the date I filed the notice of appeal` `the date I served the notice of appeal` `my last day` NOTHING

@export Under Order 19, rule 26(18), may the appellate Court extend the time for my application for permission to appeal?
GIVEN `the order extends the time for filing and serving an application for permission to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order one that extends the time for filing and serving an application for permission to appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 26(18), may the appellate Court extend the time for my application for permission to appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 26(18) the appellate Court may extend the time for filing and serving an application for permission to appeal` `the order extends the time for filing and serving an application for permission to appeal`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 27 -- security for costs`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 27(1), have I given security for costs and filed the certificate as required?
GIVEN `I have provided security for the respondent's costs of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided security for the respondent's costs of the appeal?
      `I have filed the certificate for security for costs in Form 36` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you filed the certificate for security for costs in Form 36?
      `I did both when I filed the notice of appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do both at the time you filed the notice of appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 27(1), have I given security for costs and filed the certificate as required` IS
    `o 19 r 27(1) the appellant has provided security for costs and filed the certificate as required` `I have provided security for the respondent's costs of the appeal` `I have filed the certificate for security for costs in Form 36` `I did both when I filed the notice of appeal`

@export Under Order 19, rule 27(2), need all the appellants give only one set of security?
GIVEN `there is more than one appellant in the same appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there more than one appellant in the same appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 27(2), need all the appellants give only one set of security` IS
    `o 19 r 27(2) the appellants need to provide only one set of security for the appeal` `there is more than one appellant in the same appeal`

@export Under Order 19, rule 27(3), must I give security for each respondent or each set of respondents?
GIVEN `there is more than one respondent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there more than one respondent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 27(3), must I give security for each respondent or each set of respondents` IS
    `o 19 r 27(3) the appellant must provide security for each respondent or each set of respondents` `there is more than one respondent`

@export Under Order 19, rule 27(3), how many sets of security must I give?
GIVEN `the number of respondents` IS A NUMBER @desc How many respondents are there? Count each respondent, even where two or more are represented by the same firm of solicitors.
      `the number of sets of respondents, where respondents represented by the same firm of solicitors are one set` IS A NUMBER @desc How many sets of respondents are there, counting respondents represented by the same firm of solicitors as one set?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 27(3), how many sets of security must I give` IS
    `o 19 r 27(3) the number of sets of security the appellant must provide` `the number of respondents` `the number of sets of respondents, where respondents represented by the same firm of solicitors are one set`

@export Under Order 19, rule 27(4), is my security in a form the Rules allow?
GIVEN `the form of my security` IS A `o 19 r 27(4) form of security` @desc In what form is your security: a solicitor's undertaking in Form 37, a deposit in the Registry or with the Accountant-General, or any other form?
      `the undertaking is filed and served on the respondent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a solicitor's undertaking, is it filed and served on the respondent?
      `the form is acceptable to the parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is another form, is it acceptable to the parties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 27(4), is my security in a form the Rules allow` IS
    `o 19 r 27(4) the security is in a form the text allows` `the form of my security` `the undertaking is filed and served on the respondent` `the form is acceptable to the parties`

@export Under Order 19, rule 27(5), how much security must I give?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 27(5), how much security must I give` IS
    `o 19 r 27(5) the amount of security`

@export Under Order 19, rule 27(5), is the security I gave the right amount?
GIVEN `the amount of security I provided` IS A NUMBER @desc How much security did you provide, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 27(5), is the security I gave the right amount` IS
    `o 19 r 27(5) the security is in the amount the text requires` `the amount of security I provided`

@export Under Order 19, rule 27(6), may I apply to vary or waive the amount of security?
GIVEN `I am a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party to the appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 27(6), may I apply to vary or waive the amount of security` IS
    `o 19 r 27(6) a party may apply to the appellate Court to vary or waive the amount of security` `I am a party`

@export Under Order 19, rule 27(7), may the Court order me to give further security for costs?
GIVEN `the order is for further security for costs to be given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order one for further security for costs to be given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 27(7), may the Court order me to give further security for costs` IS
    `o 19 r 27(7) the appellate Court may order further security for costs to be given` `the order is for further security for costs to be given`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 28 -- related appeals`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 28(1), may the appellate Court give directions for joint documents in related appeals?
GIVEN `there are related appeals in the appellate Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there related appeals in the appellate Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 28(1), may the appellate Court give directions for joint documents in related appeals` IS
    `o 19 r 28(1) the appellate Court may give directions for the filing and service of joint documents` `there are related appeals in the appellate Court`

@export Under Order 19, rule 28(2), may the directions be given on the Court's own motion or on a party's application or request?
GIVEN `the directions are given on the appellate Court's own motion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the directions given on the appellate Court's own motion?
      `the directions are given on the application or request of a party to any of the related appeals` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they given on the application or request of a party to any of the related appeals?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 28(2), may the directions be given on the Court's own motion or on a party's application or request` IS
    `o 19 r 28(2) the directions in paragraph (1) may be given in this way` `the directions are given on the appellate Court's own motion` `the directions are given on the application or request of a party to any of the related appeals`

@export Under Order 19, rule 28(3), may the appellate Court give directions even if some related appeals are under Order 18?
GIVEN `the related appeals are partly under this Order and partly under Order 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the related appeals comprise one or more appeals filed under this Order and one or more appeals filed under Order 18?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 28(3), may the appellate Court give directions even if some related appeals are under Order 18` IS
    `o 19 r 28(3) the appellate Court may give directions under paragraph (1) even if the related appeals are of both kinds` `the related appeals are partly under this Order and partly under Order 18`

@export Under Order 19, rule 28(4), may the appellate Court modify the rules, or switch Division 3 off and Division 5 of Order 18 on, for my related appeals?
GIVEN `the related appeals are partly under this Order and partly under Order 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the related appeals comprise one or more appeals filed under this Order and one or more appeals filed under Order 18?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 28(4), may the appellate Court modify the rules, or switch Division 3 off and Division 5 of Order 18 on, for my related appeals` IS
    `o 19 r 28(4) the appellate Court may direct modifications of the rules, including that this Division does not apply and Division 5 of Order 18 applies instead` `the related appeals are partly under this Order and partly under Order 18`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 29 -- the appellate Court may specify the rules that apply to an appeal`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 29(1), may the appellate Court order that Division 3 does not apply to my appeal and Division 5 of Order 18 applies instead?
GIVEN `the appellate Court deems it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the appellate Court deem it appropriate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 29(1), may the appellate Court order that Division 3 does not apply to my appeal and Division 5 of Order 18 applies instead` IS
    `o 19 r 29(1) the appellate Court may order that this Division, or any part of it, does not apply to an appeal before it, and that Division 5 of Order 18, or any part of it, applies instead` `the appellate Court deems it appropriate`

@export Under Order 19, rule 29(2), may the appellate Court modify the rules that apply to my appeal?
GIVEN `the appellate Court deems it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the appellate Court deem it appropriate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 29(2), may the appellate Court modify the rules that apply to my appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 29(2) the appellate Court may order or direct modifications of the rules applicable to an appeal before it` `the appellate Court deems it appropriate`

@export Under Order 19, rule 29(3), may the appellate Court act on its own motion under this Rule?
GIVEN `the order or direction is made on the appellate Court's own motion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order or direction made on the appellate Court's own motion?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 29(3), may the appellate Court act on its own motion under this Rule` IS
    `o 19 r 29(3) the appellate Court may make an order or give a direction under this Rule` `the order or direction is made on the appellate Court's own motion`

@export Under Order 19, rule 30(3), within how many weeks must written grounds of decision be issued before the appellant must apply to proceed?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 30(3), within how many weeks must written grounds of decision be issued before the appellant must apply to proceed` IS
    `o 19 r 30(3) the period for written grounds of decision`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 19, rule 30(4), within how many weeks must the appellant file and serve the appellant's documents?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 30(4), within how many weeks must the appellant file and serve the appellant's documents` IS
    `o 19 r 30(4) the period for the appellant's documents`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 19, rule 30(9), within how many days must the respondent file and serve the respondent's documents?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 30(9), within how many days must the respondent file and serve the respondent's documents` IS
    `o 19 r 30(9) the period for the respondent's documents`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 19, rule 30(11), within how many days must the appellant file and serve the Reply and the other reply documents?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 30(11), within how many days must the appellant file and serve the Reply and the other reply documents` IS
    `o 19 r 30(11) the period for the appellant's reply documents`'s `period length`


