§§ `Rule 30 -- documents to be filed`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 30(1), must the lower Court issue its written grounds of decision?
GIVEN `the notice of appeal has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the notice of appeal been filed?
      `the lower Court has already issued its written grounds of decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the lower Court already issued its written grounds of decision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 30(1), must the lower Court issue its written grounds of decision` IS
    `o 19 r 30(1) the lower Court must issue its written grounds of decision` `the notice of appeal has been filed` `the lower Court has already issued its written grounds of decision`

@export Under Order 19, rule 30(2), will the Registry notify me that the record of proceedings is ready for collection?
GIVEN `the record of proceedings is ready for collection` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the record of proceedings ready for collection?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 30(2), will the Registry notify me that the record of proceedings is ready for collection` IS
    `o 19 r 30(2) the Registry must notify the parties that the record of proceedings is ready for collection` `the record of proceedings is ready for collection`

@export Under Order 19, rule 30(3), have 12 weeks passed after filing the notice of appeal with no written grounds of decision?
GIVEN `the written grounds of decision have been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the written grounds of decision been issued?
      `the date the written grounds of decision were issued` IS A DATE @desc If they have been issued, on what date? (Give any date if they have not.)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the 12 weeks after the date of filing the notice of appeal, counted as Order 3, rule 3 directs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 30(3), have 12 weeks passed after filing the notice of appeal with no written grounds of decision` IS
    `o 19 r 30(3) no written grounds of decision are issued within 12 weeks` (`o 19 seat the date if it happened` `the written grounds of decision have been issued` `the date the written grounds of decision were issued`) `the date I am asking about` `my last day`

@export Under Order 19, rule 30(3)(a), must I, as appellant, apply in writing to the Registrar to proceed with the appeal?
GIVEN `no written grounds of decision are issued within 12 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have 12 weeks passed after filing the notice of appeal with no written grounds of decision issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 30(3)(a), must I, as appellant, apply in writing to the Registrar to proceed with the appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 30(3)(a) the appellant must apply in writing to the Registrar to proceed with the appeal and for a copy of the record of proceedings` `no written grounds of decision are issued within 12 weeks`

@export Under Order 19, rule 30(3)(b), may the respondent apply to proceed or give me 14 days' written notice of intention to strike out my appeal?
GIVEN `no written grounds of decision are issued within 12 weeks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have 12 weeks passed after filing the notice of appeal with no written grounds of decision issued?
      `the appellant has failed to apply as sub-paragraph (a) requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appellant failed to apply in writing to the Registrar to proceed with the appeal?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 30(3)(b), may the respondent apply to proceed or give me 14 days' written notice of intention to strike out my appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 30(3)(b) the respondent may apply in writing to the Registrar to proceed or give 14 days' written notice of intention to strike out the appeal` `no written grounds of decision are issued within 12 weeks` `the appellant has failed to apply as sub-paragraph (a) requires`

@export Under Order 19, rule 30(3)(c), may the respondent apply to strike out my appeal?
GIVEN `the respondent has given the appellant 14 days' written notice of intention to strike out the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the respondent given the appellant 14 days' written notice of intention to strike out the appeal?
      `the 14 days' notice period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the 14 days' notice period expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 30(3)(c), may the respondent apply to strike out my appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 30(3)(c) the respondent may apply to strike out the appeal` `the respondent has given the appellant 14 days' written notice of intention to strike out the appeal` `the 14 days' notice period has expired`

@export Under Order 19, rule 30(4), did I file and serve this document of the appellant's in time?
GIVEN `which document` IS A `o 19 r 30(4) document` @desc Which of the appellant's documents are you asking about: the record of appeal, the appellant's Case, the appellant's core bundle of documents or the appellant's bundle of authorities?
      `this is an appeal from the Appellate Division to the Court of Appeal (a case to which paragraph (5) applies)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this an appeal to the Court of Appeal against a decision of the Appellate Division (the case that paragraph (5) deals with)?
      `the written judgment or grounds of decision and the extracted order of the lower Court are in a separate volume` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is the core bundle: are the written judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court (if any) and the extracted order in a separate volume?
      `the date I filed the document` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the document?
      `the date I served the document` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the document?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the Rules give you for this step? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 directs, and if the Court extended or shortened the time under Order 3, rule 4, give the changed last day.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 30(4), did I file and serve this document of the appellant's in time` IS
    `o 19 r 30(4) the appellant's document is filed and served in time` `which document` `this is an appeal from the Appellate Division to the Court of Appeal (a case to which paragraph (5) applies)` `the written judgment or grounds of decision and the extracted order of the lower Court are in a separate volume` `the date I filed the document` `the date I served the document` `my last day` NOTHING

@export Under Order 19, rule 30(6), is my appeal deemed withdrawn?
GIVEN `I failed to file and serve the record of appeal, the core bundle of documents or the appellant's Case within the specified time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to file and serve the record of appeal, the core bundle of documents or the appellant's Case within the specified time?
      `the appellate Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 30(6), is my appeal deemed withdrawn` IS
    `o 19 r 30(6) the appeal is deemed withdrawn` `I failed to file and serve the record of appeal, the core bundle of documents or the appellant's Case within the specified time` `the appellate Court otherwise orders`

@export Under Order 19, rule 30(7), must the security for costs be paid out and the undertaking discharged where my appeal is deemed withdrawn?
GIVEN `my appeal is deemed withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your appeal deemed withdrawn?
      `all the parties to the appeal consent to the payment of the security for costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the parties to the appeal consent to the payment of the security for costs?
      `the document signifying the consent, signed by the parties, is filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the document signifying the consent, signed by the parties, been filed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 30(7), must the security for costs be paid out and the undertaking discharged where my appeal is deemed withdrawn` IS
    `o 19 r 30(7) the security for costs must be paid and the solicitor's undertaking is discharged` `my appeal is deemed withdrawn` `all the parties to the appeal consent to the payment of the security for costs` `the document signifying the consent, signed by the parties, is filed`

@export Under Order 19, rule 30(8)(a), may I request directions in writing on outstanding issues after my appeal is deemed withdrawn?
