-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 31 -- appellant's Case, respondent's Case and appellant's Reply`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 31(1), does my Case as appellant contain what it must contain?
GIVEN `my Case has a succinct summary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain a succinct summary of the facts, the decision of the lower Court, the contentions to be made at the appeal and the orders sought?
      `my Case has detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues, including the relevant authorities, highlighting any new points not raised in the lower Court?
      `my Case has references in the right-hand margin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case have references in the right-hand margin to the relevant pages in the record of appeal and your core bundle of documents?
      `my Case has submissions on the appropriate costs orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain submissions on the appropriate costs orders to be made on appeal, in its concluding paragraphs?
      `my Case has submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements that should be awarded in respect of all parties to the appeal, in its concluding paragraphs?
      `my Case has the name and signature of my solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case carry the name and signature of your solicitor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 31(1), does my Case as appellant contain what it must contain` IS
    `o 19 r 31(1) the appellant's Case contains what it must contain` (`o 19 r 31(1) the appellant's Case` `my Case has a succinct summary` `my Case has detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues` `my Case has references in the right-hand margin` `my Case has submissions on the appropriate costs orders` `my Case has submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements` `my Case has the name and signature of my solicitor`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 31(2), does my Case as respondent contain what it must contain?
GIVEN `the respondent's Case has a succinct summary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain a succinct summary of the contentions to be made at the appeal and the orders sought?
      `the respondent's Case has detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues, including the relevant authorities, highlighting any new points not raised in the lower Court?
      `the respondent's Case has references in the right-hand margin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case have references in the right-hand margin to the relevant pages in the record of appeal and your core bundle of documents (if any)?
      `I intend to submit that the lower Court's decision should be varied or affirmed on other grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you intend to submit that the lower Court's decision should be varied (where you have not appealed) or affirmed on grounds other than those the lower Court relied on?
      `the Case sets out those submissions and the reasons for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does your Case state those submissions and the reasons for them?
      `the respondent's Case has submissions on the appropriate costs orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain submissions on the appropriate costs orders to be made on appeal, in its concluding paragraphs?
      `the respondent's Case has submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case contain submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements that should be awarded in respect of all parties to the appeal, in its concluding paragraphs?
      `the respondent's Case has the name and signature of the respondent's solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Case carry the name and signature of your solicitor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 31(2), does my Case as respondent contain what it must contain` IS
    `o 19 r 31(2) the respondent's Case contains what it must contain` (`o 19 r 31(2) the respondent's Case` `the respondent's Case has a succinct summary` `the respondent's Case has detailed submissions on the facts and the legal issues` `the respondent's Case has references in the right-hand margin` `I intend to submit that the lower Court's decision should be varied or affirmed on other grounds` `the Case sets out those submissions and the reasons for them` `the respondent's Case has submissions on the appropriate costs orders` `the respondent's Case has submissions on the amount of costs and disbursements` `the respondent's Case has the name and signature of the respondent's solicitor`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 31(3), am I barred from making the submissions in paragraph (2)(d)?
GIVEN `I failed to comply with the requirements in paragraph (2)(d)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to comply with the requirements in paragraph (2)(d) (stating that you will submit the decision should be varied or affirmed on other grounds, and your reasons)?
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 31(3), am I barred from making the submissions in paragraph (2)(d)` IS
    `o 19 r 31(3) the respondent is barred from making the submissions mentioned in paragraph (2)(d)` `I failed to comply with the requirements in paragraph (2)(d)` `the Court otherwise orders`

@export Under Order 19, rule 31(4), does my Reply as appellant contain what it must contain?
GIVEN `my Reply has detailed submissions in reply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Reply contain your detailed submissions in reply to the respondent's submissions?
      `my Reply has references in the right-hand margin` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Reply have references in the right-hand margin to the relevant pages in the record of appeal and the core bundles?
      `my Reply has the name and signature of my solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your Reply carry the name and signature of your solicitor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 31(4), does my Reply as appellant contain what it must contain` IS
    `o 19 r 31(4) the appellant's Reply contains what it must contain` (`o 19 r 31(4) the appellant's Reply` `my Reply has detailed submissions in reply` `my Reply has references in the right-hand margin` `my Reply has the name and signature of my solicitor`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 31(5), does my Case or Reply contain everything I intend to put forward?
GIVEN `it contains everything that I intend to put forward and is prepared on the basis that there will be no need to supplement or to elaborate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain everything you intend to put forward at the appeal, and is it prepared on the basis that there will be no need to supplement or to elaborate on any points made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 31(5), does my Case or Reply contain everything I intend to put forward` IS
    `o 19 r 31(5) the Case or Reply contains everything the party intends to put forward` `it contains everything that I intend to put forward and is prepared on the basis that there will be no need to supplement or to elaborate`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 32 -- page limits`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 32(1), what is the page limit for a Case or Reply?
GIVEN `which document` IS A `o 19 r 32(1) document` @desc Which document: the appellant's Case, the respondent's Case or the appellant's Reply?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 32(1), what is the page limit for a Case or Reply` IS
    `o 19 r 32(1) the page limit` `which document`

@export Under Order 19, rule 32(1), is my Case or Reply within the page limit?
GIVEN `which document` IS A `o 19 r 32(1) document` @desc Which document: the appellant's Case, the respondent's Case or the appellant's Reply?
      `the number of pages` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pages is the document?
      `the appellate Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appellate Court ordered otherwise on the page limit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 32(1), is my Case or Reply within the page limit` IS
    `o 19 r 32(1) the document is within the page limit` `which document` `the number of pages` `the appellate Court otherwise orders`

@export Under Order 19, rule 32(2), what is the page limit for a core bundle?
GIVEN `which document` IS A `o 19 r 32(2) document` @desc Which document: the appellant's core bundle of documents, the respondent's core bundle of documents or the second core bundle?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 32(2), what is the page limit for a core bundle` IS
    `o 19 r 32(2) the page limit` `which document`

@export Under Order 19, rule 32(2), is my core bundle within the page limit?
GIVEN `which document` IS A `o 19 r 32(2) document` @desc Which document: the appellant's core bundle of documents, the respondent's core bundle of documents or the second core bundle?
      `the number of pages` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pages is the document?
      `the appellate Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appellate Court ordered otherwise on the page limit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 32(2), is my core bundle within the page limit` IS
    `o 19 r 32(2) the document is within the page limit` `which document` `the number of pages` `the appellate Court otherwise orders`

@export Under Order 19, rule 32(3), may the Court allow me to exceed the page limit?
GIVEN `there are special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there special circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 32(3), may the Court allow me to exceed the page limit` IS
    `o 19 r 32(3)(a) the appellate Court may allow the page limit to be exceeded` `there are special circumstances`

@export Under Order 19, rule 32(3), must I pay fees for the pages in excess of the page limit?
GIVEN `the Court allows the page limit to be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court allowed the page limit to be exceeded?
      `the Court waives the fees under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise on the fees, under paragraph (4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 32(3), must I pay fees for the pages in excess of the page limit` IS
    `o 19 r 32(3)(b) the fees and additional fees for the pages in excess are payable` `the Court allows the page limit to be exceeded` `the Court waives the fees under paragraph (4)`

@export Under Order 19, rule 32(3), how much must I pay for the pages in excess of the page limit?
GIVEN `the Court allows the page limit to be exceeded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court allowed the page limit to be exceeded?
      `the Court waives the fees under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered otherwise on the fees, under paragraph (4)?
      `the fee for the pages in excess` IS A NUMBER @desc What fee does the Fourth Schedule set for the pages in excess of the limit, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 32(3), how much must I pay for the pages in excess of the page limit` IS
    `o 19 r 32(3)(b) the amount payable for the pages in excess` `the Court allows the page limit to be exceeded` `the Court waives the fees under paragraph (4)` `the fee for the pages in excess`

@export Under Order 19, rule 32(4), may I ask the Court to waive, refund, defer or apportion the fees for the pages in excess?
GIVEN `I apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying to the Court to waive, refund, defer or apportion the fees?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 32(4), may I ask the Court to waive, refund, defer or apportion the fees for the pages in excess` IS
    `o 19 r 32(4) the appellate Court may waive, refund, defer or apportion the payment of the fees` `I apply`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 33 -- payment out of security for costs and release of undertaking`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 19, rule 33(1), do I need an order from the Court for this Rule to apply?
GIVEN `the Court has made an order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court made an order about payment out of the security?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 33(1), do I need an order from the Court for this Rule to apply` IS
    `o 19 r 33(1) an order from the Court is needed for this Rule to apply` `the Court has made an order`

@export Under Order 19, rule 33(2), must the security for costs be paid to the respondent towards the costs ordered?
GIVEN `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did the appellate Court order the appellant to pay the respondent in costs, in dollars? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 33(2), must the security for costs be paid to the respondent towards the costs ordered` IS
    `o 19 r 33(2) the security for costs must be paid to the respondent towards the costs ordered` (`o 19 seat the costs ordered if any` `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 33(2), how much of the security is paid to the respondent?
GIVEN `the security for costs provided` IS A NUMBER @desc How much security for costs was provided, in dollars?
      `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did the appellate Court order the appellant to pay the respondent in costs, in dollars? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 33(2), how much of the security is paid to the respondent` IS
    `o 19 r 33(2) the amount of the security paid to the respondent` `the security for costs provided` (`o 19 seat the costs ordered if any` `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 33(2), how much of the security is paid back to the appellant?
GIVEN `the security for costs provided` IS A NUMBER @desc How much security for costs was provided, in dollars?
      `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did the appellate Court order the appellant to pay the respondent in costs, in dollars? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 33(2), how much of the security is paid back to the appellant` IS
    `o 19 r 33(2) the balance of the security paid to the appellant` `the security for costs provided` (`o 19 seat the costs ordered if any` `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 33(3), must the security be paid to the appellant and the appellant's solicitor be released from the undertaking?
GIVEN `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent` IS A NUMBER @desc How much did the appellate Court order the appellant to pay the respondent in costs, in dollars? (0 if none.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 33(3), must the security be paid to the appellant and the appellant's solicitor be released from the undertaking` IS
    `o 19 r 33(3) the security for costs must be paid to the appellant and the appellant's solicitor is released from any undertaking` (`o 19 seat the costs ordered if any` `the costs the Court ordered the appellant to pay the respondent`)

@export Under Order 19, rule 33(4), do paragraphs (2) and (3) apply to security I gave under Rule 35(6)?
GIVEN `the security for costs was given under Rule 35(6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the security for costs given under Rule 35(6) (on an application)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 33(4), do paragraphs (2) and (3) apply to security I gave under Rule 35(6)` IS
    `o 19 r 33(4) paragraphs (2) and (3) apply, with necessary modifications, to the payment out of the security` `the security for costs was given under Rule 35(6)`


