    `o 19 r 35(4) the period for the affidavit in reply`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 19, rule 35(1), is my application to the appellate Court made in a way the Rules allow?
GIVEN `how I made my application` IS A `o 19 r 35(1) way of making an application` @desc How did you make the application: by originating application, or by summons?
      `the appeal is pending before the appellate Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the appeal pending before the appellate Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 35(1), is my application to the appellate Court made in a way the Rules allow` IS
    `o 19 r 35(1) the application to the appellate Court is made in a way the text allows` `how I made my application` `the appeal is pending before the appellate Court`

@export Under Order 19, rule 35(2), may I make my application first to the appellate Court?
GIVEN `the Rules allow the application to be made either to the lower Court or to the appellate Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Rules allow this application to be made either to the lower Court or to the appellate Court?
      `there are special circumstances which make it impossible or impracticable to apply to the lower Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are there special circumstances which make it impossible or impracticable to apply to the lower Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 35(2), may I make my application first to the appellate Court` IS
    `o 19 r 35(2) the application may be made in the first instance to the appellate Court` `the Rules allow the application to be made either to the lower Court or to the appellate Court` `there are special circumstances which make it impossible or impracticable to apply to the lower Court`

