GIVEN `the appellate Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appellate Court ordered otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 35(3), may I make oral arguments in an application to the appellate Court` IS
    `o 19 r 35(3) oral arguments may be made in an application to the appellate Court` `the appellate Court otherwise orders`

@export Under Order 19, rule 35(4), have I filed and served my affidavit in reply to the application as required?
GIVEN `Rule 26(15) provides otherwise because this is an application for permission to appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this an application for permission to appeal (to which Rule 26(15) applies)?
      `I wish to file an affidavit in reply to the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you wish to file an affidavit in reply to the application?
      `I filed and served the affidavit on the applicant and the other parties to the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file and serve the affidavit on the applicant and the other parties to the application?
      `the date I filed my affidavit in reply` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file my affidavit in reply?
      `the date I served my affidavit in reply` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve my affidavit in reply?
      `my last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day the Rules give you for this step? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 directs, and if the Court extended or shortened the time under Order 3, rule 4, give the changed last day.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 35(4), have I filed and served my affidavit in reply to the application as required` IS
    `o 19 r 35(4) the affidavit in reply is filed and served as required` `Rule 26(15) provides otherwise because this is an application for permission to appeal` `I wish to file an affidavit in reply to the application` `I filed and served the affidavit on the applicant and the other parties to the application` `the date I filed my affidavit in reply` `the date I served my affidavit in reply` `my last day` NOTHING

@export Under Order 19, rule 35(4), may I file a further affidavit?
GIVEN `the appellate Court gives permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the appellate Court given permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 35(4), may I file a further affidavit` IS
    `o 19 r 35(4) a further affidavit may be filed` `the appellate Court gives permission`

@export Under Order 19, rule 35(5), must a Case be filed for my application to the appellate Court?
GIVEN `my application is an application to the appellate Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application to the appellate Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 35(5), must a Case be filed for my application to the appellate Court` IS
    `o 19 r 35(5) a Case needs to be filed for the application` `my application is an application to the appellate Court`

@export Under Order 19, rule 35(6), have I given security for costs of my application and filed the certificate as required?
GIVEN `I filed an originating application or a summons to the appellate Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file an originating application or a summons to the appellate Court?
      `I have provided security for the opposing party's costs of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you provided security for the opposing party's costs of the application?
      `I have filed the certificate for security for costs in Form 36` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you filed the certificate for security for costs in Form 36?
      `I did both when I filed the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you do both at the time you filed the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 35(6), have I given security for costs of my application and filed the certificate as required` IS
    `o 19 r 35(6) the party has provided security for costs and filed the certificate as required` `I filed an originating application or a summons to the appellate Court` `I have provided security for the opposing party's costs of the application` `I have filed the certificate for security for costs in Form 36` `I did both when I filed the application`

@export Under Order 19, rule 35(7), need all the applicants give only one set of security?
GIVEN `there is more than one applicant in an application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there more than one applicant in the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 35(7), need all the applicants give only one set of security` IS
    `o 19 r 35(7) the applicants need to provide only one set of security for the costs of the application` `there is more than one applicant in an application`

@export Under Order 19, rule 35(8), must I give security for each opposing party or each set of opposing parties?
GIVEN `there is more than one opposing party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there more than one opposing party?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 35(8), must I give security for each opposing party or each set of opposing parties` IS
    `o 19 r 35(8) the applicant must provide security for each opposing party or each set of opposing parties` `there is more than one opposing party`

@export Under Order 19, rule 35(8), how many sets of security must I give for my application?
GIVEN `the number of opposing parties` IS A NUMBER @desc How many opposing parties are there? Count each opposing party, even where two or more are represented by the same firm of solicitors.
      `the number of sets of opposing parties, where opposing parties represented by the same firm of solicitors are one set` IS A NUMBER @desc How many sets of opposing parties are there, counting opposing parties represented by the same firm of solicitors as one set?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 35(8), how many sets of security must I give for my application` IS
    `o 19 r 35(8) the number of sets of security the applicant must provide` `the number of opposing parties` `the number of sets of opposing parties, where opposing parties represented by the same firm of solicitors are one set`

@export Under Order 19, rule 35(9), is my security for the application in a form the Rules allow?
GIVEN `the form of my security` IS A `o 19 r 35(9) form of security` @desc In what form is your security: a solicitor's undertaking in Form 37, a deposit in the Registry or with the Accountant-General, or any other form?
      `the undertaking is filed and served on the respondent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a solicitor's undertaking, is it filed and served on the respondent?
      `the form is acceptable to the parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is another form, is it acceptable to the parties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 35(9), is my security for the application in a form the Rules allow` IS
    `o 19 r 35(9) the security is in a form the text allows` `the form of my security` `the undertaking is filed and served on the respondent` `the form is acceptable to the parties`

@export Under Order 19, rule 35(10), how much security must I give for my application?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 35(10), how much security must I give for my application` IS
    `o 19 r 35(10) the amount of security`

@export Under Order 19, rule 35(10), is the security I gave for my application the right amount?
GIVEN `the amount of security I provided` IS A NUMBER @desc How much security did you provide, in dollars?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 35(10), is the security I gave for my application the right amount` IS
    `o 19 r 35(10) the security is in the amount the text requires` `the amount of security I provided`

