      `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Rule 41 itself or any other written law provide otherwise for this provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 41(10), does this provision of Order 19 apply to my appeal under section 59G of the Medical Registration Act` IS
    `o 19 r 41 the provision applies to proceedings under section 59G of the Medical Registration Act` `which provision` `this Rule or any other written law provides otherwise`

@export Under Order 19, rule 41(10), is this reference to security for costs in Rule 10 to be disregarded in my appeal?
GIVEN `which reference` IS A `o 19 r 41(10)(c) reference in Rule 10` @desc Which reference in Rule 10: the reference to security for costs in Rule 10(2), the reference to security for costs in Rule 10(4)(b)(ii), or any other reference?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 41(10), is this reference to security for costs in Rule 10 to be disregarded in my appeal` IS
    `o 19 r 41(10)(c) the reference in Rule 10 is to be disregarded` `which reference`

@export Under Order 19, rule 41(11), in my appeal under section 59G, what is a reference to the appellate Court or the lower Court in a borrowed provision read as?
GIVEN `which reference` IS A `o 19 r 41(11) reference in a provision mentioned in paragraph (10)` @desc Which reference does the borrowed provision make: to the appellate Court, to the lower Court, or to any other court or body?
      `my proceedings are an appeal under section 59G of the Medical Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your proceedings an appeal under section 59G of the Medical Registration Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE `o 19 r 41(11) court or body read in its place`
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 41(11), in my appeal under section 59G, what is a reference to the appellate Court or the lower Court in a borrowed provision read as` IS
    `o 19 r 41(11) the court or body that the reference is read as` `which reference` `my proceedings are an appeal under section 59G of the Medical Registration Act`

@export Under Order 19, rule 41(11), does the replacement of courts apply to this provision?
GIVEN `which provision` IS A `o 19 r 41(10) provision` @desc Which provision of Order 19 are you asking about: Rule 7, 8, 10, 11, 12, 34, 35(1), 35(3), 35(4), 35(16) or 37; Rule 1(f); another provision of Division 1; Order 20; or any other provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 41(11), does the replacement of courts apply to this provision` IS
    `o 19 r 41(11) the provision is one to which the replacement of courts applies` `which provision`

@export Under Order 19, rule 41(13), am I the "appellant" in the appeal under section 59G?
GIVEN `I bring an appeal to the General Division under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you bring an appeal to the General Division under paragraph (1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 41(13), am I the "appellant" in the appeal under section 59G` IS
    `o 19 r 41(13) a person is the appellant` `I bring an appeal to the General Division under paragraph (1)`

@export Under Order 19, rule 41(13), am I the "respondent" in the appeal under section 59G?
GIVEN `I am the respondent in the originating application filed under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the respondent in the originating application filed under paragraph (1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 41(13), am I the "respondent" in the appeal under section 59G` IS
    `o 19 r 41(13) a person is the respondent` `I am the respondent in the originating application filed under paragraph (1)`

@export Under Order 19, rule 41(13), is this body a "Disciplinary Tribunal"?
GIVEN `the body has the meaning of Disciplinary Tribunal given by section 2 of the Medical Registration Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a Disciplinary Tribunal as section 2 of the Medical Registration Act defines it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 41(13), is this body a "Disciplinary Tribunal"` IS
    `o 19 r 41(13) a body is a Disciplinary Tribunal` `the body has the meaning of Disciplinary Tribunal given by section 2 of the Medical Registration Act`

@export Under Order 19, rule 41(13), is this document part of the "record of proceedings" in my appeal under section 59G?
GIVEN `which document` IS A `o 19 r 41(13) document` @desc Which document: written grounds of decision, the record of evidence or notes of arguments, an affidavit or statutory declaration, a submission, another document tendered in the proceedings, a compilation of authorities, or any other document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 41(13), is this document part of the "record of proceedings" in my appeal under section 59G` IS
    `o 19 r 41(13) a document is part of the record of proceedings` `which document`

@export Under Order 19, rule 41(13), is this document a "bundle of authorities" in my appeal under section 59G?
GIVEN `which document` IS A `o 19 r 41(13) document` @desc Which document: written grounds of decision, the record of evidence or notes of arguments, an affidavit or statutory declaration, a submission, another document tendered in the proceedings, a compilation of authorities, or any other document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 41(13), is this document a "bundle of authorities" in my appeal under section 59G` IS
    `o 19 r 41(13) a document is a bundle of authorities` `which document`

@export Under Order 19, rule 41(13), may this item be in a "bundle of authorities"?
GIVEN `which item` IS A `o 19 r 41(13) authority` @desc Which item: a case authority, a statute, a law journal article, or any other item?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 19, rule 41(13), may this item be in a "bundle of authorities"` IS
    `o 19 r 41(13) an item may be in a bundle of authorities` `which item`

-- ============================================================
-- roc5: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026 -- Orders 20 to 22
-- (appeals from tribunals and case stated; costs, with Appendix 1; enforcement of judgments and orders) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a party to a civil action in the Singapore courts (a claimant, a defendant, a third party or an appellant), asking,
-- on facts they can state, what they must file or serve, by when, how, at what cost, what the Court may order, and what
-- follows if they do not.  This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions
-- that person would ask.  Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: every question calls one layer-1 rule.
-- A question about the Sheriff, the Registrar or a Judge is asked for what it means to the party (what may be done to
-- them, what they must be given, and by when); there is no seat for an official.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs: yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list, one for each
-- fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
--   * A fact that belongs to another part of the Rules or to another Act (for example whether a relief is "of the nature
--     specified in Order 52, Rule 1", or whether business is "contentious business" under the Legal Profession Act) is
--     asked as "yes / no / I am not sure"; "I am not sure" becomes NOTHING, and a rule that cannot answer without it
--     answers NOTHING.
--   * A period is counted by Order 3, Rule 3, which is another part's.  The person states the last day of the period (or
--     the first day, for a "not earlier than" rule), and the question compares the day of the act with it.
--   * A sum fixed by the Rules is read from the layer-1 module; the person states the facts, never a rule's number.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Rules themselves give; NOTHING means the Rules do not
-- answer on these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").  Never read NOTHING as no.

DECLARE `Under Orders 20 to 22, my answer` IS ONE OF
    `Under Orders 20 to 22, I answer yes`
    `Under Orders 20 to 22, I answer no`
    `Under Orders 20 to 22, I am not sure`

-- Wiring: an answer of yes, no or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.  Not a question.
GIVEN answer IS A `Under Orders 20 to 22, my answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Under Orders 20 to 22, what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `Under Orders 20 to 22, I answer yes` THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Orders 20 to 22, I answer no` THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Orders 20 to 22, I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping


§ `Order 20 -- appeals from tribunals and case stated: my questions`
-- Asked only if you are appealing the decision of a tribunal, or applying for a case to be stated.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 20, rule 1`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 1 this Order applies to the proceeding`
@export Under Order 20, rule 1, does Order 20 apply to my proceeding?
GIVEN `the kind of proceeding I have` IS A `o 20 r 1(1) kind of proceeding` @desc Which kind of proceeding do you have?
      `the appeal or application is provided by the written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the appeal or application is provided by the written law? (yes or no)
      `the appeal is from a State Court constituted under the State Courts Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the appeal is from a State Court constituted under the State Courts Act? (yes or no)
      `the appeal is one that Order 19, Rule 41 otherwise provides for` IS A `Under Orders 20 to 22, my answer` @desc Is it the case that the appeal is one that Order 19, Rule 41 otherwise provides for? (yes, no, or I am not sure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 1, does Order 20 apply to my proceeding` IS
    `o 20 r 1 this Order applies to the proceeding` `the kind of proceeding I have` `the appeal or application is provided by the written law` `the appeal is from a State Court constituted under the State Courts Act` (`Under Orders 20 to 22, what I say, as a fact` `the appeal is one that Order 19, Rule 41 otherwise provides for`)


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 20, rule 2`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 2 a document is part of the record of proceedings`
@export Under Order 20, rule 2, is this document part of the record of proceedings?
GIVEN `the kind of document` IS A `o 20 r 2 kind of document` @desc Which kind of document is it?
      `the document is in respect of the proceedings before the tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is in respect of the proceedings before the tribunal? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 2, is this document part of the record of proceedings` IS
    `o 20 r 2 a document is part of the record of proceedings` `the kind of document` `the document is in respect of the proceedings before the tribunal`

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 2 a body is a tribunal`
@export Under Order 20, rule 2, is the body whose decision I am challenging a tribunal?
GIVEN `the body is an authority, person or body of persons authorised to make decisions under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the body is an authority, person or body of persons authorised to make decisions under a written law? (yes or no)
      `the body is a Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the body is a Court? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 2, is the body whose decision I am challenging a tribunal` IS
    `o 20 r 2 a body is a tribunal` `the body is an authority, person or body of persons authorised to make decisions under a written law` `the body is a Court`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 20, rule 3`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 3(1) the appeal or application is brought in the way the rule requires`
@export Under Order 20, rule 3(1), have I brought my appeal or application in the way the rule requires?
GIVEN `my appeal or application is brought by way of an originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that my appeal or application is brought by way of an originating application? (yes or no)
      `the originating application is supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the originating application is supported by an affidavit? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 3(1), have I brought my appeal or application in the way the rule requires` IS
    `o 20 r 3(1) the appeal or application is brought in the way the rule requires` `my appeal or application is brought by way of an originating application` `the originating application is supported by an affidavit`

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 3(2) the originating application and affidavit are filed and served in time`
@export Under Order 20, rule 3(2), did I file and serve my originating application and affidavit in time?
GIVEN `the date the originating application and the affidavit are filed` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the originating application and the affidavit are filed?
      `the date they are served on all parties who have an interest in the matter` IS A DATE @desc What is the date they are served on all parties who have an interest in the matter?
      `the last day for doing this` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the period for doing this end, counting as Order 3, Rule 3 of the Rules of Court requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 3(2), did I file and serve my originating application and affidavit in time` IS
    `o 20 r 3(2) the originating application and affidavit are filed and served in time` `the date the originating application and the affidavit are filed` `the date they are served on all parties who have an interest in the matter` `the last day for doing this`

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 3(2) the originating application and affidavit are served on every interested party`
@export Under Order 20, rule 3(2), did I serve my originating application and affidavit on every party who has an interest in the matter?
GIVEN `the persons served include all the parties who have an interest in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the persons served include all the parties who have an interest in the matter? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 3(2), did I serve my originating application and affidavit on every party who has an interest in the matter` IS
    `o 20 r 3(2) the originating application and affidavit are served on every interested party` `the persons served include all the parties who have an interest in the matter`

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 3(3) the affidavit states what the rule requires`
@export Under Order 20, rule 3(3), does my affidavit state what the rule requires?
GIVEN `my affidavit states all the facts that are necessary for the appeal or the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that my affidavit states all the facts that are necessary for the appeal or the application? (yes or no)
      `my affidavit states the questions of fact or law to be determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that my affidavit states the questions of fact or law to be determined? (yes or no)
      `my affidavit states the orders that are sought before the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that my affidavit states the orders that are sought before the Court? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 3(3), does my affidavit state what the rule requires` IS
    `o 20 r 3(3) the affidavit states what the rule requires` `my affidavit states all the facts that are necessary for the appeal or the application` `my affidavit states the questions of fact or law to be determined` `my affidavit states the orders that are sought before the Court`

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 3(4) the affidavit must include the record of proceedings`
@export Under Order 20, rule 3(4), must my affidavit include the record of proceedings?
GIVEN `the record of proceedings is available` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the record of proceedings is available? (yes or no)
      `the record of proceedings is necessary for the appeal or the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the record of proceedings is necessary for the appeal or the application? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 3(4), must my affidavit include the record of proceedings` IS
    `o 20 r 3(4) the affidavit must include the record of proceedings` `the record of proceedings is available` `the record of proceedings is necessary for the appeal or the application`

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 3(5) a party served must file and serve an affidavit in reply`
@export Under Order 20, rule 3(5), must I file and serve an affidavit in reply?
GIVEN `the party was served under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party was served under paragraph (2)? (yes or no)
      `an affidavit in reply is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an affidavit in reply is necessary? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 3(5), must I file and serve an affidavit in reply` IS
    `o 20 r 3(5) a party served must file and serve an affidavit in reply` `the party was served under paragraph (2)` `an affidavit in reply is necessary`

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 3(5) the affidavit in reply is filed and served in time`
@export Under Order 20, rule 3(5), did I file and serve my affidavit in reply in time?
GIVEN `the date the affidavit in reply is filed` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the affidavit in reply is filed?
      `the date the affidavit in reply is served` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the affidavit in reply is served?
      `the last day for doing this` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the period for doing this end, counting as Order 3, Rule 3 of the Rules of Court requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 3(5), did I file and serve my affidavit in reply in time` IS
    `o 20 r 3(5) the affidavit in reply is filed and served in time` `the date the affidavit in reply is filed` `the date the affidavit in reply is served` `the last day for doing this`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 20, rule 4`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 4(1) the parties attend a case conference in time`
@export Under Order 20, rule 4(1), did the parties attend a case conference in time?
GIVEN `the parties attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the parties attend the meeting? (yes or no)
      `the meeting is a case conference as described` IS A `Under Orders 20 to 22, my answer` @desc Is it the case that the meeting is a case conference as described? (yes, no, or I am not sure)
      `the date of the case conference` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the case conference?
      `the last day for doing this` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the period for doing this end, counting as Order 3, Rule 3 of the Rules of Court requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 4(1), did the parties attend a case conference in time` IS
    `o 20 r 4(1) the parties attend a case conference in time` `the parties attend the meeting` (`Under Orders 20 to 22, what I say, as a fact` `the meeting is a case conference as described`) `the date of the case conference` `the last day for doing this`

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 4(2) the Court must give the directions that are necessary`
@export Under Order 20, rule 4(2), must the Court give the directions that are necessary at the case conference?
GIVEN `the Court is at the case conference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court is at the case conference? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 4(2), must the Court give the directions that are necessary at the case conference` IS
    `o 20 r 4(2) the Court must give the directions that are necessary` `the Court is at the case conference`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 20, rule 5`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 5(1) the written submissions are filed and served in time`
@export Under Order 20, rule 5(1), did I file and serve my written submissions in time?
GIVEN `the date the written submissions are filed` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the written submissions are filed?
      `the date the written submissions are served` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the written submissions are served?
      `the last day for doing this` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the period for doing this end, counting as Order 3, Rule 3 of the Rules of Court requires?
      `the directions given at the case conference under Rule 4 fix a different time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the directions given at the case conference under Rule 4 fix a different time? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 5(1), did I file and serve my written submissions in time` IS
    `o 20 r 5(1) the written submissions are filed and served in time` `the date the written submissions are filed` `the date the written submissions are served` `the last day for doing this` `the directions given at the case conference under Rule 4 fix a different time`

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 5(2) the written submissions are within the page limit`
@export Under Order 20, rule 5(2), are my written submissions within the page limit?
GIVEN `the number of pages of the written submissions` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of pages of the written submissions? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 5(2), are my written submissions within the page limit` IS
    `o 20 r 5(2) the written submissions are within the page limit` `the number of pages of the written submissions`

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 5(3) the Court may allow the page limit to be exceeded`
@export Under Order 20, rule 5(3), may the Court allow my written submissions to exceed the page limit?
GIVEN `there are special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that there are special circumstances? (yes or no)
      `the fees and additional fees prescribed for the pages in excess of the limit have been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the fees and additional fees prescribed for the pages in excess of the limit have been paid? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 5(3), may the Court allow my written submissions to exceed the page limit` IS
    `o 20 r 5(3) the Court may allow the page limit to be exceeded` `there are special circumstances` `the fees and additional fees prescribed for the pages in excess of the limit have been paid`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 20, rule 6`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 6 the appeal or application operates as a stay of enforcement of the tribunal's decision`
@export Under Order 20, rule 6, does my appeal or application operate as a stay of enforcement of the tribunal's decision?
GIVEN `a written law provides that the appeal or application operates as a stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a written law provides that the appeal or application operates as a stay? (yes or no)
      `the Court has ordered otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has ordered otherwise? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 6, does my appeal or application operate as a stay of enforcement of the tribunal's decision` IS
    `o 20 r 6 the appeal or application operates as a stay of enforcement of the tribunal's decision` `a written law provides that the appeal or application operates as a stay` `the Court has ordered otherwise`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 20, rule 7`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 7(1) the Court hearing the appeal or application has the power`
@export Under Order 20, rule 7(1), does the Court hearing my appeal or application have the power the rule gives it?
GIVEN `the Court is hearing the appeal or the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court is hearing the appeal or the application? (yes or no)
      `the Court has the power when hearing an appeal after trial` IS A `Under Orders 20 to 22, my answer` @desc Is it the case that the Court has the power when hearing an appeal after trial? (yes, no, or I am not sure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 7(1), does the Court hearing my appeal or application have the power the rule gives it` IS
    `o 20 r 7(1) the Court hearing the appeal or application has the power` `the Court is hearing the appeal or the application` (`Under Orders 20 to 22, what I say, as a fact` `the Court has the power when hearing an appeal after trial`)

-- layer 1: roc5-o20.l4, `o 20 r 7(2) the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal has the power`
@export Under Order 20, rule 7(2), does the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal have the power the rule gives it?
GIVEN `an appeal to the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal is permitted in the written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an appeal to the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal is permitted in the written law? (yes or no)
      `the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal is hearing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal is hearing it? (yes or no)
      `the Court has the power when hearing an appeal after trial` IS A `Under Orders 20 to 22, my answer` @desc Is it the case that the Court has the power when hearing an appeal after trial? (yes, no, or I am not sure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 20, rule 7(2), does the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal have the power the rule gives it` IS
    `o 20 r 7(2) the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal has the power` `an appeal to the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal is permitted in the written law` `the Appellate Division or Court of Appeal is hearing it` (`Under Orders 20 to 22, what I say, as a fact` `the Court has the power when hearing an appeal after trial`)


§ `Order 21 -- costs: my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 21, rule 1`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 1(1) this Order applies to the costs`
@export Under Order 21, rule 1(1), does Order 21 apply to my costs?
GIVEN `the business is contentious business` IS A `Under Orders 20 to 22, my answer` @desc Is it the case that the business is contentious business? (yes, no, or I am not sure)
      `any written law provides that this Order applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that any written law provides that this Order applies? (yes or no)
      `the parties consent that this Order applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the parties consent that this Order applies? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 1(1), does Order 21 apply to my costs` IS
    `o 21 r 1(1) this Order applies to the costs` (`Under Orders 20 to 22, what I say, as a fact` `the business is contentious business`) `any written law provides that this Order applies` `the parties consent that this Order applies`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 1(2) costs are assessed costs`
@export Under Order 21, rule 1(2), are costs assessed costs?
GIVEN `the costs were assessed in accordance with this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the costs were assessed in accordance with this Order? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 1(2), are costs assessed costs` IS
    `o 21 r 1(2) costs are assessed costs` `the costs were assessed in accordance with this Order`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 1(2) the business is contentious business`
@export Under Order 21, rule 1(2), is the business contentious business?
GIVEN `the business is contentious business` IS A `Under Orders 20 to 22, my answer` @desc Is it the case that the business is contentious business? (yes, no, or I am not sure)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 1(2), is the business contentious business` IS
    `o 21 r 1(2) the business is contentious business` (`Under Orders 20 to 22, what I say, as a fact` `the business is contentious business`)

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 1(2) a charge is within costs`
@export Under Order 21, rule 1(2), is a charge within costs?
GIVEN `the kind of charge` IS A `o 21 r 1(2) kind of charge` @desc Which kind of charge is it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 1(2), is a charge within costs` IS
    `o 21 r 1(2) a charge is within costs` `the kind of charge`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 1(2) the basis is the indemnity basis`
@export Under Order 21, rule 1(2), is the basis the indemnity basis?
GIVEN `the basis of assessment` IS A `o 21 r 22 basis of assessment` @desc On which basis is the amount of costs to be worked out?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 1(2), is the basis the indemnity basis` IS
    `o 21 r 1(2) the basis is the indemnity basis` `the basis of assessment`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 1(2) the basis is the standard basis`
@export Under Order 21, rule 1(2), is the basis the standard basis?
GIVEN `the basis of assessment` IS A `o 21 r 22 basis of assessment` @desc On which basis is the amount of costs to be worked out?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 1(2), is the basis the standard basis` IS
    `o 21 r 1(2) the basis is the standard basis` `the basis of assessment`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 1(3)(a) a reference to a fund includes a reference to the thing`
@export Under Order 21, rule 1(3)(a), is it the case that a reference to a fund includes a reference to the thing?
GIVEN `the thing is a fund out of which costs are to be paid or which is held by a trustee or personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the thing is a fund out of which costs are to be paid or which is held by a trustee or personal representative? (yes or no)
      `the thing is an estate or property, whether movable or immovable, held for the benefit of any person or class of persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the thing is an estate or property, whether movable or immovable, held for the benefit of any person or class of persons? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 1(3)(a), is it the case that a reference to a fund includes a reference to the thing` IS
    `o 21 r 1(3)(a) a reference to a fund includes a reference to the thing` `the thing is a fund out of which costs are to be paid or which is held by a trustee or personal representative` `the thing is an estate or property, whether movable or immovable, held for the benefit of any person or class of persons`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 1(3)(b) a reference to a fund held by a trustee or personal representative includes a reference to the thing`
@export Under Order 21, rule 1(3)(b), is it the case that a reference to a fund held by a trustee or personal representative includes a reference to the thing?
GIVEN `the thing is a fund held by a trustee or personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the thing is a fund held by a trustee or personal representative? (yes or no)
      `the thing is a fund to which the trustee or personal representative is entitled in that capacity, alone or together with any other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the thing is a fund to which the trustee or personal representative is entitled in that capacity, alone or together with any other person? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 1(3)(b), is it the case that a reference to a fund held by a trustee or personal representative includes a reference to the thing` IS
    `o 21 r 1(3)(b) a reference to a fund held by a trustee or personal representative includes a reference to the thing` `the thing is a fund held by a trustee or personal representative` `the thing is a fund to which the trustee or personal representative is entitled in that capacity, alone or together with any other person`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 21, rule 2`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 2(1) costs are in the discretion of the Court`
@export Under Order 21, rule 2(1), are costs in the discretion of the Court?
GIVEN `the proceedings are in the Supreme Court or the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceedings are in the Supreme Court or the State Courts? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 2(1), are costs in the discretion of the Court` IS
    `o 21 r 2(1) costs are in the discretion of the Court` `the proceedings are in the Supreme Court or the State Courts`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 2(2) the Court must have regard to the circumstance`
@export Under Order 21, rule 2(2), must the Court have regard to the circumstance?
GIVEN `the circumstance the Court has regard to` IS A `o 21 r 2(2) circumstance` @desc Which circumstance are you asking about?
      `the Court is exercising its power to fix or assess costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court is exercising its power to fix or assess costs? (yes or no)
      `the circumstance is relevant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the circumstance is relevant? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 2(2), must the Court have regard to the circumstance` IS
    `o 21 r 2(2) the Court must have regard to the circumstance` `the circumstance the Court has regard to` `the Court is exercising its power to fix or assess costs` `the circumstance is relevant`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 2(3) the costs must be fixed by the Court which heard the matter`
@export Under Order 21, rule 2(3), must the Court that heard the matter fix my costs?
GIVEN `the costs are payable by one party to another party in a matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the costs are payable by one party to another party in a matter? (yes or no)
      `the Court has directed an assessment of the costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has directed an assessment of the costs? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 2(3), must the Court that heard the matter fix my costs` IS
    `o 21 r 2(3) the costs must be fixed by the Court which heard the matter` `the costs are payable by one party to another party in a matter` `the Court has directed an assessment of the costs`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 2(3) the Court heard the parties before it fixed the costs`
@export Under Order 21, rule 2(3), did the Court hear the parties before it fixed the costs?
GIVEN `the Court heard the parties at an oral hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court heard the parties at an oral hearing? (yes or no)
      `the Court had written submissions from the parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court had written submissions from the parties? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 2(3), did the Court hear the parties before it fixed the costs` IS
    `o 21 r 2(3) the Court heard the parties before it fixed the costs` `the Court heard the parties at an oral hearing` `the Court had written submissions from the parties`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 2(4) the costs are payable from the date of the Court's order`
@export Under Order 21, rule 2(4), are my costs payable from the date of the Court's order?
GIVEN `the parties have otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the parties have otherwise agreed? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 2(4), are my costs payable from the date of the Court's order` IS
    `o 21 r 2(4) the costs are payable from the date of the Court's order` `the parties have otherwise agreed`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 2(4) the date from which the costs are payable`
@export Under Order 21, rule 2(4), from what date are my costs payable?
GIVEN `the date of the Court's order` IS A DATE @desc What is the date of the Court's order?
      `the parties have otherwise agreed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the parties have otherwise agreed? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 2(4), from what date are my costs payable` IS
    `o 21 r 2(4) the date from which the costs are payable` `the date of the Court's order` `the parties have otherwise agreed`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 2(5) the Court may order the parties' costs to be set off against one another`
@export Under Order 21, rule 2(5), may the Court order the parties' costs to be set off against one another?
GIVEN `the number of parties whose costs are in question` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of parties whose costs are in question? (a number)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 2(5), may the Court order the parties' costs to be set off against one another` IS
    `o 21 r 2(5) the Court may order the parties' costs to be set off against one another` `the number of parties whose costs are in question`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 2(6) the Court may stay or dismiss the application, action or appeal or make any other order`
@export Under Order 21, rule 2(6), may the Court stay or dismiss my application, action or appeal, or make any other order, because costs ordered have not been paid?
GIVEN `a party refuses or neglects to pay costs ordered within the specified time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a party refuses or neglects to pay costs ordered within the specified time? (yes or no)
      `the costs were ordered in the present proceedings or in some related proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the costs were ordered in the present proceedings or in some related proceedings? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 2(6), may the Court stay or dismiss my application, action or appeal, or make any other order, because costs ordered have not been paid` IS
    `o 21 r 2(6) the Court may stay or dismiss the application, action or appeal or make any other order` `a party refuses or neglects to pay costs ordered within the specified time` `the costs were ordered in the present proceedings or in some related proceedings`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 2(7) the Court hearing the appeal may deal with the costs of the proceedings giving rise to the appeal and of the appeal`
@export Under Order 21, rule 2(7), may the Court hearing the appeal deal with the costs of the proceedings giving rise to the appeal and of the appeal?
GIVEN `the proceeding is an appeal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceeding is an appeal? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 2(7), may the Court hearing the appeal deal with the costs of the proceedings giving rise to the appeal and of the appeal` IS
    `o 21 r 2(7) the Court hearing the appeal may deal with the costs of the proceedings giving rise to the appeal and of the appeal` `the proceeding is an appeal`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 2(8) the General Division may decide the costs of the whole proceedings or direct the other court to decide the costs before the transfer`
@export Under Order 21, rule 2(8), may the General Division decide the costs of the whole proceedings or direct the other court to decide the costs before the transfer?
GIVEN `the proceedings were transferred or removed to the General Division from another court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceedings were transferred or removed to the General Division from another court? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 2(8), may the General Division decide the costs of the whole proceedings or direct the other court to decide the costs before the transfer` IS
    `o 21 r 2(8) the General Division may decide the costs of the whole proceedings or direct the other court to decide the costs before the transfer` `the proceedings were transferred or removed to the General Division from another court`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 21, rule 3`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 3(1) a party is entitled to recover costs from another party`
@export Under Order 21, rule 3(1), am I entitled to recover costs from the other party?
GIVEN `there is an order of the Court for the costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that there is an order of the Court for the costs? (yes or no)
      `a later provision of this Order entitles the party to the costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a later provision of this Order entitles the party to the costs? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 3(1), am I entitled to recover costs from the other party` IS
    `o 21 r 3(1) a party is entitled to recover costs from another party` `there is an order of the Court for the costs` `a later provision of this Order entitles the party to the costs`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 3(2) the Court must order the costs in favour of the successful party`
@export Under Order 21, rule 3(2), must the Court order the costs in my favour as the successful party?
GIVEN `the party is a successful party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party is a successful party? (yes or no)
      `it appears to the Court that in the circumstances of the case some other order should be made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it appears to the Court that in the circumstances of the case some other order should be made? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 3(2), must the Court order the costs in my favour as the successful party` IS
    `o 21 r 3(2) the Court must order the costs in favour of the successful party` `the party is a successful party` `it appears to the Court that in the circumstances of the case some other order should be made`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 3(3) the party making the amendment bears the costs of and occasioned by it`
@export Under Order 21, rule 3(3), do I bear the costs of and occasioned by my amendment?
GIVEN `the amendment was made without permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the amendment was made without permission? (yes or no)
      `the amendment was made in the originating claim or any pleadings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the amendment was made in the originating claim or any pleadings? (yes or no)
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has otherwise ordered? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 3(3), do I bear the costs of and occasioned by my amendment` IS
    `o 21 r 3(3) the party making the amendment bears the costs of and occasioned by it` `the amendment was made without permission` `the amendment was made in the originating claim or any pleadings` `the Court has otherwise ordered`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 3(4) the party making the application bears the costs of and occasioned by it`
@export Under Order 21, rule 3(4), do I bear the costs of and occasioned by my application to extend time?
GIVEN `the application is an application to extend the time fixed by these Rules or the Court for serving or filing any document or doing any other act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is an application to extend the time fixed by these Rules or the Court for serving or filing any document or doing any other act? (yes or no)
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has otherwise ordered? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 3(4), do I bear the costs of and occasioned by my application to extend time` IS
    `o 21 r 3(4) the party making the application bears the costs of and occasioned by it` `the application is an application to extend the time fixed by these Rules or the Court for serving or filing any document or doing any other act` `the Court has otherwise ordered`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 3(5) the person is entitled to the costs out of the fund or the mortgaged property`
@export Under Order 21, rule 3(5), am I entitled to my costs out of the fund or the mortgaged property?
GIVEN `the capacity in which I act` IS A `o 21 r 3(5) capacity` @desc In which capacity do you act in the matter?
      `the person is or has been a party to the proceedings in that capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is or has been a party to the proceedings in that capacity? (yes or no)
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has otherwise ordered? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 3(5), am I entitled to my costs out of the fund or the mortgaged property` IS
    `o 21 r 3(5) the person is entitled to the costs out of the fund or the mortgaged property` `the capacity in which I act` `the person is or has been a party to the proceedings in that capacity` `the Court has otherwise ordered`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 3(5) the costs not recovered from or paid by any other person`
@export Under Order 21, rule 3(5), how much of my costs has not been recovered from or paid by any other person?
GIVEN `the costs of the proceedings` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the costs of the proceedings? (a number)
      `the part recovered from or paid by any other person` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the part recovered from or paid by any other person? (a number)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 3(5), how much of my costs has not been recovered from or paid by any other person` IS
    `o 21 r 3(5) the costs not recovered from or paid by any other person` `the costs of the proceedings` `the part recovered from or paid by any other person`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 21, rule 4`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 4 the Court may disallow or reduce the successful party's costs or order the party to pay costs`
@export Under Order 21, rule 4, may the Court disallow or reduce my costs as the successful party, or order me to pay costs?
GIVEN `the party failed to establish a claim or issue it raised, thereby unnecessarily increasing the time, the costs or the complexity of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party failed to establish a claim or issue it raised, thereby unnecessarily increasing the time, the costs or the complexity of the proceedings? (yes or no)
      `the party did or omitted to do anything unreasonably` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party did or omitted to do anything unreasonably? (yes or no)
      `the party has discharged its duty to consider amicable resolution or to make an offer of amicable resolution` IS A `Under Orders 20 to 22, my answer` @desc Is it the case that the party has discharged its duty to consider amicable resolution or to make an offer of amicable resolution? (yes, no, or I am not sure)
      `the party failed to comply with an order of court, a relevant pre-action protocol or a practice direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party failed to comply with an order of court, a relevant pre-action protocol or a practice direction? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 4, may the Court disallow or reduce my costs as the successful party, or order me to pay costs` IS
    `o 21 r 4 the Court may disallow or reduce the successful party's costs or order the party to pay costs` `the party failed to establish a claim or issue it raised, thereby unnecessarily increasing the time, the costs or the complexity of the proceedings` `the party did or omitted to do anything unreasonably` (`Under Orders 20 to 22, what I say, as a fact` `the party has discharged its duty to consider amicable resolution or to make an offer of amicable resolution`) `the party failed to comply with an order of court, a relevant pre-action protocol or a practice direction`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 21, rule 5`
-- Asked only if the Court is considering, or has made, a costs order against you as a non-party.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 5(1) the Court may order costs against the non-party`
@export Under Order 21, rule 5(1), may the Court order costs against me as a non-party?
GIVEN `it is just to do so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is just to do so? (yes or no)
      `the non-party assigned its right in the action to a party in return for a share of any money or property which that party may recover in the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the non-party assigned its right in the action to a party in return for a share of any money or property which that party may recover in the action? (yes or no)
      `the non-party contributed or agreed to contribute to a party's costs in return for a share of any money or property which that party may recover in the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the non-party contributed or agreed to contribute to a party's costs in return for a share of any money or property which that party may recover in the action? (yes or no)
      `the non-party contributed or agreed to contribute to a party's costs and actively instigates or encourages that party to continue with the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the non-party contributed or agreed to contribute to a party's costs and actively instigates or encourages that party to continue with the action? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 5(1), may the Court order costs against me as a non-party` IS
    `o 21 r 5(1) the Court may order costs against the non-party` `it is just to do so` `the non-party assigned its right in the action to a party in return for a share of any money or property which that party may recover in the action` `the non-party contributed or agreed to contribute to a party's costs in return for a share of any money or property which that party may recover in the action` `the non-party contributed or agreed to contribute to a party's costs and actively instigates or encourages that party to continue with the action`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 5(2) the Court must give the non-party a reasonable opportunity to be heard`
@export Under Order 21, rule 5(2), must the Court give me, as a non-party, a reasonable opportunity to be heard before it orders costs against me?
GIVEN `the Court is about to make an order under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court is about to make an order under paragraph (1)? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 5(2), must the Court give me, as a non-party, a reasonable opportunity to be heard before it orders costs against me` IS
    `o 21 r 5(2) the Court must give the non-party a reasonable opportunity to be heard` `the Court is about to make an order under paragraph (1)`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 5(2) the non-party was given a reasonable opportunity to be heard before the order`
@export Under Order 21, rule 5(2), was I given a reasonable opportunity to be heard before the order was made against me?
GIVEN `the non-party was heard at an oral hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the non-party was heard at an oral hearing? (yes or no)
      `the non-party had the opportunity to make written submissions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the non-party had the opportunity to make written submissions? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 5(2), was I given a reasonable opportunity to be heard before the order was made against me` IS
    `o 21 r 5(2) the non-party was given a reasonable opportunity to be heard before the order` `the non-party was heard at an oral hearing` `the non-party had the opportunity to make written submissions`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 21, rule 6`
-- Asked only if the Court is considering, or has made, a costs order against a solicitor (you or your solicitor).
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 6(1) the Court may make the order against the solicitor`
@export Under Order 21, rule 6(1), may the Court make this order against my solicitor?
GIVEN `the order against the solicitor` IS A `o 21 r 6(1) order against a solicitor` @desc Which order against the solicitor is in question?
      `the solicitor is responsible, either personally or through an employee or agent, for incurring costs unreasonably in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the solicitor is responsible, either personally or through an employee or agent, for incurring costs unreasonably in the proceedings? (yes or no)
      `the client has been ordered to pay costs in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the client has been ordered to pay costs in the proceedings? (yes or no)
      `costs are payable by another party in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that costs are payable by another party in the proceedings? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 6(1), may the Court make this order against my solicitor` IS
    `o 21 r 6(1) the Court may make the order against the solicitor` `the order against the solicitor` `the solicitor is responsible, either personally or through an employee or agent, for incurring costs unreasonably in the proceedings` `the client has been ordered to pay costs in the proceedings` `costs are payable by another party in the proceedings`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 6(2) the Court must give the solicitor a reasonable opportunity to be heard`
@export Under Order 21, rule 6(2), must the Court give my solicitor a reasonable opportunity to be heard before it makes the order?
GIVEN `the Court is about to make an order under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court is about to make an order under paragraph (1)? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 6(2), must the Court give my solicitor a reasonable opportunity to be heard before it makes the order` IS
    `o 21 r 6(2) the Court must give the solicitor a reasonable opportunity to be heard` `the Court is about to make an order under paragraph (1)`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 6(2) the solicitor was given a reasonable opportunity to be heard before the order`
@export Under Order 21, rule 6(2), was my solicitor given a reasonable opportunity to be heard before the order was made?
GIVEN `the solicitor was heard at an oral hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the solicitor was heard at an oral hearing? (yes or no)
      `the solicitor had the opportunity to make written submissions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the solicitor had the opportunity to make written submissions? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 6(2), was my solicitor given a reasonable opportunity to be heard before the order was made` IS
    `o 21 r 6(2) the solicitor was given a reasonable opportunity to be heard before the order` `the solicitor was heard at an oral hearing` `the solicitor had the opportunity to make written submissions`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 6(3) the Court may direct that notice be given to the solicitor's client`
@export Under Order 21, rule 6(3), may the Court direct that notice be given to the solicitor's client?
GIVEN `there are proceedings or an order against the solicitor under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that there are proceedings or an order against the solicitor under this Rule? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 6(3), may the Court direct that notice be given to the solicitor's client` IS
    `o 21 r 6(3) the Court may direct that notice be given to the solicitor's client` `there are proceedings or an order against the solicitor under this Rule`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 6(4) the Court may direct or authorise the Attorney-General to attend and take part`
@export Under Order 21, rule 6(4), may the Court direct or authorise the Attorney-General to attend and take part?
GIVEN `the proceedings or inquiry are under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceedings or inquiry are under this Rule? (yes or no)
      `the Court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court thinks fit? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 6(4), may the Court direct or authorise the Attorney-General to attend and take part` IS
    `o 21 r 6(4) the Court may direct or authorise the Attorney-General to attend and take part` `the proceedings or inquiry are under this Rule` `the Court thinks fit`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 21, rule 7`
-- Asked only if you are a successful party who is not represented by solicitors.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 7 the Court may award costs to the successful party not represented by solicitors`
@export Under Order 21, rule 7, may the Court award me costs as a successful party who is not represented by solicitors?
GIVEN `the party is a successful party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party is a successful party? (yes or no)
      `the party is not represented by solicitors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party is not represented by solicitors? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 7, may the Court award me costs as a successful party who is not represented by solicitors` IS
    `o 21 r 7 the Court may award costs to the successful party not represented by solicitors` `the party is a successful party` `the party is not represented by solicitors`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 21, rule 8`
-- Asked only if the money is claimed for, or paid to, a minor or a person who lacks capacity.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 8 the costs payable by the claimant or the claimant's solicitor must be fixed or approved by the Court or assessed by the Registrar`
@export Under Order 21, rule 8, must the costs payable by the claimant or the claimant's solicitor be fixed or approved by the Court or assessed by the Registrar?
GIVEN `the person for whom the money is claimed` IS A `o 21 r 8 person for whom money is claimed` @desc For which kind of person is the money claimed, recovered or paid into Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 8, must the costs payable by the claimant or the claimant's solicitor be fixed or approved by the Court or assessed by the Registrar` IS
    `o 21 r 8 the costs payable by the claimant or the claimant's solicitor must be fixed or approved by the Court or assessed by the Registrar` `the person for whom the money is claimed`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 21, rule 9`
-- Asked only if the claimant discontinued, or the claimant accepted money paid into Court.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-general.l4, `o 21 r 9(1) the defendant is entitled to the costs incurred to the time of discontinuance`
