§§ `Order 21, rule 20`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-assessment.l4, `o 21 r 20(1) the bill of costs has the three separate sections`
@export Under Order 21, rule 20(1), does my bill of costs have the three separate sections?
GIVEN `my bill of costs sets out work done in the cause or matter, except for assessment of costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that my bill of costs sets out work done in the cause or matter, except for assessment of costs? (yes or no)
      `my bill of costs sets out work done for and in the assessment of costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that my bill of costs sets out work done for and in the assessment of costs? (yes or no)
      `my bill of costs sets out all disbursements made in the cause or matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that my bill of costs sets out all disbursements made in the cause or matter? (yes or no)
      `the three are in separate sections` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the three are in separate sections? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 20(1), does my bill of costs have the three separate sections` IS
    `o 21 r 20(1) the bill of costs has the three separate sections` `my bill of costs sets out work done in the cause or matter, except for assessment of costs` `my bill of costs sets out work done for and in the assessment of costs` `my bill of costs sets out all disbursements made in the cause or matter` `the three are in separate sections`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-assessment.l4, `o 21 r 20(2) the costs are indicated as the rule requires`
@export Under Order 21, rule 20(2), are the costs indicated as the rule requires?
GIVEN `the costs for work done in the cause or matter are one global sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the costs for work done in the cause or matter are one global sum? (yes or no)
      `the costs for work done in the assessment of costs are one global sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the costs for work done in the assessment of costs are one global sum? (yes or no)
      `the sum for each item of disbursement is set out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the sum for each item of disbursement is set out? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 20(2), are the costs indicated as the rule requires` IS
    `o 21 r 20(2) the costs are indicated as the rule requires` `the costs for work done in the cause or matter are one global sum` `the costs for work done in the assessment of costs are one global sum` `the sum for each item of disbursement is set out`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-assessment.l4, `o 21 r 20(3) the bill of costs sets out the goods and services tax`
@export Under Order 21, rule 20(3), is it the case that the bill of costs sets out the goods and services tax?
GIVEN `goods and services tax is payable on the costs claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that goods and services tax is payable on the costs claimed? (yes or no)
      `the bill sets out the amount of goods and services tax payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the bill sets out the amount of goods and services tax payable? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 20(3), is it the case that the bill of costs sets out the goods and services tax` IS
    `o 21 r 20(3) the bill of costs sets out the goods and services tax` `goods and services tax is payable on the costs claimed` `the bill sets out the amount of goods and services tax payable`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-assessment.l4, `o 21 r 20(4) the bill of costs is headed as the rule requires`
@export Under Order 21, rule 20(4), is the bill of costs headed as the rule requires?
GIVEN `my bill of costs is headed in the cause or matter to which the bill relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that my bill of costs is headed in the cause or matter to which the bill relates? (yes or no)
      `my bill of costs is headed with the name of the party whose bill it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that my bill of costs is headed with the name of the party whose bill it is? (yes or no)
      `my bill of costs is headed with the judgment, direction or order under which the bill is to be assessed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that my bill of costs is headed with the judgment, direction or order under which the bill is to be assessed? (yes or no)
      `my bill of costs is headed with the basis of assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that my bill of costs is headed with the basis of assessment? (yes or no)
      `my bill of costs is headed with whether the bill is to be assessed between party and party or solicitor and client` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that my bill of costs is headed with whether the bill is to be assessed between party and party or solicitor and client? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 20(4), is the bill of costs headed as the rule requires` IS
    `o 21 r 20(4) the bill of costs is headed as the rule requires` `my bill of costs is headed in the cause or matter to which the bill relates` `my bill of costs is headed with the name of the party whose bill it is` `my bill of costs is headed with the judgment, direction or order under which the bill is to be assessed` `my bill of costs is headed with the basis of assessment` `my bill of costs is headed with whether the bill is to be assessed between party and party or solicitor and client`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-assessment.l4, `o 21 r 20(5) the bill of costs is endorsed as the rule requires`
@export Under Order 21, rule 20(5), is the bill of costs endorsed as the rule requires?
GIVEN `my bill of costs is endorsed with the name or firm and business address of the solicitor whose bill it is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that my bill of costs is endorsed with the name or firm and business address of the solicitor whose bill it is? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 20(5), is the bill of costs endorsed as the rule requires` IS
    `o 21 r 20(5) the bill of costs is endorsed as the rule requires` `my bill of costs is endorsed with the name or firm and business address of the solicitor whose bill it is`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-assessment.l4, `o 21 r 20(6) the bill of costs for contentious business has the content the rule requires`
@export Under Order 21, rule 20(6), does the bill of costs for contentious business have the content the rule requires?
GIVEN `the assessment is for contentious business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the assessment is for contentious business? (yes or no)
      `my bill of costs sets out sufficient information to enable the Registrar to have regard to the circumstances mentioned in Rule 2(2) and complies with the requirements in the practice directions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that my bill of costs sets out sufficient information to enable the Registrar to have regard to the circumstances mentioned in Rule 2(2) and complies with the requirements in the practice directions? (yes or no)
      `where attendances, telephone conversations and correspondence are concerned, it states the number of each and, where possible, the total hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that where attendances, telephone conversations and correspondence are concerned, it states the number of each and, where possible, the total hours? (yes or no)
      `where costs have already been awarded for any of the events set out, it indicates this fact and the amount awarded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that where costs have already been awarded for any of the events set out, it indicates this fact and the amount awarded? (yes or no)
      `my bill of costs contains a succinct narrative of the legal and factual issues involved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that my bill of costs contains a succinct narrative of the legal and factual issues involved? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 20(6), does the bill of costs for contentious business have the content the rule requires` IS
    `o 21 r 20(6) the bill of costs for contentious business has the content the rule requires` `the assessment is for contentious business` `my bill of costs sets out sufficient information to enable the Registrar to have regard to the circumstances mentioned in Rule 2(2) and complies with the requirements in the practice directions` `where attendances, telephone conversations and correspondence are concerned, it states the number of each and, where possible, the total hours` `where costs have already been awarded for any of the events set out, it indicates this fact and the amount awarded` `my bill of costs contains a succinct narrative of the legal and factual issues involved`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-assessment.l4, `o 21 r 20(6)(e) the bill of costs may contain the lists of authorities cited`
@export Under Order 21, rule 20(6)(e), may the bill of costs contain the lists of authorities cited?
GIVEN `the assessment is for contentious business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the assessment is for contentious business? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 20(6)(e), may the bill of costs contain the lists of authorities cited` IS
    `o 21 r 20(6)(e) the bill of costs may contain the lists of authorities cited` `the assessment is for contentious business`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-assessment.l4, `o 21 r 20(6)(f) the work is work done in the cause or matter`
@export Under Order 21, rule 20(6)(f), is the work I did work done in the cause or matter?
GIVEN `the assessment is for contentious business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the assessment is for contentious business? (yes or no)
      `the work is work done in connection with the negotiation of a settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the work is work done in connection with the negotiation of a settlement? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 20(6)(f), is the work I did work done in the cause or matter` IS
    `o 21 r 20(6)(f) the work is work done in the cause or matter` `the assessment is for contentious business` `the work is work done in connection with the negotiation of a settlement`


