-- layer 1: roc5-o21-assessment.l4, `o 21 r 21(1) the Registrar may disallow the costs of the party's attendance`
@export Under Order 21, rule 21(1), may the Registrar disallow the costs of the party's attendance?
GIVEN `the costs are to be paid out of a fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the costs are to be paid out of a fund? (yes or no)
      `the party is not entitled to attend by virtue of the Registrar's directions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party is not entitled to attend by virtue of the Registrar's directions? (yes or no)
      `the Registrar considers the party's attendance unnecessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar considers the party's attendance unnecessary? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 21(1), may the Registrar disallow the costs of the party's attendance` IS
    `o 21 r 21(1) the Registrar may disallow the costs of the party's attendance` `the costs are to be paid out of a fund` `the party is not entitled to attend by virtue of the Registrar's directions` `the Registrar considers the party's attendance unnecessary`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-assessment.l4, `o 21 r 21(2) the Registrar may adjourn the assessment and direct the solicitor to send a copy of the bill`
@export Under Order 21, rule 21(2), may the Registrar adjourn the assessment and direct the solicitor to send a copy of the bill?
GIVEN `the Court has directed that a solicitor's bill of costs be assessed for the purpose of being paid out of a fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has directed that a solicitor's bill of costs be assessed for the purpose of being paid out of a fund? (yes or no)
      `the Registrar thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar thinks fit? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 21(2), may the Registrar adjourn the assessment and direct the solicitor to send a copy of the bill` IS
    `o 21 r 21(2) the Registrar may adjourn the assessment and direct the solicitor to send a copy of the bill` `the Court has directed that a solicitor's bill of costs be assessed for the purpose of being paid out of a fund` `the Registrar thinks fit`


