    `o 21 r 22 in whose favour the doubts of the Registrar are resolved` `the basis of assessment`

-- layer 1: roc5-o21-assessment.l4, `o 21 r 22(1) the basis on which the amount of costs is allowed`
@export Under Order 21, rule 22(1), on what basis is the amount of my costs allowed?
GIVEN `an order is made that the costs of one party to the proceedings be paid by another party to those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an order is made that the costs of one party to the proceedings be paid by another party to those proceedings? (yes or no)
      `an order is made for the payment of costs out of any fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an order is made for the payment of costs out of any fund? (yes or no)
      `no order for costs is required` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that no order for costs is required? (yes or no)
      `it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE `o 21 r 22 basis of assessment`
DECIDE `Under Order 21, rule 22(1), on what basis is the amount of my costs allowed` IS
    `o 21 r 22(1) the basis on which the amount of costs is allowed` `an order is made that the costs of one party to the proceedings be paid by another party to those proceedings` `an order is made for the payment of costs out of any fund` `no order for costs is required` `it appears to the Court to be appropriate to order costs to be assessed on the indemnity basis`

