      `more than 6 years have passed since the date of the Court order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have more than 6 years passed since the date of the Court order? (yes or no; if exactly 6 years have passed, or fewer, answer no; count the years as Order 3, Rule 3 of the Rules of Court requires)
      `a change has occurred in the identity of the enforcement applicant or the enforcement respondent since the date of the Court order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a change has occurred in the identity of the enforcement applicant or the enforcement respondent since the date of the Court order? (yes or no)
      `the Court order requires the enforcement respondent to pay money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court order requires the enforcement respondent to pay money? (yes or no)
      `interest is payable and continues to accumulate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that interest is payable and continues to accumulate? (yes or no)
      `a specific property is to be seized, other than property already specified in the Court order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a specific property is to be seized, other than property already specified in the Court order? (yes or no)
      `the specific property is not in the possession or control of the enforcement respondent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the specific property is not in the possession or control of the enforcement respondent? (yes or no)
      `a deposit of money or other debt due to the enforcement respondent from any non-party is to be attached` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a deposit of money or other debt due to the enforcement respondent from any non-party is to be attached? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 22, rule 2(4), must my affidavit supporting the application state this item` IS
