§§ `Order 22, rule 12`
-- Asked only if the Court order provides for payment by instalments.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o22-objection.l4, `o 22 r 12 the enforcement applicant may apply for an enforcement order in respect of the instalments due and unpaid`
@export Under Order 22, rule 12, may the enforcement applicant apply for an enforcement order in respect of the instalments due and unpaid?
GIVEN `a Court order made under section 43 of the State Courts Act or under any other written law provides for payment by instalments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a Court order made under section 43 of the State Courts Act or under any other written law provides for payment by instalments? (yes or no)
      `an instalment is due and unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an instalment is due and unpaid? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 22, rule 12, may the enforcement applicant apply for an enforcement order in respect of the instalments due and unpaid` IS
    `o 22 r 12 the enforcement applicant may apply for an enforcement order in respect of the instalments due and unpaid` `a Court order made under section 43 of the State Courts Act or under any other written law provides for payment by instalments` `an instalment is due and unpaid`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 22, rule 13`
-- Asked only if someone applies to stay enforcement.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- layer 1: roc5-o22-objection.l4, `o 22 r 13(1) the party may apply for stay of enforcement or stay of the enforcement order`
@export Under Order 22, rule 13(1), may I apply for a stay of enforcement or of the enforcement order?
GIVEN `the party is liable under a Court order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party is liable under a Court order? (yes or no)
      `there is a special case making it inappropriate to enforce the Court order immediately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that there is a special case making it inappropriate to enforce the Court order immediately? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 22, rule 13(1), may I apply for a stay of enforcement or of the enforcement order` IS
    `o 22 r 13(1) the party may apply for stay of enforcement or stay of the enforcement order` `the party is liable under a Court order` `there is a special case making it inappropriate to enforce the Court order immediately`

-- layer 1: roc5-o22-objection.l4, `o 22 r 13(2) the Court may order a stay of enforcement or of an enforcement order for the duration`
@export Under Order 22, rule 13(2), may the Court order a stay of enforcement or of an enforcement order for the duration?
GIVEN `how long the stay lasts` IS A `o 22 r 13(2) how long the stay lasts` @desc For how long is the stay to last?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 22, rule 13(2), may the Court order a stay of enforcement or of an enforcement order for the duration` IS
    `o 22 r 13(2) the Court may order a stay of enforcement or of an enforcement order for the duration` `how long the stay lasts`

-- layer 1: roc5-o22-objection.l4, `o 22 r 13(3) the order may give the direction to the Sheriff`
@export Under Order 22, rule 13(3), may the order give the direction to the Sheriff?
GIVEN `the direction to the Sheriff` IS A `o 22 r 13(3) direction to the Sheriff` @desc Which direction to the Sheriff are you asking about?
      `the Sheriff has seized properties or attached a debt under the enforcement order before the Court orders a stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Sheriff has seized properties or attached a debt under the enforcement order before the Court orders a stay? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 22, rule 13(3), may the order give the direction to the Sheriff` IS
    `o 22 r 13(3) the order may give the direction to the Sheriff` `the direction to the Sheriff` `the Sheriff has seized properties or attached a debt under the enforcement order before the Court orders a stay`

-- ============================================================
-- roc6: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026 -- Orders 23 to 27, THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a party to a civil action in the Singapore courts (a claimant, a defendant, a third party or an appellant), asking on
-- facts they can state what they must file or serve, by when, how, at what cost, what the Court may order, and what follows if
-- they do not.  This layer phrases rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that person would ask.
-- Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question builds the module's inputs from the person's answers and calls
-- the module's function.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, a word or a choice from a list -- one for each fact
-- the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
--   * A fact the person may not know is asked as "Yes / No / I am not sure" (`roc6 My answer`); "I am not sure" becomes NOTHING,
--     and a rule that cannot answer without it answers NOTHING.
--   * Where a Rule counts a period, the person gives the LAST DAY of it as a date, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it (that Rule is
--     in another part of the Rules of Court and is not restated here).  The question then asks whether the act was done on or
--     before that day.
--   * A court is chosen from the core's list of courts, and a kind of proceeding from the module's own list of kinds.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Rules themselves give; NOTHING means the Rules do not answer on
-- these facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (roc6)").  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- There is no seat for an official.  Rules that address only the Registrar, the Accountant-General, the Sheriff or the Chief Justice
-- (for example Order 26 rules 1 and 2, Order 27 rules 5, 7, 12 to 16 and 18 to 21) are in layer 1 and have no question here.

DECLARE `roc6 My answer` IS ONE OF
    `roc6 Yes`
    `roc6 No`
    `roc6 I am not sure`

-- Wiring: the person's answer becomes the modules' MAYBE BOOLEAN.  Not a question.
GIVEN answer IS A `roc6 My answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`roc6 what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `roc6 Yes` THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc6 No` THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc6 I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping


§ `Order 23 -- Contempt of court (committal) -- my questions`

-- O 23 r 3(3).  The affidavit that supports an application for permission to apply for a committal order.
@export Under Order 23, rule 3(3), does the affidavit supporting my application for permission set out what the Rule requires?
GIVEN `my application is supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application for permission supported by an affidavit?
      `the affidavit sets out my name, description and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit set out your name, description and address, as the committal applicant (Rule 3(3)(a))?
      `the affidavit sets out the committal respondent's name, description and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit set out the committal respondent's name, description and address (Rule 3(3)(b))?
      `the affidavit sets out the grounds on which the committal order is sought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit set out the grounds on which the committal order is sought (Rule 3(3)(c))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 23, rule 3(3), does the affidavit supporting my application for permission set out what the Rule requires` IS
    `o 23 r 3(3) the affidavit supporting the application sets out what is required` `my application is supported by an affidavit` `the affidavit sets out my name, description and address` `the affidavit sets out the committal respondent's name, description and address` `the affidavit sets out the grounds on which the committal order is sought`

-- O 23 r 4(1).  The committal order must be applied for within 14 days after permission.
@export Under Order 23, rule 4(1), did I apply for the committal order within 14 days after the Court gave permission?
GIVEN `the Court has given permission under Rule 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given you permission under Rule 3 to apply for a committal order?
      `the date I applied for the committal order` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you apply for the committal order?
      `the last day for this` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for applying, 14 days after permission was granted, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 23, rule 4(1), did I apply for the committal order within 14 days after the Court gave permission` IS
    `o 23 r 4(1) the application for the committal order is made within 14 days after permission` `the Court has given permission under Rule 3` `the date I applied for the committal order` `the last day for this`

-- O 23 r 4(2).  At least 21 days between service on the committal respondent and the hearing.
@export Under Order 23, rule 4(2), is there at least 21 days between serving the committal respondent and the hearing date?
GIVEN `the date the committal respondent was served` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the committal respondent served?
      `the last day for this` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for serving, so that there are at least 21 days before the hearing date, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 23, rule 4(2), is there at least 21 days between serving the committal respondent and the hearing date` IS
    `o 23 r 4(2) there are at least 21 days between the service and the hearing date` `the date the committal respondent was served` `the last day for this`

-- O 23 r 7(3).  The committal applicant may rely only on the grounds set out in the affidavit.
@export Under Order 23, rule 7(3), may I, as the committal applicant, rely on this ground at the hearing?
GIVEN `the ground is set out in my affidavit under Rule 3(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ground set out in your affidavit under Rule 3(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 23, rule 7(3), may I, as the committal applicant, rely on this ground at the hearing` IS
    `o 23 r 7(3) the committal applicant may rely on the ground` `the ground is set out in my affidavit under Rule 3(3)`

-- O 23 r 8(3).  Lifting a suspension of a committal order.
@export Under Order 23, rule 8(3), may I apply for the suspension of the committal order to be lifted?
GIVEN `the committal respondent has broken a term of the suspension` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the committal respondent broken a term on which the committal order was suspended?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 23, rule 8(3), may I apply for the suspension of the committal order to be lifted` IS
    `o 23 r 8(3) the committal applicant may apply for the suspension to be lifted` `the committal respondent has broken a term of the suspension`

-- O 23 r 11(1).  The committal order is in Form 42.
@export Under Order 23, rule 11(1), is my committal order in the form the Rules require?
GIVEN `the form my committal order is in` IS A STRING @desc Which form is your committal order in (for example "Form 42")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 23, rule 11(1), is my committal order in the form the Rules require` IS
    `o 23 r 11(1) the committal order is in the form required` `the form my committal order is in`

-- O 23 r 15(4).  Permission to give a non-publication direction lapses if the direction is not served within 14 days.
@export Under Order 23, rule 15(4), has the Court's permission to give the non-publication direction lapsed?
GIVEN `I have served the non-publication direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you served the non-publication direction?
      `the date I served it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve it? (ignored if you have not)
      `the last day for this` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for serving the direction, 14 days after permission, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 23, rule 15(4), has the Court's permission to give the non-publication direction lapsed` IS
    `o 23 r 15(4) the Court's permission to give the non-publication direction lapses` (IF `I have served the non-publication direction` THEN JUST `the date I served it` ELSE NOTHING) `the last day for this` `the date I am asking about`

-- O 23 r 16(2).  An application to vary or set aside a non-publication direction is made within 14 days after the direction is served.
@export Under Order 23, rule 16(2), did I apply in time to vary or set aside the non-publication direction?
GIVEN `my application is under section 13(9) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application one under section 13(9) of the Administration of Justice (Protection) Act 2016?
      `the date I applied` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you apply?
      `the last day for this` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for applying, 14 days after the direction was served on you, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 23, rule 16(2), did I apply in time to vary or set aside the non-publication direction` IS
    `o 23 r 16(2) the application is made within 14 days after the direction is served` `my application is under section 13(9) of the Act` `the date I applied` `the last day for this`


§ `Order 24 -- Prerogative orders -- my questions`

-- O 24 r 2(2).  No application for a prerogative order before the applicant has exhausted every appeal or other remedy.
@export Under Order 24, rule 2(2), may I apply for a prerogative order now?
GIVEN `I have exhausted every right of appeal and other remedy under any written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you used up every right of appeal and every other remedy a written law gives you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 24, rule 2(2), may I apply for a prerogative order now` IS
    `o 24 r 2(2) the application for a prerogative order may be made` `I have exhausted every right of appeal and other remedy under any written law`

-- O 24 r 4(2).  The documents in an application for an Order for Review of Detention are served within 2 working days after filing.
@export Under Order 24, rule 4(2), did I serve the documents in time?
GIVEN `the date I served the documents` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the documents on the defendant and the Attorney-General?
      `the last day for this` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for serving, 2 working days after filing, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
      `I served them as soon as it was practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve them as soon as it was practicable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 24, rule 4(2), did I serve the documents in time` IS
    `o 24 r 4(2) the document is served as soon as practicable and no later than 2 working days after it is filed` `the date I served the documents` `the last day for this` `I served them as soon as it was practicable`

-- O 24 r 5(2).  Permission to apply for a Mandatory, Prohibiting or Quashing Order is applied for within 3 months.
@export Under Order 24, rule 5(2), did I apply in time for permission to apply for a Mandatory Order, Prohibiting Order or Quashing Order?
GIVEN `a written law gives a different time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a written law give a different time for this application?
      `the date I applied for permission` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you apply for permission?
      `the last day for this` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for applying, 3 months after the omission, judgment, order, conviction or proceedings, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 24, rule 5(2), did I apply in time for permission to apply for a Mandatory Order, Prohibiting Order or Quashing Order` IS
    `o 24 r 5(2) the application for permission is made within 3 months after the omission, judgment, order, conviction or proceedings` `a written law gives a different time` `the date I applied for permission` `the last day for this`

-- O 24 r 5(4).  The applicant is bound by the grounds and relief in the statement.
@export Under Order 24, rule 5(4), may I rely on this ground or ask for this relief?
GIVEN `the ground or relief is set out in my statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the ground or relief set out in your statement?
      `the Court allows me to rely on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court allowed you to rely on it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 24, rule 5(4), may I rely on this ground or ask for this relief` IS
    `o 24 r 5(4) the applicant may rely on the ground or seek the relief` `the ground or relief is set out in my statement` `the Court allows me to rely on it`

-- O 24 r 6(1).  Where permission has been granted, the application for the Order is made by summons in the originating application.
@export Under Order 24, rule 6(1), is my application for the Order made the way the Rule requires?
GIVEN `permission has been granted to apply for the Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has permission been granted to apply for a Mandatory Order, Prohibiting Order or Quashing Order?
      `I made it by summons in the originating application in which permission was obtained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make the application by summons in the originating application in which permission was obtained?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 24, rule 6(1), is my application for the Order made the way the Rule requires` IS
    `o 24 r 6(1) the application for the Order is made by summons in the originating application` `permission has been granted to apply for the Order` `I made it by summons in the originating application in which permission was obtained`

-- O 24 r 6(2).  The permission lapses unless the summons is filed within 14 days after it was granted.
@export Under Order 24, rule 6(2), has the permission I was granted lapsed?
GIVEN `I have filed the summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you filed the summons?
      `the date I filed the summons` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file it? (ignored if you have not)
      `the last day for this` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for filing the summons, 14 days after permission was granted, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 24, rule 6(2), has the permission I was granted lapsed` IS
    `o 24 r 6(2) the permission lapses` (IF `I have filed the summons` THEN JUST `the date I filed the summons` ELSE NOTHING) `the last day for this` `the date I am asking about`


§ `Order 24A -- Post-appeal applications in capital cases -- my questions`

-- O 24A r 2(2).  The written submissions and the other documents are filed at the same time as the application for PACC permission.
@export Under Order 24A, rule 2(2), did I file my written submissions and the other documents at the same time as the application for PACC permission?
GIVEN `the date I filed the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the application for PACC permission?
      `the date I filed the written submissions` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the written submissions in support?
      `the date I filed the other documents` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the other documents mentioned in paragraph (4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 24A, rule 2(2), did I file my written submissions and the other documents at the same time as the application for PACC permission` IS
    `o 24A r 2(2) the written submissions and the other documents are filed at the same time as the application` `the date I filed the application` `the date I filed the written submissions` `the date I filed the other documents`

-- O 24A r 2(3).  35 pages unless the Court of Appeal otherwise allows.
@export Under Order 24A, rule 2(3), are my written submissions within the page limit?
GIVEN `the number of pages, including any cover page and contents page` IS A NUMBER @desc How many pages are your written submissions, counting any cover page and contents page?
      `the Court of Appeal allows more` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court of Appeal allowed you more pages?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 24A, rule 2(3), are my written submissions within the page limit` IS
    `o 24A r 2(3) the written submissions are within the page limit` `the number of pages, including any cover page and contents page` `the Court of Appeal allows more`

-- O 24A r 2(10)(a).  The respondent's written submissions are filed within 3 days.
@export Under Order 24A, rule 2(10)(a), did I, as respondent, file my written submissions in time?
GIVEN `the date I filed my written submissions` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file your written submissions?
      `the last day for this` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for filing, 3 days after the application was filed and served on you, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 24A, rule 2(10)(a), did I, as respondent, file my written submissions in time` IS
    `o 24A r 2(10)(a) the respondent's written submissions are filed within 3 days after the application is filed and served on the respondent` `the date I filed my written submissions` `the last day for this`

-- O 24A r 3(1).  The PACC application is made within 3 days after permission is granted.
@export Under Order 24A, rule 3(1), did I make the PACC application within 3 days after the Court of Appeal granted permission?
GIVEN `the Court of Appeal granted permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Court of Appeal grant the application for PACC permission?
      `the date I made the PACC application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the PACC application?
      `the last day for this` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for making it, 3 days after permission was granted, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 24A, rule 3(1), did I make the PACC application within 3 days after the Court of Appeal granted permission` IS
    `o 24A r 3(1) the PACC application is made within 3 days after permission is granted` `the Court of Appeal granted permission` `the date I made the PACC application` `the last day for this`

-- O 24A r 3(3)(b).  The applicant's written submissions are filed within 3 days after the PACC application is made.
@export Under Order 24A, rule 3(3)(b), did I file my written submissions in support of the PACC application in time?
GIVEN `the date I filed my written submissions` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file your written submissions?
      `the last day for this` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for filing, 3 days after the PACC application was made, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 24A, rule 3(3)(b), did I file my written submissions in support of the PACC application in time` IS
    `o 24A r 3(3)(b) the applicant's written submissions are filed within 3 days after the PACC application is made` `the date I filed my written submissions` `the last day for this`

-- O 24A r 3(4).  The PACC application and any affidavit are served on the respondent within the day on which it is made.
@export Under Order 24A, rule 3(4), did I serve the PACC application on the respondent within the day it was made?
GIVEN `the date I made the PACC application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the PACC application?
      `the date I served it on the respondent` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the application and any affidavit on the respondent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 24A, rule 3(4), did I serve the PACC application on the respondent within the day it was made` IS
    `o 24A r 3(4) the PACC application and the affidavit are served on the respondent within the day on which it is made` `the date I made the PACC application` `the date I served it on the respondent`

-- O 24A r 4.  A notice of appointment in Form 3 when additional counsel are appointed.
@export Under Order 24A, rule 4, must I file and serve a notice of appointment?
GIVEN `I am represented by one or more counsel in the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you represented by one or more counsel in the application?
      `I decide to appoint additional counsel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you decided to appoint one or more additional counsel for the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 24A, rule 4, must I file and serve a notice of appointment` IS
    `o 24A r 4 the applicant must file and serve a notice of appointment` `I am represented by one or more counsel in the application` `I decide to appoint additional counsel`


§ `Order 25 -- Court fees -- my questions`

-- O 25 r 2.  The value of the claim for court fees in the Supreme Court.
@export Under Order 25, rule 2, what is the value of my claim for court fees in the Supreme Court, in dollars?
GIVEN `my claim is for a liquidated demand` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for a liquidated demand?
      `the value specified in the originating process` IS A NUMBER @desc What value is specified in the originating process, in Singapore dollars, without non-contractual interest? (0 if none)
      `my claim is for unliquidated damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for unliquidated damages?
      `my estimate of the damages` IS A NUMBER @desc What is your estimate of the damages, in Singapore dollars, without non-contractual interest? (0 if none)
      `my claim relates to proceedings under the Probate and Administration Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your claim relate to proceedings under the Probate and Administration Act?
      `the value of the estate` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the estate, in Singapore dollars? (0 if none)
      `my claim is a bill of costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim a bill of costs?
      `the total amount claimed in the bill of costs` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the total amount claimed in the bill of costs, in Singapore dollars? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 25, rule 2, what is the value of my claim for court fees in the Supreme Court, in dollars` IS
    `o 25 r 2 the value of the claim` `my claim is for a liquidated demand` `the value specified in the originating process` `my claim is for unliquidated damages` `my estimate of the damages` `my claim relates to proceedings under the Probate and Administration Act` `the value of the estate` `my claim is a bill of costs` `the total amount claimed in the bill of costs`

-- O 25 r 3(3)(a).  A request for refund of hearing fees is made in writing within one month.
@export Under Order 25, rule 3(3)(a), is my request for refund of hearing fees made in writing in time?
GIVEN `my request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request for a refund of hearing fees in writing?
      `the date I made the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the request?
      `the last day for this` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for the request, one month after the date of settlement, discontinuance or withdrawal or the last hearing date, whichever is later, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 25, rule 3(3)(a), is my request for refund of hearing fees made in writing in time` IS
    `o 25 r 3(3)(a) the request for refund of hearing fees is made in writing within one month` `my request is in writing` `the date I made the request` `the last day for this`

-- O 25 r 3(4).  The Court must refund the whole of the hearing fees if notified in writing not later than 14 days before the first hearing date.
@export Under Order 25, rule 3(4), must the Court refund the whole of the hearing fees I paid?
GIVEN `I notified the Court in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the Court in writing?
      `my notice says the cause or matter has been settled or discontinued, or transferred to another Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your notice say that the cause or matter has been settled or discontinued, or transferred to another Court?
      `the date I notified the Court` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you notify the Court?
      `the last day for this` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for notifying the Court, 14 days before the first date fixed for hearing, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 25, rule 3(4), must the Court refund the whole of the hearing fees I paid` IS
    `o 25 r 3(4) the Court must refund the whole of the hearing fees paid` `I notified the Court in writing` `my notice says the cause or matter has been settled or discontinued, or transferred to another Court` `the date I notified the Court` `the last day for this`

-- O 25 r 3(5).  A party dissatisfied with the Registrar's decision may apply by letter to a Judge within 14 days.
@export Under Order 25, rule 3(5), may I ask a Judge by letter to review the Registrar's decision?
GIVEN `I am dissatisfied with a decision of the Registrar made under Rule 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you dissatisfied with a decision the Registrar made under Rule 3?
      `I am applying by letter to a Judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you applying by letter to a Judge?
      `the date I applied` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you apply?
      `the last day for this` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for applying, 14 days after the decision, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 25, rule 3(5), may I ask a Judge by letter to review the Registrar's decision` IS
    `o 25 r 3(5) the party may apply by letter to a Judge to review the decision within 14 days` `I am dissatisfied with a decision of the Registrar made under Rule 3` `I am applying by letter to a Judge` `the date I applied` `the last day for this`

-- O 25 r 4(2)(b).  An application to refund the fee for an unused document is made within 3 months after payment.
@export Under Order 25, rule 4(2)(b), is my application for refund of the fee for an unused document in time?
GIVEN `the date I applied` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you apply for the refund?
      `the last day for this` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for applying, 3 months after the fee was paid, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 25, rule 4(2)(b), is my application for refund of the fee for an unused document in time` IS
    `o 25 r 4(2)(b) the application for refund is made within 3 months after the date of payment` `the date I applied` `the last day for this`

-- O 25 r 5.  No hearing fee for some proceedings.
@export Under Order 25, rule 5, is the hearing in my proceeding one for which no hearing fee is payable?
GIVEN `what my proceeding is` IS A `o 25 r 5 proceeding` @desc Which of these is your proceeding? (choose "some other proceeding" if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 25, rule 5, is the hearing in my proceeding one for which no hearing fee is payable` IS
    `o 25 r 5 no hearing fee is payable` `what my proceeding is`

-- O 25 r 6.  Hearing fees are payable in winding up proceedings fixed on special hearing dates, and in appeals relating to them.
@export Under Order 25, rule 6, is a hearing fee payable in my winding up proceedings?
GIVEN `who is being wound up` IS A `o 25 r 6 entity wound up` @desc Is a company, a limited liability partnership, or a variable capital company or one of its sub-funds being wound up?
      `the proceedings are fixed for hearing in open court on special hearing dates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings fixed for hearing in open court on special hearing dates?
      `the hearing is of an appeal relating to such proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the hearing of an appeal relating to such proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 25, rule 6, is a hearing fee payable in my winding up proceedings` IS
    `o 25 r 6 hearing fees are payable` `who is being wound up` `the proceedings are fixed for hearing in open court on special hearing dates` `the hearing is of an appeal relating to such proceedings`

-- O 25 r 7(1).  A certificate of exemption where the cause relates to criminal proceedings affecting the life or liberty of a party.
@export Under Order 25, rule 7(1), may the Registrar issue me a certificate of exemption from fees and security for costs?
GIVEN `the Registrar is satisfied that the cause or matter relates to criminal proceedings affecting the life or liberty of a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Registrar satisfied that the cause or matter relates to or is predicated upon criminal proceedings affecting the life or liberty of a party?
      `I am that party and I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you that party, and have you applied for the certificate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 25, rule 7(1), may the Registrar issue me a certificate of exemption from fees and security for costs` IS
    `o 25 r 7(1) the Registrar may issue a certificate of exemption` `the Registrar is satisfied that the cause or matter relates to criminal proceedings affecting the life or liberty of a party` `I am that party and I have applied`

-- O 25 r 8(1) with (3).  The $250 Court ADR fee in a District Court case.
@export Under Order 25, rule 8(1), is the Court ADR fee payable by me in my case?
GIVEN `the court my case is in` IS A `Court level` @desc In which court is your case?
      `I am a party in the case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a party in the case?
      `Court ADR services are provided in the case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are Court ADR services provided in the case?
      `what kind of action it is` IS A `o 25 r 8(3) kind of action` @desc What kind of action is it? (choose "some other action" if none of these)
      `it is a non-injury motor accident action as defined in Order 21, Part 6 of Appendix 1` IS A `roc6 My answer` @desc Is it a non-injury motor accident action as defined in Order 21, Part 6 of Appendix 1?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 25, rule 8(1), is the Court ADR fee payable by me in my case` IS
    `o 25 r 8(1) the Court ADR fee is payable by the party` `the court my case is in` `I am a party in the case` `Court ADR services are provided in the case` (`o 25 r 8(3) no Court ADR fee is payable in the action` `what kind of action it is` (`roc6 what I say, as a fact` `it is a non-injury motor accident action as defined in Order 21, Part 6 of Appendix 1`))

-- O 25 r 8(4).  A request for refund of the Court ADR fee is made in writing to the Registrar within one month.
@export Under Order 25, rule 8(4), is my request for refund of the Court ADR fee made in writing to the Registrar in time?
GIVEN `my request is in writing to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your request in writing to the Registrar?
      `the date I made the request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make the request?
      `the last day for this` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for the request, one month after the earlier of the written withdrawal of consent and the settlement or discontinuance, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 25, rule 8(4), is my request for refund of the Court ADR fee made in writing to the Registrar in time` IS
    `o 25 r 8(4) the request for refund of the Court ADR fee is made in writing to the Registrar within one month` `my request is in writing to the Registrar` `the date I made the request` `the last day for this`


§ `Order 26 -- Registry and administration -- my questions`

-- O 26 r 3(4).  Searching, inspecting and copying a document filed in Court.
@export Under Order 26, rule 3(4), may the Registrar allow me to search for, inspect and take a copy of a document filed in Court?
GIVEN `I show a valid interest in the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you show a valid interest in the document?
      `I pay the prescribed fee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you pay the prescribed fee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 26, rule 3(4), may the Registrar allow me to search for, inspect and take a copy of a document filed in Court` IS
    `o 26 r 3(4) the Registrar may allow the person to search for, inspect and take a copy of the document` `I show a valid interest in the document` `I pay the prescribed fee`

-- O 26 r 3(7).  Documents filed in Court are typewritten, printed and follow the practice directions.
@export Under Order 26, rule 3(7), is the document I want to file in the form the Rules require?
GIVEN `it is typewritten and printed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it typewritten and printed?
      `it follows the practice directions on paper, font size, print quality, margins and copies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it follow the practice directions on quality and dimensions of paper, font size, print quality, margins and copies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 26, rule 3(7), is the document I want to file in the form the Rules require` IS
    `o 26 r 3(7) the document filed in Court is typewritten, printed and complies with the practice directions` `it is typewritten and printed` `it follows the practice directions on paper, font size, print quality, margins and copies`

-- O 26 r 5(1).  The Registry is open every day except non-court days.
@export Under Order 26, rule 5(1), must the Registry be open on this day?
GIVEN `the day I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which day are you asking?
      `it is a public holiday` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that day a public holiday?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 26, rule 5(1), must the Registry be open on this day` IS
    `o 26 r 5(1) the Registry must be open on the day` `the day I am asking about` (`Court calendar` WITH `public holidays` IS (IF `it is a public holiday` THEN (LIST `the day I am asking about`) ELSE (LIST)))


§ `Order 27 -- Lodgment in Court, money in Registry and payment to Sheriff -- my questions`

-- O 27 r 2(1).  A trustee paying into Court under section 62 of the Trustees Act.
@export Under Order 27, rule 2(1), have I, as a trustee, applied to pay money into Court in the way the Rule requires?
GIVEN `I wish to pay money into Court under section 62 of the Trustees Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you wish to make a payment into Court under section 62 of the Trustees Act?
      `I applied by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply by summons?
      `the money represents a legacy to a minor or a person resident outside Singapore who is absolutely entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the money or securities represent a legacy, or residue or a share of a legacy, to which a minor or a person resident outside Singapore is absolutely entitled?
      `the summons is supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the summons supported by an affidavit?
      `it describes the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit describe the trust and the instrument creating it?
      `it names those interested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it name the persons interested or entitled, with their addresses so far as you know?
      `it gives my submission to answer inquiries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give your submission to answer all inquiries relating to the application of the money or securities?
      `it gives an address for service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give an address where you may be served?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 27, rule 2(1), have I, as a trustee, applied to pay money into Court in the way the Rule requires` IS
    `o 27 r 2(1) the trustee has applied by summons supported by an affidavit as required` `I wish to pay money into Court under section 62 of the Trustees Act` `I applied by summons` `the money represents a legacy to a minor or a person resident outside Singapore who is absolutely entitled` `the summons is supported by an affidavit` `it describes the trust` `it names those interested` `it gives my submission to answer inquiries` `it gives an address for service`

-- O 27 r 3.  Notice of lodgment.
@export Under Order 27, rule 3, have I given the notice of lodgment the Rule requires?
GIVEN `I have lodged money or securities in Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you lodged money or securities in Court?
      `I gave notice forthwith to everyone appearing entitled or interested` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you forthwith give notice to every person appearing to be entitled to, or have an interest in, what you lodged?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 27, rule 3, have I given the notice of lodgment the Rule requires` IS
    `o 27 r 3 the person has given notice of the lodgment` `I have lodged money or securities in Court` `I gave notice forthwith to everyone appearing entitled or interested`

-- O 27 r 4(1).  Money is lodged by a direction in Form 44(a).
@export Under Order 27, rule 4(1), am I lodging money in Court by the form the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the form of my direction to the Accountant-General` IS A STRING @desc Which form is your direction to the Accountant-General in (for example "Form 44(a)")?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 27, rule 4(1), am I lodging money in Court by the form the Rule requires` IS
    `o 27 r 4(1) the money is lodged in Court by means of a direction in the form required` `the form of my direction to the Accountant-General`

-- O 27 r 6(1).  Money lodged in Court is deemed placed on deposit and earns interest, with exceptions.
@export Under Order 27, rule 6(1), will the money I lodge in Court be placed on deposit and earn interest?
GIVEN `the amount I lodge` IS A NUMBER @desc How much money, in dollars, is lodged to the credit of the account?
      `it is paid in under Order 9, Rule 17` IS A `roc6 My answer` @desc Is it paid into Court under Order 9, Rule 17?
      `it is paid in under Order 14` IS A `roc6 My answer` @desc Is it paid into Court under Order 14?
      `it is paid in under Order 33` IS A `roc6 My answer` @desc Is it paid into Court under Order 33?
      `it is paid in as security for costs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it paid into Court as security for costs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 27, rule 6(1), will the money I lodge in Court be placed on deposit and earn interest` IS
    `o 27 r 6(1) the money lodged in Court is deemed to be placed on deposit and is credited with interest` `the amount I lodge` (`roc6 what I say, as a fact` `it is paid in under Order 9, Rule 17`) (`roc6 what I say, as a fact` `it is paid in under Order 14`) (`roc6 what I say, as a fact` `it is paid in under Order 33`) `it is paid in as security for costs`

-- O 27 r 17.  A person making a payment under a judgment or order produces a copy and gives notice.
@export Under Order 27, rule 17, have I produced a copy of the judgment or order and given notice to the person entitled?
GIVEN `I am making a payment under a judgment or order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you making a payment under a judgment or order?
      `I produced a copy of the judgment or order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you produce a copy of the judgment or order?
      `I gave notice to the person entitled to the money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give notice to the person entitled to the money?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 27, rule 17, have I produced a copy of the judgment or order and given notice to the person entitled` IS
    `o 27 r 17 the person making the payment has produced a copy and given notice` `I am making a payment under a judgment or order` `I produced a copy of the judgment or order` `I gave notice to the person entitled to the money`

-- ============================================================
-- roc7: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, Orders 28 to 33 (Order 28 electronic filing; Orders 29 and 29A foreign
-- law; Orders 30 and 31 constitutional references; Order 32 administration actions; Order 33 Admiralty and marine insurance)
-- -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a party to a civil action in the Singapore courts (a claimant, a defendant, a third party or an appellant), asking, on
-- facts the party can state, what must be filed or served, by when, how, at what cost, what the Court may order, and what
-- follows if it is not done.  This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that
-- party would ask.  Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: every question calls one function of those modules.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list -- one for each fact the
-- party can state, each with an @desc worded as the party would be asked.  A date of doing something is asked as a year, a
-- month and a day, with 0 meaning "not done yet"; the MAYBE DATE the module rule expects is built inside the question (the
-- wiring helper below).  The last day for doing a thing is a date that Order 3, Rule 3 counts; this layer takes it as an input,
-- as the modules do.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Rules themselves give; NOTHING means the Rules do not answer
-- on these facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (roc7)").  Never read NOTHING as no.  A question that asks
-- whether a duty was complied with answers NOTHING when the duty does not arise on the facts given; the question printed just
-- before it ("does the duty arise on my facts") answers that one.
--
-- There is no seat for an official: where a rule addresses only an official (the Registrar, the Sheriff, the Tribunal), the rule
-- is in layer 1, and the party meets it through the questions below that ask what the party may expect or can ask for.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the party's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The day something was done, from a year, a month and a day; 0 for the year means not done yet.
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      month IS A NUMBER
      day IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`roc7 seat wiring: the day it was done, from what I know` MEANS
    IF year EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (Date day month year) -- input mapping

-- A moment, from a day, an hour (0 to 23) and a minute (0 to 59).
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      hour IS A NUMBER
      minute IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Moment
`roc7 seat wiring: the moment, from a day, an hour and a minute` MEANS
    Moment WITH `day of the moment` IS day, `minutes after midnight` IS (hour TIMES 60) PLUS minute -- input mapping



§ `Order 28 -- Electronic filing service`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 28, rule 1 -- Definitions of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 28, rule 1.  Calls: o 28 r 1 a person is an authorised user
@export Under Order 28, rule 1, am I an authorised user of the electronic filing service?
GIVEN `the person is designated as an authorised user under Rule 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is designated as an authorised user under Rule 6?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 1, am I an authorised user of the electronic filing service` IS
    `o 28 r 1 a person is an authorised user` `the person is designated as an authorised user under Rule 6`

-- Order 28, rule 1.  Calls: o 28 r 1 a body is a registered user
@export Under Order 28, rule 1, is my body a registered user of the electronic filing service?
GIVEN `the body is an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the body is an entity?
      `the body is registered under Rule 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the body is registered under Rule 6?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 1, is my body a registered user of the electronic filing service` IS
    `o 28 r 1 a body is a registered user` `the body is an entity` `the body is registered under Rule 6`

-- Order 28, rule 1.  Calls: o 28 r 1 a body is an entity
@export Under Order 28, rule 1, is my body an entity that may use the electronic filing service?
GIVEN `the kind of body I am` IS A `o 28 r 1 kind of body` @desc What kind of body are you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 1, is my body an entity that may use the electronic filing service` IS
    `o 28 r 1 a body is an entity` `the kind of body I am`

-- Order 28, rule 1.  Calls: o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands
@export Under Order 28, rule 1, is a deeming under Order 28 still standing in my favour?
GIVEN `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 1, is a deeming under Order 28 still standing in my favour` IS
    `o 28 r 1 a deeming under this Order stands` `the contrary is proved`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 28, rule 6 -- Registered user and authorised user`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 28, rule 6(1).  Calls: o 28 r 6(1) an entity may apply to be a registered user
@export Under Order 28, rule 6(1), may I, as an entity, apply to be a registered user?
GIVEN `the applicant is an entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the applicant is an entity?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 6(1), may I, as an entity, apply to be a registered user` IS
    `o 28 r 6(1) an entity may apply to be a registered user` `the applicant is an entity`

-- Order 28, rule 6(2).  Calls: o 28 r 6(2) a registered user may designate a person as an authorised user
@export Under Order 28, rule 6(2), may I, as a registered user, designate a person as an authorised user?
GIVEN `the entity is a registered user` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the entity is a registered user?
      `the person is one of its partners, directors, officers or employees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is one of its partners, directors, officers or employees?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 6(2), may I, as a registered user, designate a person as an authorised user` IS
    `o 28 r 6(2) a registered user may designate a person as an authorised user` `the entity is a registered user` `the person is one of its partners, directors, officers or employees`

-- Order 28, rule 6(5).  Calls: o 28 r 6(5) the registered user is deemed to approve use of the identification code
@export Under Order 28, rule 6(5), am I, as a registered user, deemed to approve the use of the identification code?
GIVEN `the registered user designates an authorised user` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the registered user designates an authorised user?
      `the registered user supplies the authorised user's identification code through the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the registered user supplies the authorised user's identification code through the electronic filing service?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 6(5), am I, as a registered user, deemed to approve the use of the identification code` IS
    `o 28 r 6(5) the registered user is deemed to approve use of the identification code` `the registered user designates an authorised user` `the registered user supplies the authorised user's identification code through the electronic filing service` `the contrary is proved`

-- Order 28, rule 6(6).  Calls: o 28 r 6(6) the registered user has met the conditions for using the electronic filing service
@export Under Order 28, rule 6(6), have I met the conditions for using the electronic filing service?
GIVEN `the registered user has entered into an agreement with the electronic filing service provider for the provision of the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the registered user has entered into an agreement with the electronic filing service provider for the provision of the service?
      `the registered user has made arrangements with the Registrar for the mode of payment of the applicable fees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the registered user has made arrangements with the Registrar for the mode of payment of the applicable fees?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 6(6), have I met the conditions for using the electronic filing service` IS
    `o 28 r 6(6) the registered user has met the conditions for using the electronic filing service` `the registered user has entered into an agreement with the electronic filing service provider for the provision of the service` `the registered user has made arrangements with the Registrar for the mode of payment of the applicable fees`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 28, rule 7 -- Fee for registered user`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 28, rule 7(1).  Calls: o 28 r 7(1) the fee is payable by the registered user
@export Under Order 28, rule 7(1), is the fee payable by me as a registered user?
GIVEN `the registered user is a service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the registered user is a service bureau?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), is the fee payable by me as a registered user` IS
    `o 28 r 7(1) the fee is payable by the registered user` `the registered user is a service bureau`

-- Order 28, rule 7(1).  Calls: o 28 r 7(1) the monthly fee for a registered user
@export Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what monthly fee, in dollars, does a registered user pay?
GIVEN `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` IS A NUMBER @desc How many advocates and solicitors are there as at the relevant time? (Rule 7(4) fixes the relevant time)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what monthly fee, in dollars, does a registered user pay` IS
    `o 28 r 7(1) the monthly fee for a registered user` `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time`

-- Order 28, rule 7(1).  Calls: o 28 r 7(1) the fee for a number of months or parts of a month
@export Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what fee, in dollars, is payable for a number of months or parts of a month?
GIVEN `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` IS A NUMBER @desc How many advocates and solicitors are there as at the relevant time? (Rule 7(4) fixes the relevant time)
      `the number of months or parts of a month charged` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months or parts of a month is the fee charged?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 7(1), what fee, in dollars, is payable for a number of months or parts of a month` IS
    `o 28 r 7(1) the fee for a number of months or parts of a month` `the number of advocates and solicitors as at the relevant time` `the number of months or parts of a month charged`

-- Order 28, rule 7(2)(c).  Calls: o 28 r 7(2) the number counted in place of advocates and solicitors
@export Under Order 28, rule 7(2)(c), what monthly fee, in dollars, do I pay as an entity registered only to search or inspect?
GIVEN `the number of authorised users designated by the registered user` IS A NUMBER @desc How many authorised users have you designated? Rule 7(2)(c) counts them in place of advocates and solicitors
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 7(2)(c), what monthly fee, in dollars, do I pay as an entity registered only to search or inspect` IS
    `o 28 r 7(1) the monthly fee for a registered user` (`o 28 r 7(2) the number counted in place of advocates and solicitors` `o 28 r 7(2)(c) an entity registered solely to search or inspect under Order 26, Rule 3` (`o 28 r 7(2) headcounts` WITH `o 28 r 7(2) advocates and solicitors` IS 0, `o 28 r 7(2)(a) the Attorney-General, a Deputy Attorney-General, the Solicitor-General or a State Counsel or Deputy Public Prosecutor` IS 0, `o 28 r 7(2)(b) persons employed or engaged by the registered user who have a right to appear before the court by virtue of a written law` IS 0, `o 28 r 7(2)(c) authorised users designated by the registered user` IS `the number of authorised users designated by the registered user`, `o 28 r 7(2)(d) registered foreign lawyers` IS 0))

-- Order 28, rule 7(3).  Calls: o 28 r 7(3) no fee is payable by the registered user
@export Under Order 28, rule 7(3), is no fee payable by me as an entity registered only to make applications for a practising certificate under the Legal Profession Act?
GIVEN `the registered user is an entity registered solely for the purpose of using the electronic filing service to make applications under the Legal Profession Act 1966` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the registered user is an entity registered solely for the purpose of using the electronic filing service to make applications under the Legal Profession Act 1966?
      `each application is under section 18(2) of that Act for a provisional practising certificate or under section 25(1) for a practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that each application is under section 18(2) of that Act for a provisional practising certificate or under section 25(1) for a practising certificate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 7(3), is no fee payable by me as an entity registered only to make applications for a practising certificate under the Legal Profession Act` IS
    `o 28 r 7(3) no fee is payable by the registered user` `the registered user is an entity registered solely for the purpose of using the electronic filing service to make applications under the Legal Profession Act 1966` `each application is under section 18(2) of that Act for a provisional practising certificate or under section 25(1) for a practising certificate`

-- Order 28, rule 7(6).  Calls: o 28 r 7(6) the day the fee for a month is due and payable
@export Under Order 28, rule 7(6), on what day is the fee for a month due and payable?
GIVEN `year` IS A NUMBER @desc For which year is the fee? (for example 2026)
      `month` IS A NUMBER @desc For which month is the fee, from 1 for January to 12 for December?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 7(6), on what day is the fee for a month due and payable` IS
    `o 28 r 7(6) the day the fee for a month is due and payable` `year` `month`

-- Order 28, rule 7(8)(a).  Calls: o 28 r 7(8)(a) the Registrar must refund the amount paid in excess or error (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), does the Registrar have to refund an amount I paid in excess or by error?
GIVEN `the amount was paid in excess or error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an amount paid to the Registrar in excess, or by error?
      `the claim was made in writing to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make your claim for a refund to the Registrar in writing?
      `the year the claim was made` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year did you make your claim? (0 if you have not made it yet)
      `the month the claim was made` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month did you make your claim, from 1 for January to 12 for December? (0 if you have not made it yet)
      `the day of the month the claim was made` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month did you make your claim? (0 if you have not made it yet)
      `the last day of the 3 months` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the 3 months, counted under Order 3, Rule 3?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), does the Registrar have to refund an amount I paid in excess or by error` IS
    `o 28 r 7(8)(a) the Registrar must refund the amount paid in excess or error (the duty arises)` `the amount was paid in excess or error` `the claim was made in writing to the Registrar` (`o 28 r 7(8)(a) the claim is made in writing in time` (`roc7 seat wiring: the day it was done, from what I know` `the year the claim was made` `the month the claim was made` `the day of the month the claim was made`) `the last day of the 3 months` `the date I am asking about`)

-- Order 28, rule 7(8)(a).  Calls: o 28 r 7(8)(a) the Registrar must refund the amount paid in excess or error
@export Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), has this been done: the Registrar must refund the amount paid in excess or error?
GIVEN `the amount was paid in excess or error` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an amount paid to the Registrar in excess, or by error?
      `the claim was made in writing to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make your claim for a refund to the Registrar in writing?
      `the year the claim was made` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year did you make your claim? (0 if you have not made it yet)
      `the month the claim was made` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month did you make your claim, from 1 for January to 12 for December? (0 if you have not made it yet)
      `the day of the month the claim was made` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month did you make your claim? (0 if you have not made it yet)
      `the last day of the 3 months` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the 3 months, counted under Order 3, Rule 3?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
      `the Registrar has refunded the amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Registrar refunded the amount?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), has this been done: the Registrar must refund the amount paid in excess or error` IS
    `o 28 r 7(8)(a) the Registrar must refund the amount paid in excess or error` `the amount was paid in excess or error` `the claim was made in writing to the Registrar` (`o 28 r 7(8)(a) the claim is made in writing in time` (`roc7 seat wiring: the day it was done, from what I know` `the year the claim was made` `the month the claim was made` `the day of the month the claim was made`) `the last day of the 3 months` `the date I am asking about`) `the Registrar has refunded the amount`

-- Order 28, rule 7(8)(a).  Calls: o 28 r 7(8)(a) the claim is made in writing in time
@export Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), did I make my claim for a refund in writing within the time allowed?
GIVEN `the year it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year was it done? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the month it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month was it done, from 1 for January to 12 for December? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the day of the month it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month was it done? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, Rule 3?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 7(8)(a), did I make my claim for a refund in writing within the time allowed` IS
    `o 28 r 7(8)(a) the claim is made in writing in time` (`roc7 seat wiring: the day it was done, from what I know` `the year it was done` `the month it was done` `the day of the month it was done`) `the last day for doing the act` `the date I am asking about`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 28, rule 8 -- Electronic filing`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 28, rule 8(1).  Calls: o 28 r 8(1) the requirement to use the electronic filing service arises
@export Under Order 28, rule 8(1), am I required to use the electronic filing service for this document?
GIVEN `the document is required to be filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar under another provision of these Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is required to be filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar under another provision of these Rules?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 8(1), am I required to use the electronic filing service for this document` IS
    `o 28 r 8(1) the requirement to use the electronic filing service arises` `the document is required to be filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar under another provision of these Rules`

-- Order 28, rule 8(1).  Calls: o 28 r 8(1) the document is filed using the electronic filing service as required
@export Under Order 28, rule 8(1), have I used the electronic filing service as required for this document?
GIVEN `the document is required to be filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar under another provision of these Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is required to be filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar under another provision of these Rules?
      `it is so conveyed using the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is so conveyed using the electronic filing service?
      `it is done in accordance with this Order and the practice directions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is done in accordance with this Order and the practice directions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 8(1), have I used the electronic filing service as required for this document` IS
    `o 28 r 8(1) the document is filed using the electronic filing service as required` `the document is required to be filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar under another provision of these Rules` `it is so conveyed using the electronic filing service` `it is done in accordance with this Order and the practice directions`

-- Order 28, rule 8(2).  Calls: o 28 r 8(2) the requirement is satisfied by a single copy filed using the electronic filing service
@export Under Order 28, rule 8(2), is the requirement satisfied by a single copy filed using the electronic filing service?
GIVEN `a single copy is filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a single copy is filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service?
      `it is in accordance with this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is in accordance with this Order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 8(2), is the requirement satisfied by a single copy filed using the electronic filing service` IS
    `o 28 r 8(2) the requirement is satisfied by a single copy filed using the electronic filing service` `a single copy is filed, served, delivered or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service` `it is in accordance with this Order`

-- Order 28, rule 8(3).  Calls: o 28 r 8(3) the way of using the electronic filing service is one of the 2 ways
@export Under Order 28, rule 8(3), is the way I used the electronic filing service one of the two ways the Rules allow?
GIVEN `it is done by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is done by electronic transmission?
      `it is done via a service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is done via a service bureau?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 8(3), is the way I used the electronic filing service one of the two ways the Rules allow` IS
    `o 28 r 8(3) the way of using the electronic filing service is one of the 2 ways` `it is done by electronic transmission` `it is done via a service bureau`

-- Order 28, rule 8(4).  Calls: o 28 r 8(4) a document may be filed other than using the electronic filing service
@export Under Order 28, rule 8(4), may a document be filed other than using the electronic filing service?
GIVEN `the Registrar has allowed the document, part of a document or class of documents to be so conveyed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar has allowed the document, part of a document or class of documents to be so conveyed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 8(4), may a document be filed other than using the electronic filing service` IS
    `o 28 r 8(4) a document may be filed other than using the electronic filing service` `the Registrar has allowed the document, part of a document or class of documents to be so conveyed`

-- Order 28, rule 8(5).  Calls: o 28 r 8(5) the form of the document is as required
@export Under Order 28, rule 8(5), is the form of my document as required?
GIVEN `the document is in the form set out in the practice directions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is in the form set out in the practice directions?
      `the document is remotely composed on the provider's computer system and is in the form made available through the service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is remotely composed on the provider's computer system and is in the form made available through the service?
      `there is no such prescription and the document is in the form prescribed by Order 3, Rule 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that there is no such prescription and the document is in the form prescribed by Order 3, Rule 6?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 8(5), is the form of my document as required` IS
    `o 28 r 8(5) the form of the document is as required` `the document is in the form set out in the practice directions` `the document is remotely composed on the provider's computer system and is in the form made available through the service` `there is no such prescription and the document is in the form prescribed by Order 3, Rule 6`

-- Order 28, rule 8(6).  Calls: o 28 r 8(6) the document is deemed filed by the registered user with that user's intention
@export Under Order 28, rule 8(6), is my document deemed filed by me as registered user with my intention?
GIVEN `the document is filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service?
      `it is by a registered user` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is by a registered user?
      `it is done using an identification code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is done using an identification code?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 8(6), is my document deemed filed by me as registered user with my intention` IS
    `o 28 r 8(6) the document is deemed filed by the registered user with that user's intention` `the document is filed with, served on, delivered or otherwise conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service` `it is by a registered user` `it is done using an identification code` `the contrary is proved`

-- Order 28, rule 8(7)(a).  Calls: o 28 r 8(7)(a) the document is deemed conveyed by the authorised user on behalf and with the authority of the registered user
@export Under Order 28, rule 8(7)(a), is my document deemed conveyed by an authorised user on behalf of the registered user and with that user's authority?
GIVEN `the document is conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service?
      `it is by an authorised user who is not an employee of a service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is by an authorised user who is not an employee of a service bureau?
      `it is done using an identification code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is done using an identification code?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 8(7)(a), is my document deemed conveyed by an authorised user on behalf of the registered user and with that user's authority` IS
    `o 28 r 8(7)(a) the document is deemed conveyed by the authorised user on behalf and with the authority of the registered user` `the document is conveyed to the Registrar through the electronic filing service` `it is by an authorised user who is not an employee of a service bureau` `it is done using an identification code` `the contrary is proved`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 28, rule 9 -- Signing of electronic documents`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 28, rule 9(1).  Calls: o 28 r 9(1) a requirement of signing by an authorised user or a registered user is deemed complied with
@export Under Order 28, rule 9(1), is a requirement of signing deemed complied with when my document is filed through an authorised user or registered user?
GIVEN `the document is filed, served, delivered or conveyed using the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is filed, served, delivered or conveyed using the electronic filing service?
      `the identification code of the authorised user or registered user has been applied to or associated with the document or the transmission containing it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the identification code of the authorised user or registered user has been applied to or associated with the document or the transmission containing it?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 9(1), is a requirement of signing deemed complied with when my document is filed through an authorised user or registered user` IS
    `o 28 r 9(1) a requirement of signing by an authorised user or a registered user is deemed complied with` `the document is filed, served, delivered or conveyed using the electronic filing service` `the identification code of the authorised user or registered user has been applied to or associated with the document or the transmission containing it` `the contrary is proved`

-- Order 28, rule 9(3).  Calls: o 28 r 9(3) the requirement for the signature of an advocate or solicitor is deemed met
@export Under Order 28, rule 9(3), is the requirement for the signature of an advocate or solicitor deemed met?
GIVEN `a written law or practice direction requires the signature of an advocate or solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a written law or practice direction requires the signature of an advocate or solicitor?
      `the identification code of the advocate or solicitor has been applied to or associated with the document or transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the identification code of the advocate or solicitor has been applied to or associated with the document or transmission?
      `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 9(3), is the requirement for the signature of an advocate or solicitor deemed met` IS
    `o 28 r 9(3) the requirement for the signature of an advocate or solicitor is deemed met` `a written law or practice direction requires the signature of an advocate or solicitor` `the identification code of the advocate or solicitor has been applied to or associated with the document or transmission` `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service` `the contrary is proved`

-- Order 28, rule 9(4).  Calls: o 28 r 9(4) the application of the identification code is a secure electronic signature
@export Under Order 28, rule 9(4), is the application of the identification code a secure electronic signature?
GIVEN `the identification code of an authorised user or a registered user is applied to or associated with a document or transmission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the identification code of an authorised user or a registered user is applied to or associated with a document or transmission?
      `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 9(4), is the application of the identification code a secure electronic signature` IS
    `o 28 r 9(4) the application of the identification code is a secure electronic signature` `the identification code of an authorised user or a registered user is applied to or associated with a document or transmission` `it is in compliance with the security procedures of the electronic filing service`

