§§ `Order 28, rule 10 -- Date of filing`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 28, rule 10(1).  Calls: o 28 r 10(1) the document is deemed filed, served, delivered or conveyed
@export Under Order 28, rule 10(1), is my document deemed filed, served, delivered or conveyed through the electronic filing service?
GIVEN `the document is filed with, served on, delivered or conveyed to the Registrar using the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is filed with, served on, delivered or conveyed to the Registrar using the electronic filing service?
      `the document is subsequently accepted by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is subsequently accepted by the Registrar?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 10(1), is my document deemed filed, served, delivered or conveyed through the electronic filing service` IS
    `o 28 r 10(1) the document is deemed filed, served, delivered or conveyed` `the document is filed with, served on, delivered or conveyed to the Registrar using the electronic filing service` `the document is subsequently accepted by the Registrar` `the contrary is proved`

-- Order 28, rule 10(2).  Calls: o 28 r 10(2) paragraph (1) applies to the document
@export Under Order 28, rule 10(2), does the deeming in paragraph (1) apply to my caveat?
GIVEN `the document is a caveat against the issue of a warrant to arrest filed pursuant to Order 33, Rule 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is a caveat against the issue of a warrant to arrest filed pursuant to Order 33, Rule 5?
      `the document is a caveat against release and payment out of Court filed pursuant to Order 33, Rule 14` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is a caveat against release and payment out of Court filed pursuant to Order 33, Rule 14?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 10(2), does the deeming in paragraph (1) apply to my caveat` IS
    `o 28 r 10(2) paragraph (1) applies to the document` `the document is a caveat against the issue of a warrant to arrest filed pursuant to Order 33, Rule 5` `the document is a caveat against release and payment out of Court filed pursuant to Order 33, Rule 14`

-- Order 28, rule 10(4).  Calls: o 28 r 10(4) the originating process is deemed issued
@export Under Order 28, rule 10(4), is my originating process deemed issued when filed through the electronic filing service?
GIVEN `the originating process is filed or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the originating process is filed or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service?
      `the Registrar subsequently accepts it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar subsequently accepts it?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 10(4), is my originating process deemed issued when filed through the electronic filing service` IS
    `o 28 r 10(4) the originating process is deemed issued` `the originating process is filed or otherwise conveyed using the electronic filing service` `the Registrar subsequently accepts it` `the contrary is proved`

-- Order 28, rule 10(5).  Calls: o 28 r 10(5) the registered user may produce a record as evidence of filing or issuance
@export Under Order 28, rule 10(5), may I, as a registered user, produce a record as evidence of filing or issuance?
GIVEN `the record of the transmission is issued by the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the record of the transmission is issued by the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau?
      `it is produced together with a copy of the Registrar's notification of acceptance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is produced together with a copy of the Registrar's notification of acceptance?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 10(5), may I, as a registered user, produce a record as evidence of filing or issuance` IS
    `o 28 r 10(5) the registered user may produce a record as evidence of filing or issuance` `the record of the transmission is issued by the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau` `it is produced together with a copy of the Registrar's notification of acceptance`

