§§ `Order 28, rule 12 -- Service of documents`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 28, rule 12(1).  Calls: o 28 r 12(1) service may be effected using the electronic filing service
@export Under Order 28, rule 12(1), may I serve this document using the electronic filing service?
GIVEN `the document is required by these Rules to be served personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is required by these Rules to be served personally?
      `the party to be served has agreed that it may be served using the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party to be served has agreed that it may be served using the electronic filing service?
      `the person to be served is an authorised user or a registered user, or is represented by a solicitor who is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person to be served is an authorised user or a registered user, or is represented by a solicitor who is?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 12(1), may I serve this document using the electronic filing service` IS
    `o 28 r 12(1) service may be effected using the electronic filing service` `the document is required by these Rules to be served personally` `the party to be served has agreed that it may be served using the electronic filing service` `the person to be served is an authorised user or a registered user, or is represented by a solicitor who is`

-- Order 28, rule 12(2).  Calls: o 28 r 12(2) the party is deemed to have agreed to be served using the electronic filing service
@export Under Order 28, rule 12(2), am I deemed to have agreed to be served using the electronic filing service?
GIVEN `the party has instructed the party's solicitor to accept service of a document which is required by these Rules to be served personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party has instructed the party's solicitor to accept service of a document which is required by these Rules to be served personally?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 12(2), am I deemed to have agreed to be served using the electronic filing service` IS
    `o 28 r 12(2) the party is deemed to have agreed to be served using the electronic filing service` `the party has instructed the party's solicitor to accept service of a document which is required by these Rules to be served personally` `the contrary is proved`

-- Order 28, rule 12(3)(a).  Calls: o 28 r 12(3)(a) the document is deemed served by electronic transmission
@export Under Order 28, rule 12(3)(a), is my document deemed served by electronic transmission?
GIVEN `the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by electronic transmission from the computer system of the authorised user or registered user` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by electronic transmission from the computer system of the authorised user or registered user?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 12(3)(a), is my document deemed served by electronic transmission` IS
    `o 28 r 12(3)(a) the document is deemed served by electronic transmission` `the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by electronic transmission from the computer system of the authorised user or registered user` `the contrary is proved`

-- Order 28, rule 12(5).  Calls: o 28 r 12(5) the person serving may file a Registrar's certificate of service in lieu of an affidavit
@export Under Order 28, rule 12(5), may I file a Registrar's certificate of service instead of an affidavit?
GIVEN `the certificate is a Registrar's certificate of service issued through the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the certificate is a Registrar's certificate of service issued through the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 12(5), may I file a Registrar's certificate of service instead of an affidavit` IS
    `o 28 r 12(5) the person serving may file a Registrar's certificate of service in lieu of an affidavit` `the certificate is a Registrar's certificate of service issued through the electronic filing service provider or the service bureau`

-- Order 28, rule 12(5).  Calls: o 28 r 12(5) the certificate is regarded as prima facie evidence of service
@export Under Order 28, rule 12(5), is the Registrar's certificate of service regarded as prima facie evidence of service?
GIVEN `the person serving files a Registrar's certificate of service in lieu of an affidavit of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person serving files a Registrar's certificate of service in lieu of an affidavit of service?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 12(5), is the Registrar's certificate of service regarded as prima facie evidence of service` IS
    `o 28 r 12(5) the certificate is regarded as prima facie evidence of service` `the person serving files a Registrar's certificate of service in lieu of an affidavit of service` `the contrary is proved`

-- Order 28, rule 12(7).  Calls: o 28 r 12(7) the document is deemed served by the registered user with that user's intention
@export Under Order 28, rule 12(7), is my document deemed served by the registered user with that user's intention?
GIVEN `the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by a registered user to a person through the electronic filing service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by a registered user to a person through the electronic filing service?
      `it is done using an identification code` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is done using an identification code?
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the contrary been proved?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 12(7), is my document deemed served by the registered user with that user's intention` IS
    `o 28 r 12(7) the document is deemed served by the registered user with that user's intention` `the document is served, delivered or otherwise conveyed by a registered user to a person through the electronic filing service` `it is done using an identification code` `the contrary is proved`

-- Order 28, rule 12(11).  Calls: o 28 r 12(11) Order 7, Rule 8 applies to the service
@export Under Order 28, rule 12(11), does Order 7, Rule 8 apply to my service through the electronic filing service?
GIVEN `the service is effected under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the service is effected under this Rule?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 12(11), does Order 7, Rule 8 apply to my service through the electronic filing service` IS
    `o 28 r 12(11) Order 7, Rule 8 applies to the service` `the service is effected under this Rule`

-- Order 28, rule 12(11).  Calls: o 28 r 12(11) the day service through the electronic filing service is deemed effected
@export Under Order 28, rule 12(11), on what day is service through the electronic filing service deemed effected?
GIVEN `the service is effected under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the service effected through the electronic filing service under this Rule?
      `o 7 r 8 the day service is deemed effected` IS A DATE @desc On what day does Order 7, Rule 8 deem the service effected?
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 12(11), on what day is service through the electronic filing service deemed effected` IS
