    `o 28 r 17(1) a user registered by the Registrar of the Supreme Court is treated as also registered by the other two Registrars` `the user is registered as a registered user or an authorised user by the Registrar of the Supreme Court under Rule 6` `the contrary is proved`

-- Order 28, rule 17(4)(a).  Calls: o 28 r 17(4)(a) a Supreme Court service bureau may be used for State Courts proceedings
@export Under Order 28, rule 17(4)(a), may I use a Supreme Court service bureau for State Courts proceedings?
GIVEN `the service bureau was established or authorised to be established by the Registrar of the Supreme Court under Rule 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the service bureau was established or authorised to be established by the Registrar of the Supreme Court under Rule 5?
      `the proceedings are in the State Courts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceedings are in the State Courts?
      `the Registrar of the State Courts has prescribed the cases and circumstances in practice directions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar of the State Courts has prescribed the cases and circumstances in practice directions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 28, rule 17(4)(a), may I use a Supreme Court service bureau for State Courts proceedings` IS
    `o 28 r 17(4)(a) a Supreme Court service bureau may be used for State Courts proceedings` `the service bureau was established or authorised to be established by the Registrar of the Supreme Court under Rule 5` `the proceedings are in the State Courts` `the Registrar of the State Courts has prescribed the cases and circumstances in practice directions`


§ `Order 29 -- Referrals on issues of law`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 29, rule 2 -- Order for reference of questions of foreign law to foreign courts on application of parties`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 29, rule 2(1).  Calls: o 29 r 2(1) the Court may order proceedings in a specified court in a specified foreign country
@export Under Order 29, rule 2(1), may the Court order that proceedings be commenced in a specified court in a specified foreign country?
GIVEN `the proceedings are before the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceedings are before the Court?
      `a question relating to the law of a specified foreign country or to the application of such law arises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a question relating to the law of a specified foreign country or to the application of such law arises?
      `one or more of the parties apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that one or more of the parties apply?
      `the order is that proceedings be commenced in a specified court in that specified foreign country seeking a determination of the question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the order is that proceedings be commenced in a specified court in that specified foreign country seeking a determination of the question?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 29, rule 2(1), may the Court order that proceedings be commenced in a specified court in a specified foreign country` IS
    `o 29 r 2(1) the Court may order proceedings in a specified court in a specified foreign country` `the proceedings are before the Court` `a question relating to the law of a specified foreign country or to the application of such law arises` `one or more of the parties apply` `the order is that proceedings be commenced in a specified court in that specified foreign country seeking a determination of the question`

-- Order 29, rule 2(2).  Calls: o 29 r 2(2) the application is made by summons and supported by an affidavit (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 29, rule 2(2), must my application for that order be made by summons supported by an affidavit?
GIVEN `the application is for an order under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is for an order under paragraph (1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 29, rule 2(2), must my application for that order be made by summons supported by an affidavit` IS
    `o 29 r 2(2) the application is made by summons and supported by an affidavit (the duty arises)` `the application is for an order under paragraph (1)`

-- Order 29, rule 2(2).  Calls: o 29 r 2(2) the application is made by summons and supported by an affidavit
@export Under Order 29, rule 2(2), have I made my application by summons and supported it by an affidavit?
GIVEN `the application is for an order under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is for an order under paragraph (1)?
      `the application is made by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is made by summons?
      `it is supported by an affidavit stating the grounds for the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is supported by an affidavit stating the grounds for the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 29, rule 2(2), have I made my application by summons and supported it by an affidavit` IS
    `o 29 r 2(2) the application is made by summons and supported by an affidavit` `the application is for an order under paragraph (1)` `the application is made by summons` `it is supported by an affidavit stating the grounds for the application`

-- Order 29, rule 2(3).  Calls: o 29 r 2(3) the Court may give directions for a statement of the issue
@export Under Order 29, rule 2(3), may the Court give directions for a statement of the issue?
GIVEN `the directions are for the preparation of a statement of the issue from which the question arises, for inclusion with the question of law to be determined by the specified court in the specified foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the directions are for the preparation of a statement of the issue from which the question arises, for inclusion with the question of law to be determined by the specified court in the specified foreign country?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 29, rule 2(3), may the Court give directions for a statement of the issue` IS
    `o 29 r 2(3) the Court may give directions for a statement of the issue` `the directions are for the preparation of a statement of the issue from which the question arises, for inclusion with the question of law to be determined by the specified court in the specified foreign country`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 29, rule 3 -- Referral of questions of foreign law on Court's own motion`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 29, rule 3.  Calls: o 29 r 3 this Order does not prevent the Court ordering proceedings in another foreign country on its own motion
@export Under Order 29, rule 3, may the Court, on its own motion, order proceedings in a foreign country that is not a specified foreign country?
GIVEN `the order is made on the Court's own motion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the order is made on the Court's own motion?
      `the proceedings are to be commenced in a court of competent jurisdiction in a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceedings are to be commenced in a court of competent jurisdiction in a foreign country?
      `the foreign country is not a specified foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the foreign country is not a specified foreign country?
      `it seeks a determination of a question relating to the law of that foreign country or to the application of such law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it seeks a determination of a question relating to the law of that foreign country or to the application of such law?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 29, rule 3, may the Court, on its own motion, order proceedings in a foreign country that is not a specified foreign country` IS
    `o 29 r 3 this Order does not prevent the Court ordering proceedings in another foreign country on its own motion` `the order is made on the Court's own motion` `the proceedings are to be commenced in a court of competent jurisdiction in a foreign country` `the foreign country is not a specified foreign country` `it seeks a determination of a question relating to the law of that foreign country or to the application of such law`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 29, rule 4 -- Order for referral of questions of foreign law`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 29, rule 4.  Calls: o 29 r 4 the order states what it must state (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 29, rule 4, must the Court's order state the question, the facts and the other matters this rule lists?
GIVEN `the order is made by the Court under Rule 2 or 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the order is made by the Court under Rule 2 or 3?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 29, rule 4, must the Court's order state the question, the facts and the other matters this rule lists` IS
    `o 29 r 4 the order states what it must state (the duty arises)` `the order is made by the Court under Rule 2 or 3`

-- Order 29, rule 4.  Calls: o 29 r 4 the order states what it must state
@export Under Order 29, rule 4, does the Court's order state what it must state?
GIVEN `the order is made by the Court under Rule 2 or 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the order is made by the Court under Rule 2 or 3?
      `it states the question that is to be determined in relation to the law of the foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it states the question that is to be determined in relation to the law of the foreign country?
      `it states the facts or assumptions upon which the question is to be determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it states the facts or assumptions upon which the question is to be determined?
      `it contains a statement to the effect that the court in the foreign country may vary the facts or assumptions and the question to be determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it contains a statement to the effect that the court in the foreign country may vary the facts or assumptions and the question to be determined?
      `it states whether and to what extent the parties may depart from the facts or assumptions in the determination of the question by the court of the foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it states whether and to what extent the parties may depart from the facts or assumptions in the determination of the question by the court of the foreign country?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 29, rule 4, does the Court's order state what it must state` IS
    `o 29 r 4 the order states what it must state` `the order is made by the Court under Rule 2 or 3` `it states the question that is to be determined in relation to the law of the foreign country` `it states the facts or assumptions upon which the question is to be determined` `it contains a statement to the effect that the court in the foreign country may vary the facts or assumptions and the question to be determined` `it states whether and to what extent the parties may depart from the facts or assumptions in the determination of the question by the court of the foreign country`

