§§ `Order 29, rule 5 -- Determination of issues arising in foreign court proceedings`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 29, rule 5(1).  Calls: o 29 r 5(1) proceedings on an issue of Singapore law may be commenced by originating application
@export Under Order 29, rule 5(1), may proceedings on an issue of Singapore law be commenced by originating application?
GIVEN `the issue relates to Singapore law and is relevant to an issue in proceedings before a specified court in a specified foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the issue relates to Singapore law and is relevant to an issue in proceedings before a specified court in a specified foreign country?
      `the proceedings are commenced by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceedings are commenced by originating application?
      `the application is supported by affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is supported by affidavit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 29, rule 5(1), may proceedings on an issue of Singapore law be commenced by originating application` IS
    `o 29 r 5(1) proceedings on an issue of Singapore law may be commenced by originating application` `the issue relates to Singapore law and is relevant to an issue in proceedings before a specified court in a specified foreign country` `the proceedings are commenced by originating application` `the application is supported by affidavit`

-- Order 29, rule 5(2).  Calls: o 29 r 5(2) the originating application or affidavit states what it must state (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 29, rule 5(2), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the originating application or affidavit states what it must state?
GIVEN `the proceedings are under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceedings are under paragraph (1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 29, rule 5(2), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the originating application or affidavit states what it must state` IS
    `o 29 r 5(2) the originating application or affidavit states what it must state (the duty arises)` `the proceedings are under paragraph (1)`

-- Order 29, rule 5(2).  Calls: o 29 r 5(2) the originating application or affidavit states what it must state
@export Under Order 29, rule 5(2), does my originating application or affidavit state what it must state?
GIVEN `the proceedings are under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceedings are under paragraph (1)?
      `the originating application or supporting affidavit states the question that is to be determined in relation to Singapore law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the originating application or supporting affidavit states the question that is to be determined in relation to Singapore law?
      `it states the facts or assumptions upon which the question is to be determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it states the facts or assumptions upon which the question is to be determined?
      `it contains a statement to the effect that the Court in Singapore may vary the facts or assumptions and the question to be determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it contains a statement to the effect that the Court in Singapore may vary the facts or assumptions and the question to be determined?
      `it states whether and to what extent the parties may depart from the facts or assumptions in the determination of the question by the Court in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it states whether and to what extent the parties may depart from the facts or assumptions in the determination of the question by the Court in Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 29, rule 5(2), does my originating application or affidavit state what it must state` IS
    `o 29 r 5(2) the originating application or affidavit states what it must state` `the proceedings are under paragraph (1)` `the originating application or supporting affidavit states the question that is to be determined in relation to Singapore law` `it states the facts or assumptions upon which the question is to be determined` `it contains a statement to the effect that the Court in Singapore may vary the facts or assumptions and the question to be determined` `it states whether and to what extent the parties may depart from the facts or assumptions in the determination of the question by the Court in Singapore`

