-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 29A, rule 2(1).  Calls: o 29A r 2(1) the Court may transmit a request for an opinion to a specified court
@export Under Order 29A, rule 2(1), may the Court transmit a request for an opinion to a specified court?
GIVEN `the proceedings are before the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceedings are before the Court?
      `a question relating to the law of a specified foreign country or to the application of such law arises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a question relating to the law of a specified foreign country or to the application of such law arises?
      `all of the parties consent to the transmission of the initial request and any subsequent request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that all of the parties consent to the transmission of the initial request and any subsequent request?
      `all of the parties consent to the admission as evidence in the proceedings of any opinion and any clarification provided by the specified court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that all of the parties consent to the admission as evidence in the proceedings of any opinion and any clarification provided by the specified court?
      `all of the parties consent to the dispensation with cross-examination of the maker of the opinion and clarification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that all of the parties consent to the dispensation with cross-examination of the maker of the opinion and clarification?
      `the request is transmitted on the application of one or more of the parties or on the Court's own motion to a specified court in that specified foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the request is transmitted on the application of one or more of the parties or on the Court's own motion to a specified court in that specified foreign country?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 29A, rule 2(1), may the Court transmit a request for an opinion to a specified court` IS
    `o 29A r 2(1) the Court may transmit a request for an opinion to a specified court` `the proceedings are before the Court` `a question relating to the law of a specified foreign country or to the application of such law arises` `all of the parties consent to the transmission of the initial request and any subsequent request` `all of the parties consent to the admission as evidence in the proceedings of any opinion and any clarification provided by the specified court` `all of the parties consent to the dispensation with cross-examination of the maker of the opinion and clarification` `the request is transmitted on the application of one or more of the parties or on the Court's own motion to a specified court in that specified foreign country`

-- Order 29A, rule 2(2).  Calls: o 29A r 2(2) the application is made by summons (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 29A, rule 2(2), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the application is made by summons?
