-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 33, rule 5 -- Caveat against arrest`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 33, rule 5(1).  Calls: o 33 r 5(1) the caveat against arrest is filed in Form 52 and entered in the record of caveats (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 33, rule 5(1), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the caveat against arrest is filed in Form 52 and entered in the record of caveats?
GIVEN `the person desires to prevent the arrest of any property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person desires to prevent the arrest of any property?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 5(1), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the caveat against arrest is filed in Form 52 and entered in the record of caveats` IS
    `o 33 r 5(1) the caveat against arrest is filed in Form 52 and entered in the record of caveats (the duty arises)` `the person desires to prevent the arrest of any property`

-- Order 33, rule 5(1).  Calls: o 33 r 5(1) the caveat against arrest is filed in Form 52 and entered in the record of caveats
@export Under Order 33, rule 5(1), have I filed my caveat against arrest in Form 52 with the solicitor's undertakings and had it entered?
GIVEN `the person desires to prevent the arrest of any property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person desires to prevent the arrest of any property?
      `the person files in the Registry a caveat in Form 52` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person files in the Registry a caveat in Form 52?
      `it is signed by the person's solicitor undertaking to file a notice of intention to contest or not contest in any action that may be begun against the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is signed by the person's solicitor undertaking to file a notice of intention to contest or not contest in any action that may be begun against the property?
      `it is signed by the person's solicitor undertaking within 3 days after receiving notice that such an action has been begun to give bail in the action in a sum not exceeding an amount specified in the caveat or to pay the amount so specified into Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is signed by the person's solicitor undertaking within 3 days after receiving notice that such an action has been begun to give bail in the action in a sum not exceeding an amount specified in the caveat or to pay the amount so specified into Court?
      `the caveat so filed is entered in the record of caveats` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the caveat so filed is entered in the record of caveats?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 5(1), have I filed my caveat against arrest in Form 52 with the solicitor's undertakings and had it entered` IS
    `o 33 r 5(1) the caveat against arrest is filed in Form 52 and entered in the record of caveats` `the person desires to prevent the arrest of any property` `the person files in the Registry a caveat in Form 52` `it is signed by the person's solicitor undertaking to file a notice of intention to contest or not contest in any action that may be begun against the property` `it is signed by the person's solicitor undertaking within 3 days after receiving notice that such an action has been begun to give bail in the action in a sum not exceeding an amount specified in the caveat or to pay the amount so specified into Court` `the caveat so filed is entered in the record of caveats`

-- Order 33, rule 5(1).  Calls: o 33 r 5 a caveat against arrest is issued under this Rule
@export Under Order 33, rule 5(1), is my caveat against arrest issued under Rule 5?
GIVEN `the caveat is filed in the Registry in Form 52 signed by the person's solicitor with the undertakings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the caveat is filed in the Registry in Form 52 signed by the person's solicitor with the undertakings?
      `the caveat is entered in the record of caveats` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the caveat is entered in the record of caveats?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 5(1), is my caveat against arrest issued under Rule 5` IS
    `o 33 r 5 a caveat against arrest is issued under this Rule` `the caveat is filed in the Registry in Form 52 signed by the person's solicitor with the undertakings` `the caveat is entered in the record of caveats`

-- Order 33, rule 5(1)(b).  Calls: o 33 r 5(1)(b) bail is given or the amount is paid into Court in time
@export Under Order 33, rule 5(1)(b), did I give bail or pay the amount into Court in time?
GIVEN `the year it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year was it done? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the month it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month was it done, from 1 for January to 12 for December? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the day of the month it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month was it done? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, Rule 3?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 5(1)(b), did I give bail or pay the amount into Court in time` IS
    `o 33 r 5(1)(b) bail is given or the amount is paid into Court in time` (`roc7 seat wiring: the day it was done, from what I know` `the year it was done` `the month it was done` `the day of the month it was done`) `the last day for doing the act` `the date I am asking about`

-- Order 33, rule 5(2).  Calls: o 33 r 5(2) a caveat against arrest in force prevents the issue of a warrant to arrest the property
@export Under Order 33, rule 5(2), does a caveat against arrest in force prevent the issue of a warrant to arrest the property?
GIVEN `there is a caveat against arrest in force with respect to the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that there is a caveat against arrest in force with respect to the property?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 5(2), does a caveat against arrest in force prevent the issue of a warrant to arrest the property` IS
    `o 33 r 5(2) a caveat against arrest in force prevents the issue of a warrant to arrest the property` `there is a caveat against arrest in force with respect to the property`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 33, rule 6 -- Remedy where property protected by caveat is arrested without good and sufficient reason`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 33, rule 6.  Calls: o 33 r 6 the Court may discharge the warrant
