GIVEN `property with respect to which a caveat against arrest is in force is arrested in pursuance of a warrant of arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that property with respect to which a caveat against arrest is in force is arrested in pursuance of a warrant of arrest?
      `the party at whose instance the caveat was entered applies to the Court by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party at whose instance the caveat was entered applies to the Court by summons?
      `the Court is not satisfied that the party procuring the arrest had a good and sufficient reason for so doing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court is not satisfied that the party procuring the arrest had a good and sufficient reason for so doing?
      `the Court orders the last mentioned party to pay to the applicant damages in respect of the loss suffered by the applicant as a result of the arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court orders the last mentioned party to pay to the applicant damages in respect of the loss suffered by the applicant as a result of the arrest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 6, may the Court order the party who procured the arrest to pay me damages` IS
    `o 33 r 6 the Court may order the party procuring the arrest to pay damages` `property with respect to which a caveat against arrest is in force is arrested in pursuance of a warrant of arrest` `the party at whose instance the caveat was entered applies to the Court by summons` `the Court is not satisfied that the party procuring the arrest had a good and sufficient reason for so doing` `the Court orders the last mentioned party to pay to the applicant damages in respect of the loss suffered by the applicant as a result of the arrest`

