§§ `Order 33, rule 10 -- Service on ships, etc.: How effected`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 33, rule 10(1).  Calls: o 33 r 10(1) service on a ship, freight or cargo is effected by affixing and leaving a copy (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 33, rule 10(1), does the duty arise on my facts, so that service on a ship, freight or cargo is effected by affixing and leaving a copy?
GIVEN `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo?
      `neither paragraph (2) nor Rule 11 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that neither paragraph (2) nor Rule 11 applies?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 10(1), does the duty arise on my facts, so that service on a ship, freight or cargo is effected by affixing and leaving a copy` IS
    `o 33 r 10(1) service on a ship, freight or cargo is effected by affixing and leaving a copy (the duty arises)` `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo` `neither paragraph (2) nor Rule 11 applies`

-- Order 33, rule 10(1).  Calls: o 33 r 10(1) service on a ship, freight or cargo is effected by affixing and leaving a copy
@export Under Order 33, rule 10(1), has service on the ship, freight or cargo been effected by affixing and leaving a copy?
GIVEN `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo?
      `neither paragraph (2) nor Rule 11 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that neither paragraph (2) nor Rule 11 applies?
      `the warrant or originating claim is affixed for a short time on any mast of the ship or on the outside of any suitable part of the ship’s superstructure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the warrant or originating claim is affixed for a short time on any mast of the ship or on the outside of any suitable part of the ship’s superstructure?
      `on removing it, a copy is left affixed (in the case of the warrant) in its place or (in the case of the originating claim) on a sheltered, conspicuous part of the ship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that on removing it, a copy is left affixed (in the case of the warrant) in its place or (in the case of the originating claim) on a sheltered, conspicuous part of the ship?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 10(1), has service on the ship, freight or cargo been effected by affixing and leaving a copy` IS
    `o 33 r 10(1) service on a ship, freight or cargo is effected by affixing and leaving a copy` `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo` `neither paragraph (2) nor Rule 11 applies` `the warrant or originating claim is affixed for a short time on any mast of the ship or on the outside of any suitable part of the ship’s superstructure` `on removing it, a copy is left affixed (in the case of the warrant) in its place or (in the case of the originating claim) on a sheltered, conspicuous part of the ship`

-- Order 33, rule 10(2).  Calls: o 33 r 10(2) service on landed or transhipped cargo is effected as required (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 33, rule 10(2), does the duty arise on my facts, so that service on landed or transhipped cargo is effected as required?
GIVEN `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against freight or cargo or both` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against freight or cargo or both?
      `the cargo has been landed or transhipped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the cargo has been landed or transhipped?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 10(2), does the duty arise on my facts, so that service on landed or transhipped cargo is effected as required` IS
    `o 33 r 10(2) service on landed or transhipped cargo is effected as required (the duty arises)` `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against freight or cargo or both` `the cargo has been landed or transhipped`

-- Order 33, rule 10(2).  Calls: o 33 r 10(2) service on landed or transhipped cargo is effected as required
@export Under Order 33, rule 10(2), has service on landed or transhipped cargo been effected as required?
GIVEN `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against freight or cargo or both` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against freight or cargo or both?
      `the cargo has been landed or transhipped` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the cargo has been landed or transhipped?
      `service is by placing the warrant or originating claim for a short time on the cargo and, on removing it, leaving a copy of it on the cargo` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that service is by placing the warrant or originating claim for a short time on the cargo and, on removing it, leaving a copy of it on the cargo?
      `the cargo is in the custody of a person who will not permit access to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the cargo is in the custody of a person who will not permit access to it?
      `service is by leaving a copy of the warrant or originating claim with that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that service is by leaving a copy of the warrant or originating claim with that person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 10(2), has service on landed or transhipped cargo been effected as required` IS
    `o 33 r 10(2) service on landed or transhipped cargo is effected as required` `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against freight or cargo or both` `the cargo has been landed or transhipped` `service is by placing the warrant or originating claim for a short time on the cargo and, on removing it, leaving a copy of it on the cargo` `the cargo is in the custody of a person who will not permit access to it` `service is by leaving a copy of the warrant or originating claim with that person`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 33, rule 11 -- Service on ships, etc., during relevant period`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 33, rule 11(1).  Calls: o 33 r 11(1) service may be effected on the agent of the ship during the relevant period
@export Under Order 33, rule 11(1), may service be effected on the agent of the ship during the relevant period?
GIVEN `it is the relevant period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is the relevant period?
      `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo?
      `Rule 10(2) does not apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that Rule 10(2) does not apply?
      `a copy is left with the agent of the ship or, where the agent is a body corporate, at the registered or principal office of the agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a copy is left with the agent of the ship or, where the agent is a body corporate, at the registered or principal office of the agent?
      `the warrant or originating claim is transmitted by fax to the fax number (if any) specified by the agent or by electronic mail to the electronic mail address (if any) specified by the agent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the warrant or originating claim is transmitted by fax to the fax number (if any) specified by the agent or by electronic mail to the electronic mail address (if any) specified by the agent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 11(1), may service be effected on the agent of the ship during the relevant period` IS
    `o 33 r 11(1) service may be effected on the agent of the ship during the relevant period` `it is the relevant period` `the service is of a warrant of arrest or originating claim in an action in rem against a ship, freight or cargo` `Rule 10(2) does not apply` `a copy is left with the agent of the ship or, where the agent is a body corporate, at the registered or principal office of the agent` `the warrant or originating claim is transmitted by fax to the fax number (if any) specified by the agent or by electronic mail to the electronic mail address (if any) specified by the agent`

-- Order 33, rule 11(2).  Calls: o 33 r 11(2)(a) the warrant or originating claim is deemed served on the property
@export Under Order 33, rule 11(2), is the warrant or originating claim deemed served on the property?
GIVEN `the warrant of arrest or originating claim is served in accordance with paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the warrant of arrest or originating claim is served in accordance with paragraph (1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 11(2), is the warrant or originating claim deemed served on the property` IS
    `o 33 r 11(2)(a) the warrant or originating claim is deemed served on the property` `the warrant of arrest or originating claim is served in accordance with paragraph (1)`

-- Order 33, rule 11(4).  Calls: o 33 r 11(4) Order 6 Rule 6(5) and (6) applies to the originating claim
@export Under Order 33, rule 11(4), do Order 6, Rule 6(5) and (6) apply to my originating claim served on the agent?
GIVEN `the originating claim issued under this Order is served in accordance with paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the originating claim issued under this Order is served in accordance with paragraph (1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 11(4), do Order 6, Rule 6(5) and (6) apply to my originating claim served on the agent` IS
    `o 33 r 11(4) Order 6 Rule 6(5) and (6) applies to the originating claim` `the originating claim issued under this Order is served in accordance with paragraph (1)`

-- Order 33, rule 11(4).  Calls: o 33 r 11(4)(a) the claimant files a memorandum of service in Form 12 with the particulars
@export Under Order 33, rule 11(4), may I, as claimant, file a memorandum of service in Form 12 to avoid the bar on default judgment?
GIVEN `an originating claim issued under this Order is served in accordance with paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an originating claim issued under this Order is served in accordance with paragraph (1)?
      `the claimant files a memorandum of service in Form 12` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the claimant files a memorandum of service in Form 12?
      `it contains the day of the week, date and time on which the originating claim was served, where it was served, how it was served, and the person on whom it was served and the capacity in which that person was served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it contains the day of the week, date and time on which the originating claim was served, where it was served, how it was served, and the person on whom it was served and the capacity in which that person was served?
      `there is annexed a copy of the results of a search showing the identity of the agent of the ship and the location of the ship or, where the property is cargo, the ship in which the cargo was carried, within the limits of the port declared under section 3(1) of the Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore Act, on the date and at the time of the service of the originating claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that there is annexed a copy of the results of a search showing the identity of the agent of the ship and the location of the ship or, where the property is cargo, the ship in which the cargo was carried, within the limits of the port declared under section 3(1) of the Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore Act, on the date and at the time of the service of the originating claim?
      `it states the date and time on which the search was conducted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it states the date and time on which the search was conducted?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 11(4), may I, as claimant, file a memorandum of service in Form 12 to avoid the bar on default judgment` IS
    `o 33 r 11(4)(a) the claimant files a memorandum of service in Form 12 with the particulars` `an originating claim issued under this Order is served in accordance with paragraph (1)` `the claimant files a memorandum of service in Form 12` `it contains the day of the week, date and time on which the originating claim was served, where it was served, how it was served, and the person on whom it was served and the capacity in which that person was served` `there is annexed a copy of the results of a search showing the identity of the agent of the ship and the location of the ship or, where the property is cargo, the ship in which the cargo was carried, within the limits of the port declared under section 3(1) of the Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore Act, on the date and at the time of the service of the originating claim` `it states the date and time on which the search was conducted`

-- Order 33, rule 11(4).  Calls: o 33 r 11(4) the claimant is entitled to enter final or interlocutory judgment in default
@export Under Order 33, rule 11(4), am I entitled to enter judgment in default of notice or defence?
GIVEN `an originating claim issued under this Order is served in accordance with paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an originating claim issued under this Order is served in accordance with paragraph (1)?
      `within 8 days after service the claimant files the memorandum of service in Form 12 with the particulars, the annexed search results and the statement of the date and time of the search` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that within 8 days after service the claimant files the memorandum of service in Form 12 with the particulars, the annexed search results and the statement of the date and time of the search?
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court otherwise orders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 11(4), am I entitled to enter judgment in default of notice or defence` IS
    `o 33 r 11(4) the claimant is entitled to enter final or interlocutory judgment in default` `an originating claim issued under this Order is served in accordance with paragraph (1)` `within 8 days after service the claimant files the memorandum of service in Form 12 with the particulars, the annexed search results and the statement of the date and time of the search` `the Court otherwise orders`

-- Order 33, rule 11(4)(a).  Calls: o 33 r 11(4)(a) the claimant files the memorandum of service in time
@export Under Order 33, rule 11(4)(a), did I, as claimant, file the memorandum of service in time?
GIVEN `the year it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year was it done? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the month it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month was it done, from 1 for January to 12 for December? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the day of the month it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month was it done? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, Rule 3?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 11(4)(a), did I, as claimant, file the memorandum of service in time` IS
    `o 33 r 11(4)(a) the claimant files the memorandum of service in time` (`roc7 seat wiring: the day it was done, from what I know` `the year it was done` `the month it was done` `the day of the month it was done`) `the last day for doing the act` `the date I am asking about`

-- Order 33, rule 11(5).  Calls: o 33 r 11(5) it is the relevant period by (a) or (b)
@export Under Order 33, rule 11(5), is it the relevant period?
GIVEN `regulations 61A, 61B and 61C of the Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore (Port) Regulations (Cap. 170A, Rg 7) are in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that regulations 61A, 61B and 61C of the Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore (Port) Regulations (Cap. 170A, Rg 7) are in force?
      `Part 3 of the Second Schedule to the COVID-19 (Temporary Measures) (Control Order) Regulations 2020 (G.N. No. S 254/2020) is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that Part 3 of the Second Schedule to the COVID-19 (Temporary Measures) (Control Order) Regulations 2020 (G.N. No. S 254/2020) is in force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 11(5), is it the relevant period` IS
    `o 33 r 11(5) it is the relevant period by (a) or (b)` `regulations 61A, 61B and 61C of the Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore (Port) Regulations (Cap. 170A, Rg 7) are in force` `Part 3 of the Second Schedule to the COVID-19 (Temporary Measures) (Control Order) Regulations 2020 (G.N. No. S 254/2020) is in force`

