§§ `Order 33, rule 13 -- Release of property under arrest`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 33, rule 13.  Calls: o 33 r 13 an instrument of release is issued under this Rule
@export Under Order 33, rule 13, is an instrument of release issued under this Rule?
GIVEN `an instrument of release in Form 54 is issued out of the Registry for property arrested in pursuance of a warrant of arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an instrument of release in Form 54 is issued out of the Registry for property arrested in pursuance of a warrant of arrest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 13, is an instrument of release issued under this Rule` IS
    `o 33 r 13 an instrument of release is issued under this Rule` `an instrument of release in Form 54 is issued out of the Registry for property arrested in pursuance of a warrant of arrest`

-- Order 33, rule 13(1).  Calls: o 33 r 13(1) the property is released only under an instrument of release in Form 54 (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 33, rule 13(1), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the property is released only under an instrument of release in Form 54?
GIVEN `the property has been arrested in pursuance of a warrant of arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the property has been arrested in pursuance of a warrant of arrest?
      `the property is not sold under an order of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the property is not sold under an order of the Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 13(1), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the property is released only under an instrument of release in Form 54` IS
    `o 33 r 13(1) the property is released only under an instrument of release in Form 54 (the duty arises)` `the property has been arrested in pursuance of a warrant of arrest` `the property is not sold under an order of the Court`

-- Order 33, rule 13(1).  Calls: o 33 r 13(1) the property is released only under an instrument of release in Form 54
@export Under Order 33, rule 13(1), is the property released only under an instrument of release in Form 54?
GIVEN `the property has been arrested in pursuance of a warrant of arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the property has been arrested in pursuance of a warrant of arrest?
      `the property is not sold under an order of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the property is not sold under an order of the Court?
      `the property is released under the authority of an instrument of release, in Form 54, issued out of the Registry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the property is released under the authority of an instrument of release, in Form 54, issued out of the Registry?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 13(1), is the property released only under an instrument of release in Form 54` IS
    `o 33 r 13(1) the property is released only under an instrument of release in Form 54` `the property has been arrested in pursuance of a warrant of arrest` `the property is not sold under an order of the Court` `the property is released under the authority of an instrument of release, in Form 54, issued out of the Registry`

-- Order 33, rule 13(2).  Calls: o 33 r 13(2) a release may be issued
@export Under Order 33, rule 13(2), may a release be issued while a caveat against release is in force?
GIVEN `a caveat against release is in force with respect to the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a caveat against release is in force with respect to the property?
      `at the time of the issue of the release the property is under arrest in one or more other actions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that at the time of the issue of the release the property is under arrest in one or more other actions?
      `the Court so orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court so orders?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 13(2), may a release be issued while a caveat against release is in force` IS
    `o 33 r 13(2) a release may be issued` `a caveat against release is in force with respect to the property` `at the time of the issue of the release the property is under arrest in one or more other actions` `the Court so orders`

-- Order 33, rule 13(3).  Calls: o 33 r 13(3) a release may be issued on the application
@export Under Order 33, rule 13(3), may a release be issued on my application?
GIVEN `the applicant is a party to the action in which the warrant of arrest was issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the applicant is a party to the action in which the warrant of arrest was issued?
      `the Court so orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court so orders?
      `all the other parties to the action, except any defendant who has not filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest, consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that all the other parties to the action, except any defendant who has not filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest, consent?
      `paragraph (2) bars the issue of the release` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that paragraph (2) bars the issue of the release?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 13(3), may a release be issued on my application` IS
    `o 33 r 13(3) a release may be issued on the application` `the applicant is a party to the action in which the warrant of arrest was issued` `the Court so orders` `all the other parties to the action, except any defendant who has not filed a notice of intention to contest or not contest, consent` `paragraph (2) bars the issue of the release`

-- Order 33, rule 13(4).  Calls: o 33 r 13(4) the applicant has done what paragraph (4) requires before the release is issued (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 33, rule 13(4), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the applicant has done what paragraph (4) requires before the release is issued?
GIVEN `a release is to be issued on the application of the party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a release is to be issued on the application of the party?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 13(4), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the applicant has done what paragraph (4) requires before the release is issued` IS
    `o 33 r 13(4) the applicant has done what paragraph (4) requires before the release is issued (the duty arises)` `a release is to be issued on the application of the party`

-- Order 33, rule 13(4).  Calls: o 33 r 13(4) the applicant has done what paragraph (4) requires before the release is issued
@export Under Order 33, rule 13(4), have I done what paragraph (4) requires before the release is issued?
GIVEN `a release is to be issued on the application of the party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a release is to be issued on the application of the party?
      `paragraph (2)(a) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that paragraph (2)(a) applies?
      `the party has given notice to any party at whose instance a subsisting caveat against release has been entered, or that party's solicitor, requiring the caveat to be withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party has given notice to any party at whose instance a subsisting caveat against release has been entered, or that party's solicitor, requiring the caveat to be withdrawn?
      `the party has filed an instrument of release in Form 54` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party has filed an instrument of release in Form 54?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 13(4), have I done what paragraph (4) requires before the release is issued` IS
    `o 33 r 13(4) the applicant has done what paragraph (4) requires before the release is issued` `a release is to be issued on the application of the party` `paragraph (2)(a) applies` `the party has given notice to any party at whose instance a subsisting caveat against release has been entered, or that party's solicitor, requiring the caveat to be withdrawn` `the party has filed an instrument of release in Form 54`

-- Order 33, rule 13(5).  Calls: o 33 r 13(5) the party has done what paragraph (5) requires before the property is released (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 33, rule 13(5), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the party has done what paragraph (5) requires before the property is released?
GIVEN `the property under arrest is about to be released in compliance with a release issued under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the property under arrest is about to be released in compliance with a release issued under this Rule?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 13(5), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the party has done what paragraph (5) requires before the property is released` IS
    `o 33 r 13(5) the party has done what paragraph (5) requires before the property is released (the duty arises)` `the property under arrest is about to be released in compliance with a release issued under this Rule`

-- Order 33, rule 13(5).  Calls: o 33 r 13(5) the party has done what paragraph (5) requires before the property is released
@export Under Order 33, rule 13(5), have I done what paragraph (5) requires before the property is released?
GIVEN `the property under arrest is about to be released in compliance with a release issued under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the property under arrest is about to be released in compliance with a release issued under this Rule?
      `the party has paid the fees of the Sheriff already incurred and lodged in the Sheriff's office an undertaking to pay on demand the other fees and expenses in connection with the arrest, care and custody of the property and its release` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party has paid the fees of the Sheriff already incurred and lodged in the Sheriff's office an undertaking to pay on demand the other fees and expenses in connection with the arrest, care and custody of the property and its release?
      `the party has lodged in the Sheriff's office an undertaking to pay on demand all such fees and expenses, whether incurred or to be incurred` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party has lodged in the Sheriff's office an undertaking to pay on demand all such fees and expenses, whether incurred or to be incurred?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 13(5), have I done what paragraph (5) requires before the property is released` IS
    `o 33 r 13(5) the party has done what paragraph (5) requires before the property is released` `the property under arrest is about to be released in compliance with a release issued under this Rule` `the party has paid the fees of the Sheriff already incurred and lodged in the Sheriff's office an undertaking to pay on demand the other fees and expenses in connection with the arrest, care and custody of the property and its release` `the party has lodged in the Sheriff's office an undertaking to pay on demand all such fees and expenses, whether incurred or to be incurred`

-- Order 33, rule 13(6).  Calls: o 33 r 13(6) the Court may vary or revoke the Sheriff's directions
@export Under Order 33, rule 13(6), may the Court vary or revoke the Sheriff's directions to me?
GIVEN `a party objects to directions given to that party by the Sheriff under paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a party objects to directions given to that party by the Sheriff under paragraph (5)?
      `the party applies to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party applies to the Court?
      `the Court varies or revokes the directions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court varies or revokes the directions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 13(6), may the Court vary or revoke the Sheriff's directions to me` IS
    `o 33 r 13(6) the Court may vary or revoke the Sheriff's directions` `a party objects to directions given to that party by the Sheriff under paragraph (5)` `the party applies to the Court` `the Court varies or revokes the directions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 33, rule 14 -- Caveat against release and payment`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 33, rule 14(1).  Calls: o 33 r 14(1) the caveat against release and payment is filed in Form 55 and entered in the record of caveats (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 33, rule 14(1), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the caveat against release and payment is filed in Form 55 and entered in the record of caveats?
GIVEN `the person desires to prevent the release of any property under arrest in an action in rem and the payment out of Court of any money in Court representing the proceeds of sale of that property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person desires to prevent the release of any property under arrest in an action in rem and the payment out of Court of any money in Court representing the proceeds of sale of that property?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 14(1), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the caveat against release and payment is filed in Form 55 and entered in the record of caveats` IS
    `o 33 r 14(1) the caveat against release and payment is filed in Form 55 and entered in the record of caveats (the duty arises)` `the person desires to prevent the release of any property under arrest in an action in rem and the payment out of Court of any money in Court representing the proceeds of sale of that property`

-- Order 33, rule 14(1).  Calls: o 33 r 14(1) the caveat against release and payment is filed in Form 55 and entered in the record of caveats
@export Under Order 33, rule 14(1), have I filed my caveat against release and payment in Form 55 and had it entered?
GIVEN `the person desires to prevent the release of any property under arrest in an action in rem and the payment out of Court of any money in Court representing the proceeds of sale of that property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person desires to prevent the release of any property under arrest in an action in rem and the payment out of Court of any money in Court representing the proceeds of sale of that property?
      `the person files in the Registry a caveat in Form 55` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person files in the Registry a caveat in Form 55?
      `the caveat so filed is entered in the record of caveats` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the caveat so filed is entered in the record of caveats?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 14(1), have I filed my caveat against release and payment in Form 55 and had it entered` IS
    `o 33 r 14(1) the caveat against release and payment is filed in Form 55 and entered in the record of caveats` `the person desires to prevent the release of any property under arrest in an action in rem and the payment out of Court of any money in Court representing the proceeds of sale of that property` `the person files in the Registry a caveat in Form 55` `the caveat so filed is entered in the record of caveats`

-- Order 33, rule 14(2).  Calls: o 33 r 14(2) the Court may order the person who procured the caveat to pay damages
@export Under Order 33, rule 14(2), may the Court order the person who procured the caveat to pay me damages for the delay?
GIVEN `the release of any property under arrest is delayed by the entry of a caveat under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the release of any property under arrest is delayed by the entry of a caveat under this Rule?
      `the applicant has an interest in that property and applies to the Court by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the applicant has an interest in that property and applies to the Court by summons?
      `the Court is not satisfied that the person procuring the entry of the caveat had a good and sufficient reason for doing so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court is not satisfied that the person procuring the entry of the caveat had a good and sufficient reason for doing so?
      `the Court makes an order requiring the person who procured the entry of the caveat to pay to the applicant damages in respect of the loss suffered by the applicant by reason of the delay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court makes an order requiring the person who procured the entry of the caveat to pay to the applicant damages in respect of the loss suffered by the applicant by reason of the delay?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 14(2), may the Court order the person who procured the caveat to pay me damages for the delay` IS
    `o 33 r 14(2) the Court may order the person who procured the caveat to pay damages` `the release of any property under arrest is delayed by the entry of a caveat under this Rule` `the applicant has an interest in that property and applies to the Court by summons` `the Court is not satisfied that the person procuring the entry of the caveat had a good and sufficient reason for doing so` `the Court makes an order requiring the person who procured the entry of the caveat to pay to the applicant damages in respect of the loss suffered by the applicant by reason of the delay`

