§§ `Order 33, rule 15 -- Duration of caveats`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 33, rule 15(1).  Calls: o 33 r 15(1) the person at whose instance a caveat was entered may withdraw it
@export Under Order 33, rule 15(1), may I withdraw my caveat by filing a withdrawal in Form 56?
GIVEN `the person is the person at whose instance the caveat was entered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is the person at whose instance the caveat was entered?
      `the person files a withdrawal of caveat in Form 56` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person files a withdrawal of caveat in Form 56?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 15(1), may I withdraw my caveat by filing a withdrawal in Form 56` IS
    `o 33 r 15(1) the person at whose instance a caveat was entered may withdraw it` `the person is the person at whose instance the caveat was entered` `the person files a withdrawal of caveat in Form 56`

-- Order 33, rule 15(1).  Calls: o 33 r 15(1) the caveat is valid on the date
@export Under Order 33, rule 15(1), is the caveat still valid on the date I am asking about?
GIVEN `the last day of the validity` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the validity, counted under Order 3, Rule 3?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 15(1), is the caveat still valid on the date I am asking about` IS
    `o 33 r 15(1) the caveat is valid on the date` `the last day of the validity` `the date I am asking about`

-- Order 33, rule 15(2).  Calls: o 33 r 15(2) the period of validity of a caveat may be extended
@export Under Order 33, rule 15(2), may the period of validity of a caveat be extended?
GIVEN `a caveat is entered in the record of caveats` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a caveat is entered in the record of caveats?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 15(2), may the period of validity of a caveat be extended` IS
    `o 33 r 15(2) the period of validity of a caveat may be extended` `a caveat is entered in the record of caveats`

-- Order 33, rule 15(2).  Calls: o 33 r 15(2) the bar on extension prevents the entry of successive caveats
@export Under Order 33, rule 15(2), does the bar on extension prevent me entering a successive caveat?
GIVEN `the person seeks to enter a caveat after an earlier caveat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person seeks to enter a caveat after an earlier caveat?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 15(2), does the bar on extension prevent me entering a successive caveat` IS
    `o 33 r 15(2) the bar on extension prevents the entry of successive caveats` `the person seeks to enter a caveat after an earlier caveat`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 33, rule 16 -- Bail`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 33, rule 16(1).  Calls: o 33 r 16(1) bail is given by bond in Form 57 entered into before a commissioner for oaths or the Registrar (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 33, rule 16(1), does the duty arise on my facts, so that bail is given by bond in Form 57 entered into before a commissioner for oaths or the Registrar?
GIVEN `bail on behalf of a party to an action in rem is to be given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that bail on behalf of a party to an action in rem is to be given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 16(1), does the duty arise on my facts, so that bail is given by bond in Form 57 entered into before a commissioner for oaths or the Registrar` IS
    `o 33 r 16(1) bail is given by bond in Form 57 entered into before a commissioner for oaths or the Registrar (the duty arises)` `bail on behalf of a party to an action in rem is to be given`

-- Order 33, rule 16(1).  Calls: o 33 r 16(1) bail is given by bond in Form 57 entered into before a commissioner for oaths or the Registrar
@export Under Order 33, rule 16(1), is the bail given by bond in Form 57, entered into before the right person?
GIVEN `bail on behalf of a party to an action in rem is to be given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that bail on behalf of a party to an action in rem is to be given?
      `bail is given by bond in Form 57` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that bail is given by bond in Form 57?
      `the sureties to the bond enter into the bond before a commissioner for oaths not being a commissioner who, or whose partner, is acting as solicitor or agent for the party on whose behalf the bail is to be given, or before the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the sureties to the bond enter into the bond before a commissioner for oaths not being a commissioner who, or whose partner, is acting as solicitor or agent for the party on whose behalf the bail is to be given, or before the Registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 16(1), is the bail given by bond in Form 57, entered into before the right person` IS
    `o 33 r 16(1) bail is given by bond in Form 57 entered into before a commissioner for oaths or the Registrar` `bail on behalf of a party to an action in rem is to be given` `bail is given by bond in Form 57` `the sureties to the bond enter into the bond before a commissioner for oaths not being a commissioner who, or whose partner, is acting as solicitor or agent for the party on whose behalf the bail is to be given, or before the Registrar`

-- Order 33, rule 16(2).  Calls: o 33 r 16(2) the surety makes an affidavit that the surety is able to pay (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 33, rule 16(2), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the surety makes an affidavit that the surety is able to pay?
GIVEN `a surety is a surety to a bail bond` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a surety is a surety to a bail bond?
      `paragraph (3) does not excuse the affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that paragraph (3) does not excuse the affidavit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 16(2), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the surety makes an affidavit that the surety is able to pay` IS
    `o 33 r 16(2) the surety makes an affidavit that the surety is able to pay (the duty arises)` `a surety is a surety to a bail bond` `paragraph (3) does not excuse the affidavit`

-- Order 33, rule 16(2).  Calls: o 33 r 16(2) the surety makes an affidavit that the surety is able to pay
@export Under Order 33, rule 16(2), has the surety made an affidavit that the surety is able to pay?
GIVEN `a surety is a surety to a bail bond` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a surety is a surety to a bail bond?
      `paragraph (3) does not excuse the affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that paragraph (3) does not excuse the affidavit?
      `the surety makes an affidavit stating that the surety is able to pay the sum for which the bond is given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the surety makes an affidavit stating that the surety is able to pay the sum for which the bond is given?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 16(2), has the surety made an affidavit that the surety is able to pay` IS
    `o 33 r 16(2) the surety makes an affidavit that the surety is able to pay` `a surety is a surety to a bail bond` `paragraph (3) does not excuse the affidavit` `the surety makes an affidavit stating that the surety is able to pay the sum for which the bond is given`

-- Order 33, rule 16(3).  Calls: o 33 r 16(3) an affidavit is to be made on behalf of the corporation
@export Under Order 33, rule 16(3), is an affidavit to be made on behalf of a corporation that is a surety?
GIVEN `a corporation is a surety to a bail bond given on behalf of a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a corporation is a surety to a bail bond given on behalf of a party?
      `the opposite party requires the affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the opposite party requires the affidavit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 16(3), is an affidavit to be made on behalf of a corporation that is a surety` IS
    `o 33 r 16(3) an affidavit is to be made on behalf of the corporation` `a corporation is a surety to a bail bond given on behalf of a party` `the opposite party requires the affidavit`

-- Order 33, rule 16(3).  Calls: o 33 r 16(3) the affidavit required of a corporation is made by an officer (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 33, rule 16(3), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the affidavit required of a corporation is made by an officer?
GIVEN `a corporation is a surety to a bail bond given on behalf of a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a corporation is a surety to a bail bond given on behalf of a party?
      `the opposite party requires the affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the opposite party requires the affidavit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 16(3), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the affidavit required of a corporation is made by an officer` IS
    `o 33 r 16(3) the affidavit required of a corporation is made by an officer (the duty arises)` `a corporation is a surety to a bail bond given on behalf of a party` `the opposite party requires the affidavit`

-- Order 33, rule 16(3).  Calls: o 33 r 16(3) the affidavit required of a corporation is made by an officer
@export Under Order 33, rule 16(3), is the corporation's affidavit made by an officer of the corporation?
GIVEN `a corporation is a surety to a bail bond given on behalf of a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a corporation is a surety to a bail bond given on behalf of a party?
      `the opposite party requires the affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the opposite party requires the affidavit?
      `the affidavit is made by a director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the affidavit is made by a director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the corporation?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 16(3), is the corporation's affidavit made by an officer of the corporation` IS
    `o 33 r 16(3) the affidavit required of a corporation is made by an officer` `a corporation is a surety to a bail bond given on behalf of a party` `the opposite party requires the affidavit` `the affidavit is made by a director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the corporation`

-- Order 33, rule 16(4).  Calls: o 33 r 16(4) the bond may be filed at the moment
@export Under Order 33, rule 16(4), may the bond be filed at this time?
GIVEN `the day the notice of bail was served` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice of bail served?
      `the hour the notice of bail was served` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day was the notice of bail served, from 0 to 23?
      `the minute the notice of bail was served` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute past that hour was the notice of bail served, from 0 to 59?
      `the day the bond is to be filed` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the bond to be filed?
      `the hour the bond is to be filed` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day is the bond to be filed, from 0 to 23?
      `the minute the bond is to be filed` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute past that hour is the bond to be filed, from 0 to 59?
      `the opposite party has consented to filing sooner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the opposite party consented to the bond being filed sooner?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 16(4), may the bond be filed at this time` IS
    `o 33 r 16(4) the bond may be filed at the moment` (`roc7 seat wiring: the moment, from a day, an hour and a minute` `the day the notice of bail was served` `the hour the notice of bail was served` `the minute the notice of bail was served`) (`roc7 seat wiring: the moment, from a day, an hour and a minute` `the day the bond is to be filed` `the hour the bond is to be filed` `the minute the bond is to be filed`) `the opposite party has consented to filing sooner`

-- Order 33, rule 16(4).  Calls: o 33 r 16(4) the earliest moment the bond may be filed without consent
@export Under Order 33, rule 16(4), from what time may the bond be filed without the consent of the opposite party?
GIVEN `the day the notice of bail was served` IS A DATE @desc On what day was the notice of bail served?
      `the hour the notice of bail was served` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day was the notice of bail served, from 0 to 23?
      `the minute the notice of bail was served` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute past that hour was the notice of bail served, from 0 to 59?
GIVETH A Moment
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 16(4), from what time may the bond be filed without the consent of the opposite party` IS
    `o 33 r 16(4) the earliest moment the bond may be filed without consent` (`roc7 seat wiring: the moment, from a day, an hour and a minute` `the day the notice of bail was served` `the hour the notice of bail was served` `the minute the notice of bail was served`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 33, rule 17 -- Interveners`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 33, rule 17(1).  Calls: o 33 r 17(1) a person with an interest may intervene with the permission of the Court
@export Under Order 33, rule 17(1), may I, as a person with an interest, intervene with the permission of the Court?
GIVEN `property against which an action in rem is brought is under arrest or money representing the proceeds of sale of that property is in Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that property against which an action in rem is brought is under arrest or money representing the proceeds of sale of that property is in Court?
      `the person has an interest in that property or money and is not a defendant to the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person has an interest in that property or money and is not a defendant to the action?
      `the Court gives permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court gives permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 17(1), may I, as a person with an interest, intervene with the permission of the Court` IS
    `o 33 r 17(1) a person with an interest may intervene with the permission of the Court` `property against which an action in rem is brought is under arrest or money representing the proceeds of sale of that property is in Court` `the person has an interest in that property or money and is not a defendant to the action` `the Court gives permission`

-- Order 33, rule 17(2).  Calls: o 33 r 17(2) the application for permission to intervene is made by summons without notice with an affidavit (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 33, rule 17(2), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the application for permission to intervene is made by summons without notice with an affidavit?
GIVEN `an application is made for permission to intervene` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an application is made for permission to intervene?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 17(2), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the application for permission to intervene is made by summons without notice with an affidavit` IS
    `o 33 r 17(2) the application for permission to intervene is made by summons without notice with an affidavit (the duty arises)` `an application is made for permission to intervene`

-- Order 33, rule 17(2).  Calls: o 33 r 17(2) the application for permission to intervene is made by summons without notice with an affidavit
@export Under Order 33, rule 17(2), is my application for permission to intervene made by summons without notice with an affidavit?
GIVEN `an application is made for permission to intervene` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an application is made for permission to intervene?
      `the application is made by summons without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is made by summons without notice?
      `it is supported by an affidavit showing the interest of the applicant in the property against which the action is brought or in the money in Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is supported by an affidavit showing the interest of the applicant in the property against which the action is brought or in the money in Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 17(2), is my application for permission to intervene made by summons without notice with an affidavit` IS
    `o 33 r 17(2) the application for permission to intervene is made by summons without notice with an affidavit` `an application is made for permission to intervene` `the application is made by summons without notice` `it is supported by an affidavit showing the interest of the applicant in the property against which the action is brought or in the money in Court`

-- Order 33, rule 17(3).  Calls: o 33 r 17(3) the intervener files and serves a notice of intention to contest or not contest (the duty arises)
@export Under Order 33, rule 17(3), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the intervener files and serves a notice of intention to contest or not contest?
GIVEN `permission has been granted to the person to intervene in an action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been granted permission to intervene in the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 17(3), does the duty arise on my facts, so that the intervener files and serves a notice of intention to contest or not contest` IS
    `o 33 r 17(3) the intervener files and serves a notice of intention to contest or not contest (the duty arises)` `permission has been granted to the person to intervene in an action`

-- Order 33, rule 17(3).  Calls: o 33 r 17(3) the intervener files and serves a notice of intention to contest or not contest
@export Under Order 33, rule 17(3), have I, as an intervener, filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest?
GIVEN `permission has been granted to the person to intervene in an action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been granted permission to intervene in the action?
      `the person files and serves a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action in the Registry within the period specified in the order granting permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person files and serves a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action in the Registry within the period specified in the order granting permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 17(3), have I, as an intervener, filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest` IS
    `o 33 r 17(3) the intervener files and serves a notice of intention to contest or not contest` `permission has been granted to the person to intervene in an action` `the person files and serves a notice of intention to contest or not contest in the action in the Registry within the period specified in the order granting permission`

-- Order 33, rule 17(4).  Calls: o 33 r 17(4) the Court may order the intervener to serve a pleading
@export Under Order 33, rule 17(4), may the Court order me, as an intervener, to serve a pleading?
GIVEN `permission has been granted to the person to intervene in an action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person been granted permission to intervene in the action?
      `the Court orders the person to serve on every other party to the action such pleading as may be specified within such period as may be specified` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court orders the person to serve on every other party to the action such pleading as may be specified within such period as may be specified?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 17(4), may the Court order me, as an intervener, to serve a pleading` IS
    `o 33 r 17(4) the Court may order the intervener to serve a pleading` `permission has been granted to the person to intervene in an action` `the Court orders the person to serve on every other party to the action such pleading as may be specified within such period as may be specified`

