      `the party to the reference makes a written request to the Registrar to file such a statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party to the reference makes a written request to the Registrar to file such a statement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 42(5), may I request a statement of the grounds of the decision` IS
    `o 33 r 42(5) a party may request a statement of the grounds of the decision` `no statement of the grounds of the Registrar’s decision is filed with the decision` `no intimation has been given by the Registrar that the Registrar intends to file such a statement later` `the party to the reference makes a written request to the Registrar to file such a statement`

-- Order 33, rule 42(5).  Calls: o 33 r 42(5) the party makes the written request in time
@export Under Order 33, rule 42(5), did I make my written request for the grounds of the decision in time?
GIVEN `the year it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year was it done? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the month it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month was it done, from 1 for January to 12 for December? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the day of the month it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month was it done? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, Rule 3?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 42(5), did I make my written request for the grounds of the decision in time` IS
    `o 33 r 42(5) the party makes the written request in time` (`roc7 seat wiring: the day it was done, from what I know` `the year it was done` `the month it was done` `the day of the month it was done`) `the last day for doing the act` `the date I am asking about`

