§§ `Order 33, rule 43 -- Objection to decision on reference`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 33, rule 43(1).  Calls: o 33 r 43(1) a party to a reference may apply to a Judge to set aside or vary the decision
@export Under Order 33, rule 43(1), may I apply to a Judge to set aside or vary the Registrar's decision?
GIVEN `the party is a party to a reference to the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party is a party to a reference to the Registrar?
      `the party applies by summons to a Judge to set aside or vary the decision of the Registrar on the reference` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the party applies by summons to a Judge to set aside or vary the decision of the Registrar on the reference?
      `the summons specifies the points of objection to the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the summons specifies the points of objection to the decision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 43(1), may I apply to a Judge to set aside or vary the Registrar's decision` IS
    `o 33 r 43(1) a party to a reference may apply to a Judge to set aside or vary the decision` `the party is a party to a reference to the Registrar` `the party applies by summons to a Judge to set aside or vary the decision of the Registrar on the reference` `the summons specifies the points of objection to the decision`

-- Order 33, rule 43(1)(a).  Calls: o 33 r 43(1)(a) the summons is filed in time after the notice of the filing of the decision
@export Under Order 33, rule 43(1)(a), did I file my summons in time after the notice of the filing of the decision?
GIVEN `the year it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year was it done? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the month it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month was it done, from 1 for January to 12 for December? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the day of the month it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month was it done? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, Rule 3?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 43(1)(a), did I file my summons in time after the notice of the filing of the decision` IS
    `o 33 r 43(1)(a) the summons is filed in time after the notice of the filing of the decision` (`roc7 seat wiring: the day it was done, from what I know` `the year it was done` `the month it was done` `the day of the month it was done`) `the last day for doing the act` `the date I am asking about`

-- Order 33, rule 43(1)(b).  Calls: o 33 r 43(1)(b) the summons is filed in time after the notice of the statement of the grounds
@export Under Order 33, rule 43(1)(b), did I file my summons in time after the notice of the statement of the grounds?
GIVEN `the year it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year was it done? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the month it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc In which month was it done, from 1 for January to 12 for December? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the day of the month it was done` IS A NUMBER @desc On which day of the month was it done? (0 if it has not been done yet)
      `the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, Rule 3?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 43(1)(b), did I file my summons in time after the notice of the statement of the grounds` IS
    `o 33 r 43(1)(b) the summons is filed in time after the notice of the statement of the grounds` (`roc7 seat wiring: the day it was done, from what I know` `the year it was done` `the month it was done` `the day of the month it was done`) `the last day for doing the act` `the date I am asking about`

-- Order 33, rule 43(2).  Calls: o 33 r 43(2) the decision cannot yet be acted upon
@export Under Order 33, rule 43(2), can the Registrar's decision not yet be acted upon?
GIVEN `the time has elapsed for filing the summons referred to in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the time has elapsed for filing the summons referred to in paragraph (1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 43(2), can the Registrar's decision not yet be acted upon` IS
    `o 33 r 43(2) the decision cannot yet be acted upon` `the time has elapsed for filing the summons referred to in paragraph (1)`

-- Order 33, rule 43(2).  Calls: o 33 r 43(2) the decision may be acted upon
@export Under Order 33, rule 43(2), may the Registrar's decision be acted upon?
GIVEN `the time has elapsed for filing the summons referred to in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the time has elapsed for filing the summons referred to in paragraph (1)?
      `the Registrar or the Judge has otherwise directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Registrar or the Judge has otherwise directed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 43(2), may the Registrar's decision be acted upon` IS
    `o 33 r 43(2) the decision may be acted upon` `the time has elapsed for filing the summons referred to in paragraph (1)` `the Registrar or the Judge has otherwise directed`

-- Order 33, rule 43(3).  Calls: o 33 r 43(3) a direction may be given under paragraph (2) without the parties being given an opportunity of being heard
@export Under Order 33, rule 43(3), may a direction be given without the parties being given an opportunity of being heard?
GIVEN `a direction is to be given under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a direction is to be given under paragraph (2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 43(3), may a direction be given without the parties being given an opportunity of being heard` IS
    `o 33 r 43(3) a direction may be given under paragraph (2) without the parties being given an opportunity of being heard` `a direction is to be given under paragraph (2)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 33, rule 45 -- Saving for defence under Merchant Shipping Act`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 33, rule 45.  Calls: o 33 r 45 Rules 35 to 40 limit the right to rely by way of defence on the Merchant Shipping Act
@export Under Order 33, rule 45, do Rules 35 to 40 limit my right to rely on the limitation of liability in the Merchant Shipping Act?
GIVEN `the person is a shipowner or other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person is a shipowner or other person?
      `the person relies by way of defence on a provision of the Merchant Shipping Act which limits the amount of liability in connection with a ship or other property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the person relies by way of defence on a provision of the Merchant Shipping Act which limits the amount of liability in connection with a ship or other property?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 45, do Rules 35 to 40 limit my right to rely on the limitation of liability in the Merchant Shipping Act` IS
    `o 33 r 45 Rules 35 to 40 limit the right to rely by way of defence on the Merchant Shipping Act` `the person is a shipowner or other person` `the person relies by way of defence on a provision of the Merchant Shipping Act which limits the amount of liability in connection with a ship or other property`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 33, rule 46 -- Production of certain documents in marine insurance actions`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Order 33, rule 46(1).  Calls: o 33 r 46(1) the Court may order the production of documents in a marine insurance action
@export Under Order 33, rule 46(1), may the Court order the production of documents in my marine insurance action?
GIVEN `the action relates to a marine insurance policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the action relates to a marine insurance policy?
      `an application for production of documents is made by the insurer under Order 11, Rule 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an application for production of documents is made by the insurer under Order 11, Rule 2?
      `the Court is satisfied that the circumstances of the case are such that it is necessary or expedient to make an order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court is satisfied that the circumstances of the case are such that it is necessary or expedient to make an order?
      `the Court makes an order, either in Form 33 or in such other form as the Court thinks fit, for the production of such documents as are therein specified or described` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court makes an order, either in Form 33 or in such other form as the Court thinks fit, for the production of such documents as are therein specified or described?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 46(1), may the Court order the production of documents in my marine insurance action` IS
    `o 33 r 46(1) the Court may order the production of documents in a marine insurance action` `the action relates to a marine insurance policy` `an application for production of documents is made by the insurer under Order 11, Rule 2` `the Court is satisfied that the circumstances of the case are such that it is necessary or expedient to make an order` `the Court makes an order, either in Form 33 or in such other form as the Court thinks fit, for the production of such documents as are therein specified or described`

-- Order 33, rule 46(2).  Calls: o 33 r 46(2) the order may be made on terms as to staying proceedings or otherwise
@export Under Order 33, rule 46(2), may the order be made on terms as to staying proceedings?
GIVEN `an order is made under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that an order is made under this Rule?
      `the order is made on such terms, if any, as to staying proceedings in the action or otherwise, as the Court thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the order is made on such terms, if any, as to staying proceedings in the action or otherwise, as the Court thinks fit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 33, rule 46(2), may the order be made on terms as to staying proceedings` IS
    `o 33 r 46(2) the order may be made on terms as to staying proceedings or otherwise` `an order is made under this Rule` `the order is made on such terms, if any, as to staying proceedings in the action or otherwise, as the Court thinks fit`

-- ============================================================
-- roc8: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, Orders 34 to 38 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online; it is not the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a party to a civil action in the Singapore courts (a claimant, a defendant, a third party or an appellant), asking, on facts
-- they can state, what they must file or serve, by when, how, at what cost, what the Court may order, and what follows if they do not.
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in the modules imported above as the questions that person would ask.
-- Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question calls ONE layer-1 function.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, or a choice from a list -- one for each fact the person can
-- state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.  Where a rule asks about a document with several required parts, each part is
-- a yes/no question and the record the module expects is built inside the question by a wiring function.  Where a rule gives the Court a
-- time to fix ("such other period as the Court may fix"), the person says whether the Court has fixed one and, if so, the last day.
--   * A period is counted by Order 3, rule 3, which is not in these Orders.  Wherever the answer depends on a period, the person gives the
--     last day for the act (or, for a bar on a date, the first day it may be done), counted as Order 3, rule 3 requires.
--   * A question that the Rules answer only by a number of days has its own question ("how many days do I have to ...").
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Rules themselves give; NOTHING means the Rules do not answer on these
-- facts (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").  Never read NOTHING as no.  Order 3, rule 2(1) is a caveat on every answer:
-- the Court may order otherwise.
--
-- There is no seat for an official: where a provision addresses only the Registrar or the Court (for example Order 38, rule 11, the
-- Registrar's certificate), the rule is in layer 1 and the person meets it only through the questions below.

§ `Orders 34 to 38 of the Rules of Court 2021 -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's yes/no answers become the records the modules expect.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, b IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, d IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `o 34 r 5(2) supporting affidavit`
`o 34 r 5(2) supporting affidavit from my answers` MEANS `o 34 r 5(2) supporting affidavit` WITH
