      `my answer: o 37 r 2(2)(g) it states that there are no circumstances under Part 3 of the Act in which the Court must refuse to recognise or enforce` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this true of your document: it states that there are no circumstances under Part 3 of the Act in which the Court must refuse to recognise or enforce?
      `my answer: o 37 r 2(2)(h) it states whether there are any circumstances under Part 3 of the Act in which the Court may refuse to recognise or enforce` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this true of your document: it states whether there are any circumstances under Part 3 of the Act in which the Court may refuse to recognise or enforce?
      `my answer: o 37 r 2(2)(i) it states each reason why the Court should nevertheless recognise or enforce the judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this true of your document: it states each reason why the Court should nevertheless recognise or enforce the judgment?
      `the foreign judgment or part is to be recognised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that the foreign judgment or part is to be recognised?
      `the foreign judgment or part is to be enforced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that the foreign judgment or part is to be enforced?
      `there are circumstances in which the Court may refuse to recognise or enforce the foreign judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that there are circumstances in which the Court may refuse to recognise or enforce the foreign judgment?
