    `o 37 r 2(2) the supporting affidavit states what the paragraph requires` (`o 37 r 2(2) supporting affidavit from my answers` `my answer: o 37 r 2(2) it states the matters to the best of the information or belief of the deponent` `my answer: o 37 r 2(2)(a) it states that the judgment is a foreign judgment within the meaning of section 2(1)` `my answer: o 37 r 2(2)(b) it states that the judgment or that part has effect in the State of origin` `my answer: o 37 r 2(2)(c) it states that the judgment or that part is enforceable in the State of origin` `my answer: o 37 r 2(2)(d) it states that the exclusive choice of court agreement was concluded in a civil or commercial matter` `my answer: o 37 r 2(2)(e)(i) it states that at the date of the application the foreign judgment, or the part, has not been satisfied` `my answer: o 37 r 2(2)(e)(ii) it states the amount in respect of which, at the date of the application, the foreign judgment, or the part, remains unsatisfied` `my answer: o 37 r 2(2)(f) it states that the foreign judgment does not relate to a matter mentioned in section 9 or 10` `my answer: o 37 r 2(2)(g) it states that there are no circumstances under Part 3 of the Act in which the Court must refuse to recognise or enforce` `my answer: o 37 r 2(2)(h) it states whether there are any circumstances under Part 3 of the Act in which the Court may refuse to recognise or enforce` `my answer: o 37 r 2(2)(i) it states each reason why the Court should nevertheless recognise or enforce the judgment`) `the foreign judgment or part is to be recognised` `the foreign judgment or part is to be enforced` `there are circumstances in which the Court may refuse to recognise or enforce the foreign judgment`

