@export Under Order 37, rule 8, does the Court order still not take effect?
GIVEN `the date asked about` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (the date asked about)
      `has the Court fixed or allowed a date for: the last day on which an application to set aside may still be filed by a party on whom the Court order and the copy were served under Rule 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court fixed or allowed a date for this? (the last day on which an application to set aside may still be filed by a party on whom the Court order and the copy were served under Rule 6)
      `the date fixed or allowed for: the last day on which an application to set aside may still be filed by a party on whom the Court order and the copy were served under Rule 6` IS A DATE @desc If the Court has fixed or allowed a date, what is it? (any date if it has not)
      `an application to set aside the Court order is pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that an application to set aside the Court order is pending?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 37, rule 8, does the Court order still not take effect` IS
    `o 37 r 8 the Court order does not take effect yet` `the date asked about` (IF `has the Court fixed or allowed a date for: the last day on which an application to set aside may still be filed by a party on whom the Court order and the copy were served under Rule 6` THEN JUST `the date fixed or allowed for: the last day on which an application to set aside may still be filed by a party on whom the Court order and the copy were served under Rule 6` ELSE NOTHING) `an application to set aside the Court order is pending`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 38 -- Companies Act`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 38, rule 2(1), must my application under the Act be made by originating application?
GIVEN `it is an application under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that it is an application under the Act?
      `it is otherwise provided in the Act or this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that it is otherwise provided in the Act or this Order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 38, rule 2(1), must my application under the Act be made by originating application` IS
    `o 38 r 2(1) the application must be made by originating application` `it is an application under the Act` `it is otherwise provided in the Act or this Order`

@export Under Order 38, rule 2(3), must my application under section 216 be made by originating claim?
GIVEN `it is an application under section 216` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that it is an application under section 216?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 38, rule 2(3), must my application under section 216 be made by originating claim` IS
    `o 38 r 2(3) the application must be made by originating claim` `it is an application under section 216`

@export Under Order 38, rule 5(1), must the company file an affidavit verifying a list of qualifying creditors?
GIVEN `the Court orders under Rule 4 the proceedings mentioned in paragraph (2) of that Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that the Court orders under Rule 4 the proceedings mentioned in paragraph (2) of that Rule?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 38, rule 5(1), must the company file an affidavit verifying a list of qualifying creditors` IS
    `o 38 r 5(1) the duty arises to file in the Registry an affidavit verifying a list` `the Court orders under Rule 4 the proceedings mentioned in paragraph (2) of that Rule`

@export Under Order 38, rule 5(1), how many days does the company have to file the affidavit?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 38, rule 5(1), how many days does the company have to file the affidavit` IS
    (`o 38 r 5(1) the period for filing the affidavit`'s `period length`)

@export Under Order 38, rule 5(1), did the company file the affidavit in time?
GIVEN `the Court orders under Rule 4 the proceedings mentioned in paragraph (2) of that Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that the Court orders under Rule 4 the proceedings mentioned in paragraph (2) of that Rule?
      `the date the affidavit was filed in the Registry` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (the date the affidavit was filed in the Registry)
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 requires, from the event the Rule names.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 38, rule 5(1), did the company file the affidavit in time` IS
    `o 38 r 5(1) the affidavit is filed in time` `the Court orders under Rule 4 the proceedings mentioned in paragraph (2) of that Rule` `the date the affidavit was filed in the Registry` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

@export Under Order 38, rule 5(1), does the affidavit and list have the required content?
GIVEN `my answer: o 38 r 5(1) the affidavit is made by an officer of the company competent to make it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this true of your document: the affidavit is made by an officer of the company competent to make it?
      `my answer: o 38 r 5(1) the affidavit verifies a list` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this true of your document: the affidavit verifies a list?
      `my answer: o 38 r 5(1)(a) the list contains the name and address of every qualifying creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this true of your document: the list contains the name and address of every qualifying creditor?
      `my answer: o 38 r 5(1)(b) the list contains the amount due to each qualifying creditor or, for a claim subject to a contingency, sounding only in damages or not bearing a certain value, a just estimate of its value` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this true of your document: the list contains the amount due to each qualifying creditor or, for a claim subject to a contingency, sounding only in damages or not bearing a certain value, a just estimate of its value?
      `my answer: o 38 r 5(1)(c) the list contains the total of those amounts and values` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this true of your document: the list contains the total of those amounts and values?
      `the Court orders under Rule 4 the proceedings mentioned in paragraph (2) of that Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that the Court orders under Rule 4 the proceedings mentioned in paragraph (2) of that Rule?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 38, rule 5(1), does the affidavit and list have the required content` IS
    `o 38 r 5(1) the affidavit and the list have the required content` (`o 38 r 5(1) affidavit and list of qualifying creditors from my answers` `my answer: o 38 r 5(1) the affidavit is made by an officer of the company competent to make it` `my answer: o 38 r 5(1) the affidavit verifies a list` `my answer: o 38 r 5(1)(a) the list contains the name and address of every qualifying creditor` `my answer: o 38 r 5(1)(b) the list contains the amount due to each qualifying creditor or, for a claim subject to a contingency, sounding only in damages or not bearing a certain value, a just estimate of its value` `my answer: o 38 r 5(1)(c) the list contains the total of those amounts and values`) `the Court orders under Rule 4 the proceedings mentioned in paragraph (2) of that Rule`

@export Under Order 38, rule 6(2), am I entitled to inspect the list of qualifying creditors?
GIVEN `it is during ordinary business hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that it is during ordinary business hours?
      `the fee paid, in cents` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number or amount? (the fee paid, in cents)
      `it is at an office mentioned in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that it is at an office mentioned in paragraph (1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 38, rule 6(2), am I entitled to inspect the list of qualifying creditors` IS
    `o 38 r 6(2) the person is entitled to inspect the list and take extracts` `it is during ordinary business hours` `the fee paid, in cents` `it is at an office mentioned in paragraph (1)`

@export Under Order 38, rule 7, did the company send the notice in time?
GIVEN `the company has filed the affidavit required by Rule 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you filed the affidavit required by Rule 5?
      `the date the notice was sent by post` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (the date the notice was sent by post)
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 requires, from the event the Rule names.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 38, rule 7, did the company send the notice in time` IS
    `o 38 r 7 the notice is sent in time` `the company has filed the affidavit required by Rule 5` `the date the notice was sent by post` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

@export Under Order 38, rule 10, must the company send the person a notice requiring proof of the debt?
GIVEN `the company contends that a person is not entitled to be entered in the list of qualifying creditors in respect of any debt or claim or the full amount claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you contend that a person is not entitled to be entered in the list of qualifying creditors in respect of any debt or claim or the full amount claimed?
      `the company is willing to secure payment of that debt or claim by appropriating the full amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you willing to secure payment of that debt or claim by appropriating the full amount?
      `the Court so directs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that the Court so directs?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 38, rule 10, must the company send the person a notice requiring proof of the debt` IS
    `o 38 r 10 the duty arises to send the person a notice` `the company contends that a person is not entitled to be entered in the list of qualifying creditors in respect of any debt or claim or the full amount claimed` `the company is willing to secure payment of that debt or claim by appropriating the full amount` `the Court so directs`

@export Under Order 38, rule 10(a), is the time I give the person to file an affidavit at least 4 clear days after service of the notice?
GIVEN `the number of clear days between service of the notice and the time specified for filing the affidavit` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number or amount? (the number of clear days between service of the notice and the time specified for filing the affidavit)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 38, rule 10(a), is the time I give the person to file an affidavit at least 4 clear days after service of the notice` IS
    `o 38 r 10(a) the time specified is at least 4 clear days after service of the notice` `the number of clear days between service of the notice and the time specified for filing the affidavit`

@export Under Order 38, rule 13(1), is the hearing barred as too early?
GIVEN `the Court has ordered proceedings pursuant to paragraph (2) of Rule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that the Court has ordered proceedings pursuant to paragraph (2) of Rule 4?
      `the date of the hearing` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (the date of the hearing)
      `o 3 r 3 the first day on which the act may be done` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day on which this may be done? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 requires, from the event the Rule names.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 38, rule 13(1), is the hearing barred as too early` IS
    `o 38 r 13(1) the hearing is barred as too early` `the Court has ordered proceedings pursuant to paragraph (2) of Rule 4` `the date of the hearing` `o 3 r 3 the first day on which the act may be done`

@export Under Order 38, rule 14(1), did the bankrupt serve the copies at least 28 days before the hearing?
GIVEN `the person is a bankrupt who intends to make an application under section 148` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a bankrupt who intends to make an application under section 148?
      `the date a copy was served on the Official Assignee` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (the date a copy was served on the Official Assignee)
      `the trustee of the bankrupt's estate is not the Official Assignee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that the trustee of the bankrupt's estate is not the Official Assignee?
      `the date a copy was served on the trustee` IS A DATE @desc On what date? (the date a copy was served on the trustee)
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this? Count it as Order 3, rule 3 requires, from the event the Rule names.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 38, rule 14(1), did the bankrupt serve the copies at least 28 days before the hearing` IS
    `o 38 r 14(1) the copies are served at least 28 days before the hearing` `the person is a bankrupt who intends to make an application under section 148` `the date a copy was served on the Official Assignee` `the trustee of the bankrupt's estate is not the Official Assignee` `the date a copy was served on the trustee` `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`

@export Under Order 38, rule 14(2), does the bankrupt's affidavit state the particulars the rule requires?
GIVEN `my answer: o 38 r 14(2)(a) it states the name and registration number of the corporation in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this true of your document: it states the name and registration number of the corporation in question?
      `my answer: o 38 r 14(2)(b) it states the nature of the business or intended business of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this true of your document: it states the nature of the business or intended business of the corporation?
      `my answer: o 38 r 14(2)(c) it states the place or places where the business of the corporation is to be carried on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this true of your document: it states the place or places where the business of the corporation is to be carried on?
      `my answer: o 38 r 14(2)(d) it states whether the corporation is to be incorporated as a private or public company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this true of your document: it states whether the corporation is to be incorporated as a private or public company?
      `my answer: o 38 r 14(2)(e) it states the persons who are, or are to be, principally responsible for conducting the affairs of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this true of your document: it states the persons who are, or are to be, principally responsible for conducting the affairs of the corporation?
      `my answer: o 38 r 14(2)(f) it states the manner and capacity in which the bankrupt proposes to take part in or be concerned in the management of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this true of your document: it states the manner and capacity in which the bankrupt proposes to take part in or be concerned in the management of the corporation?
      `my answer: o 38 r 14(2)(g) it states the emoluments or other benefits to be obtained by the bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this true of your document: it states the emoluments or other benefits to be obtained by the bankrupt?
      `the corporation is not yet incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true in your case that the corporation is not yet incorporated?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 38, rule 14(2), does the bankrupt's affidavit state the particulars the rule requires` IS
    `o 38 r 14(2) the affidavit states the particulars the paragraph requires` (`o 38 r 14(2) affidavit from my answers` `my answer: o 38 r 14(2)(a) it states the name and registration number of the corporation in question` `my answer: o 38 r 14(2)(b) it states the nature of the business or intended business of the corporation` `my answer: o 38 r 14(2)(c) it states the place or places where the business of the corporation is to be carried on` `my answer: o 38 r 14(2)(d) it states whether the corporation is to be incorporated as a private or public company` `my answer: o 38 r 14(2)(e) it states the persons who are, or are to be, principally responsible for conducting the affairs of the corporation` `my answer: o 38 r 14(2)(f) it states the manner and capacity in which the bankrupt proposes to take part in or be concerned in the management of the corporation` `my answer: o 38 r 14(2)(g) it states the emoluments or other benefits to be obtained by the bankrupt`) `the corporation is not yet incorporated`

-- ============================================================
-- roc9: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026:
-- Orders 39 to 45 -- THE SEAT LAYER (part roc9).
-- The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a party to a civil action in the Singapore courts (a claimant, a defendant, a third party or an appellant), asking, on facts the party can state,
-- what the party must file or serve, by when, how, at what cost, what the court may order, and what follows if the party does not.
-- This layer phrases the rules already encoded in roc9-order-39 to roc9-order-45 as the questions that person would ask.
-- Nothing here is new law, and no rule is restated: each question turns plain answers into the arguments of ONE layer-1 function and calls it.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, a time of day, or a choice from a list -- one for each fact the person can state,
-- each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.  The records, MAYBE values and layer-1 choices the long modules expect are built inside each question, in its WHERE
-- (or by a wiring function named "Under Orders 39 to 45, ..."), from those answers.
--   * A date the Rules compute (the last day for doing an act, Order 3, Rule 3; the day service is deemed effected, Order 7, Rule 8; the moment a document is deemed filed, Order 28, Rule 10)
--     is asked as a date the person states: those Orders are another part's.  The person says the date; this layer never computes it.
--   * A person who may or may not exist ("where a receiver has been appointed", "the authorised officer") is asked as a choice: served, not served, or there is no such person.
--   * Whether a statement or document is required at all is asked as a choice: it is stated (filed), it is not, or it is not required on these facts.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Rules themselves give; NOTHING means the Rules do not answer on these facts
-- (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (roc9)").  Never read NOTHING as no.
-- Order 3, Rule 2(1) (the Rules' own caveat on every answer: the Court may extend or shorten a time, and may excuse an irregularity) applies to every answer here; it is not an input.
--
-- A question is asked of a PARTY's own situation.  There is no seat for an official: where a provision addresses only an official (the Registrar, the Sheriff, the Public Prosecutor
-- as a litigant is the exception, being a party), the rule is in layer 1 and the person meets it only through the questions below, as what they may claim, must give, or may expect.
-- The regulative rules with a deadline and a consequence (the DEONTIC cycles in Orders 42 and 44) are checked by #TRACE in the tests; a #TRACE is not a question the Interact form can ask,
-- so they are not exported here.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- A time of day from the hour and minute the person states (the modules count minutes after midnight).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      hour IS A NUMBER
      minute IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Moment
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my moment from a day and a time` MEANS
    Moment WITH
        `day of the moment` IS d -- input mapping
        `minutes after midnight` IS hour TIMES 60 PLUS minute -- input mapping

-- The choices for `Decision maker`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Orders 39 to 45, who would decide it` IS ONE OF
    `Under Orders 39 to 45, the court itself`
    `Under Orders 39 to 45, a Judge`
    `Under Orders 39 to 45, a District Judge`
    `Under Orders 39 to 45, a Magistrate`
    `Under Orders 39 to 45, the Registrar`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Orders 39 to 45, who would decide it`
GIVETH A `Decision maker`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for Decision maker` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Orders 39 to 45, the court itself` THEN `The court itself` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Orders 39 to 45, a Judge` THEN `A Judge` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Orders 39 to 45, a District Judge` THEN `A District Judge` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Orders 39 to 45, a Magistrate` THEN `A Magistrate` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Orders 39 to 45, the Registrar` THEN `The Registrar` -- input mapping

-- The choices for `o 39 r 2 kind of instrument`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Order 39, rule 2: kind of instrument` IS ONE OF
    `Under Order 39, rule 2(a): a Commitment`
    `Under Order 39, rule 2(b): a Direction`
    `Under Order 39, rule 2(c): a Decision`
    `Under Order 39, rule 2: not one of the three kinds`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Order 39, rule 2: kind of instrument`
GIVETH A `o 39 r 2 kind of instrument`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 39 r 2 kind of instrument` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Order 39, rule 2(a): a Commitment` THEN `o 39 r 2(a) a Commitment` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 39, rule 2(b): a Direction` THEN `o 39 r 2(b) a Direction` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 39, rule 2(c): a Decision` THEN `o 39 r 2(c) a Decision` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 39, rule 2: not one of the three kinds` THEN `o 39 r 2 not one of the three kinds` -- input mapping

-- The choices for `o 39 r 2 how the application is made`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Order 39, rule 2: how the application is made` IS ONE OF
    `Under Order 39, rule 2: by originating application without notice`
    `Under Order 39, rule 2: by originating application with notice`
    `Under Order 39, rule 2: by summons`
    `Under Order 39, rule 2: in some other way`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Order 39, rule 2: how the application is made`
GIVETH A `o 39 r 2 how the application is made`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 39 r 2 how the application is made` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Order 39, rule 2: by originating application without notice` THEN `o 39 r 2 by originating application without notice` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 39, rule 2: by originating application with notice` THEN `o 39 r 2 by originating application with notice` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 39, rule 2: by summons` THEN `o 39 r 2 by summons` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 39, rule 2: in some other way` THEN `o 39 r 2 in some other way` -- input mapping

-- The choices for `o 40 r 1(3) how the application is made`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Order 40, rule 1(3): how the application is made` IS ONE OF
    `Under Order 40, rule 1(3): by summons in the action`
    `Under Order 40, rule 1(3): by originating application`
    `Under Order 40, rule 1(3): in some other way`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Order 40, rule 1(3): how the application is made`
GIVETH A `o 40 r 1(3) how the application is made`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 1(3) how the application is made` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Order 40, rule 1(3): by summons in the action` THEN `o 40 r 1(3) by summons in the action` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 40, rule 1(3): by originating application` THEN `o 40 r 1(3) by originating application` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 40, rule 1(3): in some other way` THEN `o 40 r 1(3) in some other way` -- input mapping

-- The choices for `o 40 r 2(4) service on a person`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): service on a person` IS ONE OF
    `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): served`
    `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): not served`
    `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): there is no such person`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): service on a person`
GIVETH A `o 40 r 2(4) service on a person`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(4) service on a person` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): served` THEN `o 40 r 2(4) served` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): not served` THEN `o 40 r 2(4) not served` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): there is no such person` THEN `o 40 r 2(4) there is no such person` -- input mapping

-- The choices for `o 40 r 2(1) a statement may be required`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): a statement may be required` IS ONE OF
    `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): it is stated`
    `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): it is not stated`
    `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): it is not applicable on these facts`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): a statement may be required`
GIVETH A `o 40 r 2(1) a statement may be required`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(1) a statement may be required` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): it is stated` THEN `o 40 r 2(1) it is stated` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): it is not stated` THEN `o 40 r 2(1) it is not stated` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): it is not applicable on these facts` THEN `o 40 r 2(1) it is not applicable on these facts` -- input mapping

-- The choices for `o 40 r 19(4) whom the copy is served on`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Order 40, rule 19(4): whom the copy is served on` IS ONE OF
    `Under Order 40, rule 19(4): the authorised officer by whom the application for an order was made`
    `Under Order 40, rule 19(4): another authorised officer because that officer is not known or cannot be found`
    `Under Order 40, rule 19(4): someone else`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Order 40, rule 19(4): whom the copy is served on`
GIVETH A `o 40 r 19(4) whom the copy is served on`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 19(4) whom the copy is served on` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Order 40, rule 19(4): the authorised officer by whom the application for an order was made` THEN `o 40 r 19(4) the authorised officer by whom the application for an order was made` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 40, rule 19(4): another authorised officer because that officer is not known or cannot be found` THEN `o 40 r 19(4) another authorised officer because that officer is not known or cannot be found` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 40, rule 19(4): someone else` THEN `o 40 r 19(4) someone else` -- input mapping

-- The choices for `o 42 r 19 to whom the debtor pays`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Order 42, rule 19: to whom the debtor pays` IS ONE OF
    `Under Order 42, rule 19: the Sheriff`
    `Under Order 42, rule 19: the officer in charge of the prison`
    `Under Order 42, rule 19: someone else`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Order 42, rule 19: to whom the debtor pays`
GIVETH A `o 42 r 19 to whom the debtor pays`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 42 r 19 to whom the debtor pays` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Order 42, rule 19: the Sheriff` THEN `o 42 r 19 the Sheriff` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 42, rule 19: the officer in charge of the prison` THEN `o 42 r 19 the officer in charge of the prison` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 42, rule 19: someone else` THEN `o 42 r 19 someone else` -- input mapping

-- The choices for `o 43 r 3(4) a statement may be required`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Order 43, rule 3(4): a statement may be required` IS ONE OF
    `Under Order 43, rule 3(4): it is stated`
    `Under Order 43, rule 3(4): it is not stated`
    `Under Order 43, rule 3(4): it is not applicable on these facts`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Order 43, rule 3(4): a statement may be required`
GIVETH A `o 43 r 3(4) a statement may be required`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 43 r 3(4) a statement may be required` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Order 43, rule 3(4): it is stated` THEN `o 43 r 3(4) it is stated` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 43, rule 3(4): it is not stated` THEN `o 43 r 3(4) it is not stated` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 43, rule 3(4): it is not applicable on these facts` THEN `o 43 r 3(4) it is not applicable on these facts` -- input mapping

-- The choices for `o 44 r 2(2) a statement may be required`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Order 44, rule 2(2): a statement may be required` IS ONE OF
    `Under Order 44, rule 2(2): it is stated`
    `Under Order 44, rule 2(2): it is not stated`
    `Under Order 44, rule 2(2): it is not applicable on these facts`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Order 44, rule 2(2): a statement may be required`
GIVETH A `o 44 r 2(2) a statement may be required`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 44 r 2(2) a statement may be required` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 2(2): it is stated` THEN `o 44 r 2(2) it is stated` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 2(2): it is not stated` THEN `o 44 r 2(2) it is not stated` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 2(2): it is not applicable on these facts` THEN `o 44 r 2(2) it is not applicable on these facts` -- input mapping

-- The choices for `o 44 r 4(5) the step`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Order 44, rule 4(5): the step` IS ONE OF
    `Under Order 44, rule 4(5)(a): use the name of a person as litigation representative of the person under disability`
    `Under Order 44, rule 4(5)(b): file a notice of intention to contest or not contest for the person under disability`
    `Under Order 44, rule 4(5)(c): appear by the litigation representative on the hearing of a summons served on the person under disability`
    `Under Order 44, rule 4(5): some other step`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Order 44, rule 4(5): the step`
GIVETH A `o 44 r 4(5) the step`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 44 r 4(5) the step` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 4(5)(a): use the name of a person as litigation representative of the person under disability` THEN `o 44 r 4(5)(a) use the name of a person as litigation representative of the person under disability` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 4(5)(b): file a notice of intention to contest or not contest for the person under disability` THEN `o 44 r 4(5)(b) file a notice of intention to contest or not contest for the person under disability` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 4(5)(c): appear by the litigation representative on the hearing of a summons served on the person under disability` THEN `o 44 r 4(5)(c) appear by the litigation representative on the hearing of a summons served on the person under disability` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 4(5): some other step` THEN `o 44 r 4(5) some other step` -- input mapping

-- The choices for `o 44 r 4(6) a document is required`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): a document is required` IS ONE OF
    `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): it is filed`
    `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): it is not filed`
    `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): it is not required on these facts`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): a document is required`
GIVETH A `o 44 r 4(6) a document is required`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 44 r 4(6) a document is required` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): it is filed` THEN `o 44 r 4(6) it is filed` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): it is not filed` THEN `o 44 r 4(6) it is not filed` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): it is not required on these facts` THEN `o 44 r 4(6) it is not required on these facts` -- input mapping

-- The choices for `o 44 r 4(6) a statement may be required`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): a statement may be required` IS ONE OF
    `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): it is stated`
    `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): it is not stated`
    `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): it is not applicable on these facts`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): a statement may be required`
GIVETH A `o 44 r 4(6) a statement may be required`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 44 r 4(6) a statement may be required` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): it is stated` THEN `o 44 r 4(6) it is stated` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): it is not stated` THEN `o 44 r 4(6) it is not stated` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 4(6): it is not applicable on these facts` THEN `o 44 r 4(6) it is not applicable on these facts` -- input mapping

-- The choices for `o 44 r 13(2) whom the document is served on`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Order 44, rule 13(2): whom the document is served on` IS ONE OF
    `Under Order 44, rule 13(2): the father or guardian`
    `Under Order 44, rule 13(2): the person with whom the person under disability resides or in whose care the person is`
    `Under Order 44, rule 13(2): the person authorised under the Act`
    `Under Order 44, rule 13(2): someone else`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Order 44, rule 13(2): whom the document is served on`
GIVETH A `o 44 r 13(2) whom the document is served on`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 44 r 13(2) whom the document is served on` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 13(2): the father or guardian` THEN `o 44 r 13(2) the father or guardian` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 13(2): the person with whom the person under disability resides or in whose care the person is` THEN `o 44 r 13(2) the person with whom the person under disability resides or in whose care the person is` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 13(2): the person authorised under the Act` THEN `o 44 r 13(2) the person authorised under the Act` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 44, rule 13(2): someone else` THEN `o 44 r 13(2) someone else` -- input mapping

-- The choices for `o 45 r 7(2) an item`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Order 45, rule 7(2): an item` IS ONE OF
    `Under Order 45, rule 7(2): the rent in respect of which the writ was issued`
    `Under Order 45, rule 7(2): the expenses of the sale and of execution of the writ`
    `Under Order 45, rule 7(2): the Court fees`
    `Under Order 45, rule 7(2): all costs due to the landlord`
    `Under Order 45, rule 7(2): any other item`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Order 45, rule 7(2): an item`
GIVETH A `o 45 r 7(2) an item`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 45 r 7(2) an item` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Order 45, rule 7(2): the rent in respect of which the writ was issued` THEN `o 45 r 7(2) the rent in respect of which the writ was issued` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 45, rule 7(2): the expenses of the sale and of execution of the writ` THEN `o 45 r 7(2) the expenses of the sale and of execution of the writ` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 45, rule 7(2): the Court fees` THEN `o 45 r 7(2) the Court fees` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 45, rule 7(2): all costs due to the landlord` THEN `o 45 r 7(2) all costs due to the landlord` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 45, rule 7(2): any other item` THEN `o 45 r 7(2) any other item` -- input mapping

-- The choices for `o 45 r 11 service on a person`, as the person would pick them.
DECLARE `Under Order 45, rule 11: service on a person` IS ONE OF
    `Under Order 45, rule 11: served`
    `Under Order 45, rule 11: not served`
    `Under Order 45, rule 11: there is no such person`

GIVEN x IS A `Under Order 45, rule 11: service on a person`
GIVETH A `o 45 r 11 service on a person`
`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 45 r 11 service on a person` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `Under Order 45, rule 11: served` THEN `o 45 r 11 served` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 45, rule 11: not served` THEN `o 45 r 11 not served` -- input mapping
    WHEN `Under Order 45, rule 11: there is no such person` THEN `o 45 r 11 there is no such person` -- input mapping

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 39 -- Competition Act — Applications Under Section 85 of Competition Act`
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Order 39, rule 1 -- Powers under relevant Acts exercisable by Judge or Registrar`

-- o 39 r 1(1) the person may exercise the powers conferred on the District Court by section 85
@export Under Order 39, rule 1(1), is it so that the person may exercise the powers conferred on the District Court by section 85?
GIVEN `who would decide it` IS A `Under Orders 39 to 45, who would decide it` @desc Which of these applies: who would decide it?
      `the District Judge is sitting in chambers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the District Judge is sitting in chambers? (yes or no)
      `the power is the power conferred by section 85(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the power is the power conferred by section 85(3)? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 1(1), is it so that the person may exercise the powers conferred on the District Court by section 85` IS
    `o 39 r 1(1) the person may exercise the powers conferred on the District Court by section 85` (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for Decision maker` `who would decide it`) `the District Judge is sitting in chambers` `the power is the power conferred by section 85(3)`

-- o 39 r 1(2) the person may exercise the powers conferred on the District Court by section 85(3)
@export Under Order 39, rule 1(2), is it so that the person may exercise the powers conferred on the District Court by section 85(3)?
GIVEN `who would decide it` IS A `Under Orders 39 to 45, who would decide it` @desc Which of these applies: who would decide it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 1(2), is it so that the person may exercise the powers conferred on the District Court by section 85(3)` IS
    `o 39 r 1(2) the person may exercise the powers conferred on the District Court by section 85(3)` (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for Decision maker` `who would decide it`)

§§ `Order 39, rule 2 -- Application for registration`

-- o 39 r 2 the application for registration is made as the Rule requires
@export Under Order 39, rule 2, is it so that the application for registration is made as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `kind of instrument` IS A `Under Order 39, rule 2: kind of instrument` @desc Which of these applies: kind of instrument?
      `the application is for registration in the District Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application is for registration in the District Court? (yes or no)
      `how the application is made` IS A `Under Order 39, rule 2: how the application is made` @desc Which of these applies: how the application is made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 2, is it so that the application for registration is made as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 39 r 2 the application for registration is made as the Rule requires` (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 39 r 2 kind of instrument` `kind of instrument`) `the application is for registration in the District Court` (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 39 r 2 how the application is made` `how the application is made`)

§§ `Order 39, rule 3 -- Evidence in support of application for registration`

-- o 39 r 3(c)(iii) a statement of the unsatisfied financial penalty is required
@export Under Order 39, rule 3(c)(iii), is it so that a statement of the unsatisfied financial penalty is required?
GIVEN `a financial penalty was imposed under the instrument and part of it remains unsatisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a financial penalty was imposed under the instrument and part of it remains unsatisfied? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 3(c)(iii), is it so that a statement of the unsatisfied financial penalty is required` IS
    `o 39 r 3(c)(iii) a statement of the unsatisfied financial penalty is required` `a financial penalty was imposed under the instrument and part of it remains unsatisfied`

-- o 39 r 3 the application is supported by an affidavit as the Rule requires
@export Under Order 39, rule 3, is it so that the application is supported by an affidavit as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `an affidavit supports the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an affidavit supports the application? (yes or no)
      `a financial penalty was imposed under the instrument and part of it remains unsatisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a financial penalty was imposed under the instrument and part of it remains unsatisfied? (yes or no)
      `it exhibits the Commitment, Direction or Decision, or a verified or certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the affidavit does: is it true that it exhibits the Commitment, Direction or Decision, or a verified or certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy? (yes or no)
      `it states the name, trade or business and the usual or last known place of residence or business of the party seeking to register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the affidavit does: is it true that it states the name, trade or business and the usual or last known place of residence or business of the party seeking to register? (yes or no)
      `it states the same of the other party, so far as known to the deponent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the affidavit does: is it true that it states the same of the other party, so far as known to the deponent? (yes or no)
      `it states to the best of the information or belief of the deponent that the applying party is entitled to enforce the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the affidavit does: is it true that it states to the best of the information or belief of the deponent that the applying party is entitled to enforce the instrument? (yes or no)
      `it states to the best of the information or belief of the deponent that as at the date of the application the instrument has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the affidavit does: is it true that it states to the best of the information or belief of the deponent that as at the date of the application the instrument has not been complied with? (yes or no)
      `it states to the best of the information or belief of the deponent the amount of financial penalty which remains unsatisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the affidavit does: is it true that it states to the best of the information or belief of the deponent the amount of financial penalty which remains unsatisfied? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 3, is it so that the application is supported by an affidavit as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 39 r 3 the application is supported by an affidavit as the Rule requires` `an affidavit supports the application` `a financial penalty was imposed under the instrument and part of it remains unsatisfied` `what the affidavit does as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `what the affidavit does as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 39 r 3 what the affidavit does` WITH
            `o 39 r 3(a) it exhibits the Commitment, Direction or Decision, or a verified or certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy` IS `it exhibits the Commitment, Direction or Decision, or a verified or certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy`
            `o 39 r 3(b)(i) it states the name, trade or business and the usual or last known place of residence or business of the party seeking to register` IS `it states the name, trade or business and the usual or last known place of residence or business of the party seeking to register`
            `o 39 r 3(b)(ii) it states the same of the other party, so far as known to the deponent` IS `it states the same of the other party, so far as known to the deponent`
            `o 39 r 3(c)(i) it states to the best of the information or belief of the deponent that the applying party is entitled to enforce the instrument` IS `it states to the best of the information or belief of the deponent that the applying party is entitled to enforce the instrument`
            `o 39 r 3(c)(ii) it states to the best of the information or belief of the deponent that as at the date of the application the instrument has not been complied with` IS `it states to the best of the information or belief of the deponent that as at the date of the application the instrument has not been complied with`
            `o 39 r 3(c)(iii) it states to the best of the information or belief of the deponent the amount of financial penalty which remains unsatisfied` IS `it states to the best of the information or belief of the deponent the amount of financial penalty which remains unsatisfied`

§§ `Order 39, rule 4 -- Security for costs`

-- o 39 r 4 the Court may order the person to give security for costs
@export Under Order 39, rule 4, is it so that the Court may order the person to give security for costs?
GIVEN `the person is the party applying for the registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is the party applying for the registration? (yes or no)
      `the security is for the costs of the application or of proceedings which may be brought to set aside the registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the security is for the costs of the application or of proceedings which may be brought to set aside the registration? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 4, is it so that the Court may order the person to give security for costs` IS
    `o 39 r 4 the Court may order the person to give security for costs` `the person is the party applying for the registration` `the security is for the costs of the application or of proceedings which may be brought to set aside the registration`

§§ `Order 39, rule 5 -- Order for registration`

-- o 39 r 5(1) the order for registration is drawn up and served as the Rule requires
@export Under Order 39, rule 5(1), is it so that the order for registration is drawn up and served as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `kind of instrument` IS A `Under Order 39, rule 2: kind of instrument` @desc Which of these applies: kind of instrument?
      `the number of the form of the order` IS A STRING @desc What is the number of the form of the order?
      `the order is drawn up by or on behalf of the party applying to register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order is drawn up by or on behalf of the party applying to register? (yes or no)
      `the order is served on the party who provided the Commitment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order is served on the party who provided the Commitment? (yes or no)
      `the order is served on the party against whom the Direction or Decision has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order is served on the party against whom the Direction or Decision has been made? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 5(1), is it so that the order for registration is drawn up and served as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 39 r 5(1) the order for registration is drawn up and served as the Rule requires` (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 39 r 2 kind of instrument` `kind of instrument`) `the number of the form of the order` `the order is drawn up by or on behalf of the party applying to register` `the order is served on the party who provided the Commitment` `the order is served on the party against whom the Direction or Decision has been made`

-- o 39 r 5(2) the order must state the period and contain the notification
@export Under Order 39, rule 5(2), is it so that the order must state the period and contain the notification?
GIVEN `the Court has otherwise directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has otherwise directed? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 5(2), is it so that the order must state the period and contain the notification` IS
    `o 39 r 5(2) the order must state the period and contain the notification` `the Court has otherwise directed`

-- o 39 r 5(2) the order states the period and contains the notification
@export Under Order 39, rule 5(2), is it so that the order states the period and contains the notification?
GIVEN `the Court has otherwise directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has otherwise directed? (yes or no)
      `the order states the period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order states the period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration? (yes or no)
      `the order contains a notification that an enforcement order will not be issued until after the expiration of that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order contains a notification that an enforcement order will not be issued until after the expiration of that period? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 5(2), is it so that the order states the period and contains the notification` IS
    `o 39 r 5(2) the order states the period and contains the notification` `the Court has otherwise directed` `the order states the period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration` `the order contains a notification that an enforcement order will not be issued until after the expiration of that period`

-- o 39 r 5(3) the application to extend the period is made in time
@export Under Order 39, rule 5(3), is it so that the application to extend the period is made in time?
GIVEN `the date the application to extend is made` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the application to extend is made?
      `the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 5(3), is it so that the application to extend the period is made in time` IS
    `o 39 r 5(3) the application to extend the period is made in time` `the date the application to extend is made` `the last day for doing the act`

-- o 39 r 5(4) the Court may extend the period
@export Under Order 39, rule 5(4), is it so that the Court may extend the period?
GIVEN `the period is the period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the period is the period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 5(4), is it so that the Court may extend the period` IS
    `o 39 r 5(4) the Court may extend the period` `the period is the period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration`

§§ `Order 39, rule 6 -- Register of Commitments, Directions and Decisions`

-- o 39 r 6 the instrument is to be entered in the register kept in the Registry
@export Under Order 39, rule 6, is it so that the instrument is to be entered in the register kept in the Registry?
GIVEN `the instrument is registered under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the instrument is registered under this Order? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 6, is it so that the instrument is to be entered in the register kept in the Registry` IS
    `o 39 r 6 the instrument is to be entered in the register kept in the Registry` `the instrument is registered under this Order`

§§ `Order 39, rule 7 -- Notice of registration`

-- o 39 r 7(1) the requirement of personal service of the notice applies
@export Under Order 39, rule 7(1), is it so that the requirement of personal service of the notice applies?
GIVEN `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has otherwise ordered? (yes or no)
      `the notice is served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice is served out of Singapore? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 7(1), is it so that the requirement of personal service of the notice applies` IS
    `o 39 r 7(1) the requirement of personal service of the notice applies` `the Court has otherwise ordered` `the notice is served out of Singapore`

-- o 39 r 7(1) the notice of registration is served as the Rule requires
@export Under Order 39, rule 7(1), is it so that the notice of registration is served as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the notice is served on the party who provided the Commitment or against whom the Direction or Decision has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice is served on the party who provided the Commitment or against whom the Direction or Decision has been made? (yes or no)
      `the notice is served personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice is served personally? (yes or no)
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has otherwise ordered? (yes or no)
      `the notice is served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice is served out of Singapore? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 7(1), is it so that the notice of registration is served as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 39 r 7(1) the notice of registration is served as the Rule requires` `the notice is served on the party who provided the Commitment or against whom the Direction or Decision has been made` `the notice is served personally` `the Court has otherwise ordered` `the notice is served out of Singapore`

-- o 39 r 7(2) the notice may be served out of Singapore without permission
@export Under Order 39, rule 7(2), is it so that the notice may be served out of Singapore without permission?
GIVEN `the notice is served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice is served out of Singapore? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 7(2), is it so that the notice may be served out of Singapore without permission` IS
    `o 39 r 7(2) the notice may be served out of Singapore without permission` `the notice is served out of Singapore`

-- o 39 r 7(2) Order 8, Rules 2, 3, 7 and 8 apply to the notice
@export Under Order 39, rule 7(2), is it so that Order 8, Rules 2, 3, 7 and 8 apply to the notice?
GIVEN `the notice is served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the notice is served out of Singapore? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 7(2), is it so that Order 8, Rules 2, 3, 7 and 8 apply to the notice` IS
    `o 39 r 7(2) Order 8, Rules 2, 3, 7 and 8 apply to the notice` `the notice is served out of Singapore`

-- o 39 r 7(3) the notice of registration states what the Rule requires
@export Under Order 39, rule 7(3), is it so that the notice of registration states what the Rule requires?
GIVEN `full particulars of the instrument registered and the order for registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the notice states: is it true that full particulars of the instrument registered and the order for registration? (yes or no)
      `the name and address of the party seeking to enforce or of the party's solicitor on whom any summons may be served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the notice states: is it true that the name and address of the party seeking to enforce or of the party's solicitor on whom any summons may be served? (yes or no)
      `that the other party has a right to apply to have the registration set aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the notice states: is it true that that the other party has a right to apply to have the registration set aside? (yes or no)
      `the period within which an application to set aside the registration may be made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the notice states: is it true that the period within which an application to set aside the registration may be made? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 7(3), is it so that the notice of registration states what the Rule requires` IS
    `o 39 r 7(3) the notice of registration states what the Rule requires` `what the notice states as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `what the notice states as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 39 r 7(3) what the notice states` WITH
            `o 39 r 7(3)(a) full particulars of the instrument registered and the order for registration` IS `full particulars of the instrument registered and the order for registration`
            `o 39 r 7(3)(b) the name and address of the party seeking to enforce or of the party's solicitor on whom any summons may be served` IS `the name and address of the party seeking to enforce or of the party's solicitor on whom any summons may be served`
            `o 39 r 7(3)(c) that the other party has a right to apply to have the registration set aside` IS `that the other party has a right to apply to have the registration set aside`
            `o 39 r 7(3)(d) the period within which an application to set aside the registration may be made` IS `the period within which an application to set aside the registration may be made`

§§ `Order 39, rule 8 -- Endorsement of service`

-- o 39 r 8(1) the notice is endorsed in time
@export Under Order 39, rule 8(1), is it so that the notice is endorsed in time?
GIVEN `the date the notice was endorsed` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the notice was endorsed?
      `the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 requires?
      `I can say the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you state this? the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances (yes or no)
      `the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 8(1), is it so that the notice is endorsed in time` IS
    `o 39 r 8(1) the notice is endorsed in time` `the date the notice was endorsed` `the last day for doing the act` (IF `I can say the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances` THEN JUST `the last day of the longer period the Court has allowed in special circumstances` ELSE NOTHING)

-- o 39 r 8(1) the endorsement is as the Rule requires
@export Under Order 39, rule 8(1), is it so that the endorsement is as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the endorsement gives the day of the week and the date on which the notice was served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the endorsement gives the day of the week and the date on which the notice was served? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 8(1), is it so that the endorsement is as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 39 r 8(1) the endorsement is as the Rule requires` `the endorsement gives the day of the week and the date on which the notice was served`

-- o 39 r 8(2) the person seeking to enforce may apply for an enforcement order
@export Under Order 39, rule 8(2), is it so that the person seeking to enforce may apply for an enforcement order?
