§§ `Order 39, rule 10 -- Issue of enforcement order`

-- o 39 r 10(1) the bar on issuing an enforcement order until the specified period expires applies
@export Under Order 39, rule 10(1), is it so that the bar on issuing an enforcement order until the specified period expires applies?
GIVEN `the Court has specified a period under Rule 5(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has specified a period under Rule 5(2)? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 10(1), is it so that the bar on issuing an enforcement order until the specified period expires applies` IS
    `o 39 r 10(1) the bar on issuing an enforcement order until the specified period expires applies` `the Court has specified a period under Rule 5(2)`

-- o 39 r 10(1) the enforcement order cannot yet be issued
@export Under Order 39, rule 10(1), is it so that the enforcement order cannot yet be issued?
GIVEN `the Court has specified a period under Rule 5(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has specified a period under Rule 5(2)? (yes or no)
      `the date on which the enforcement order is proposed to be issued` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the enforcement order is proposed to be issued?
      `the last day of the specified period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the specified period?
      `I can say the last day of the period as extended by the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you state this? the last day of the period as extended by the Court (yes or no)
      `the last day of the period as extended by the Court` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day of the period as extended by the Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 10(1), is it so that the enforcement order cannot yet be issued` IS
    `o 39 r 10(1) the enforcement order cannot yet be issued` `the Court has specified a period under Rule 5(2)` `the date on which the enforcement order is proposed to be issued` `the last day of the specified period` (IF `I can say the last day of the period as extended by the Court` THEN JUST `the last day of the period as extended by the Court` ELSE NOTHING)

-- o 39 r 10(2) the bar on issuing an enforcement order until the application is disposed of applies
@export Under Order 39, rule 10(2), is it so that the bar on issuing an enforcement order until the application is disposed of applies?
GIVEN `an application is made to set aside the registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an application is made to set aside the registration? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 10(2), is it so that the bar on issuing an enforcement order until the application is disposed of applies` IS
    `o 39 r 10(2) the bar on issuing an enforcement order until the application is disposed of applies` `an application is made to set aside the registration`

-- o 39 r 10(2) the enforcement order cannot yet be issued
@export Under Order 39, rule 10(2), is it so that the enforcement order cannot yet be issued?
GIVEN `an application is made to set aside the registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an application is made to set aside the registration? (yes or no)
      `the application has been disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application has been disposed of? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 10(2), is it so that the enforcement order cannot yet be issued` IS
    `o 39 r 10(2) the enforcement order cannot yet be issued` `an application is made to set aside the registration` `the application has been disposed of`

-- o 39 r 10(3) the party wishing to apply has produced what the Rule requires
@export Under Order 39, rule 10(3), is it so that the party wishing to apply has produced what the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the party wishes to apply for an enforcement order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the party wishes to apply for an enforcement order? (yes or no)
      `an affidavit of service of the notice of registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the party produces: is it true that an affidavit of service of the notice of registration? (yes or no)
      `every order made by the Court in relation to the instrument, if there is one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the party produces: is it true that every order made by the Court in relation to the instrument, if there is one? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 39, rule 10(3), is it so that the party wishing to apply has produced what the Rule requires` IS
    `o 39 r 10(3) the party wishing to apply has produced what the Rule requires` `the party wishes to apply for an enforcement order` `what the party produces as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `what the party produces as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 39 r 10(3) what the party produces` WITH
            `o 39 r 10(3) an affidavit of service of the notice of registration` IS `an affidavit of service of the notice of registration`
            `o 39 r 10(3) every order made by the Court in relation to the instrument, if there is one` IS `every order made by the Court in relation to the instrument, if there is one`

