GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 3(2), is it so that the application by the defendant and its supporting affidavit are filed and served as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 40 r 3(2) the application by the defendant and its supporting affidavit are filed and served as the Rule requires` `the application by the defendant and its supporting affidavit are filed` (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my moment from a day and a time` `the moment the document is deemed filed (the day)` `the moment the document is deemed filed (the hour, 0 to 23)` `the moment the document is deemed filed (the minute, 0 to 59)`) `the day service is deemed effected` `the last day for doing the act` `the persons to be served as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `the persons to be served as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 40 r 3(2) the persons to be served` WITH
            `o 40 r 3(2)(a) service on the Public Prosecutor` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(4) service on a person` `service on the Public Prosecutor`)
            `o 40 r 3(2)(b) service on the receiver, where one has been appointed in the matter` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(4) service on a person` `service on the receiver, where one has been appointed in the matter`)

§§ `Order 40, rule 4 -- Protection of rights of third party where confiscation order is about to be made`

-- o 40 r 4 the application and its supporting affidavit are filed and served as the Rule requires
@export Under Order 40, rule 4, is it so that the application and its supporting affidavit are filed and served as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the application and its supporting affidavit are filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application and its supporting affidavit are filed? (yes or no)
      `the moment the document is deemed filed (the day)` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the document deemed filed, under Order 28, Rule 10?
      `the moment the document is deemed filed (the hour, 0 to 23)` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day (0 to 23) is the document deemed filed?
      `the moment the document is deemed filed (the minute, 0 to 59)` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute past that hour (0 to 59) is the document deemed filed?
      `the day service is deemed effected` IS A DATE @desc On what day is service deemed effected, under Order 7, Rule 8?
      `the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 requires?
      `service on the Public Prosecutor` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): service on a person` @desc the persons to be served: which of these applies to service on the Public Prosecutor?
      `service on the defendant` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): service on a person` @desc the persons to be served: which of these applies to service on the defendant?
      `service on any other person having any interest in the property to which the application relates` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): service on a person` @desc the persons to be served: which of these applies to service on any other person having any interest in the property to which the application relates?
      `service on the receiver, where one has been appointed in the matter` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): service on a person` @desc the persons to be served: which of these applies to service on the receiver, where one has been appointed in the matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 4, is it so that the application and its supporting affidavit are filed and served as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 40 r 4 the application and its supporting affidavit are filed and served as the Rule requires` `the application and its supporting affidavit are filed` (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my moment from a day and a time` `the moment the document is deemed filed (the day)` `the moment the document is deemed filed (the hour, 0 to 23)` `the moment the document is deemed filed (the minute, 0 to 59)`) `the day service is deemed effected` `the last day for doing the act` `the persons to be served as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `the persons to be served as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 40 r 4 the persons to be served` WITH
            `o 40 r 4(a) service on the Public Prosecutor` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(4) service on a person` `service on the Public Prosecutor`)
            `o 40 r 4(b) service on the defendant` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(4) service on a person` `service on the defendant`)
            `o 40 r 4(c) service on any other person having any interest in the property to which the application relates` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(4) service on a person` `service on any other person having any interest in the property to which the application relates`)
            `o 40 r 4(d) service on the receiver, where one has been appointed in the matter` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(4) service on a person` `service on the receiver, where one has been appointed in the matter`)

§§ `Order 40, rule 5 -- Application for restraint order or charging order`

-- o 40 r 5(1) the supporting affidavit states what the Rule requires
@export Under Order 40, rule 5(1), is it so that the supporting affidavit states what the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the application is filed and served with a supporting affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application is filed and served with a supporting affidavit? (yes or no)
      `proceedings have been instituted against the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that proceedings have been instituted against the defendant? (yes or no)
      `the grounds for believing that the defendant has derived benefits from drug dealing or criminal conduct, as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the supporting affidavit states: is it true that the grounds for believing that the defendant has derived benefits from drug dealing or criminal conduct, as the case may be? (yes or no)
      `that proceedings have been instituted against the defendant for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars) and that they have not been concluded` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): a statement may be required` @desc what the supporting affidavit states: which of these applies to that proceedings have been instituted against the defendant for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars) and that they have not been concluded?
      `that the defendant has been officially informed under section 23(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code that the defendant may be prosecuted for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): a statement may be required` @desc what the supporting affidavit states: which of these applies to that the defendant has been officially informed under section 23(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code that the defendant may be prosecuted for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence?
      `that after investigations for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence have been commenced against the defendant, the defendant has died or cannot be found or is outside the jurisdiction` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): a statement may be required` @desc what the supporting affidavit states: which of these applies to that after investigations for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence have been commenced against the defendant, the defendant has died or cannot be found or is outside the jurisdiction?
      `full particulars of the realisable property in respect of which the order is sought, specifying the person or persons holding such property, as far as the deponent is able to provide` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the supporting affidavit states: is it true that full particulars of the realisable property in respect of which the order is sought, specifying the person or persons holding such property, as far as the deponent is able to provide? (yes or no)
      `an indication of when it is intended that they should be instituted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the supporting affidavit states: is it true that an indication of when it is intended that they should be instituted? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 5(1), is it so that the supporting affidavit states what the Rule requires` IS
    `o 40 r 5(1) the supporting affidavit states what the Rule requires` `the application is filed and served with a supporting affidavit` `proceedings have been instituted against the defendant` `what the supporting affidavit states as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `what the supporting affidavit states as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 40 r 5(1) what the supporting affidavit states` WITH
            `o 40 r 5(1)(a) the grounds for believing that the defendant has derived benefits from drug dealing or criminal conduct, as the case may be` IS `the grounds for believing that the defendant has derived benefits from drug dealing or criminal conduct, as the case may be`
            `o 40 r 5(1)(b)(i) that proceedings have been instituted against the defendant for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars) and that they have not been concluded` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(1) a statement may be required` `that proceedings have been instituted against the defendant for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars) and that they have not been concluded`)
            `o 40 r 5(1)(b)(ii) that the defendant has been officially informed under section 23(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code that the defendant may be prosecuted for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(1) a statement may be required` `that the defendant has been officially informed under section 23(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code that the defendant may be prosecuted for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence`)
            `o 40 r 5(1)(b)(iii) that after investigations for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence have been commenced against the defendant, the defendant has died or cannot be found or is outside the jurisdiction` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(1) a statement may be required` `that after investigations for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence have been commenced against the defendant, the defendant has died or cannot be found or is outside the jurisdiction`)
            `o 40 r 5(1)(c) full particulars of the realisable property in respect of which the order is sought, specifying the person or persons holding such property, as far as the deponent is able to provide` IS `full particulars of the realisable property in respect of which the order is sought, specifying the person or persons holding such property, as far as the deponent is able to provide`
            `o 40 r 5(1)(d) an indication of when it is intended that they should be instituted` IS `an indication of when it is intended that they should be instituted`

-- o 40 r 5(1) an application for the appointment of a receiver may be joined
@export Under Order 40, rule 5(1), is it so that an application for the appointment of a receiver may be joined?
GIVEN `the application is for a restraint order under section 16 or a charging order under section 17` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application is for a restraint order under section 16 or a charging order under section 17? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 5(1), is it so that an application for the appointment of a receiver may be joined` IS
    `o 40 r 5(1) an application for the appointment of a receiver may be joined` `the application is for a restraint order under section 16 or a charging order under section 17`

-- o 40 r 5(2) the application is entitled as the Rule requires
@export Under Order 40, rule 5(2), is it so that the application is entitled as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the application is entitled in the matter of the defendant, naming the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc how the application is entitled: is it true that the application is entitled in the matter of the defendant, naming the defendant? (yes or no)
      `the application is entitled in the matter of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc how the application is entitled: is it true that the application is entitled in the matter of the Act? (yes or no)
      `all subsequent documents in the matter are so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc how the application is entitled: is it true that all subsequent documents in the matter are so entitled? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 5(2), is it so that the application is entitled as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 40 r 5(2) the application is entitled as the Rule requires` `how the application is entitled as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `how the application is entitled as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 40 r 5(2) how the application is entitled` WITH
            `o 40 r 5(2)(1) the application is entitled in the matter of the defendant, naming the defendant` IS `the application is entitled in the matter of the defendant, naming the defendant`
            `o 40 r 5(2)(2) the application is entitled in the matter of the Act` IS `the application is entitled in the matter of the Act`
            `o 40 r 5(2)(3) all subsequent documents in the matter are so entitled` IS `all subsequent documents in the matter are so entitled`

-- o 40 r 5(3) the supporting affidavit may contain statements of information or belief
@export Under Order 40, rule 5(3), is it so that the supporting affidavit may contain statements of information or belief?
GIVEN `the Court has otherwise directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has otherwise directed? (yes or no)
      `the statements give their sources and grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statements give their sources and grounds? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 5(3), is it so that the supporting affidavit may contain statements of information or belief` IS
    `o 40 r 5(3) the supporting affidavit may contain statements of information or belief` `the Court has otherwise directed` `the statements give their sources and grounds`

