            `o 40 r 12(4)(a) service on the Public Prosecutor` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(4) service on a person` `service on the Public Prosecutor`)
            `o 40 r 12(4)(b) service on the receiver, where one has been appointed in the matter` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(4) service on a person` `service on the receiver, where one has been appointed in the matter`)

§§ `Order 40, rule 13 -- Application for restraint order or charging order for enabling satisfaction of s`

-- o 40 r 13(1) the application for a restraint order or a charging order is filed with a supporting affidavit as the Rule requires
@export Under Order 40, rule 13(1), is it so that the application for a restraint order or a charging order is filed with a supporting affidavit as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the application for a restraint order or a charging order is filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application for a restraint order or a charging order is filed? (yes or no)
      `the application for a restraint order or a charging order is supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application for a restraint order or a charging order is supported by an affidavit? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 13(1), is it so that the application for a restraint order or a charging order is filed with a supporting affidavit as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 40 r 13(1) the application for a restraint order or a charging order is filed with a supporting affidavit as the Rule requires` `the application for a restraint order or a charging order is filed` `the application for a restraint order or a charging order is supported by an affidavit`

-- o 40 r 13(1) an application for the appointment of a receiver may be joined
@export Under Order 40, rule 13(1), is it so that an application for the appointment of a receiver may be joined?
GIVEN `the application is for a restraint order under section 16 read with section 29C(1), or a charging order under section 17 read with section 29C(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application is for a restraint order under section 16 read with section 29C(1), or a charging order under section 17 read with section 29C(1)? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 13(1), is it so that an application for the appointment of a receiver may be joined` IS
    `o 40 r 13(1) an application for the appointment of a receiver may be joined` `the application is for a restraint order under section 16 read with section 29C(1), or a charging order under section 17 read with section 29C(1)`

-- o 40 r 13(2) the application is entitled as the Rule requires
@export Under Order 40, rule 13(2), is it so that the application is entitled as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the application is entitled in the matter of the defendant, naming the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc how the application is entitled: is it true that the application is entitled in the matter of the defendant, naming the defendant? (yes or no)
      `the application is entitled in the matter of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc how the application is entitled: is it true that the application is entitled in the matter of the Act? (yes or no)
      `all subsequent documents in the matter are so entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc how the application is entitled: is it true that all subsequent documents in the matter are so entitled? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 13(2), is it so that the application is entitled as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 40 r 13(2) the application is entitled as the Rule requires` `how the application is entitled as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `how the application is entitled as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 40 r 13(2) how the application is entitled` WITH
            `o 40 r 13(2)(1) the application is entitled in the matter of the defendant, naming the defendant` IS `the application is entitled in the matter of the defendant, naming the defendant`
            `o 40 r 13(2)(2) the application is entitled in the matter of the Act` IS `the application is entitled in the matter of the Act`
            `o 40 r 13(2)(3) all subsequent documents in the matter are so entitled` IS `all subsequent documents in the matter are so entitled`

-- o 40 r 13(3) the supporting affidavit states what the Rule requires
@export Under Order 40, rule 13(3), is it so that the supporting affidavit states what the Rule requires?
GIVEN `proceedings have been instituted against the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that proceedings have been instituted against the defendant? (yes or no)
      `that proceedings have been instituted against the defendant for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars of the offence), and that those proceedings have not been concluded` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): a statement may be required` @desc what the supporting affidavit states: which of these applies to that proceedings have been instituted against the defendant for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars of the offence), and that those proceedings have not been concluded?
      `that the defendant has been officially informed under section 23(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code that the defendant may be prosecuted for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars of the offence)` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): a statement may be required` @desc what the supporting affidavit states: which of these applies to that the defendant has been officially informed under section 23(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code that the defendant may be prosecuted for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars of the offence)?
      `that after investigations for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars of the offence) have been commenced against the defendant, the defendant has died or cannot be found or is outside the jurisdiction` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): a statement may be required` @desc what the supporting affidavit states: which of these applies to that after investigations for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars of the offence) have been commenced against the defendant, the defendant has died or cannot be found or is outside the jurisdiction?
      `that the defendant had used or intended to use an instrumentality (giving particulars of the instrumentality) for the commission of the offence mentioned in sub-paragraph (a)(i), (ii) or (iii), as the case may be` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the supporting affidavit states: is it true that that the defendant had used or intended to use an instrumentality (giving particulars of the instrumentality) for the commission of the offence mentioned in sub-paragraph (a)(i), (ii) or (iii), as the case may be? (yes or no)
      `that the instrumentality is not available for forfeiture` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the supporting affidavit states: is it true that that the instrumentality is not available for forfeiture? (yes or no)
      `the reason mentioned in section 29B(2)(a), (b) or (c) that the instrumentality is not available for forfeiture (giving particulars of that reason)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the supporting affidavit states: is it true that the reason mentioned in section 29B(2)(a), (b) or (c) that the instrumentality is not available for forfeiture (giving particulars of that reason)? (yes or no)
      `the value of the instrumentality at the time the offence was committed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the supporting affidavit states: is it true that the value of the instrumentality at the time the offence was committed? (yes or no)
      `full particulars of the realisable property in respect of which the order is sought, and the person or persons who (to the best of the deponent's knowledge) hold the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the supporting affidavit states: is it true that full particulars of the realisable property in respect of which the order is sought, and the person or persons who (to the best of the deponent's knowledge) hold the property? (yes or no)
      `an indication of when it is intended that they should be instituted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the supporting affidavit states: is it true that an indication of when it is intended that they should be instituted? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 13(3), is it so that the supporting affidavit states what the Rule requires` IS
    `o 40 r 13(3) the supporting affidavit states what the Rule requires` `proceedings have been instituted against the defendant` `what the supporting affidavit states as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `what the supporting affidavit states as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 40 r 13(3) what the supporting affidavit states` WITH
            `o 40 r 13(3)(a)(i) that proceedings have been instituted against the defendant for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars of the offence), and that those proceedings have not been concluded` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(1) a statement may be required` `that proceedings have been instituted against the defendant for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars of the offence), and that those proceedings have not been concluded`)
            `o 40 r 13(3)(a)(ii) that the defendant has been officially informed under section 23(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code that the defendant may be prosecuted for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars of the offence)` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(1) a statement may be required` `that the defendant has been officially informed under section 23(1) of the Criminal Procedure Code that the defendant may be prosecuted for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars of the offence)`)
            `o 40 r 13(3)(a)(iii) that after investigations for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars of the offence) have been commenced against the defendant, the defendant has died or cannot be found or is outside the jurisdiction` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(1) a statement may be required` `that after investigations for a drug dealing offence or a serious offence (giving particulars of the offence) have been commenced against the defendant, the defendant has died or cannot be found or is outside the jurisdiction`)
            `o 40 r 13(3)(b)(i) that the defendant had used or intended to use an instrumentality (giving particulars of the instrumentality) for the commission of the offence mentioned in sub-paragraph (a)(i), (ii) or (iii), as the case may be` IS `that the defendant had used or intended to use an instrumentality (giving particulars of the instrumentality) for the commission of the offence mentioned in sub-paragraph (a)(i), (ii) or (iii), as the case may be`
            `o 40 r 13(3)(b)(ii) that the instrumentality is not available for forfeiture` IS `that the instrumentality is not available for forfeiture`
            `o 40 r 13(3)(b)(iii) the reason mentioned in section 29B(2)(a), (b) or (c) that the instrumentality is not available for forfeiture (giving particulars of that reason)` IS `the reason mentioned in section 29B(2)(a), (b) or (c) that the instrumentality is not available for forfeiture (giving particulars of that reason)`
            `o 40 r 13(3)(b)(iv) the value of the instrumentality at the time the offence was committed` IS `the value of the instrumentality at the time the offence was committed`
            `o 40 r 13(3)(c) full particulars of the realisable property in respect of which the order is sought, and the person or persons who (to the best of the deponent's knowledge) hold the property` IS `full particulars of the realisable property in respect of which the order is sought, and the person or persons who (to the best of the deponent's knowledge) hold the property`
            `o 40 r 13(3)(d) an indication of when it is intended that they should be instituted` IS `an indication of when it is intended that they should be instituted`

-- o 40 r 13(4) the supporting affidavit may contain statements of information or belief
@export Under Order 40, rule 13(4), is it so that the supporting affidavit may contain statements of information or belief?
GIVEN `the Court has otherwise directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has otherwise directed? (yes or no)
      `the statements give the sources of information and grounds of belief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the statements give the sources of information and grounds of belief? (yes or no)
