-- o 40 r 15(2) the supporting affidavit contains what the Rule requires
@export Under Order 40, rule 15(2), is it so that the supporting affidavit contains what the Rule requires?
GIVEN `full particulars of the realisable property to which the application relates, and the person or persons who (to the best of the deponent's knowledge) hold the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the supporting affidavit contains: is it true that full particulars of the realisable property to which the application relates, and the person or persons who (to the best of the deponent's knowledge) hold the property? (yes or no)
      `a copy of the substitute property confiscation order is exhibited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the supporting affidavit contains: is it true that a copy of the substitute property confiscation order is exhibited? (yes or no)
      `a copy of any certificate issued by the Court under section 10(2) read with section 29C(1) is exhibited` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): a statement may be required` @desc what the supporting affidavit contains: which of these applies to a copy of any certificate issued by the Court under section 10(2) read with section 29C(1) is exhibited?
      `a copy of any charging order made in the matter is exhibited` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): a statement may be required` @desc what the supporting affidavit contains: which of these applies to a copy of any charging order made in the matter is exhibited?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 15(2), is it so that the supporting affidavit contains what the Rule requires` IS
    `o 40 r 15(2) the supporting affidavit contains what the Rule requires` `what the supporting affidavit contains as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `what the supporting affidavit contains as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 40 r 15(2) what the supporting affidavit contains` WITH
            `o 40 r 15(2)(a) full particulars of the realisable property to which the application relates, and the person or persons who (to the best of the deponent's knowledge) hold the property` IS `full particulars of the realisable property to which the application relates, and the person or persons who (to the best of the deponent's knowledge) hold the property`
            `o 40 r 15(2)(b)(i) a copy of the substitute property confiscation order is exhibited` IS `a copy of the substitute property confiscation order is exhibited`
            `o 40 r 15(2)(b)(ii) a copy of any certificate issued by the Court under section 10(2) read with section 29C(1) is exhibited` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(1) a statement may be required` `a copy of any certificate issued by the Court under section 10(2) read with section 29C(1) is exhibited`)
            `o 40 r 15(2)(b)(iii) a copy of any charging order made in the matter is exhibited` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(1) a statement may be required` `a copy of any charging order made in the matter is exhibited`)

-- o 40 r 15(3) the application and the supporting affidavit are served as the Rule requires
@export Under Order 40, rule 15(3), is it so that the application and the supporting affidavit are served as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the day service is deemed effected` IS A DATE @desc On what day is service deemed effected, under Order 7, Rule 8?
      `the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 requires?
      `service on the defendant` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): service on a person` @desc the persons to be served: which of these applies to service on the defendant?
      `service on any person who has an interest in the realisable property to which the application relates` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): service on a person` @desc the persons to be served: which of these applies to service on any person who has an interest in the realisable property to which the application relates?
      `service on the receiver, where one has been appointed in the matter` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): service on a person` @desc the persons to be served: which of these applies to service on the receiver, where one has been appointed in the matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 15(3), is it so that the application and the supporting affidavit are served as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 40 r 15(3) the application and the supporting affidavit are served as the Rule requires` `the day service is deemed effected` `the last day for doing the act` `the persons to be served as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `the persons to be served as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 40 r 15(3) the persons to be served` WITH
            `o 40 r 15(3)(a) service on the defendant` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(4) service on a person` `service on the defendant`)
            `o 40 r 15(3)(b) service on any person who has an interest in the realisable property to which the application relates` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(4) service on a person` `service on any person who has an interest in the realisable property to which the application relates`)
            `o 40 r 15(3)(c) service on the receiver, where one has been appointed in the matter` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(4) service on a person` `service on the receiver, where one has been appointed in the matter`)

-- o 40 r 15(4) the Court may exercise the power conferred by section 20(1) read with section 29C(1) to direct payments by the receiver
@export Under Order 40, rule 15(4), is it so that the Court may exercise the power conferred by section 20(1) read with section 29C(1) to direct payments by the receiver?
