            `o 40 r 18(1)(1) the nature of the order sought` IS `the nature of the order sought`
            `o 40 r 18(1)(2) the grounds of the application` IS `the grounds of the application`
            `o 40 r 18(1)(3) whether material sought to be disclosed is to be disclosed to a receiver appointed under section 16 or 19, or under section 16 or 19 read with section 29C(1), or pursuant to a charging order or to an authorised officer` IS `whether material sought to be disclosed is to be disclosed to a receiver appointed under section 16 or 19, or under section 16 or 19 read with section 29C(1), or pursuant to a charging order or to an authorised officer`

-- o 40 r 18(2)(a) the application and the supporting affidavit are filed and served as the Rule requires
@export Under Order 40, rule 18(2)(a), is it so that the application and the supporting affidavit are filed and served as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the application and the supporting affidavit are filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application and the supporting affidavit are filed? (yes or no)
      `the moment the document is deemed filed (the day)` IS A DATE @desc On what day is the document deemed filed, under Order 28, Rule 10?
      `the moment the document is deemed filed (the hour, 0 to 23)` IS A NUMBER @desc At what hour of that day (0 to 23) is the document deemed filed?
      `the moment the document is deemed filed (the minute, 0 to 59)` IS A NUMBER @desc At what minute past that hour (0 to 59) is the document deemed filed?
      `the day service is deemed effected` IS A DATE @desc On what day is service deemed effected, under Order 7, Rule 8?
      `the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this act, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 requires?
      `service on the public body` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(4): service on a person` @desc the persons to be served: which of these applies to service on the public body?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 18(2)(a), is it so that the application and the supporting affidavit are filed and served as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 40 r 18(2)(a) the application and the supporting affidavit are filed and served as the Rule requires` `the application and the supporting affidavit are filed` (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my moment from a day and a time` `the moment the document is deemed filed (the day)` `the moment the document is deemed filed (the hour, 0 to 23)` `the moment the document is deemed filed (the minute, 0 to 59)`) `the day service is deemed effected` `the last day for doing the act` `the persons to be served as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `the persons to be served as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 40 r 18(2)(a) the persons to be served` WITH
            `o 40 r 18(2)(a)(a) service on the public body` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(4) service on a person` `service on the public body`)

-- o 40 r 18(2)(b) the duty to serve in accordance with Order 59, Rule 3 arises
@export Under Order 40, rule 18(2)(b), is it so that the duty to serve in accordance with Order 59, Rule 3 arises?
GIVEN `the public body is a Government department` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the public body is a Government department? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 18(2)(b), is it so that the duty to serve in accordance with Order 59, Rule 3 arises` IS
    `o 40 r 18(2)(b) the duty to serve in accordance with Order 59, Rule 3 arises` `the public body is a Government department`

-- o 40 r 18(2)(b) the application and supporting affidavit are served on the Government department in accordance with Order 59, Rule 3
@export Under Order 40, rule 18(2)(b), is it so that the application and supporting affidavit are served on the Government department in accordance with Order 59, Rule 3?
GIVEN `the public body is a Government department` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the public body is a Government department? (yes or no)
      `the application and supporting affidavit are served in the way Order 59, Rule 3 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application and supporting affidavit are served in the way Order 59, Rule 3 requires? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 18(2)(b), is it so that the application and supporting affidavit are served on the Government department in accordance with Order 59, Rule 3` IS
    `o 40 r 18(2)(b) the application and supporting affidavit are served on the Government department in accordance with Order 59, Rule 3` `the public body is a Government department` `the application and supporting affidavit are served in the way Order 59, Rule 3 requires`

-- o 40 r 18(3) the supporting affidavit states what the Rule requires
@export Under Order 40, rule 18(3), is it so that the supporting affidavit states what the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the grounds for believing that the conditions in section 42(4) are fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the supporting affidavit states: is it true that the grounds for believing that the conditions in section 42(4) are fulfilled? (yes or no)
      `the grounds for believing that the conditions in section 42(7A) are fulfilled` IS A `Under Order 40, rule 2(1): a statement may be required` @desc what the supporting affidavit states: which of these applies to the grounds for believing that the conditions in section 42(7A) are fulfilled?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 40, rule 18(3), is it so that the supporting affidavit states what the Rule requires` IS
    `o 40 r 18(3) the supporting affidavit states what the Rule requires` `what the supporting affidavit states as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `what the supporting affidavit states as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 40 r 18(3) what the supporting affidavit states` WITH
            `o 40 r 18(3)(1) the grounds for believing that the conditions in section 42(4) are fulfilled` IS `the grounds for believing that the conditions in section 42(4) are fulfilled`
            `o 40 r 18(3)(2) the grounds for believing that the conditions in section 42(7A) are fulfilled` IS (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 40 r 2(1) a statement may be required` `the grounds for believing that the conditions in section 42(7A) are fulfilled`)

