-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 41 -- Debenture Holders’ Action: Receiver’s Register`
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Order 41, rule 1 -- Receiver’s register`

-- o 41 r 1 the duty to keep a receiver's register arises
@export Under Order 41, rule 1, is it so that the duty to keep a receiver's register arises?
GIVEN `the receiver was appointed by the Court in an action to enforce registered debentures or registered debenture stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the receiver was appointed by the Court in an action to enforce registered debentures or registered debenture stock? (yes or no)
      `the Court has directed the receiver to keep a register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has directed the receiver to keep a register? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 1, is it so that the duty to keep a receiver's register arises` IS
    `o 41 r 1 the duty to keep a receiver's register arises` `the receiver was appointed by the Court in an action to enforce registered debentures or registered debenture stock` `the Court has directed the receiver to keep a register`

-- o 41 r 1 a register is the receiver's register
@export Under Order 41, rule 1, is it so that a register is the receiver's register?
GIVEN `it is a register of transfers of, and other transmissions of title to, such debentures or stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a register of transfers of, and other transmissions of title to, such debentures or stock? (yes or no)
      `it is kept by a receiver as Rule 1 requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is kept by a receiver as Rule 1 requires? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 1, is it so that a register is the receiver's register` IS
    `o 41 r 1 a register is the receiver's register` `it is a register of transfers of, and other transmissions of title to, such debentures or stock` `it is kept by a receiver as Rule 1 requires`

§§ `Order 41, rule 2 -- Registration of transfers, etc.`

-- o 41 r 2(1) the receiver's duty to register the transfer or other transmission of title arises
@export Under Order 41, rule 2(1), is it so that the receiver's duty to register the transfer or other transmission of title arises?
GIVEN `the receiver was appointed by the Court in an action to enforce registered debentures or registered debenture stock` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the receiver was appointed by the Court in an action to enforce registered debentures or registered debenture stock? (yes or no)
      `the Court has directed the receiver to keep a register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has directed the receiver to keep a register? (yes or no)
      `a person entitled to debentures or debenture stock by virtue of a transfer or other transmission of title has applied for registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a person entitled to debentures or debenture stock by virtue of a transfer or other transmission of title has applied for registration? (yes or no)
      `that person has produced such evidence of identity and title as the receiver may reasonably require` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that that person has produced such evidence of identity and title as the receiver may reasonably require? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 2(1), is it so that the receiver's duty to register the transfer or other transmission of title arises` IS
    `o 41 r 2(1) the receiver's duty to register the transfer or other transmission of title arises` `the receiver was appointed by the Court in an action to enforce registered debentures or registered debenture stock` `the Court has directed the receiver to keep a register` `a person entitled to debentures or debenture stock by virtue of a transfer or other transmission of title has applied for registration` `that person has produced such evidence of identity and title as the receiver may reasonably require`

-- o 41 r 2(2) the receiver's duty to send a notice before registering a transfer arises
@export Under Order 41, rule 2(2), is it so that the receiver's duty to send a notice before registering a transfer arises?
GIVEN `what is to be registered is a transfer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that what is to be registered is a transfer? (yes or no)
      `the due execution of the transfer is proved by affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the due execution of the transfer is proved by affidavit? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 2(2), is it so that the receiver's duty to send a notice before registering a transfer arises` IS
    `o 41 r 2(2) the receiver's duty to send a notice before registering a transfer arises` `what is to be registered is a transfer` `the due execution of the transfer is proved by affidavit`

-- o 41 r 2(2) the notice is as the Rule requires
@export Under Order 41, rule 2(2), is it so that the notice is as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it is sent by post to the registered holder of the debentures or debenture stock transferred at the holder's registered address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the notice: is it true that it is sent by post to the registered holder of the debentures or debenture stock transferred at the holder's registered address? (yes or no)
      `it states that an application for the registration of the transfer has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the notice: is it true that it states that an application for the registration of the transfer has been made? (yes or no)
      `it states that the transfer will be registered unless within the period specified in the notice the holder informs the receiver that the holder objects to the registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the notice: is it true that it states that the transfer will be registered unless within the period specified in the notice the holder informs the receiver that the holder objects to the registration? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 2(2), is it so that the notice is as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 41 r 2(2) the notice is as the Rule requires` `the notice as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `the notice as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 41 r 2(2) the notice` WITH
            `o 41 r 2(2) it is sent by post to the registered holder of the debentures or debenture stock transferred at the holder's registered address` IS `it is sent by post to the registered holder of the debentures or debenture stock transferred at the holder's registered address`
            `o 41 r 2(2)(a) it states that an application for the registration of the transfer has been made` IS `it states that an application for the registration of the transfer has been made`
            `o 41 r 2(2)(b) it states that the transfer will be registered unless within the period specified in the notice the holder informs the receiver that the holder objects to the registration` IS `it states that the transfer will be registered unless within the period specified in the notice the holder informs the receiver that the holder objects to the registration`

-- o 41 r 2(2) the transfer cannot yet be registered
@export Under Order 41, rule 2(2), is it so that the transfer cannot yet be registered?
GIVEN `a notice specifying a period was sent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a notice specifying a period was sent? (yes or no)
      `the date on which registration is proposed` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which registration is proposed?
      `the last day of the period specified in the notice` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period specified in the notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 2(2), is it so that the transfer cannot yet be registered` IS
    `o 41 r 2(2) the transfer cannot yet be registered` `a notice specifying a period was sent` `the date on which registration is proposed` `the last day of the period specified in the notice`

-- o 41 r 2(3) the day a reply would in the ordinary course of post reach the receiver
@export Under Order 41, rule 2(3), what is the day a reply would in the ordinary course of post reach the receiver?
GIVEN `the day the notice would in the ordinary course of post be delivered` IS A DATE @desc What is the day the notice would in the ordinary course of post be delivered?
      `the days a reply would in the ordinary course of post take to reach the receiver` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the days a reply would in the ordinary course of post take to reach the receiver? (a number)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 2(3), what is the day a reply would in the ordinary course of post reach the receiver` IS
    `o 41 r 2(3) the day a reply would in the ordinary course of post reach the receiver` `the day the notice would in the ordinary course of post be delivered` `the days a reply would in the ordinary course of post take to reach the receiver`

-- o 41 r 2(3) the period specified in the notice is long enough
@export Under Order 41, rule 2(3), is it so that the period specified in the notice is long enough?
GIVEN `the last day of the period specified in the notice` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period specified in the notice?
      `the first day on which the act may be done` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day on which this act may be done, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 2(3), is it so that the period specified in the notice is long enough` IS
    `o 41 r 2(3) the period specified in the notice is long enough` `the last day of the period specified in the notice` `the first day on which the act may be done`

-- o 41 r 2(4) the receiver's duty to endorse a memorandum arises
@export Under Order 41, rule 2(4), is it so that the receiver's duty to endorse a memorandum arises?
GIVEN `the receiver has registered a transfer or other transmission of title under Rule 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the receiver has registered a transfer or other transmission of title under Rule 2? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 2(4), is it so that the receiver's duty to endorse a memorandum arises` IS
    `o 41 r 2(4) the receiver's duty to endorse a memorandum arises` `the receiver has registered a transfer or other transmission of title under Rule 2`

-- o 41 r 2(4) the memorandum is as the Rule requires
@export Under Order 41, rule 2(4), is it so that the memorandum is as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the receiver has registered a transfer or other transmission of title under Rule 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the receiver has registered a transfer or other transmission of title under Rule 2? (yes or no)
      `it is endorsed on the debentures or on the certificate of debenture stock transferred or transmitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the memorandum: is it true that it is endorsed on the debentures or on the certificate of debenture stock transferred or transmitted? (yes or no)
      `it contains a reference to the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the memorandum: is it true that it contains a reference to the action? (yes or no)
      `it contains a reference to the order appointing the receiver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the memorandum: is it true that it contains a reference to the order appointing the receiver? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 2(4), is it so that the memorandum is as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 41 r 2(4) the memorandum is as the Rule requires` `the receiver has registered a transfer or other transmission of title under Rule 2` `the memorandum as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `the memorandum as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 41 r 2(4) the memorandum` WITH
            `o 41 r 2(4) it is endorsed on the debentures or on the certificate of debenture stock transferred or transmitted` IS `it is endorsed on the debentures or on the certificate of debenture stock transferred or transmitted`
            `o 41 r 2(4) it contains a reference to the action` IS `it contains a reference to the action`
            `o 41 r 2(4) it contains a reference to the order appointing the receiver` IS `it contains a reference to the order appointing the receiver`

§§ `Order 41, rule 3 -- Application for rectification of receiver’s register`

-- o 41 r 3(1) the person may apply to the Court for rectification of the receiver's register
@export Under Order 41, rule 3(1), is it so that the person may apply to the Court for rectification of the receiver's register?
GIVEN `the person is aggrieved by something done or omitted by a receiver under Rule 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is aggrieved by something done or omitted by a receiver under Rule 2? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 3(1), is it so that the person may apply to the Court for rectification of the receiver's register` IS
    `o 41 r 3(1) the person may apply to the Court for rectification of the receiver's register` `the person is aggrieved by something done or omitted by a receiver under Rule 2`

-- o 41 r 3(1) the application is made in the way the Rule requires
@export Under Order 41, rule 3(1), is it so that the application is made in the way the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the application is made by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application is made by summons? (yes or no)
      `the summons is in the action in which the receiver was appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the summons is in the action in which the receiver was appointed? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 3(1), is it so that the application is made in the way the Rule requires` IS
    `o 41 r 3(1) the application is made in the way the Rule requires` `the application is made by summons` `the summons is in the action in which the receiver was appointed`

-- o 41 r 3(2) the summons is served as the Rule requires in the first instance
@export Under Order 41, rule 3(2), is it so that the summons is served as the Rule requires in the first instance?
GIVEN `the summons is served on the claimant or other party having the conduct of the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the summons is served on the claimant or other party having the conduct of the action? (yes or no)
      `the summons is also served on any other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the summons is also served on any other person? (yes or no)
      `the Court has directed the summons or notice of the application to be served on that other person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has directed the summons or notice of the application to be served on that other person? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 3(2), is it so that the summons is served as the Rule requires in the first instance` IS
    `o 41 r 3(2) the summons is served as the Rule requires in the first instance` `the summons is served on the claimant or other party having the conduct of the action` `the summons is also served on any other person` `the Court has directed the summons or notice of the application to be served on that other person`

-- o 41 r 3(3) the Court hearing the application may decide the question
@export Under Order 41, rule 3(3), is it so that the Court hearing the application may decide the question?
GIVEN `the question relates to the title of a person who is a party to the application to have that person's name entered in or omitted from the receiver's register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the question relates to the title of a person who is a party to the application to have that person's name entered in or omitted from the receiver's register? (yes or no)
      `the question is necessary or expedient to be decided for the rectification of the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the question is necessary or expedient to be decided for the rectification of the register? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 3(3), is it so that the Court hearing the application may decide the question` IS
    `o 41 r 3(3) the Court hearing the application may decide the question` `the question relates to the title of a person who is a party to the application to have that person's name entered in or omitted from the receiver's register` `the question is necessary or expedient to be decided for the rectification of the register`

§§ `Order 41, rule 4 -- Receiver’s register evidence of transfers, etc.`

-- o 41 r 4 the entry is evidence of the transfer or transmission of title
@export Under Order 41, rule 4, is it so that the entry is evidence of the transfer or transmission of title?
GIVEN `the entry is made in the receiver's register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the entry is made in the receiver's register? (yes or no)
      `the proceedings are proceedings in the action in which the receiver was appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the proceedings are proceedings in the action in which the receiver was appointed? (yes or no)
      `the entry is verified by an affidavit made by the receiver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the entry is verified by an affidavit made by the receiver? (yes or no)
      `the entry is verified by an affidavit made by another person the Court has directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the entry is verified by an affidavit made by another person the Court has directed? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 4, is it so that the entry is evidence of the transfer or transmission of title` IS
    `o 41 r 4 the entry is evidence of the transfer or transmission of title` `the entry is made in the receiver's register` `the proceedings are proceedings in the action in which the receiver was appointed` `the entry is verified by an affidavit made by the receiver` `the entry is verified by an affidavit made by another person the Court has directed`

§§ `Order 41, rule 5 -- Proof of title of holder of bearer debenture, etc.`

-- o 41 r 5(1) this Rule applies to the action
@export Under Order 41, rule 5(1), is it so that this Rule applies to the action?
GIVEN `the action is to enforce bearer debentures` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the action is to enforce bearer debentures? (yes or no)
      `the action is to enforce debenture stock in respect of which the company has issued debenture stock bearer certificates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the action is to enforce debenture stock in respect of which the company has issued debenture stock bearer certificates? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 5(1), is it so that this Rule applies to the action` IS
    `o 41 r 5(1) this Rule applies to the action` `the action is to enforce bearer debentures` `the action is to enforce debenture stock in respect of which the company has issued debenture stock bearer certificates`

-- o 41 r 5(2) the title of the person claiming to be the holder is sufficiently proved
@export Under Order 41, rule 5(2), is it so that the title of the person claiming to be the holder is sufficiently proved?
GIVEN `the debentures or debenture stock certificates are produced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the debentures or debenture stock certificates are produced? (yes or no)
      `a certificate of identification signed by the person producing them is produced with them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a certificate of identification signed by the person producing them is produced with them? (yes or no)
      `the certificate of identification identifies the debenture or certificate produced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate of identification identifies the debenture or certificate produced? (yes or no)
      `the certificate of identification certifies the name and address of the holder of the debenture or certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate of identification certifies the name and address of the holder of the debenture or certificate? (yes or no)
      `there is notice of a defect in the title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is notice of a defect in the title? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 5(2), is it so that the title of the person claiming to be the holder is sufficiently proved` IS
    `o 41 r 5(2) the title of the person claiming to be the holder is sufficiently proved` `the debentures or debenture stock certificates are produced` `a certificate of identification signed by the person producing them is produced with them` `the certificate of identification identifies the debenture or certificate produced` `the certificate of identification certifies the name and address of the holder of the debenture or certificate` `there is notice of a defect in the title`

-- o 41 r 5(3) the claimant's solicitor's duty to cause a notice to be endorsed arises
@export Under Order 41, rule 5(3), is it so that the claimant's solicitor's duty to cause a notice to be endorsed arises?
GIVEN `the debenture or certificate is produced in the chambers of the Judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the debenture or certificate is produced in the chambers of the Judge? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 5(3), is it so that the claimant's solicitor's duty to cause a notice to be endorsed arises` IS
    `o 41 r 5(3) the claimant's solicitor's duty to cause a notice to be endorsed arises` `the debenture or certificate is produced in the chambers of the Judge`

-- o 41 r 5(3) the notice endorsed is as the Rule requires
@export Under Order 41, rule 5(3), is it so that the notice endorsed is as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the debenture or certificate is produced in the chambers of the Judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the debenture or certificate is produced in the chambers of the Judge? (yes or no)
      `it states that the person named as the holder in the certificate of identification has been recorded in the chambers of the Judge as the holder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the notice endorsed: is it true that it states that the person named as the holder in the certificate of identification has been recorded in the chambers of the Judge as the holder? (yes or no)
      `it states that that person will, on producing the debenture or certificate, be entitled to receive payment of any dividend unless before payment a new holder proves the new holder's title in accordance with paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the notice endorsed: is it true that it states that that person will, on producing the debenture or certificate, be entitled to receive payment of any dividend unless before payment a new holder proves the new holder's title in accordance with paragraph (2)? (yes or no)
      `it states that if a new holder neglects to prove title the new holder may incur additional delay, trouble and expense in obtaining payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the notice endorsed: is it true that it states that if a new holder neglects to prove title the new holder may incur additional delay, trouble and expense in obtaining payment? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 5(3), is it so that the notice endorsed is as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 41 r 5(3) the notice endorsed is as the Rule requires` `the debenture or certificate is produced in the chambers of the Judge` `the notice endorsed as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `the notice endorsed as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 41 r 5(3) the notice endorsed` WITH
            `o 41 r 5(3)(a) it states that the person named as the holder in the certificate of identification has been recorded in the chambers of the Judge as the holder` IS `it states that the person named as the holder in the certificate of identification has been recorded in the chambers of the Judge as the holder`
            `o 41 r 5(3)(b) it states that that person will, on producing the debenture or certificate, be entitled to receive payment of any dividend unless before payment a new holder proves the new holder's title in accordance with paragraph (2)` IS `it states that that person will, on producing the debenture or certificate, be entitled to receive payment of any dividend unless before payment a new holder proves the new holder's title in accordance with paragraph (2)`
            `o 41 r 5(3)(c) it states that if a new holder neglects to prove title the new holder may incur additional delay, trouble and expense in obtaining payment` IS `it states that if a new holder neglects to prove title the new holder may incur additional delay, trouble and expense in obtaining payment`

-- o 41 r 5(4) the solicitor has preserved the certificates and kept the record
@export Under Order 41, rule 5(4), is it so that the solicitor has preserved the certificates and kept the record?
GIVEN `has preserved every certificate of identification produced under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the solicitor has done: is it true that has preserved every certificate of identification produced under paragraph (2)? (yes or no)
      `has kept a record of the debentures and certificates produced, of the names and addresses of the persons producing them and of the holders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what the solicitor has done: is it true that has kept a record of the debentures and certificates produced, of the names and addresses of the persons producing them and of the holders? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 5(4), is it so that the solicitor has preserved the certificates and kept the record` IS
    `o 41 r 5(4) the solicitor has preserved the certificates and kept the record` `what the solicitor has done as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `what the solicitor has done as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 41 r 5(4) what the solicitor has done` WITH
            `o 41 r 5(4) has preserved every certificate of identification produced under paragraph (2)` IS `has preserved every certificate of identification produced under paragraph (2)`
            `o 41 r 5(4) has kept a record of the debentures and certificates produced, of the names and addresses of the persons producing them and of the holders` IS `has kept a record of the debentures and certificates produced, of the names and addresses of the persons producing them and of the holders`

-- o 41 r 5(4) the solicitor's duty to verify the record by affidavit arises
@export Under Order 41, rule 5(4), is it so that the solicitor's duty to verify the record by affidavit arises?
GIVEN `the Court requires the record to be verified by affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court requires the record to be verified by affidavit? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 5(4), is it so that the solicitor's duty to verify the record by affidavit arises` IS
    `o 41 r 5(4) the solicitor's duty to verify the record by affidavit arises` `the Court requires the record to be verified by affidavit`

§§ `Order 41, rule 6 -- Requirements in connection with payments`

-- o 41 r 6(1) the bar on payment by the Accountant-General applies
@export Under Order 41, rule 6(1), is it so that the bar on payment by the Accountant-General applies?
GIVEN `an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock in an action to enforce them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock in an action to enforce them? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 6(1), is it so that the bar on payment by the Accountant-General applies` IS
    `o 41 r 6(1) the bar on payment by the Accountant-General applies` `an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock in an action to enforce them`

-- o 41 r 6(1) the Accountant-General may make a payment in respect of the debenture or stock
@export Under Order 41, rule 6(1), is it so that the Accountant-General may make a payment in respect of the debenture or stock?
GIVEN `an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock in an action to enforce them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock in an action to enforce them? (yes or no)
      `the certificate for which paragraph (2) provides is produced to the Accountant-General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate for which paragraph (2) provides is produced to the Accountant-General? (yes or no)
      `the Court has for special reason dispensed with the need for the certificate and directed payment without it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has for special reason dispensed with the need for the certificate and directed payment without it? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 6(1), is it so that the Accountant-General may make a payment in respect of the debenture or stock` IS
    `o 41 r 6(1) the Accountant-General may make a payment in respect of the debenture or stock` `an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock in an action to enforce them` `the certificate for which paragraph (2) provides is produced to the Accountant-General` `the Court has for special reason dispensed with the need for the certificate and directed payment without it`

-- o 41 r 6(1) the Accountant-General is barred from making the payment
@export Under Order 41, rule 6(1), is it so that the Accountant-General is barred from making the payment?
GIVEN `an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock in an action to enforce them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock in an action to enforce them? (yes or no)
      `the certificate for which paragraph (2) provides is produced to the Accountant-General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the certificate for which paragraph (2) provides is produced to the Accountant-General? (yes or no)
      `the Court has for special reason dispensed with the need for the certificate and directed payment without it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court has for special reason dispensed with the need for the certificate and directed payment without it? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 6(1), is it so that the Accountant-General is barred from making the payment` IS
    `o 41 r 6(1) the Accountant-General is barred from making the payment` `an order is made for payment in respect of the debentures or stock in an action to enforce them` `the certificate for which paragraph (2) provides is produced to the Accountant-General` `the Court has for special reason dispensed with the need for the certificate and directed payment without it`

-- o 41 r 6(2) the steps for obtaining payment are done
@export Under Order 41, rule 6(2), is it so that the steps for obtaining payment are done?
GIVEN `the debenture or certificate is produced to the solicitor of the claimant or to the person the Court directs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what has been done: is it true that the debenture or certificate is produced to the solicitor of the claimant or to the person the Court directs? (yes or no)
      `a memorandum of payment is endorsed on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what has been done: is it true that a memorandum of payment is endorsed on it? (yes or no)
      `a certificate certifying the endorsement is made and signed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what has been done: is it true that a certificate certifying the endorsement is made and signed? (yes or no)
      `the certificate is sent to the Accountant-General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc what has been done: is it true that the certificate is sent to the Accountant-General? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 41, rule 6(2), is it so that the steps for obtaining payment are done` IS
    `o 41 r 6(2) the steps for obtaining payment are done` `what has been done as the Rule needs it`
    WHERE
        `what has been done as the Rule needs it` MEANS `o 41 r 6(2) what has been done` WITH
            `o 41 r 6(2) the debenture or certificate is produced to the solicitor of the claimant or to the person the Court directs` IS `the debenture or certificate is produced to the solicitor of the claimant or to the person the Court directs`
            `o 41 r 6(2)(a) a memorandum of payment is endorsed on it` IS `a memorandum of payment is endorsed on it`
            `o 41 r 6(2)(b) a certificate certifying the endorsement is made and signed` IS `a certificate certifying the endorsement is made and signed`
            `o 41 r 6(2)(b) the certificate is sent to the Accountant-General` IS `the certificate is sent to the Accountant-General`

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 42 -- Debtors Act`
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Order 42, rule 1 -- Application and definitions of this Order`

-- o 42 r 1(1) these Rules apply to the proceedings
@export Under Order 42, rule 1(1), is it so that these Rules apply to the proceedings?
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under the Debtors Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the proceedings are proceedings under the Debtors Act? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 42, rule 1(1), is it so that these Rules apply to the proceedings` IS
    `o 42 r 1(1) these Rules apply to the proceedings` `the proceedings are proceedings under the Debtors Act`

-- o 42 r 1(2) a court is the Court
@export Under Order 42, rule 1(2), is it so that a court is the Court?
GIVEN `the court is a court within the meaning of section 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the court is a court within the meaning of section 2? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 42, rule 1(2), is it so that a court is the Court` IS
    `o 42 r 1(2) a court is the Court` `the court is a court within the meaning of section 2`

-- o 42 r 1(2) a judge is a Judge
@export Under Order 42, rule 1(2), is it so that a judge is a Judge?
GIVEN `the judge is a judge within the meaning of section 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the judge is a judge within the meaning of section 2? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 42, rule 1(2), is it so that a judge is a Judge` IS
    `o 42 r 1(2) a judge is a Judge` `the judge is a judge within the meaning of section 2`

-- o 42 r 1(2) an order is a judgment
@export Under Order 42, rule 1(2), is it so that an order is a judgment?
GIVEN `the order is an order for the payment of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order is an order for the payment of money? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 42, rule 1(2), is it so that an order is a judgment` IS
    `o 42 r 1(2) an order is a judgment` `the order is an order for the payment of money`

§§ `Order 42, rule 2 -- Application under section 3`

-- o 42 r 2 the requirement as to how the application is made applies
@export Under Order 42, rule 2, is it so that the requirement as to how the application is made applies?
GIVEN `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court otherwise orders? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 42, rule 2, is it so that the requirement as to how the application is made applies` IS
    `o 42 r 2 the requirement as to how the application is made applies` `the Court otherwise orders`

-- o 42 r 2 the application for an order of arrest is made as the Rule requires
@export Under Order 42, rule 2, is it so that the application for an order of arrest is made as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Court otherwise orders? (yes or no)
      `the application is made by summons without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application is made by summons without notice? (yes or no)
      `the summons is supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the summons is supported by an affidavit? (yes or no)
      `the application is made to a Judge sitting in chambers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the application is made to a Judge sitting in chambers? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 42, rule 2, is it so that the application for an order of arrest is made as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 42 r 2 the application for an order of arrest is made as the Rule requires` `the Court otherwise orders` `the application is made by summons without notice` `the summons is supported by an affidavit` `the application is made to a Judge sitting in chambers`

§§ `Order 42, rule 3 -- Form of order of arrest`

-- o 42 r 3 the order for arrest under section 3 is in Form 62
@export Under Order 42, rule 3, is it so that the order for arrest under section 3 is in Form 62?
GIVEN `the order is in Form 62` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order is in Form 62? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 42, rule 3, is it so that the order for arrest under section 3 is in Form 62` IS
    `o 42 r 3 the order for arrest under section 3 is in Form 62` `the order is in Form 62`

§§ `Order 42, rule 4 -- Where judgment debtor summons issued under section 24`

-- o 42 r 4(1) the issue of a judgment debtor summons prevents the judgment creditor from applying for an order of arrest
@export Under Order 42, rule 4(1), is it so that the issue of a judgment debtor summons prevents the judgment creditor from applying for an order of arrest?
GIVEN `a judgment debtor summons under section 24 has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a judgment debtor summons under section 24 has been issued? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 42, rule 4(1), is it so that the issue of a judgment debtor summons prevents the judgment creditor from applying for an order of arrest` IS
    `o 42 r 4(1) the issue of a judgment debtor summons prevents the judgment creditor from applying for an order of arrest` `a judgment debtor summons under section 24 has been issued`

-- o 42 r 4(2) the order for arrest under section 24 is in Form 63
@export Under Order 42, rule 4(2), is it so that the order for arrest under section 24 is in Form 63?
GIVEN `the order is in Form 63` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the order is in Form 63? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 42, rule 4(2), is it so that the order for arrest under section 24 is in Form 63` IS
    `o 42 r 4(2) the order for arrest under section 24 is in Form 63` `the order is in Form 63`

§§ `Order 42, rule 5 -- Conveyance and subsistence money`

-- o 42 r 5(1) the judgment creditor's duty to deposit before the arrest applies
@export Under Order 42, rule 5(1), is it so that the judgment creditor's duty to deposit before the arrest applies?
GIVEN `an arrest is about to be made under section 3 or 24` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an arrest is about to be made under section 3 or 24? (yes or no)
      `the Registrar otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar otherwise orders? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 42, rule 5(1), is it so that the judgment creditor's duty to deposit before the arrest applies` IS
    `o 42 r 5(1) the judgment creditor's duty to deposit before the arrest applies` `an arrest is about to be made under section 3 or 24` `the Registrar otherwise orders`

-- o 42 r 5(1) the judgment creditor has deposited what the Rule requires before the arrest
@export Under Order 42, rule 5(1), is it so that the judgment creditor has deposited what the Rule requires before the arrest?
GIVEN `an arrest is about to be made under section 3 or 24` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an arrest is about to be made under section 3 or 24? (yes or no)
      `the Registrar otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the Registrar otherwise orders? (yes or no)
      `a sum of money has been deposited in the Registry before the arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a sum of money has been deposited in the Registry before the arrest? (yes or no)
      `the sum is sufficient to defray the cost of bringing the debtor before the Court and detaining the debtor in custody pending the debtor's appearance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the sum is sufficient to defray the cost of bringing the debtor before the Court and detaining the debtor in custody pending the debtor's appearance? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 42, rule 5(1), is it so that the judgment creditor has deposited what the Rule requires before the arrest` IS
    `o 42 r 5(1) the judgment creditor has deposited what the Rule requires before the arrest` `an arrest is about to be made under section 3 or 24` `the Registrar otherwise orders` `a sum of money has been deposited in the Registry before the arrest` `the sum is sufficient to defray the cost of bringing the debtor before the Court and detaining the debtor in custody pending the debtor's appearance`

-- o 42 r 5(1) the deposit is made before the arrest
@export Under Order 42, rule 5(1), is it so that the deposit is made before the arrest?
GIVEN `a sum of money has been deposited in the Registry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a sum of money has been deposited in the Registry? (yes or no)
      `the deposit was made before the arrest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the deposit was made before the arrest? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 42, rule 5(1), is it so that the deposit is made before the arrest` IS
    `o 42 r 5(1) the deposit is made before the arrest` `a sum of money has been deposited in the Registry` `the deposit was made before the arrest`

-- o 42 r 5(2) the judgment creditor's duty to deposit before the order of commitment is executed applies
@export Under Order 42, rule 5(2), is it so that the judgment creditor's duty to deposit before the order of commitment is executed applies?
GIVEN `an order of commitment made under the Act is about to be executed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an order of commitment made under the Act is about to be executed? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 42, rule 5(2), is it so that the judgment creditor's duty to deposit before the order of commitment is executed applies` IS
    `o 42 r 5(2) the judgment creditor's duty to deposit before the order of commitment is executed applies` `an order of commitment made under the Act is about to be executed`

-- o 42 r 5(2) the judgment creditor has deposited what the Rule requires before the order of commitment is executed
