§§ `Order 44, rule 13 -- Service of certain documents on person under disability`

-- o 44 r 13(1) this Rule applies
@export Under Order 44, rule 13(1), is it so that this Rule applies?
GIVEN `a document is required to be served personally on the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a document is required to be served personally on the person? (yes or no)
      `the person is a person under disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person is a person under disability? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 44, rule 13(1), is it so that this Rule applies` IS
    `o 44 r 13(1) this Rule applies` `a document is required to be served personally on the person` `the person is a person under disability`

-- o 44 r 13(2) the document is served on the person the Rule names
@export Under Order 44, rule 13(2), is it so that the document is served on the person the Rule names?
GIVEN `this Rule applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that this Rule applies? (yes or no)
      `Order 11, Rule 7(c) otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that Order 11, Rule 7(c) otherwise provides? (yes or no)
      `the person under disability is a minor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person under disability is a minor? (yes or no)
      `the person under disability is a person lacking capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person under disability is a person lacking capacity? (yes or no)
      `the minor has a father or guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the minor has a father or guardian? (yes or no)
      `there is a person authorised under the Act to conduct the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that there is a person authorised under the Act to conduct the proceedings? (yes or no)
      `whom the document is served on` IS A `Under Order 44, rule 13(2): whom the document is served on` @desc Which of these applies: whom the document is served on?
      `the document is served in the manner required by these Rules with respect to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the document is served in the manner required by these Rules with respect to it? (yes or no)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 44, rule 13(2), is it so that the document is served on the person the Rule names` IS
    `o 44 r 13(2) the document is served on the person the Rule names` `this Rule applies` `Order 11, Rule 7(c) otherwise provides` `the person under disability is a minor` `the person under disability is a person lacking capacity` `the minor has a father or guardian` `there is a person authorised under the Act to conduct the proceedings` (`Under Orders 39 to 45, my choice for o 44 r 13(2) whom the document is served on` `whom the document is served on`) `the document is served in the manner required by these Rules with respect to it`

-- o 44 r 13(3) the Court may order the document to be deemed duly served on the person under disability
