§ `Order 48 -- International Arbitration Act: I am applying to the Court about an arbitration, or resisting such an application`
-- This group arises only if the proceedings are under the International Arbitration Act: ask "Does this apply to you?" before showing it.
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Rule 2 -- Challenging an arbitrator, an arbitral ruling or an award (O. 48, r. 2)`

@export Under Order 48, rule 2(1), must my application to a Judge about an arbitrator, a ruling or an award be made by originating application?
GIVEN `my application is made to a Judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application made to a Judge?
      `the kind of application I am making` IS A `o 48 r 2(1) the kind of application to a Judge` @desc What are you applying for? One of the choices offered by the form (challenge of an arbitrator under Article 13(3); termination of an arbitrator's mandate under Article 14(1); appeal against a ruling under section 10 or Article 16(3); setting aside an award under section 24 or Article 34(2); another kind)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 2(1), must my application be made by originating application` IS
    `o 48 r 2(1) the application must be made by originating application` `my application is made to a Judge` `the kind of application I am making`

@export Under Order 48, rule 2(1), have I made my application in the form I must use?
GIVEN `my application is made to a Judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application made to a Judge?
      `the kind of application I am making` IS A `o 48 r 2(1) the kind of application to a Judge` @desc What are you applying for?
      `the document I used` IS A `Document kind` @desc What document did you use to make the application? One of: Originating claim, Originating application, Statement of claim, Defence, Defence and counterclaim, Reply, Reply to a defence and counterclaim, Summons, Summons without notice, Affidavit, Notice of intention to contest or not contest, Notice of appeal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 2(1), have I made my application by originating application as I must` IS
    `o 48 r 2(1) the application is made by originating application as it must be` `my application is made to a Judge` `the kind of application I am making` `the document I used`

@export Under Order 48, rule 2(2), within how many days after I receive the arbitral tribunal's decision or ruling must I apply to challenge an arbitrator, end an arbitrator's mandate or appeal a ruling?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 2(2), how many days after receipt of the decision or ruling do I have to apply` IS
    `o 48 r 2(2) the period after receipt of the decision or ruling`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 48, rule 2(2), am I in time to apply to challenge an arbitrator, end an arbitrator's mandate or appeal a ruling?
GIVEN `the kind of application I am making` IS A `o 48 r 2(1) the kind of application to a Judge` @desc What are you applying for?
      `the date I made, or will make, the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make (or will you make) the application?
      `the last day for making it, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day: 30 days after you received the tribunal's decision or ruling (the period begins the day after receipt, which is fixed by Article 3 of the Model Law; if the last day falls on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, take the next court day)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 2(2), am I in time to make my application` IS
    `o 48 r 2(2) the application is made within 30 days after receipt of the decision or ruling` `the kind of application I am making` `the date I made, or will make, the application` `the last day for making it, counted under Order 3, Rule 3`

@export Under Order 48, rule 2(3), within how many months must I apply to set aside an award?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 2(3), how many months after the later date do I have to apply to set aside an award` IS
    `o 48 r 2(3) the period after the later date`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 48, rule 2(3), which date do the 3 months for setting aside an award run from?
GIVEN `the date I received the award` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you receive the award?
      `I asked the arbitral tribunal for a correction or interpretation under Article 33 of the Model Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you make a request to the arbitral tribunal under Article 33 of the Model Law?
      `the date the tribunal disposed of that request` IS A DATE @desc On what date did the tribunal dispose of that request? (Any date if you made none.)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 2(3), from which date do the 3 months run` IS
    `o 48 r 2(3) the later date from which the 3 months run` `the date I received the award` (`roc10 a date if there is one` `I asked the arbitral tribunal for a correction or interpretation under Article 33 of the Model Law` `the date the tribunal disposed of that request`)

@export Under Order 48, rule 2(3), am I in time to apply to set aside an award?
GIVEN `the date I made, or will make, the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make (or will you make) the application to set aside the award?
      `the last day for making it, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day: 3 months after the later of the date you received the award and (if you asked for a correction under Article 33) the date that request was disposed of (the period begins the day after; a month is a calendar month; if the last day falls on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, take the next court day)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 2(3), am I in time to apply to set aside the award` IS
    `o 48 r 2(3) the application to set aside an award is made in time` `o 48 r 2(1)(d) an application to set aside an award under section 24 or Article 34(2) of the Model Law` `the date I made, or will make, the application` `the last day for making it, counted under Order 3, Rule 3`

@export Under Order 48, rule 2(4), does my affidavit in support of my application have everything it must?
GIVEN `the affidavit supports an application under Rule 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit support an application of one of the kinds in Order 48, Rule 2(1)?
      `it states the grounds in support of the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the grounds in support of the application?
      `it exhibits a copy of the arbitration agreement or any record of its content` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it exhibit a copy of the arbitration agreement, or any record of its content?
      `it exhibits the award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it exhibit the award?
      `it exhibits any other document I rely on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it exhibit any other document you rely on?
      `it sets out any evidence I rely on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out any evidence you rely on?
      `it is served with the originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it served with the originating application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 2(4), does my affidavit in support have everything it must` IS
    `o 48 r 2(4) the affidavit in support is as it must be` `the affidavit supports an application under Rule 2(1)` `it states the grounds in support of the application` `it exhibits a copy of the arbitration agreement or any record of its content` `it exhibits the award` `it exhibits any other document I rely on` `it sets out any evidence I rely on` `it is served with the originating application`

@export Under Order 48, rule 2(5), must I file an affidavit as the defendant, and within how many days?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 2(5), within how many days of being served must a defendant who opposes file an affidavit` IS
    `o 48 r 2(5) the period after service of the originating application`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 48, rule 2(5), must I, as the defendant, file an affidavit stating why I oppose the application?
GIVEN `I have been served with the originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been served with the originating application?
      `I wish to oppose the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you wish to oppose the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 2(5), must I file an affidavit stating why I oppose` IS
    `o 48 r 2(5) the duty to file an affidavit stating the grounds of opposition arises` `I have been served with the originating application` `I wish to oppose the application`

@export Under Order 48, rule 2(5), did I file my affidavit of opposition in time?
GIVEN `I have been served with the originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been served with the originating application?
      `I wish to oppose the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you wish to oppose the application?
      `the date I filed my affidavit` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file your affidavit stating the grounds on which you oppose the application?
      `the last day for filing it, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day: 14 days after you were served with the originating application (the period begins the day after service; if the last day falls on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, take the next court day)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 2(5), did I file my affidavit of opposition in time` IS
    `o 48 r 2(5) the affidavit of opposition has been filed in time` `I have been served with the originating application` `I wish to oppose the application` `the date I filed my affidavit` `the last day for filing it, counted under Order 3, Rule 3`

@export Under Order 48, rule 2(6), am I in time to apply for permission to appeal against the Court's decision under section 10?
GIVEN `my application is for permission to appeal against a decision of the Court under section 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application for permission to appeal against a decision of the Court under section 10 of the Act?
      `the date I made, or will make, the application` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you make (or will you make) the application?
      `the last day for making it, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day: 14 days after the Court's decision (the period begins the day after the decision; if the last day falls on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, take the next court day)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 2(6), am I in time to apply for permission to appeal` IS
    `o 48 r 2(6) the application for permission to appeal is made in time` `my application is for permission to appeal against a decision of the Court under section 10` `the date I made, or will make, the application` `the last day for making it, counted under Order 3, Rule 3`

§§ `Rule 3 -- Other applications to the Court under the Act (O. 48, r. 3)`

@export Under Order 48, rule 3(1), must my application be made to a Judge or the Registrar?
GIVEN `the kind of application I am making` IS A `o 48 r 3(1) the kind of application or request to the Court` @desc What are you applying for? One of the choices offered by the form (to hear an application in open court under section 22; permission to enforce interim orders or directions under section 12(6); interim orders or directions under section 12A; to reinstate discontinued proceedings under section 6(4); permission to enforce an award under section 18 or 19; permission to enforce a foreign award under section 29; another kind)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 3(1), must my application be made to a Judge or the Registrar` IS
    `o 48 r 3(1) the application must be made to a Judge or the Registrar` `the kind of application I am making`

@export Under Order 48, rule 3(2), must I apply by summons or by originating application?
GIVEN `the kind of application I am making` IS A `o 48 r 3(1) the kind of application or request to the Court` @desc What are you applying for?
      `an action is pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an action already pending in the Court?
      `the document I used` IS A `Document kind` @desc What document did you use to make the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 3(2), have I used the document I must use` IS
    `o 48 r 3(2) the application is made by the document this paragraph requires` `the kind of application I am making` `an action is pending` `the document I used`

@export Under Order 48, rule 3(3), may my application be made without notice to the other side?
GIVEN `the case is one of urgency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the case one of urgency?
      `the kind of application I am making` IS A `o 48 r 3(1) the kind of application or request to the Court` @desc What are you applying for?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 3(3), may my application be made without notice` IS
    `o 48 r 3(3) the application may be made without notice` `the case is one of urgency` `the kind of application I am making`

§§ `Rule 4 -- Serving the originating application out of Singapore (O. 48, r. 4)`

@export Under Order 48, rule 4(1), may I serve the originating application, or an order made on it, out of Singapore?
GIVEN `the document is the originating application or an order made on it under Order 48` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document the originating application, or an order made on it under Order 48?
      `the Court has given me permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given you permission to serve it out of Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 4(1), may I serve the document out of Singapore` IS
    `o 48 r 4(1) service out of Singapore is permissible` `the document is the originating application or an order made on it under Order 48` `the Court has given me permission`

@export Under Order 48, rule 4(2), does my application for permission to serve out of Singapore have the affidavit it needs?
GIVEN `it is an application for permission under Rule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for permission to serve out of Singapore under Order 48, Rule 4?
      `my affidavit states the ground on which I apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your affidavit state the ground on which you apply?
      `my affidavit shows where the person to be served is, or probably may be found` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your affidavit show in what place or country the person to be served is, or probably may be found?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 4(2), is my application supported by the affidavit it needs` IS
    `o 48 r 4(2) the application is supported by an affidavit as it must be` `it is an application for permission under Rule 4` `my affidavit states the ground on which I apply` `my affidavit shows where the person to be served is, or probably may be found`

@export Under Order 48, rule 4(2), is the Court barred from giving me permission to serve out of Singapore?
GIVEN `it is made sufficiently to appear to the Court that the case is a proper one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made sufficiently to appear to the Court that the case is a proper one for service out of Singapore under Order 48, Rule 4?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 4(2), is the Court barred from giving me permission` IS
    `o 48 r 4(2) the Court is barred from granting permission` `it is made sufficiently to appear to the Court that the case is a proper one`

@export Under Order 48, rule 4(2), may the Court give me permission to serve out of Singapore?
GIVEN `it is made sufficiently to appear to the Court that the case is a proper one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made sufficiently to appear to the Court that the case is a proper one for service out of Singapore under Order 48, Rule 4?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 4(2), may the Court give me permission` IS
    `o 48 r 4(2) the Court may grant permission` `it is made sufficiently to appear to the Court that the case is a proper one`

§§ `Rule 5 -- Enforcing an interim order or direction of the arbitral tribunal (O. 48, r. 5)`

@export Under Order 48, rule 5(1), does my affidavit supporting my application to enforce an interim order or direction have what it needs?
GIVEN `it is an application for permission to enforce an order or direction given by an arbitral tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for permission to enforce an order or direction given by an arbitral tribunal?
      `my affidavit exhibits a copy of the arbitration agreement or any record of its content` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your affidavit exhibit a copy of the arbitration agreement, or any record of its content?
      `my affidavit exhibits the original order or direction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your affidavit exhibit the original order or direction you want to enforce?
      `my affidavit states the provisions I rely on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your affidavit state the provisions in the Act or the applicable rules adopted in the arbitration on which you rely?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 5(1), does my affidavit have what it needs` IS
    `o 48 r 5(1) the application is supported by an affidavit as it must be` `it is an application for permission to enforce an order or direction given by an arbitral tribunal` `my affidavit exhibits a copy of the arbitration agreement or any record of its content` `my affidavit exhibits the original order or direction` `my affidavit states the provisions I rely on`

@export Under Order 48, rule 5(2), may the Court give me permission to enforce an interim injunction of the arbitral tribunal?
GIVEN `the order is in the nature of an interim injunction under section 12(1)(e) or (f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order in the nature of an interim injunction under section 12(1)(e) or (f) of the Act?
      `I undertake to abide by any order as to damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you undertake to abide by any order the Court or the arbitral tribunal may make as to damages?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 5(2), may the Court give me permission to enforce the interim injunction` IS
    `o 48 r 5(2) permission may be granted` `the order is in the nature of an interim injunction under section 12(1)(e) or (f)` `I undertake to abide by any order as to damages`

§§ `Rule 6 -- Enforcing an award or a foreign award (O. 48, r. 6)`

@export Under Order 48, rule 6(1), may I apply without notice for permission to enforce an award?
GIVEN `it is an application for permission to enforce an award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for permission to enforce an award?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 6(1), may I apply without notice to enforce an award` IS
    `o 48 r 6(1) the application for permission to enforce an award may be made without notice` `it is an application for permission to enforce an award`

@export Under Order 48, rule 6(1), does my affidavit supporting my application to enforce an award have everything it must?
GIVEN `it is an application for permission to enforce an award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for permission to enforce an award?
      `it exhibits the arbitration agreement or record and the authenticated original award, or certified copies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit exhibit the arbitration agreement (or any record of its content) and the duly authenticated original award, or duly certified copies of them?
      `the award, agreement or record is in a language other than English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the award, agreement or record in a language other than English?
      `it exhibits a translation in English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit exhibit a translation in the English language?
      `the translation was certified by` IS A `o 48 r 6(1)(a) the person who certified the translation` @desc Who certified the translation as a correct translation? One of: a sworn translator; an official; a diplomatic or consular agent of the country in which the award was made; someone else
      `it states the names and the usual or last known places of residence or business of the creditor and the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state the name and the usual or last known place of residence or business of the creditor and of the debtor?
      `it states whether, and to what extent, the award has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state either that the award has not been complied with or the extent to which it has not been complied with at the date of the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 6(1), does my affidavit have everything it must` IS
    `o 48 r 6(1) the application is supported by an affidavit as it must be` `it is an application for permission to enforce an award` `it exhibits the arbitration agreement or record and the authenticated original award, or certified copies` `the award, agreement or record is in a language other than English` `it exhibits a translation in English` `the translation was certified by` `it states the names and the usual or last known places of residence or business of the creditor and the debtor` `it states whether, and to what extent, the award has not been complied with`

@export Under Order 48, rule 6(2), may I apply without notice for permission to enforce a foreign award?
GIVEN `it is an application for permission to enforce a foreign award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for permission to enforce a foreign award?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 6(2), may I apply without notice to enforce a foreign award` IS
    `o 48 r 6(2) the application for permission to enforce a foreign award may be made without notice` `it is an application for permission to enforce a foreign award`

@export Under Order 48, rule 6(2), does my affidavit supporting my application to enforce a foreign award have everything it must?
GIVEN `it is an application for permission to enforce a foreign award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for permission to enforce a foreign award?
      `it exhibits the arbitration agreement and the authenticated original award, or certified copies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit exhibit the arbitration agreement and the duly authenticated original award, or duly certified copies of them?
      `the award or agreement is in a language other than English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the award or agreement in a language other than English?
      `it exhibits a translation in English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit exhibit a translation in the English language?
      `the translation was certified by` IS A `o 48 r 6(1)(a) the person who certified the translation` @desc Who certified the translation as a correct translation? One of: a sworn translator; an official; a diplomatic or consular agent of the country in which the award was made; someone else
      `it states the names and the usual or last known places of residence or business of the creditor and the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state the name and the usual or last known place of residence or business of the creditor and of the debtor?
      `it states whether, and to what extent, the award has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state either that the award has not been complied with or the extent to which it has not been complied with at the date of the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 6(2), does my affidavit have everything it must` IS
    `o 48 r 6(2) the application for a foreign award is supported by an affidavit as it must be` `it is an application for permission to enforce a foreign award` `it exhibits the arbitration agreement and the authenticated original award, or certified copies` `the award or agreement is in a language other than English` `it exhibits a translation in English` `the translation was certified by` `it states the names and the usual or last known places of residence or business of the creditor and the debtor` `it states whether, and to what extent, the award has not been complied with`

@export Under Order 48, rule 6(3), have I drawn up and served the order giving permission as I must?
GIVEN `I drew up the order on behalf of the creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the order giving permission drawn up by or on behalf of the creditor?
      `how I served it on the debtor` IS A `o 48 r 6(3) the way the order is served on the debtor` @desc How was the order served on the debtor? One of: delivering a copy to the debtor personally; sending a copy to the debtor's usual or last known place of residence or business; another manner the Court has directed; another manner the Court has not directed
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 6(3), have I drawn up and served the order as I must` IS
    `o 48 r 6(3) the order is drawn up and served as it must be` `I drew up the order on behalf of the creditor` `how I served it on the debtor`

@export Under Order 48, rule 6(4), may I serve the order giving permission out of Singapore without the Court's permission?
GIVEN `it is the order giving permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document the order giving permission to enforce the award?
      `it is to be served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it to be served out of Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 6(4), may I serve the order out of Singapore without permission` IS
    `o 48 r 6(4) service of the order out of Singapore is permissible without permission` `it is the order giving permission` `it is to be served out of Singapore`

@export Under Order 48, rule 6(5), within how many days of service may the debtor apply to set aside the order?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 6(5), how many days after service of the order may the debtor apply to set it aside` IS
    `o 48 r 6(5) the period after service of the order`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 48, rule 6(5), am I, the debtor, in time to apply to set aside the order?
GIVEN `the date I applied, or will apply, to set aside the order` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you apply (or will you apply) to set aside the order?
      `the last day for applying, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day: 14 days after the order was served on you or, if it was served out of Singapore, the period the Court fixed (the period begins the day after service; if the last day falls on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, take the next court day)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 6(5), am I in time to apply to set aside the order` IS
    `o 48 r 6(5) the debtor may apply to set aside the order` `the date I applied, or will apply, to set aside the order` `the last day for applying, counted under Order 3, Rule 3`

@export Under Order 48, rule 6(5), is enforcement of the award barred at present?
GIVEN `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking whether the award can be enforced?
      `the last day for the debtor to apply, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for the debtor to apply to set aside the order: 14 days after service of the order or, if served out of Singapore, the period the Court fixed (the period begins the day after service; if the last day falls on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, take the next court day)?
      `the debtor applied within that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the debtor apply within that period to set aside the order?
      `that application is finally disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that application been finally disposed of?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 6(5), is enforcement of the award barred` IS
    `o 48 r 6(5) enforcement of the award is barred` `the date I am asking about` `the last day for the debtor to apply, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` `the debtor applied within that period` `that application is finally disposed of`

@export Under Order 48, rule 6(5), may the award be enforced?
GIVEN `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking whether the award can be enforced?
      `the last day for the debtor to apply, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for the debtor to apply to set aside the order: 14 days after service of the order or, if served out of Singapore, the period the Court fixed (the period begins the day after service; if the last day falls on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, take the next court day)?
      `the debtor applied within that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the debtor apply within that period to set aside the order?
      `that application is finally disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that application been finally disposed of?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 6(5), may the award be enforced` IS
    `o 48 r 6(5) the award may be enforced` `the date I am asking about` `the last day for the debtor to apply, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` `the debtor applied within that period` `that application is finally disposed of`

@export Under Order 48, rule 6(6), does the copy of the order I serve on the debtor state the effect of paragraph (5)?
GIVEN `it is the copy served on the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the copy of the order that is served on the debtor?
      `it states the effect of Rule 6(5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the effect of Order 48, Rule 6(5) (that the debtor may apply within the period and that the award may not be enforced before it ends)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 48, rule 6(6), does the copy served state the effect of paragraph (5)` IS
    `o 48 r 6(6) the copy served states the effect of paragraph (5) as it must` `it is the copy served on the debtor` `it states the effect of Rule 6(5)`

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 49 -- Land Titles (Strata) Act: I am a party to a collective sale application`
-- This group arises only if the proceedings are an application to the General Division for a collective sale order under section 84A(1), 84D(2), 84E(3) or 84FA(2) of the Land Titles (Strata) Act after a stop order: ask "Does this apply to you?" before showing it.
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Rule 2 -- Starting the application (O. 49, r. 2)`

@export Under Order 49, rule 2(1), must a collective sale application be made by originating application?
GIVEN `the provision of the Act my application is made under` IS A `o 49 r 1 the provision of the Act under which an application is made` @desc Under which provision of the Land Titles (Strata) Act is the application made? One of: section 84A(1) (sale of all the lots and common property in a strata title plan); section 84D(2) (sale of all the flats and the land in a development); section 84E(3) (sale of all the flats and the land in a development); section 84FA(2) (sale of all the lots and common property in a plan to which section 84FA applies); another provision
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 49, rule 2(1), must my application be made by originating application` IS
    `o 49 r 2(1) the application must be made by originating application` `the provision of the Act my application is made under`

@export Under Order 49, rule 2(1), have I made my application by originating application, as I must?
