      `I wish to adduce evidence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you wish to adduce evidence with reference to the originating application?
      `my evidence is adduced by affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your evidence adduced by affidavit?
      `the date I filed it and served a copy on the claimants` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you file the affidavit and serve a copy on the claimants?
      `the last day for doing it, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day: 21 days after the claimants served you with a copy of their affidavits (the period begins the day after service; if the last day falls on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, take the next court day)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 49, rule 5(1), have I adduced my objecting evidence by affidavit in time` IS
    `o 49 r 5(1) the objecting evidence has been adduced by affidavit filed and served in time` `I intend to object to the application` `I wish to adduce evidence` `my evidence is adduced by affidavit` `the date I filed it and served a copy on the claimants` `the last day for doing it, counted under Order 3, Rule 3`

@export Under Order 49, rule 5(2), am I barred from putting in a further affidavit without the Court's permission?
GIVEN `the General Division has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division given permission to receive a further affidavit in evidence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 49, rule 5(2), is a further affidavit barred` IS
    `o 49 r 5(2) a further affidavit is barred from being received in evidence` `the General Division has given permission`

@export Under Order 49, rule 5(2), may a further affidavit be received in evidence?
GIVEN `the General Division has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division given permission to receive a further affidavit in evidence?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 49, rule 5(2), may a further affidavit be received in evidence` IS
    `o 49 r 5(2) a further affidavit may be received in evidence` `the General Division has given permission`

§§ `Rule 6 -- Disputing the Court's jurisdiction (O. 49, r. 6)`

@export Under Order 49, rule 6(1), within how many days of service must a defendant who disputes the Court's jurisdiction apply?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 49, rule 6(1), within how many days of service must a defendant apply` IS
    `o 49 r 6(1) the period after service of the originating application and affidavits`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 49, rule 6(1), must I apply for a relief because I wish to dispute the Court's jurisdiction?
GIVEN `I wish to dispute the jurisdiction of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, as a defendant, wish to dispute the jurisdiction of the General Division in the proceedings (for an irregularity in the originating application or its service, an irregularity in an order for service out of Singapore or extending validity, or any other ground)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 49, rule 6(1), must I apply for a relief` IS
    `o 49 r 6(1) the duty to apply for a relief in paragraph (2) arises` `I wish to dispute the jurisdiction of the General Division`

@export Under Order 49, rule 6(1), did I apply for a relief in time?
GIVEN `I wish to dispute the jurisdiction of the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you, as a defendant, wish to dispute the jurisdiction of the General Division in the proceedings (for an irregularity in the originating application or its service, an irregularity in an order for service out of Singapore or extending validity, or any other ground)?
      `the date I applied to the General Division` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you apply to the General Division?
      `the last day for applying, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day: 21 days after the originating application and supporting affidavit or affidavits were served on you under Rule 4(1) (the period begins the day after service; if the last day falls on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, take the next court day)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 49, rule 6(1), did I apply for a relief in time` IS
    `o 49 r 6(1) the defendant has applied for a relief in paragraph (2) in time` `I wish to dispute the jurisdiction of the General Division` `the date I applied to the General Division` `the last day for applying, counted under Order 3, Rule 3`

@export Under Order 49, rule 6(2), is the relief I want one the Rules mention?
GIVEN `the relief I want` IS A `o 49 r 6(2) the relief` @desc Which relief do you want? One of: setting aside the originating application or service of it; a declaration that it was not duly served; discharge of an order for service out of Singapore; discharge of an order extending validity for service; protection or release of property seized or threatened with seizure; discharge of an order preventing dealing with property; a declaration that the Court has no jurisdiction over you; such other relief as may be appropriate
      `the other relief is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you want some other relief: is it appropriate? (Any answer if you want one of the others.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 49, rule 6(2), is the relief I want one the Rules mention` IS
    `o 49 r 6(2) the relief is one mentioned in paragraph (1)` `the relief I want` `the other relief is appropriate`

@export Under Order 49, rule 6(3), have I made my jurisdiction application by summons with a verifying affidavit served with it?
GIVEN `it is an application under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application under Order 49, Rule 6(1)?
      `the document I used` IS A `Document kind` @desc What document did you use to make the application? One of: Originating claim, Originating application, Statement of claim, Defence, Defence and counterclaim, Reply, Reply to a defence and counterclaim, Summons, Summons without notice, Affidavit, Notice of intention to contest or not contest, Notice of appeal
      `it is supported by an affidavit verifying the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it supported by an affidavit verifying the facts on which the application is based?
      `a copy of the affidavit is served with the summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a copy of the affidavit served with the summons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 49, rule 6(3), have I made my application as I must` IS
    `o 49 r 6(3) the application is made by summons supported by an affidavit as it must be` `it is an application under paragraph (1)` `the document I used` `it is supported by an affidavit verifying the facts` `a copy of the affidavit is served with the summons`

@export Under Order 49, rule 6(4), may the Court make such order and give such directions as it thinks fit at the hearing of my jurisdiction application?
GIVEN `my application under paragraph (1) is being heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application under Order 49, Rule 6(1) being heard?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 49, rule 6(4), may the Court make such order and give such directions as it thinks fit` IS
    `o 49 r 6(4) the Court may make such order and give such directions as it thinks fit` `my application under paragraph (1) is being heard`

§§ `Rule 7 -- Directions at the first case conference (O. 49, r. 7)`

@export Under Order 49, rule 7, may the Court give directions at the first case conference on my collective sale application?
GIVEN `it is the first case conference in respect of an originating application to which Order 49 relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the first case conference in respect of an originating application to which Order 49 relates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 49, rule 7, may the Court give directions at the first case conference` IS
    `o 49 r 7 the Court may by order give such directions as to the proceedings to be taken as it thinks fit` `it is the first case conference in respect of an originating application to which Order 49 relates`

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 50 -- Limited Liability Partnerships Act: I am a party to an application under that Act`
-- This group arises only if the proceedings are an application under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act: ask "Does this apply to you?" before showing it.
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Rules 2 to 5 -- My application under the Act (O. 50, rr. 2 to 5)`

@export Under Order 50, rule 2, does Order 56 apply to my limited liability partnership?
GIVEN `the partnership is a limited liability partnership registered under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the partnership a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 50, rule 2, does Order 56 apply to my partnership` IS
    `o 50 r 2 Order 56 applies to the partnership` `the partnership is a limited liability partnership registered under the Act`

@export Under Order 50, rule 3(1), must my application under the Act be made by originating application?
GIVEN `it is an application under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act?
      `the Act or Order 50 provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act, or Order 50, provide that the application is to be made some other way?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 50, rule 3(1), must my application be made by originating application` IS
    `o 50 r 3(1) the application must be made by originating application` `it is an application under the Act` `the Act or Order 50 provides otherwise`

@export Under Order 50, rule 3(1), have I made my application by originating application, as I must?
GIVEN `it is an application under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act?
      `the Act or Order 50 provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Act, or Order 50, provide that the application is to be made some other way?
      `the document I used` IS A `Document kind` @desc What document did you use to make the application? One of: Originating claim, Originating application, Statement of claim, Defence, Defence and counterclaim, Reply, Reply to a defence and counterclaim, Summons, Summons without notice, Affidavit, Notice of intention to contest or not contest, Notice of appeal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 50, rule 3(1), have I made my application by originating application as I must` IS
    `o 50 r 3(1) the application is made by originating application as it must be` `it is an application under the Act` `the Act or Order 50 provides otherwise` `the document I used`

@export Under Order 50, rule 3(2), may the Court order my winding up application to continue as if it had been begun by originating claim?
GIVEN `it is a winding up originating application presented under paragraph 3(1)(e) of the Fifth Schedule to the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a winding up originating application presented under paragraph 3(1)(e) of the Fifth Schedule to the Limited Liability Partnerships Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 50, rule 3(2), may the Court order my application to continue as if begun by originating claim` IS
    `o 50 r 3(2) the Court may order the proceedings to continue as if begun by originating claim` `it is a winding up originating application presented under paragraph 3(1)(e) of the Fifth Schedule to the Act`

@export Under Order 50, rule 3(2), may the Court make this order in my winding up application?
GIVEN `the order` IS A `o 50 r 3(2) the particular order` @desc What order is in question? One of: that pleadings be delivered or that the originating application or any affidavits stand as pleadings; that any persons be added as parties; that Order 9 applies with the necessary modifications; another order
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 50, rule 3(2), may the Court make this order` IS
    `o 50 r 3(2) the Court may order that` `the order`

@export Under Order 50, rule 4(1), is my document entitled as it must be?
GIVEN `it is an originating application to which Order 50 relates or an affidavit, notice or other document in those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an originating application to which Order 50 relates, or an affidavit, notice or other document in those proceedings?
      `it is entitled in the matter of the limited liability partnership in question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it entitled in the matter of the limited liability partnership in question?
      `it is entitled in the matter of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it entitled in the matter of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 50, rule 4(1), is my document entitled as it must be` IS
    `o 50 r 4(1) the document is entitled as it must be` `it is an originating application to which Order 50 relates or an affidavit, notice or other document in those proceedings` `it is entitled in the matter of the limited liability partnership in question` `it is entitled in the matter of the Act`

@export Under Order 50, rule 4(2), is my originating application for permission under section 36 entitled as it must be?
GIVEN `it is the originating application by which an application for permission under section 36 is made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the originating application by which an application for permission under section 36 of the Act is made?
      `it is entitled in the matter of the limited liability partnership of my conviction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it entitled in the matter of the limited liability partnership (if any) in relation to which you were convicted?
      `it is entitled in the matter of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it entitled in the matter of the Limited Liability Partnerships Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 50, rule 4(2), is my originating application entitled as it must be` IS
    `o 50 r 4(2) the originating application for permission under section 36 is entitled as it must be` `it is the originating application by which an application for permission under section 36 is made` `it is entitled in the matter of the limited liability partnership of my conviction` `it is entitled in the matter of the Act`

@export Under Order 50, rule 5, may the Court give directions at the first case conference on my application?
GIVEN `it is the first case conference in respect of an originating application to which Order 50 relates` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the first case conference in respect of an originating application to which Order 50 relates?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 50, rule 5, may the Court give directions at the first case conference` IS
    `o 50 r 5 the Court may by order give such direction as to the proceedings to be taken as it thinks fit` `it is the first case conference in respect of an originating application to which Order 50 relates`

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 51 -- Moneylenders' actions: I am a party to an action by or against a moneylender`
-- This group arises only if the action is a moneylender's action (an action for recovery of money lent by a moneylender, or enforcement of an agreement or security relating to it, brought by the lender or an assignee): ask "Does this apply to you?" before showing it.
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Rules 1 to 5 -- My moneylender's action (O. 51, rr. 1 to 5)`

@export Under Order 51, rule 1(2), is my action a moneylender's action?
GIVEN `it is an action for the recovery of money lent by a moneylender or for the enforcement of an agreement or security relating to it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an action for the recovery of money lent by a moneylender, or for the enforcement of an agreement or security relating to money so lent?
      `it is brought by the lender or an assignee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it brought by the lender or an assignee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 1(2), is my action a moneylender's action` IS
    `o 51 r 1(2) an action is a moneylender's action` `it is an action for the recovery of money lent by a moneylender or for the enforcement of an agreement or security relating to it` `it is brought by the lender or an assignee`

@export Under Order 51, rule 2, must I endorse my originating claim before it is issued?
GIVEN `it is an originating claim beginning a moneylender's action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an originating claim beginning a moneylender's action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 2, must I endorse my originating claim` IS
    `o 51 r 2 the duty to endorse the originating claim arises` `it is an originating claim beginning a moneylender's action`

@export Under Order 51, rule 2, have I endorsed my originating claim as I must?
GIVEN `it is an originating claim beginning a moneylender's action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an originating claim beginning a moneylender's action?
      `it was endorsed before issue with a statement that the lender was licensed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it endorsed, before it was issued, with a statement that at the time of making the loan or contract or giving the security the lender was licensed as a moneylender?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 2, have I endorsed my originating claim as I must` IS
    `o 51 r 2 the originating claim has been endorsed as it must be` `it is an originating claim beginning a moneylender's action` `it was endorsed before issue with a statement that the lender was licensed`

@export Under Order 51, rule 3, does my statement of claim state everything it must?
GIVEN `it is a statement of claim in a moneylender's action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a statement of claim in a moneylender's action (whether endorsed on the originating claim or not)?
      `the date on which the loan was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Does the statement of claim state the date on which the loan was made?
      `the amount actually lent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Does it state the amount actually lent to the borrower?
      `the rate of interest per annum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Does it state the rate per cent per annum of interest charged?
      `the date of the contract for repayment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (d) Does it state the date when the contract for repayment was made?
      `that a note or memorandum was made and signed by the borrower` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (e) Does it state that a note or memorandum of the contract was made and was signed by the borrower?
      `the date a copy of the note or memorandum was delivered or sent to the borrower` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (f) Does it state the date when a copy of the note or memorandum was delivered or sent to the borrower?
      `the amount repaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (g) Does it state the amount repaid?
      `the amount due but unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (h) Does it state the amount due but unpaid?
      `the date the unpaid sum or sums became due` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (i) Does it state the date upon which such unpaid sum or sums became due?
      `the interest accrued due and unpaid on every such sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (j) Does it state the amount of interest accrued due and unpaid on every such sum?
      `the form in which the money was lent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (k) Does it state the form in which the money was lent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 3, does my statement of claim state everything it must` IS
    `o 51 r 3 the statement of claim states what it must` `it is a statement of claim in a moneylender's action` (`o 51 r 3 what the statement of claim states` OF `the date on which the loan was made`, `the amount actually lent`, `the rate of interest per annum`, `the date of the contract for repayment`, `that a note or memorandum was made and signed by the borrower`, `the date a copy of the note or memorandum was delivered or sent to the borrower`, `the amount repaid`, `the amount due but unpaid`, `the date the unpaid sum or sums became due`, `the interest accrued due and unpaid on every such sum`, `the form in which the money was lent`)

@export Under Order 51, rule 4(1), am I barred from entering judgment in default without the Court's permission?
GIVEN `it is a moneylender's action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a moneylender's action?
      `the judgment is in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest or in default of defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judgment sought in default of a notice of intention to contest or not contest, or in default of a defence?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given permission to enter the judgment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 4(1), am I barred from entering judgment in default` IS
    `o 51 r 4(1) entry of the judgment in default is barred` `it is a moneylender's action` `the judgment is in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest or in default of defence` `the Court has given permission`

@export Under Order 51, rule 4(1), may judgment in default be entered?
GIVEN `it is a moneylender's action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a moneylender's action?
      `the judgment is in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest or in default of defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judgment sought in default of a notice of intention to contest or not contest, or in default of a defence?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given permission to enter the judgment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 4(1), may the judgment in default be entered` IS
    `o 51 r 4(1) the judgment in default may be entered` `it is a moneylender's action` `the judgment is in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest or in default of defence` `the Court has given permission`

@export Under Order 51, rule 4(2), have I made my application for permission by summons, as I must?
GIVEN `it is an application for permission under Rule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for permission under Order 51, Rule 4?
      `the document I used` IS A `Document kind` @desc What document did you use? One of: Originating claim, Originating application, Statement of claim, Defence, Defence and counterclaim, Reply, Reply to a defence and counterclaim, Summons, Summons without notice, Affidavit, Notice of intention to contest or not contest, Notice of appeal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 4(2), have I made my application for permission by summons as I must` IS
    `o 51 r 4(2) the application for permission is made by summons as it must be` `it is an application for permission under Rule 4` `the document I used`

@export Under Order 51, rule 4(2), must I serve the summons on the defendant?
GIVEN `it is a summons on an application for permission under Rule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the summons on an application for permission under Order 51, Rule 4?
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that the summons need not be served on the defendant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 4(2), must I serve the summons on the defendant` IS
    `o 51 r 4(2) the duty to serve the summons on the defendant arises` `it is a summons on an application for permission under Rule 4` `the Court has otherwise ordered`

@export Under Order 51, rule 4(2), have I served the summons on the defendant, as I must?
GIVEN `it is a summons on an application for permission under Rule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the summons on an application for permission under Order 51, Rule 4?
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that the summons need not be served on the defendant?
      `the summons has been served on the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the summons been served on the defendant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 4(2), have I served the summons on the defendant as I must` IS
    `o 51 r 4(2) the summons has been served on the defendant as it must be` `it is a summons on an application for permission under Rule 4` `the Court has otherwise ordered` `the summons has been served on the defendant`

@export Under Order 51, rule 4(3), is issue of the summons barred at present?
GIVEN `the application is for permission to enter judgment in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for permission to enter judgment in default of a notice of intention to contest or not contest?
      `the date the summons is issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date is (or was) the summons issued?
      `the last day for the notice, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the time limited for filing and serving the notice of intention to contest or not contest (counted under Order 3, Rule 3, from the Order that fixes that time)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 4(3), is issue of the summons barred` IS
    `o 51 r 4(3) issue of the summons is barred` `the application is for permission to enter judgment in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest` `the date the summons is issued` `the last day for the notice, counted under Order 3, Rule 3`

@export Under Order 51, rule 4(3), may the summons be issued?
GIVEN `the application is for permission to enter judgment in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for permission to enter judgment in default of a notice of intention to contest or not contest?
      `the date the summons is issued` IS A DATE @desc On what date is (or was) the summons issued?
      `the last day for the notice, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the time limited for filing and serving the notice of intention to contest or not contest (counted under Order 3, Rule 3, from the Order that fixes that time)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 4(3), may the summons be issued` IS
    `o 51 r 4(3) the summons may be issued` `the application is for permission to enter judgment in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest` `the date the summons is issued` `the last day for the notice, counted under Order 3, Rule 3`

@export Under Order 51, rule 4(4), does it matter whether the defendant appears at the hearing of my application for permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 4(4), does the defendant's appearance matter` IS
    `o 51 r 4(4) the defendant's appearance at the hearing affects the Court's powers`

@export Under Order 51, rule 4(4)(a), may the Court exercise its powers under section 23 of the Moneylenders Act at the hearing?
GIVEN `the application for permission is being heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for permission being heard?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 4(4)(a), may the Court exercise its powers under section 23` IS
    `o 51 r 4(4)(a) the Court may exercise the powers of the Court under section 23 of the Moneylenders Act` `the application for permission is being heard`

@export Under Order 51, rule 4(4)(b), if the Court refuses permission, may it make the orders it might have made under Order 9, Rule 17(1)?
GIVEN `the application for permission is being heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application for permission being heard?
      `the Court refuses permission to enter judgment on a claim or any part of a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Court refuse permission to enter judgment on a claim or any part of a claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 4(4)(b), may the Court make the orders it might under Order 9 Rule 17(1)` IS
    `o 51 r 4(4)(b) the Court may make or give any order or directions it might have made on an application under Order 9, Rule 17(1)` `the application for permission is being heard` `the Court refuses permission to enter judgment on a claim or any part of a claim`

@export Under Order 51, rule 5, must the supporting affidavit of my originating application contain the matters in Rules 2 and 3?
GIVEN `my moneylender's action is begun by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your moneylender's action begun by originating application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 5, must my supporting affidavit contain the matters in Rules 2 and 3` IS
    `o 51 r 5 the duty to put the matters in Rules 2 and 3 in the supporting affidavit arises` `my moneylender's action is begun by originating application`

@export Under Order 51, rule 5, does my supporting affidavit contain the statement, as it must?
GIVEN `my moneylender's action is begun by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your moneylender's action begun by originating application?
      `it contains a statement of the matters specified in Rules 2 and 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the supporting affidavit contain a statement of the matters specified in Order 51, Rules 2 and 3?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 51, rule 5, does my supporting affidavit contain the statement as it must` IS
    `o 51 r 5 the supporting affidavit contains the statement as it must` `my moneylender's action is begun by originating application` `it contains a statement of the matters specified in Rules 2 and 3`

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 52 -- Mortgage actions: I am a party to an action about a mortgage`
-- This group arises only if the action is by a mortgagee or mortgagor (or a person with the right to foreclose or redeem) and claims one of the reliefs in Order 52, Rule 1(1): ask "Does this apply to you?" before showing it.
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Rules 1 to 5 -- My mortgage action (O. 52, rr. 1 to 5)`

@export Under Order 52, rule 1(1), does Order 52 apply to my action?
GIVEN `the action is by a mortgagee or mortgagor or by a person having the right to foreclose or redeem a mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action by a mortgagee or mortgagor, or by a person having the right to foreclose or redeem a mortgage?
      `payment of moneys secured by the mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (a) Do you claim payment of moneys secured by the mortgage?
      `sale of the mortgaged property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (b) Do you claim sale of the mortgaged property?
      `foreclosure` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (c) Do you claim foreclosure?
      `delivery of possession to the mortgagee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (d) Do you claim delivery of possession to the mortgagee by the mortgagor or by any other person who is or is alleged to be in possession?
      `redemption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (e) Do you claim redemption?
      `reconveyance or release from the security` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (f) Do you claim reconveyance of the property or its release from the security?
      `delivery of possession by the mortgagee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (g) Do you claim delivery of possession by the mortgagee?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 1(1), does Order 52 apply to my action` IS
    `o 52 r 1(1) this Order applies to the action` `the action is by a mortgagee or mortgagor or by a person having the right to foreclose or redeem a mortgage` (`o 52 r 1(1) the reliefs claimed` OF `payment of moneys secured by the mortgage`, `sale of the mortgaged property`, `foreclosure`, `delivery of possession to the mortgagee`, `redemption`, `reconveyance or release from the security`, `delivery of possession by the mortgagee`)

@export Under Order 52, rule 1(2), is my security a mortgage for the purposes of Order 52?
GIVEN `the kind of security` IS A `o 52 r 1(2) the kind of security` @desc What kind of security is it? One of: a legal mortgage; an equitable mortgage; a legal charge; an equitable charge; another kind of security
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 1(2), is my security a mortgage` IS
    `o 52 r 1(2) a security is a mortgage` `the kind of security`

@export Under Order 52, rule 1(4), do the Rules of Court apply to my mortgage action, subject to Order 52?
GIVEN `the action is a mortgage action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action a mortgage action (an action to which Order 52 applies)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 1(4), do the Rules apply to my mortgage action` IS
    `o 52 r 1(4) these Rules apply to the action subject to the following provisions of this Order` `the action is a mortgage action`

@export Under Order 52, rule 2(1), do the provisions of Order 52, Rule 2 on claims for possession apply to my action?
GIVEN `the action is a mortgage action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action a mortgage action?
      `the document I used` IS A `Document kind` @desc What document did you use? One of: Originating claim, Originating application, Statement of claim, Defence, Defence and counterclaim, Reply, Reply to a defence and counterclaim, Summons, Summons without notice, Affidavit, Notice of intention to contest or not contest, Notice of appeal
      `the claimant is the mortgagee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claimant the mortgagee?
      `the claimant claims delivery of possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the claimant claim delivery of possession?
      `the claimant claims payment of moneys secured by the mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the claimant claim payment of moneys secured by the mortgage?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 2(1), do the provisions of Rule 2 apply to my action` IS
    `o 52 r 2(1) the provisions of this Rule apply` `the action is a mortgage action` `the document I used` `the claimant is the mortgagee` `the claimant claims delivery of possession` `the claimant claims payment of moneys secured by the mortgage`

@export Under Order 52, rule 2(2), must I endorse a notice on the outside fold of the affidavit I serve on the defendant?
GIVEN `the provisions of Rule 2 apply to my action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the provisions of Order 52, Rule 2 apply to your action (see the question on Rule 2(1))?
      `the claimant claims delivery of possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the claimant claim delivery of possession?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 2(2), must I endorse a notice on the affidavit` IS
    `o 52 r 2(2) the duty to endorse a notice on the affidavit arises` `the provisions of Rule 2 apply to my action` `the claimant claims delivery of possession`

@export Under Order 52, rule 2(2), have I endorsed the notice on the affidavit as I must?
GIVEN `the provisions of Rule 2 apply to my action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the provisions of Order 52, Rule 2 apply to your action (see the question on Rule 2(1))?
      `the claimant claims delivery of possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the claimant claim delivery of possession?
      `a notice is endorsed on the outside fold of the copy served on the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a notice endorsed on the outside fold of the copy of the affidavit served on the defendant?
      `the notice informs the defendant of the order and other relief the claimant intends to apply for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice inform the defendant that the claimant intends at the hearing to apply for an order that the defendant deliver up possession of the mortgaged property, and for such other relief (if any) claimed by the originating application as the claimant intends to apply for?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 2(2), have I endorsed the notice on the affidavit as I must` IS
    `o 52 r 2(2) the notice has been endorsed as it must be` `the provisions of Rule 2 apply to my action` `the claimant claims delivery of possession` `a notice is endorsed on the outside fold of the copy served on the defendant` `the notice informs the defendant of the order and other relief the claimant intends to apply for`

@export Under Order 52, rule 2(3), must I serve a written notice of the adjourned hearing on the defendant?
GIVEN `the provisions of Rule 2 apply to my action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the provisions of Order 52, Rule 2 apply to your action?
      `the hearing is adjourned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the hearing adjourned?
      `the defendant was absent from the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the defendant absent from the hearing?
      `the Court has given directions on the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given directions on the notice of the adjourned hearing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 2(3), must I serve a written notice of the adjourned hearing` IS
    `o 52 r 2(3) the duty to serve a written notice of the adjourned hearing arises` `the provisions of Rule 2 apply to my action` `the hearing is adjourned` `the defendant was absent from the hearing` `the Court has given directions on the notice`

@export Under Order 52, rule 2(3), did I serve the notice of the adjourned hearing in time?
GIVEN `the provisions of Rule 2 apply to my action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the provisions of Order 52, Rule 2 apply to your action?
      `the hearing is adjourned` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the hearing adjourned?
      `the defendant was absent from the hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the defendant absent from the hearing?
      `the Court has given directions on the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given directions on the notice of the adjourned hearing?
      `the date I served the notice and any further affidavit` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the written notice of the adjourned hearing and a copy of any further affidavit on the defendant?
      `the last day for serving, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day: 2 clear days before the day fixed for the hearing (a clear day excludes both the day of service and the day fixed; if the last day falls on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, take the next court day)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 2(3), did I serve the notice of the adjourned hearing in time` IS
    `o 52 r 2(3) the written notice has been served in time` `the provisions of Rule 2 apply to my action` `the hearing is adjourned` `the defendant was absent from the hearing` `the Court has given directions on the notice` `the date I served the notice and any further affidavit` `the last day for serving, counted under Order 3, Rule 3`

@export Under Order 52, rule 2(4), is the copy of the further affidavit endorsed as it must be?
GIVEN `it is a copy of an affidavit served under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a copy of an affidavit served under Order 52, Rule 2(3)?
      `it is endorsed in accordance with paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it endorsed in accordance with Order 52, Rule 2(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 2(4), is the copy of the affidavit endorsed as it must be` IS
    `o 52 r 2(4) the copy of the affidavit is endorsed as it must be` `it is a copy of an affidavit served under paragraph (3)` `it is endorsed in accordance with paragraph (2)`

@export Under Order 52, rule 2(5), may I prove service by a certificate signed by this person?
GIVEN `the claimant sues in person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the claimant sue in person?
      `who signed the certificate` IS A `o 52 r 2(5) who signed the certificate` @desc Who signed the certificate? One of: the claimant; the claimant's solicitor; someone else
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 2(5), may service be proved by this certificate` IS
    `o 52 r 2(5) service may be proved by the certificate` `the claimant sues in person` `who signed the certificate`

@export Under Order 52, rule 3(2), does the Rule on the supporting affidavit apply to my action?
GIVEN `the action is a mortgage action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action a mortgage action?
      `the document I used` IS A `Document kind` @desc What document did you use? One of: Originating claim, Originating application, Statement of claim, Defence, Defence and counterclaim, Reply, Reply to a defence and counterclaim, Summons, Summons without notice, Affidavit, Notice of intention to contest or not contest, Notice of appeal
      `the claimant is the mortgagee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claimant the mortgagee?
      `the claimant claims delivery of possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the claimant claim delivery of possession?
      `the claimant claims payment of moneys secured by the mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the claimant claim payment of moneys secured by the mortgage?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 3(2), does Rule 3 apply to my action` IS
    `o 52 r 3(2) this Rule applies to the action` `the action is a mortgage action` `the document I used` `the claimant is the mortgagee` `the claimant claims delivery of possession` `the claimant claims payment of moneys secured by the mortgage`

@export Under Order 52, rule 3, does my supporting affidavit contain everything the Rule requires?
GIVEN `Rule 3 applies to my action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Order 52, Rule 3 apply to your action (see the question on Rule 3(2))?
      `the claimant claims delivery of possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the claimant claim delivery of possession?
      `the claimant claims payment of moneys secured by the mortgage` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the claimant claim payment of moneys secured by the mortgage?
      `the mortgage creates a tenancy other than a tenancy at will` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the mortgage create a tenancy other than a tenancy at will between the mortgagor and mortgagee?
      `the Court has otherwise directed as to the state of the account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court, in the case or class, otherwise directed as to the state of the account?
      `a true copy of the mortgage is exhibited` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (r 3(3)) Does the affidavit exhibit a true copy of the mortgage?
      `the circumstances under which the right to possession arises are shown` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (r 3(4)) Does it show the circumstances under which the right to possession arises?
      `particulars of instalments in arrears` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (r 3(4)(a)) Does it give particulars of the amount and number of any instalments in arrears at the date of issue of the originating application and at the date of the affidavit?
      `particulars of the amount remaining due` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (r 3(4)(b)) Does it give particulars of the amount remaining due under the mortgage?
      `particulars of every person known to be in possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (r 3(5)) Does it give particulars of every person who, to the best of the claimant's knowledge, is in possession of the mortgaged property?
      `how and when the tenancy was determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (r 3(6)) Does it show how and when the tenancy was determined and, if by service of notice, when the notice was duly served?
      `it proves that the money is due and payable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc (r 3(7)) Does it prove that the money is due and payable?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 3, does my supporting affidavit contain everything the Rule requires` IS
    `o 52 r 3(1) the supporting affidavit complies with this Rule` `Rule 3 applies to my action` `the claimant claims delivery of possession` `the claimant claims payment of moneys secured by the mortgage` `the mortgage creates a tenancy other than a tenancy at will` `the Court has otherwise directed as to the state of the account` (`o 52 r 3 what the affidavit contains` OF `a true copy of the mortgage is exhibited`, `the circumstances under which the right to possession arises are shown`, `particulars of instalments in arrears`, `particulars of the amount remaining due`, `particulars of every person known to be in possession`, `how and when the tenancy was determined`, `it proves that the money is due and payable`)

@export Under Order 52, rule 4(1), do Order 6, Rules 6(5) and 7(7) let me enter judgment in default without permission in my mortgage action?
GIVEN `it is a mortgage action begun by originating claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a mortgage action begun by originating claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 4(1), do Order 6 Rules 6(5) and 7(7) let me enter judgment in default without permission` IS
    `o 52 r 4(1) Order 6, Rules 6(5) and 7(7) allow judgment in default without permission in the action` `it is a mortgage action begun by originating claim`

@export Under Order 52, rule 4(1), am I barred from entering judgment in default without the Court's permission?
GIVEN `it is a mortgage action begun by originating claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a mortgage action begun by originating claim?
      `the judgment is in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest or in default of defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judgment sought in default of a notice of intention to contest or not contest, or in default of a defence?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given permission to enter the judgment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 4(1), am I barred from entering judgment in default` IS
    `o 52 r 4(1) entry of the judgment in default is barred` `it is a mortgage action begun by originating claim` `the judgment is in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest or in default of defence` `the Court has given permission`

@export Under Order 52, rule 4(1), may judgment in default be entered?
GIVEN `it is a mortgage action begun by originating claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a mortgage action begun by originating claim?
      `the judgment is in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest or in default of defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judgment sought in default of a notice of intention to contest or not contest, or in default of a defence?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given permission to enter the judgment?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 4(1), may the judgment in default be entered` IS
    `o 52 r 4(1) the judgment in default may be entered` `it is a mortgage action begun by originating claim` `the judgment is in default of notice of intention to contest or not contest or in default of defence` `the Court has given permission`

@export Under Order 52, rule 4(2), have I made my application for permission by summons, as I must?
GIVEN `it is an application for permission under Rule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for permission under Order 52, Rule 4?
      `the document I used` IS A `Document kind` @desc What document did you use? One of: Originating claim, Originating application, Statement of claim, Defence, Defence and counterclaim, Reply, Reply to a defence and counterclaim, Summons, Summons without notice, Affidavit, Notice of intention to contest or not contest, Notice of appeal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 4(2), have I made my application for permission by summons as I must` IS
    `o 52 r 4(2) the application for permission is made by summons as it must be` `it is an application for permission under Rule 4` `the document I used`

@export Under Order 52, rule 4(2), within how many clear days before the hearing must I serve the summons on the defendant?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 4(2), how many clear days before the hearing must the summons be served` IS
    `o 52 r 4(2) the period before the hearing of the summons`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 52, rule 4(2), must I serve the summons on the defendant?
GIVEN `it is a summons on an application for permission under Rule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the summons on an application for permission under Order 52, Rule 4?
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that the summons need not be served on the defendant at least 4 clear days before the hearing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 4(2), must I serve the summons on the defendant` IS
    `o 52 r 4(2) the duty to serve the summons on the defendant arises` `it is a summons on an application for permission under Rule 4` `the Court has otherwise ordered`

@export Under Order 52, rule 4(2), did I serve the summons on the defendant in time?
GIVEN `it is a summons on an application for permission under Rule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the summons on an application for permission under Order 52, Rule 4?
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that the summons need not be served on the defendant at least 4 clear days before the hearing?
      `the date I served the summons on the defendant` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the summons on the defendant?
      `the last day for serving, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day: 4 clear days before the hearing of the summons (a clear day excludes both the day of service and the day of the hearing; if the last day falls on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, take the next court day)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 4(2), did I serve the summons in time` IS
    `o 52 r 4(2) the summons has been served in time` `it is a summons on an application for permission under Rule 4` `the Court has otherwise ordered` `the date I served the summons on the defendant` `the last day for serving, counted under Order 3, Rule 3`

@export Under Order 52, rule 4(3), do Rule 2(2) to (5) apply to my action once a summons for permission is issued?
GIVEN `a summons for permission under Rule 4 is issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a summons for permission under Order 52, Rule 4 issued?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 4(3), do Rule 2(2) to (5) apply with the summons in place of the originating application` IS
    `o 52 r 4(3) Rule 2(2), (3), (4) and (5) applies in relation to the action with the summons in place of the originating application` `a summons for permission under Rule 4 is issued`

@export Under Order 52, rule 4(4), must the affidavit in support of my summons contain the information Rule 3 requires?
GIVEN `a summons for permission under Rule 4 is issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a summons for permission under Order 52, Rule 4 issued?
      `Rule 3 would apply had the action been begun by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would Order 52, Rule 3 apply had the action been begun by originating application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 4(4), must the affidavit in support contain the information Rule 3 requires` IS
    `o 52 r 4(4) the duty to put the information required by Rule 3 in the affidavit in support arises` `a summons for permission under Rule 4 is issued` `Rule 3 would apply had the action been begun by originating application`

@export Under Order 52, rule 4(4), does the affidavit in support of my summons contain the information, as it must?
GIVEN `a summons for permission under Rule 4 is issued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a summons for permission under Order 52, Rule 4 issued?
      `Rule 3 would apply had the action been begun by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would Order 52, Rule 3 apply had the action been begun by originating application?
      `the affidavit in support contains the information required by Rule 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit in support of the summons contain the information required by Order 52, Rule 3?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 4(4), does the affidavit in support contain the information as it must` IS
    `o 52 r 4(4) the affidavit in support contains the information as it must` `a summons for permission under Rule 4 is issued` `Rule 3 would apply had the action been begun by originating application` `the affidavit in support contains the information required by Rule 3`

@export Under Order 52, rule 5, may I, as defendant, apply by summons for delivery of possession after foreclosure in my favour?
GIVEN `foreclosure has taken place by reason of the claimant's failure to redeem` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has foreclosure taken place by reason of the failure of the claimant in a mortgage action for redemption to redeem?
      `the foreclosure has taken place in favour of the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the foreclosure taken place in favour of the defendant (you)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 5, may I apply by summons for delivery of possession` IS
    `o 52 r 5 the defendant may apply by summons for an order for delivery of possession` `foreclosure has taken place by reason of the claimant's failure to redeem` `the foreclosure has taken place in favour of the defendant`

@export Under Order 52, rule 5, may the Court make such order as it thinks fit on my application?
GIVEN `the defendant has applied by summons for an order for delivery of possession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the defendant applied by summons for an order for delivery of possession?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 52, rule 5, may the Court make such order as it thinks fit` IS
    `o 52 r 5 the Court may make such order on the application as it thinks fit` `the defendant has applied by summons for an order for delivery of possession`

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 53 -- Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act: I am affected by a proceeding under that Act`
-- This group arises only if the proceeding is under the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act (a production, restraint, charging or confiscation order, or foreign process, affecting you): ask "Does this apply to you?" before showing it.
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Rule 1 -- Interpretation and mode of application (O. 53, r. 1)`

@export Under Order 53, rule 1(1), is an instrument the Act?
GIVEN `the instrument is the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 1(1), is an instrument the Act` IS
    `o 53 r 1(1) an instrument is the Act` `the instrument is the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act`

@export Under Order 53, rule 1(1)(a), is a reference to a section a reference to a section in the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act?
GIVEN `the reference is a reference to a section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reference a reference to a section?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 1(1)(a), is a reference to a section a reference to a section in the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act` IS
    `o 53 r 1(1)(a) a reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Mutual Assistance in Criminal Matters Act` `the reference is a reference to a section`

@export Under Order 53, rule 1(1)(b), is a reference to the Third Schedule a reference to the Third Schedule to the Act?
GIVEN `the reference is a reference to the Third Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reference a reference to the Third Schedule?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 1(1)(b), is a reference to the Third Schedule a reference to the Third Schedule to the Act` IS
    `o 53 r 1(1)(b) a reference to the Third Schedule is a reference to the Third Schedule to the Act` `the reference is a reference to the Third Schedule`

@export Under Order 53, rule 1(2), does the expression have the same meaning in this Order as in the Act?
GIVEN `the expression is used in this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the expression used in this Order?
      `the expression is used in the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the expression used in the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 1(2), does the expression have the same meaning in this Order as in the Act` IS
    `o 53 r 1(2) the expression has the same meaning in this Order as in the Act` `the expression is used in this Order` `the expression is used in the Act`

@export Under Order 53, rule 1(3), is the application made by the document this paragraph requires?
GIVEN `it is an application to which this Order applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application to which this Order applies?
      `an action is pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an action pending?
      `the document I used` IS A `Document kind` @desc What document did you use? One of: Originating claim, Originating application, Statement of claim, Defence, Defence and counterclaim, Reply, Reply to a defence and counterclaim, Summons, Summons without notice, Affidavit, Notice of intention to contest or not contest, Notice of appeal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 1(3), is the application made by the document this paragraph requires` IS
    `o 53 r 1(3) the application is made by the document this paragraph requires` `it is an application to which this Order applies` `an action is pending` `the document I used`

§§ `Rule 2 -- Production orders (O. 53, r. 2)`

@export Under Order 53, rule 2(1), is the application supported by an affidavit as it must be?
GIVEN `it is an application for an order under section 22` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for an order under section 22?
      `it is supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it supported by an affidavit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 2(1), is the application supported by an affidavit as it must be` IS
    `o 53 r 2(1) the application is supported by an affidavit as it must be` `it is an application for an order under section 22` `it is supported by an affidavit`

@export Under Order 53, rule 2(1), may the application be made without notice?
GIVEN `it is an application for an order under section 22` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for an order under section 22?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 2(1), may the application be made without notice` IS
    `o 53 r 2(1) the application may be made without notice` `it is an application for an order under section 22`

@export Under Order 53, rule 2(2), may the Court discharge the order or vary it as it thinks fit?
GIVEN `an order under section 22 has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an order under section 22 been made?
      `the application is by the person required to comply with the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application by the person required to comply with the order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 2(2), may the Court discharge the order or vary it as it thinks fit` IS
    `o 53 r 2(2) the Court may discharge the order or vary it as it thinks fit` `an order under section 22 has been made` `the application is by the person required to comply with the order`

@export Under Order 53, rule 2(3), how many clear days before the filing of the application is the time limited?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 2(3), how many clear days before the filing of the application is the time limited` IS
    `o 53 r 2(3) the period before the filing of the application`'s `period length`

@export Under Order 53, rule 2(3), does the duty to serve a copy of the application arise?
GIVEN `a person proposes to file an application under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you propose to file an application under paragraph (2) to discharge or vary the order?
      `the Court has directed that paragraph (3) need not be complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court directed that paragraph (3) need not be complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 2(3), does the duty to serve a copy of the application arise` IS
    `o 53 r 2(3) the duty to serve a copy of the application arises` `a person proposes to file an application under paragraph (2)` `the Court has directed that paragraph (3) need not be complied with`

@export Under Order 53, rule 2(3), has the copy been served in time?
GIVEN `a person proposes to file an application under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you propose to file an application under paragraph (2) to discharge or vary the order?
      `the Court has directed that paragraph (3) need not be complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court directed that paragraph (3) need not be complied with?
      `the date the copy was served on the Attorney-General or the person who made the application for the order` IS A DATE @desc On what date was (or will) the copy be served on the Attorney-General or on the person who made the application for the order?
      `the last day for doing it, counted under Order 3, Rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing it: 2 clear days before the filing of the application (counted under Order 3, Rule 3: a clear day excludes both the day the act is done and the day fixed; if the time expires on a non-court day, take the next day that is not a non-court day)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 2(3), has the copy been served in time` IS
    `o 53 r 2(3) the copy has been served in time` `a person proposes to file an application under paragraph (2)` `the Court has directed that paragraph (3) need not be complied with` `the date the copy was served on the Attorney-General or the person who made the application for the order` `the last day for doing it, counted under Order 3, Rule 3`

@export Under Order 53, rule 2(4), may the Court direct that paragraph (3) need not be complied with?
GIVEN `the Court is satisfied that the person making the application has good reason to seek a discharge or variation as soon as possible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied that the person making the application has good reason to seek a discharge or variation as soon as possible?
      `it is not practicable to comply with paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it not practicable to comply with paragraph (3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 2(4), may the Court direct that paragraph (3) need not be complied with` IS
    `o 53 r 2(4) the Court may direct that paragraph (3) need not be complied with` `the Court is satisfied that the person making the application has good reason to seek a discharge or variation as soon as possible` `it is not practicable to comply with paragraph (3)`

§§ `Rule 3 -- Confidentiality of documents relating to production orders (O. 53, r. 3)`

