§§ `Rules 4 and 5 -- Registration of a foreign confiscation order (O. 53, rr. 4 and 5)`

@export Under Order 53, rule 4, may the application for registration be made without notice?
GIVEN `it is an application for registration of a foreign confiscation order under section 30(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for registration of a foreign confiscation order under section 30(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 4, may the application for registration be made without notice` IS
    `o 53 r 4 the application for registration may be made without notice` `it is an application for registration of a foreign confiscation order under section 30(1)`

@export Under Order 53, rule 5, is the supporting affidavit as it must be?
GIVEN `it is an application for registration of a foreign confiscation order under section 30(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for registration of a foreign confiscation order under section 30(1)?
      `the order is not in English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order not in English?
      `a person affected by the order did not appear in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did a person affected by the order not appear in the proceedings?
      `the order is in the case of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order one for the payment of money?
      `it exhibits the order or a duly authenticated copy within the meaning of section 31(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it exhibit the order or a duly authenticated copy within the meaning of section 31(2)?
      `it exhibits a duly translated copy of the order in English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it exhibit a duly translated copy of the order in English?
      `it states that the order is in force and is not subject to further appeal in the foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the order is in force and is not subject to further appeal in the foreign country?
      `it states that the person affected who did not appear received notice in sufficient time to enable that person to defend` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the person affected who did not appear received notice in sufficient time to enable that person to defend?
      `it states that the sum payable has not been paid or the amount which remains unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the sum payable has not been paid or the amount which remains unpaid?
      `it states the property which has not been recovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the property which has not been recovered?
      `it gives, to the best of the deponent's knowledge, particulars of the property believed to be in Singapore and the source of the knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give, to the best of the deponent's knowledge, particulars of the property believed to be in Singapore and the source of the knowledge?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 5, is the supporting affidavit as it must be` IS
    `o 53 r 5 the supporting affidavit is as it must be` `it is an application for registration of a foreign confiscation order under section 30(1)` `the order is not in English` `a person affected by the order did not appear in the proceedings` `the order is in the case of money` (`o 53 r 5 what the affidavit says` OF `it exhibits the order or a duly authenticated copy within the meaning of section 31(2)`, `it exhibits a duly translated copy of the order in English`, `it states that the order is in force and is not subject to further appeal in the foreign country`, `it states that the person affected who did not appear received notice in sufficient time to enable that person to defend`, `it states that the sum payable has not been paid or the amount which remains unpaid`, `it states the property which has not been recovered`, `it gives, to the best of the deponent's knowledge, particulars of the property believed to be in Singapore and the source of the knowledge`)

