§§ `Rule 11 -- Application for restraint order or charging order (O. 53, r. 11)`

@export Under Order 53, rule 11(1), is the application filed and served with a supporting affidavit as it must be?
GIVEN `it is an application for a restraint order under paragraph 7(1) of the Third Schedule or a charging order under paragraph 8(1) of that Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for a restraint order under paragraph 7(1) of the Third Schedule or a charging order under paragraph 8(1) of that Schedule?
      `it is filed and served with a supporting affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it filed and served with a supporting affidavit?
      `proceedings have been instituted in a prescribed foreign country and have not been concluded (where applicable)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have proceedings been instituted in a prescribed foreign country and not yet been concluded?
      `paragraph 6(2) of the Third Schedule applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does paragraph 6(2) of the Third Schedule apply?
      `it states that proceedings have been instituted in a prescribed foreign country and have not been concluded, and the grounds for believing that a foreign confiscation order may be made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that proceedings have been instituted in a prescribed foreign country and have not been concluded, and the grounds for believing that a foreign confiscation order may be made?
      `it contains full particulars of the property and specifies the persons holding it, as far as the deponent is able` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain full particulars of the property and specifies the persons holding it, as far as the deponent is able?
      `it indicates when it is intended that proceedings should be instituted in the prescribed foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it indicate when it is intended that proceedings should be instituted in the prescribed foreign country?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 11(1), is the application filed and served with a supporting affidavit as it must be` IS
    `o 53 r 11(1) the application is filed and served with a supporting affidavit as it must be` `it is an application for a restraint order under paragraph 7(1) of the Third Schedule or a charging order under paragraph 8(1) of that Schedule` `it is filed and served with a supporting affidavit` `proceedings have been instituted in a prescribed foreign country and have not been concluded (where applicable)` `paragraph 6(2) of the Third Schedule applies` (`o 53 r 11(1) what the supporting affidavit says` OF `it states that proceedings have been instituted in a prescribed foreign country and have not been concluded, and the grounds for believing that a foreign confiscation order may be made`, `it contains full particulars of the property and specifies the persons holding it, as far as the deponent is able`, `it indicates when it is intended that proceedings should be instituted in the prescribed foreign country`)

@export Under Order 53, rule 11(2), is the document entitled as it must be?
GIVEN `it is the originating application or a subsequent document in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the originating application or a subsequent document in the matter?
      `it is entitled in the matter of the defendant, naming the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it entitled in the matter of the defendant, naming the defendant?
      `it is entitled in the matter of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it entitled in the matter of the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 11(2), is the document entitled as it must be` IS
    `o 53 r 11(2) the document is entitled as it must be` `it is the originating application or a subsequent document in the matter` `it is entitled in the matter of the defendant, naming the defendant` `it is entitled in the matter of the Act`

@export Under Order 53, rule 11(3), may the supporting affidavit contain statements of information or belief?
GIVEN `the Court has otherwise directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court otherwise directed?
      `the statements give the sources and grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the statements give the sources and grounds?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 11(3), may the supporting affidavit contain statements of information or belief` IS
    `o 53 r 11(3) the supporting affidavit may contain statements of information or belief` `the Court has otherwise directed` `the statements give the sources and grounds`

§§ `Rule 12 -- Restraint order and charging order (O. 53, r. 12)`

@export Under Order 53, rule 12(1), may the restraint order be made subject to the condition or exception?
GIVEN `the condition or exception` IS A `o 53 r 12(1) the condition or exception` @desc What condition or exception is it? One of: a condition relating to the indemnifying of third parties against expenses incurred in complying with the order; an exception relating to the living expenses and legal expenses of the defendant; another condition or exception
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
