    `o 53 r 12(3) the copies have been served and the persons notified as required` `a restraint order has been made` `the Court has otherwise provided as to service` `copies of the order and supporting affidavit are served on the defendant and on all other named persons restrained` `all other persons or bodies affected by the order are notified of its terms`

@export Under Order 53, rule 12(4), does the duty to serve arise?
GIVEN `a charging order has been made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a charging order been made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 12(4), does the duty to serve arise` IS
    `o 53 r 12(4) the duty to serve arises` `a charging order has been made`

@export Under Order 53, rule 12(4), have the copies of the charging order been served as required?
