      `the Court has otherwise directed as to service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court otherwise directed as to how the order and affidavit are to be served?
      `the property to which the order relates is held by another person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the property to which the order relates held by another person?
      `copies of the order and supporting affidavit are served on the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are copies of the order and supporting affidavit served on the defendant?
      `copies are served on the other person holding the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are copies served on the other person holding the property?
      `a copy of the order is served on the Accountant-General or a company, as is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a copy of the order served on the Accountant-General or a company, as is appropriate?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 53, rule 12(4), have the copies of the charging order been served as required` IS
