§ `Order 54 -- Oaths and Declarations Act: I am taking an oath or making an affirmation`
-- This group arises only if an oath or affirmation is taken or made, and administered, for a court document such as an affidavit: ask "Does this apply to you?" before showing it.
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Rule 1 -- Application and definition of this Order (O. 54, r. 1)`

@export Under Order 54, rule 1(1), is an instrument the Act?
GIVEN `the instrument is the Oaths and Declarations Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument the Oaths and Declarations Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 54, rule 1(1), is an instrument the Act` IS
    `o 54 r 1(1) an instrument is the Act` `the instrument is the Oaths and Declarations Act`

@export Under Order 54, rule 1(1), does this Order apply?
GIVEN `an oath or affirmation is taken or made, and administered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an oath or affirmation taken or made, and administered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 54, rule 1(1), does this Order apply` IS
    `o 54 r 1(1) this Order applies` `an oath or affirmation is taken or made, and administered`

@export Under Order 54, rule 1(1), does Order 1, Rule 2 prevent this Order from applying?
GIVEN `an oath or affirmation is taken or made, and administered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an oath or affirmation taken or made, and administered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 54, rule 1(1), does Order 1, Rule 2 prevent this Order from applying` IS
    `o 54 r 1(1) Order 1, Rule 2 prevents this Order from applying` `an oath or affirmation is taken or made, and administered`

@export Under Order 54, rule 1(2), is the person an officer?
GIVEN `the place where the word is used` IS A `o 54 r 1(2) the place where the word is used` @desc In which Rule is the word “officer” used? One of: Rule 2, which is about oaths; Rule 3, which is about affirmations; Rule 4, which is about both; somewhere else
      `the person is duly authorised to administer oaths` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person duly authorised to administer oaths?
      `the person is duly authorised to administer affirmations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person duly authorised to administer affirmations?
      `the occasion is an oath` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the occasion an oath?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 54, rule 1(2), is the person an officer` IS
    `o 54 r 1(2) the person is an officer` `the place where the word is used` `the person is duly authorised to administer oaths` `the person is duly authorised to administer affirmations` `the occasion is an oath`

§§ `Rule 2 -- Forms and formalities of oaths (O. 54, r. 2)`

@export Under Order 54, rule 2(1), must the oath be taken and administered in the form and manner prescribed in Rule 2?
GIVEN `it is an oath under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an oath under the Act?
