§ `Order 55 -- Obtaining evidence for foreign courts: I am a witness or an applicant in a proceeding to obtain evidence for a court or tribunal outside Singapore`
-- This group arises only if the evidence is wanted for a matter pending before a court or tribunal in a place outside Singapore: ask "Does this apply to you?" before showing it.
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Rule 1 -- Jurisdiction of Registrar to make order (O. 55, r. 1)`

@export Under Order 55, rule 1(1), may the Registrar exercise the power to make the order?
GIVEN `the matter is pending before a court or tribunal in a place outside the jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter pending before a court or tribunal in a place outside the jurisdiction?
      `the matter in question is a criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter in question a criminal matter?
      `the kind of order` IS A `o 55 r 1(1) the kind of order` @desc What kind of order is it? One of: an order for the examination of witnesses; an order for attendance; an order for production of documents; a direction; another kind of order
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 55, rule 1(1), may the Registrar exercise the power to make the order` IS
    `o 55 r 1(1) the Registrar may exercise the power to make the order` `the matter is pending before a court or tribunal in a place outside the jurisdiction` `the matter in question is a criminal matter` `the kind of order`

@export Under Order 55, rule 1(2), is the Registrar barred from making the order?
GIVEN `it is an order of the kind mentioned in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an order of the kind mentioned in paragraph (1)?
      `the matter in question is a criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter in question a criminal matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 55, rule 1(2), is the Registrar barred from making the order` IS
    `o 55 r 1(2) the Registrar is barred from making the order` `it is an order of the kind mentioned in paragraph (1)` `the matter in question is a criminal matter`

@export Under Order 55, rule 1(2), may the Registrar make the order?
GIVEN `it is an order of the kind mentioned in paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an order of the kind mentioned in paragraph (1)?
      `the matter in question is a criminal matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the matter in question a criminal matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 55, rule 1(2), may the Registrar make the order` IS
    `o 55 r 1(2) the Registrar may make the order` `it is an order of the kind mentioned in paragraph (1)` `the matter in question is a criminal matter`

§§ `Rule 2 -- Application for order (O. 55, r. 2)`

@export Under Order 55, rule 2(1), must the application be made without notice by an authorised person and supported by affidavit?
GIVEN `it is an application for an order under Rule 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for an order under Rule 1?
      `it is an application for a further order or directions in relation to the same matter after an earlier application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for a further order or directions in relation to the same matter, after an earlier application for an order under Rule 1?
      `Rule 3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Rule 3 apply?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 55, rule 2(1), must the application be made without notice by an authorised person and supported by affidavit` IS
    `o 55 r 2(1) the application must be made without notice by an authorised person and supported by affidavit` `it is an application for an order under Rule 1` `it is an application for a further order or directions in relation to the same matter after an earlier application` `Rule 3 applies`

@export Under Order 55, rule 2(1), is the application made as it must be?
GIVEN `it is an application for an order under Rule 1` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for an order under Rule 1?
      `it is an application for a further order or directions in relation to the same matter after an earlier application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for a further order or directions in relation to the same matter, after an earlier application for an order under Rule 1?
