    `o 55 r 2(3) the further application must be made by summons` `an application for an order mentioned in paragraph (1) has been made in relation to the matter` `it is an application for a further order or directions in relation to the same matter`

@export Under Order 55, rule 2(3), is the further application made by summons as it must be?
GIVEN `an application for an order mentioned in paragraph (1) has been made in relation to the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application for an order mentioned in paragraph (1) been made in relation to the matter?
      `it is an application for a further order or directions in relation to the same matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for a further order or directions in relation to the same matter?
      `the document I used` IS A `Document kind` @desc What document did you use? One of: Originating claim, Originating application, Statement of claim, Defence, Defence and counterclaim, Reply, Reply to a defence and counterclaim, Summons, Summons without notice, Affidavit, Notice of intention to contest or not contest, Notice of appeal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 55, rule 2(3), is the further application made by summons as it must be` IS
    `o 55 r 2(3) the further application is made by summons as it must be` `an application for an order mentioned in paragraph (1) has been made in relation to the matter` `it is an application for a further order or directions in relation to the same matter` `the document I used`

§§ `Rule 3 -- Application by Attorney-General in certain cases (O. 55, r. 3)`

