    `o 56 r 9 the individual may be sued in that name or style as if it were the name of a firm` `it is an individual carrying on business within the jurisdiction in a name or style other than his or her own name`

@export Under Order 56, rule 9, do Rules 2 to 8 apply as if the individual were a partner?
GIVEN `it is an individual carrying on business within the jurisdiction in a name or style other than his or her own name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an individual carrying on business within the jurisdiction in a name or style other than his or her own name?
      `the Rule is applicable to the case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Rule applicable to the individual in this case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 56, rule 9, do Rules 2 to 8 apply as if the individual were a partner` IS
    `o 56 r 9 Rules 2 to 8 apply as if the individual were a partner` `it is an individual carrying on business within the jurisdiction in a name or style other than his or her own name` `the Rule is applicable to the case`

§§ `Rule 10 -- Applications for orders charging partner's interest in property, etc. (O. 56, r. 10)`

@export Under Order 56, rule 10(1), must the application be made by summons?
GIVEN `it is an application to the Court by a judgment creditor of a partner for an order under section 23 of the Partnership Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application to the Court by a judgment creditor of a partner for an order under section 23 of the Partnership Act?
      `it is an application to the Court by a partner of the judgment debtor made in consequence of that application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application to the Court by a partner of the judgment debtor made in consequence of that application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 56, rule 10(1), must the application be made by summons` IS
    `o 56 r 10(1) the application must be made by summons` `it is an application to the Court by a judgment creditor of a partner for an order under section 23 of the Partnership Act` `it is an application to the Court by a partner of the judgment debtor made in consequence of that application`

@export Under Order 56, rule 10(1), is the application made by summons as it must be?
GIVEN `it is an application to the Court by a judgment creditor of a partner for an order under section 23 of the Partnership Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application to the Court by a judgment creditor of a partner for an order under section 23 of the Partnership Act?
      `it is an application to the Court by a partner of the judgment debtor made in consequence of that application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application to the Court by a partner of the judgment debtor made in consequence of that application?
      `the document I used` IS A `Document kind` @desc What document did you use? One of: Originating claim, Originating application, Statement of claim, Defence, Defence and counterclaim, Reply, Reply to a defence and counterclaim, Summons, Summons without notice, Affidavit, Notice of intention to contest or not contest, Notice of appeal
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 56, rule 10(1), is the application made by summons as it must be` IS
    `o 56 r 10(1) the application is made by summons as it must be` `it is an application to the Court by a judgment creditor of a partner for an order under section 23 of the Partnership Act` `it is an application to the Court by a partner of the judgment debtor made in consequence of that application` `the document I used`

@export Under Order 56, rule 10(2), may the Registrar exercise the power?
GIVEN `it is a power conferred on a Judge by section 23 of the Partnership Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a power conferred on a Judge by section 23 of the Partnership Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 56, rule 10(2), may the Registrar exercise the power` IS
    `o 56 r 10(2) the Registrar may exercise the power` `it is a power conferred on a Judge by section 23 of the Partnership Act`

@export Under Order 56, rule 10(3), does the duty to serve the judgment debtor and the partners within Singapore arise?
GIVEN `it is a summons issued by a judgment creditor under this Rule, or an order made on such a summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a summons issued by a judgment creditor under this Rule, or an order made on such a summons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 56, rule 10(3), does the duty to serve the judgment debtor and the partners within Singapore arise` IS
    `o 56 r 10(3) the duty to serve the judgment debtor and the partners within Singapore arises` `it is a summons issued by a judgment creditor under this Rule, or an order made on such a summons`

@export Under Order 56, rule 10(3), is the summons or order served as it must be?
GIVEN `it is a summons issued by a judgment creditor under this Rule, or an order made on such a summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a summons issued by a judgment creditor under this Rule, or an order made on such a summons?
      `it is served on the judgment debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it served on the judgment debtor?
      `it is served on such of the judgment debtor's partners as are within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it served on such of the judgment debtor's partners as are within Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 56, rule 10(3), is the summons or order served as it must be` IS
    `o 56 r 10(3) the summons or order is served as it must be` `it is a summons issued by a judgment creditor under this Rule, or an order made on such a summons` `it is served on the judgment debtor` `it is served on such of the judgment debtor's partners as are within Singapore`

@export Under Order 56, rule 10(4), does the duty to serve the judgment creditor, the judgment debtor and the other partners arise?
GIVEN `it is a summons issued by a partner of a judgment debtor under this Rule, or an order made on such a summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a summons issued by a partner of a judgment debtor under this Rule, or an order made on such a summons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 56, rule 10(4), does the duty to serve the judgment creditor, the judgment debtor and the other partners arise` IS
    `o 56 r 10(4) the duty to serve the judgment creditor, the judgment debtor and the other partners arises` `it is a summons issued by a partner of a judgment debtor under this Rule, or an order made on such a summons`

@export Under Order 56, rule 10(4), is the summons or order served as it must be?
GIVEN `it is a summons issued by a partner of a judgment debtor under this Rule, or an order made on such a summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a summons issued by a partner of a judgment debtor under this Rule, or an order made on such a summons?
      `it is served on the judgment creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it served on the judgment creditor?
      `it is served on the judgment debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it served on the judgment debtor?
      `it is served on such of the other partners of the judgment debtor as do not join in the application and are within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it served on such of the other partners of the judgment debtor as do not join in the application and are within Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 56, rule 10(4), is the summons or order served as it must be` IS
    `o 56 r 10(4) the summons or order is served as it must be` `it is a summons issued by a partner of a judgment debtor under this Rule, or an order made on such a summons` `it is served on the judgment creditor` `it is served on the judgment debtor` `it is served on such of the other partners of the judgment debtor as do not join in the application and are within Singapore`

@export Under Order 56, rule 10(5), is the summons or order deemed to have been served on all the partners?
GIVEN `it is a summons or an order served in accordance with this Rule on some only of the partners of a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a summons or an order served in accordance with this Rule on some only of the partners of a partnership?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 56, rule 10(5), is the summons or order deemed to have been served on all the partners` IS
    `o 56 r 10(5) the summons or order is deemed to have been served on all the partners` `it is a summons or an order served in accordance with this Rule on some only of the partners of a partnership`

-- ============================================================
-- roc11: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- SEAT for roc11 (Orders 57 to 63).  The person asking is a private party, never the Commission,
-- the Authority, the Government or the Registrar.  Every question calls a rule in layer 1; none restates one.
-- Where a rule needs "the last day for doing the act" the person is asked for it, described as O 3 r 3 counts it;
-- the merged file replaces that input with a call to roc1 (see NOTES.md, Seams).

-- ===========================================================================
-- ORDER 57 -- PERSONAL DATA PROTECTION ACT 2012 -- wiring
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `roc11 who made it` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 the Personal Data Protection Commission`
    `roc11 a Data Protection Appeal Committee`
    `roc11 someone else`

DECLARE `roc11 the provision it was made under` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 section 48H(2)`
    `roc11 section 48I`
    `roc11 section 48L(4)`
    `roc11 section 48N(6)(b)(i), a direction varied on reconsideration`
    `roc11 section 48Q(5)`
    `roc11 another provision`

GIVEN who IS A `roc11 who made it`
GIVETH A `o 57 r 3 who made the instrument`
`roc11 the maker as Order 57 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `roc11 the Personal Data Protection Commission` THEN `o 57 r 3 the Commission` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a Data Protection Appeal Committee` THEN `o 57 r 3 an Appeal Committee` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 someone else` THEN `o 57 r 3 someone else` -- input mapping

GIVEN provision IS A `roc11 the provision it was made under`
GIVETH A `o 57 r 3 provision it was made under`
`roc11 the provision as Order 57 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER provision
    WHEN `roc11 section 48H(2)` THEN `o 57 r 3 section 48H(2)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 section 48I` THEN `o 57 r 3 section 48I` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 section 48L(4)` THEN `o 57 r 3 section 48L(4)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 section 48N(6)(b)(i), a direction varied on reconsideration` THEN `o 57 r 3 section 48N(6)(b)(i)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 section 48Q(5)` THEN `o 57 r 3 section 48Q(5)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 another provision` THEN `o 57 r 3 another provision` -- input mapping

-- The instrument the person holds, from the facts the person can state.
GIVEN who IS A `roc11 who made it`
      provision IS A `roc11 the provision it was made under`
      `a direction or a decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written notice for the payment of a sum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `penalty` IS A BOOLEAN
      `interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `o 57 r 3 instrument`
`roc11 the instrument made against me` MEANS
    `o 57 r 3 instrument` OF (`roc11 the maker as Order 57 has it` who), (`roc11 the provision as Order 57 has it` provision), `a direction or a decision`, `a written notice for the payment of a sum`, penalty, interest -- input mapping

§ `Order 57 -- registering a Personal Data Protection Commission Direction, Notice or Decision in the District Court -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The defined terms (rule 1)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 57 r 1
@export Under Order 57, rule 1, is the panel an Appeal Committee?
GIVEN `the panel is a Data Protection Appeal Committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the panel a Data Protection Appeal Committee?
      `the panel was nominated under section 48P(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the panel nominated under section 48P(4) of the Personal Data Protection Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 1, is the panel an Appeal Committee` IS
    `o 57 r 1 the panel is an Appeal Committee` `the panel is a Data Protection Appeal Committee` `the panel was nominated under section 48P(4)`

@ref O 57 r 1
@export Under Order 57, rule 1, is the body the Commission?
GIVEN `the body is the Personal Data Protection Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the body the Personal Data Protection Commission?
      `the body is the one established by section 5 of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the Commission established by section 5 of the Personal Data Protection Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 1, is the body the Commission` IS
    `o 57 r 1 the body is the Commission` `the body is the Personal Data Protection Commission` `the body is the one established by section 5 of the Act`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Who may hear an application under section 48M (rule 2)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 57 r 2
@export Under Order 57, rule 2, can the Registrar exercise the District Court's power under section 48M that is being asked for?
GIVEN `the order asked for is one that section 48M(4) provides` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order asked for one that section 48M(4) of the Personal Data Protection Act provides for?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 2, can the Registrar exercise the District Court's power under section 48M that is being asked for` IS
    `o 57 r 2 the power under section 48M may be exercised by the person` `the order asked for is one that section 48M(4) provides` `The Registrar` FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `What may be registered, and how I apply (rule 3)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 57 r 3(a)
@export Under Order 57, rule 3(a), is the instrument made against me a Direction?
GIVEN who IS A `roc11 who made it` @desc Who made the instrument?
      provision IS A `roc11 the provision it was made under` @desc Under which provision was the instrument made?
      `a direction or a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a direction or a decision (rather than a notice)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 3(a), is the instrument made against me a Direction` IS
    `o 57 r 3(a) the instrument is a Direction` (`roc11 the instrument made against me` who provision `a direction or a decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

@ref O 57 r 3(b)
@export Under Order 57, rule 3(b), is the instrument made against me a Notice?
GIVEN who IS A `roc11 who made it` @desc Who made the instrument?
      `a written notice for the payment of a sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a written notice for the payment of a sum?
      `penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the sum include a financial penalty imposed under section 48J(1), or varied under section 48N(6)(b)(ii)?
      `interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the sum include the interest payable under section 48K(10) on that penalty?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 3(b), is the instrument made against me a Notice` IS
    `o 57 r 3(b) the instrument is a Notice` (`roc11 the instrument made against me` who `roc11 another provision` FALSE `a written notice for the payment of a sum` penalty interest)

@ref O 57 r 3(c)
@export Under Order 57, rule 3(c), is the instrument made against me a Decision?
GIVEN who IS A `roc11 who made it` @desc Who made the instrument?
      provision IS A `roc11 the provision it was made under` @desc Under which provision was the instrument made?
      `a direction or a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the instrument a direction or a decision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 3(c), is the instrument made against me a Decision` IS
    `o 57 r 3(c) the instrument is a Decision` (`roc11 the instrument made against me` who provision `a direction or a decision` FALSE FALSE FALSE)

@ref O 57 r 3
@export Under Order 57, rule 3, was the Commission's application to register the instrument made against me made by originating application without notice, as the Rule requires?
GIVEN who IS A `roc11 who made it` @desc Who made the instrument that was made against you?
      provision IS A `roc11 the provision it was made under` @desc Under which provision was it made?
      `a direction or a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a direction or a decision?
      `a written notice for the payment of a sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a written notice for the payment of a sum?
      `penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a notice, does the sum include a financial penalty imposed under section 48J(1), or varied under section 48N(6)(b)(ii)?
      `interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a notice, does the sum include the interest payable under section 48K(10) on that penalty?
      `by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission apply by originating application?
      `without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission apply without notice to you?
      `in the District Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Commission apply to register it in the District Court (and not in another court)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 3, was the Commission's application to register the instrument made against me made by originating application without notice` IS
    `o 57 r 3 the application to register in the District Court is made in the way the Rule requires` `in the District Court` (`roc11 the instrument made against me` who provision `a direction or a decision` `a written notice for the payment of a sum` penalty interest) `by originating application` `without notice`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The affidavit that supports the application (rule 4)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 57 r 4(1)
@export Under Order 57, rule 4(1), what has the affidavit supporting the Commission's application to register left out that the Rule requires?
GIVEN `exhibits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit exhibit the Direction, Notice or Decision, or a verified, certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy of it?
      `commission is the party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state that the Commission is the party seeking to register it?
      `name and place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state the name and the usual or last known place of business or residence of the party against whom it has been made, so far as you know?
      `entitled to enforce` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state, to the best of your information or belief, that the Commission is entitled to enforce it?
      `not appealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state that, as at the date of the application, it has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired?
      `appeals disposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state that, as at the date of the application, all appeals have been finally disposed of and no further appeal is feasible?
      `not complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state that, as at the date of the application, it has not been complied with?
      `penalty imposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a financial penalty imposed?
      `amount unsatisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state the amount of the financial penalty that remains unsatisfied?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 4(1), what has the affidavit supporting the Commission's application to register left out that the Rule requires` IS
    `o 57 r 4(1) the matters the affidavit has not yet stated` (`o 57 r 4(1) affidavit` OF `exhibits`, `commission is the party`, `name and place`, `entitled to enforce`, `not appealed`, `appeals disposed`, `not complied with`, `penalty imposed`, `amount unsatisfied`)

@ref O 57 r 4(2)
@export Under Order 57, rule 4(2), does the affidavit supporting the Commission's application make the additional statement the Rule requires about reconsideration?
GIVEN who IS A `roc11 who made it` @desc Who made the instrument that was made against you?
      provision IS A `roc11 the provision it was made under` @desc Under which provision was it made?
      `a direction or a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a direction or a decision?
      `a written notice for the payment of a sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a written notice for the payment of a sum?
      `penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a notice, does the sum include a financial penalty imposed under section 48J(1), or varied under section 48N(6)(b)(ii)?
      `interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a notice, does the sum include the interest payable under section 48K(10) on that penalty?
      `no reconsideration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state that no application was made under section 48N(1) to reconsider and the time allowed to apply has expired?
      `reconsideration not appealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state that all applications to reconsider have been finally disposed of and the decision on reconsideration has not been appealed against and the time for appealing has expired?
      `reconsideration appeals disposed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state that all applications to reconsider have been finally disposed of, all appeals against the decision on reconsideration have been finally disposed of and the time for a further appeal has expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 4(2), does the affidavit supporting the Commission's application make the additional statement the Rule requires about reconsideration` IS
    `o 57 r 4(2) the affidavit makes the additional statement the Rule requires` (`roc11 the instrument made against me` who provision `a direction or a decision` `a written notice for the payment of a sum` penalty interest) (`o 57 r 4(2) additional statements` OF `no reconsideration`, `reconsideration not appealed`, `reconsideration appeals disposed`)

@ref O 57 r 4(1)
@export Under Order 57, rule 4(1)(d)(ii)(A), can the Commission's affidavit state that the instrument made against me has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired?
GIVEN `appealed against` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the instrument made against you been appealed against?
      `time to appeal expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the time allowed for appealing against it expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 4(1)(d)(ii)(A), can the Commission's affidavit state that the instrument made against me has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired` IS
    `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(ii)(A) the affidavit may state that it has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired` `appealed against` `time to appeal expired`

@ref O 57 r 4(1)
@export Under Order 57, rule 4(1)(d)(ii)(B), can the Commission's affidavit state that all appeals against the instrument made against me have been finally disposed of and no further appeal is feasible?
GIVEN `all appeals disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all appeals against the instrument made against you been finally disposed of?
      `further appeal feasible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a further appeal against it feasible?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 4(1)(d)(ii)(B), can the Commission's affidavit state that all appeals against the instrument made against me have been finally disposed of and no further appeal is feasible` IS
    `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(ii)(B) the affidavit may state that all appeals have been finally disposed of and no further appeal is feasible` `all appeals disposed of` `further appeal feasible`

@ref O 57 r 4(1)
@export Under Order 57, rule 4(1)(d)(ii), can the Commission's affidavit state, on these facts, either that the instrument made against me has not been appealed against and the time to appeal has expired, or that all appeals have been finally disposed of and no further appeal is feasible?
GIVEN `appealed against` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the instrument made against you been appealed against?
      `time to appeal expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the time allowed for appealing against it expired?
      `all appeals disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all appeals against it been finally disposed of?
      `further appeal feasible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a further appeal against it feasible?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 4(1)(d)(ii), can the Commission's affidavit state, on these facts, either that the instrument made against me has not been appealed against and the time to appeal has expired, or that all appeals have been finally disposed of and no further appeal is feasible` IS
    `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(ii) the affidavit may state the matter the Rule requires about appeals` `appealed against` `time to appeal expired` `all appeals disposed of` `further appeal feasible`

@ref O 57 r 4(1)
@export Under Order 57, rule 4(1)(d)(iii), can the Commission's affidavit state that the instrument made against me has not been complied with?
GIVEN `complied with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the instrument made against you been complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 4(1)(d)(iii), can the Commission's affidavit state that the instrument made against me has not been complied with` IS
    `o 57 r 4(1)(d)(iii) the affidavit may state that it has not been complied with` `complied with`

@ref O 57 r 4(2)
@export Under Order 57, rule 4(2)(a), can the Commission's affidavit state that no application to reconsider was made and the time allowed to apply has expired?
GIVEN who IS A `roc11 who made it` @desc Who made the instrument that was made against you?
      provision IS A `roc11 the provision it was made under` @desc Under which provision was it made?
      `a direction or a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a direction or a decision?
      `a written notice for the payment of a sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a written notice for the payment of a sum?
      `penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a notice, does the sum include a financial penalty imposed under section 48J(1), or varied under section 48N(6)(b)(ii)?
      `interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a notice, does the sum include the interest payable under section 48K(10) on that penalty?
      `reconsideration applied for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made under section 48N(1) to the Commission to reconsider it?
      `time to apply expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the time allowed to apply for reconsideration expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 4(2)(a), can the Commission's affidavit state that no application to reconsider was made and the time allowed to apply has expired` IS
    `o 57 r 4(2)(a) the affidavit may state that no application to reconsider was made and the time allowed to apply has expired` (`roc11 the instrument made against me` who provision `a direction or a decision` `a written notice for the payment of a sum` penalty interest) `reconsideration applied for` `time to apply expired`

@ref O 57 r 4(2)
@export Under Order 57, rule 4(2)(b)(i), can the Commission's affidavit state that the decision on reconsideration has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired?
GIVEN who IS A `roc11 who made it` @desc Who made the instrument that was made against you?
      provision IS A `roc11 the provision it was made under` @desc Under which provision was it made?
      `a direction or a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a direction or a decision?
      `a written notice for the payment of a sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a written notice for the payment of a sum?
      `penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a notice, does the sum include a financial penalty imposed under section 48J(1), or varied under section 48N(6)(b)(ii)?
      `interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a notice, does the sum include the interest payable under section 48K(10) on that penalty?
      `reconsiderations disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all applications made under section 48N(1) to reconsider it been finally disposed of?
      `decision appealed against` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission's decision on reconsideration been appealed against?
      `time to appeal expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the time allowed for appealing against that decision expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 4(2)(b)(i), can the Commission's affidavit state that the decision on reconsideration has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired` IS
    `o 57 r 4(2)(b)(i) the affidavit may state that the decision on reconsideration has not been appealed against and the time allowed for appealing has expired` (`roc11 the instrument made against me` who provision `a direction or a decision` `a written notice for the payment of a sum` penalty interest) `reconsiderations disposed of` `decision appealed against` `time to appeal expired`

@ref O 57 r 4(2)
@export Under Order 57, rule 4(2)(b)(ii), can the Commission's affidavit state that all appeals against the decision on reconsideration have been finally disposed of and the time allowed for a further appeal has expired?
GIVEN who IS A `roc11 who made it` @desc Who made the instrument that was made against you?
      provision IS A `roc11 the provision it was made under` @desc Under which provision was it made?
      `a direction or a decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a direction or a decision?
      `a written notice for the payment of a sum` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a written notice for the payment of a sum?
      `penalty` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a notice, does the sum include a financial penalty imposed under section 48J(1), or varied under section 48N(6)(b)(ii)?
      `interest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is a notice, does the sum include the interest payable under section 48K(10) on that penalty?
      `reconsiderations disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all applications made under section 48N(1) to reconsider it been finally disposed of?
      `appeals disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have all appeals against the Commission's decision on reconsideration been finally disposed of?
      `further appeal lies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a further appeal lie under section 48Q(1)(c) or section 48R(1) or (4)?
      `time for further appeal expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the time allowed for making a further appeal expired?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 4(2)(b)(ii), can the Commission's affidavit state that all appeals against the decision on reconsideration have been finally disposed of and the time allowed for a further appeal has expired` IS
    `o 57 r 4(2)(b)(ii) the affidavit may state that all appeals against the decision on reconsideration have been finally disposed of and the time allowed for a further appeal has expired` (`roc11 the instrument made against me` who provision `a direction or a decision` `a written notice for the payment of a sum` penalty interest) `reconsiderations disposed of` `appeals disposed of` `further appeal lies` `time for further appeal expired`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The order for registration (rule 5)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 57 r 5(2)
@export Under Order 57, rule 5(2), does the order registering the instrument against me state the period to apply to set aside and contain the notification the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the Court has directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court directed that the order need not state the period and contain the notification?
      `states the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order state the period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration?
      `contains the notification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order contain a notification that an enforcement order will not be issued until after the expiry of that period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 5(2), does the order registering the instrument against me state the period to apply to set aside and contain the notification` IS
    `o 57 r 5(2) the order for registration states and notifies what the Rule requires` `the Court has directed otherwise` `states the period` `contains the notification`

@ref O 57 r 5(3)
@export Under Order 57, rule 5(3), is my application to extend the period for applying to set aside made before that period expires?
GIVEN `the date I apply` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you make (or did you make) the application to extend the period?
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period, as originally fixed or as subsequently extended, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 5(3), is my application to extend the period for applying to set aside made before that period expires` IS
    `o 57 r 5(3) the application to extend the period is made before the period expires` `the date I apply` `the last day of the period`

@ref O 57 r 5(4)
@export Under Order 57, rule 5(4), may the Court extend the period for applying to set aside, on such terms as it thinks fit?
GIVEN `the period is the one referred to in paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the period the one within which an application may be made to set aside the registration (as originally fixed or as subsequently extended)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 5(4), may the Court extend the period for applying to set aside` IS
    `o 57 r 5(4) the Court may extend the period on such terms as it thinks fit` `the period is the one referred to in paragraph (3)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The notice of registration served on me (rules 7 and 8)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 57 r 7(1)
@export Under Order 57, rule 7(1), was the notice of registration served on me as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `served on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice of registration served on you, the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision has been made?
      `served personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it served on you personally?
      `court ordered other service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that it be served in some way other than personally?
      `served as the court ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the Court ordered another way, was it served that way?
      `served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it served on you outside Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 7(1), was the notice of registration served on me as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 57 r 7(1) the notice of registration is served as the Rule requires` `served on me` `served personally` `court ordered other service` `served as the court ordered` `served out of Singapore`

@ref O 57 r 7(2)
@export Under Order 57, rule 7(2), does the Commission need permission to serve the notice of registration on me outside Singapore?
GIVEN `served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the notice of registration served on you outside Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 7(2), does the Commission need permission to serve the notice of registration on me outside Singapore` IS
    `o 57 r 7(2) permission is needed to serve the notice out of Singapore` `served out of Singapore`

@ref O 57 r 7(3)
@export Under Order 57, rule 7(3), what has the notice of registration served on me left out that the Rule requires it to state?
GIVEN `particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state full particulars of the Direction, Notice or Decision registered and the order for registration?
      `name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the name and address of the party seeking to enforce it, or of that party's solicitor, on whom a summons may be served?
      `right to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that you have a right to apply to have the registration set aside?
      `period to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the period within which an application to set aside the registration may be made?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 7(3), what has the notice of registration served on me left out that the Rule requires it to state` IS
    `o 57 r 7(3) the matters the notice has not yet stated` (`o 57 r 7(3) notice of registration` OF `particulars`, `name and address`, `right to apply`, `period to apply`)

@ref O 57 r 8(1)
@export Under Order 57, rule 8(1), was the notice of registration endorsed in time?
GIVEN `endorsed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the notice (or a copy) been endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date of service?
      `the date it was endorsed` IS A DATE @desc If it has been endorsed, on what date? (Give any date if it has not.)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the 3 days after service, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
      `a longer period was allowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court, in special circumstances, allowed a longer period?
      `the last day of the longer period` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is its last day? (Give any date if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 8(1), was the notice of registration endorsed in time` IS
    `o 57 r 8(1) the notice is endorsed in time` (IF `endorsed` THEN JUST `the date it was endorsed` ELSE NOTHING) `the date I am asking about` `the last day` (IF `a longer period was allowed` THEN JUST `the last day of the longer period` ELSE NOTHING)

@ref O 57 r 8(2)
@export Under Order 57, rule 8(2), may the Commission apply for an enforcement order against me without the Court's permission?
GIVEN `endorsed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the notice (or a copy) been endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date of service?
      `the date it was endorsed` IS A DATE @desc If it has been endorsed, on what date? (Give any date if it has not.)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the 3 days after service, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
      `a longer period was allowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court, in special circumstances, allowed a longer period?
      `the last day of the longer period` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is its last day? (Give any date if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 8(2), may the Commission apply for an enforcement order against me without the Court's permission` IS
    `o 57 r 8(2) the person seeking to enforce may apply for an enforcement order without the permission of the Court` (`o 57 r 8(1) the notice is endorsed in time` (IF `endorsed` THEN JUST `the date it was endorsed` ELSE NOTHING) `the date I am asking about` `the last day` (IF `a longer period was allowed` THEN JUST `the last day of the longer period` ELSE NOTHING))

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Setting aside the registration (rule 9)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 57 r 9(1)
@export Under Order 57, rule 9(1), is my application to set aside the registration made by summons supported by an affidavit?
GIVEN `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you apply by summons?
      `supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application supported by an affidavit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 9(1), is my application to set aside the registration made by summons supported by an affidavit` IS
    `o 57 r 9(1) the application to set aside the registration is made as the Rule requires` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`) `supported by an affidavit`

@ref O 57 r 9(2)
@export Under Order 57, rule 9(2), may the Court order the issue between the parties to be tried as an issue in an action is tried?
GIVEN `between the Commission and me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the issue between the Commission and the party against whom the Direction, Notice or Decision is made?
      `between the complainant and me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the issue between the complainant referred to in section 48H(1), on whose application the Direction, Notice or Decision was made, and the party against whom it is made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 9(2), may the Court order the issue between the parties to be tried as an issue in an action is tried` IS
    `o 57 r 9(2) the Court may order the issue to be tried as an issue in an action is tried` `between the Commission and me` `between the complainant and me`

@ref O 57 r 9(3)
@export Under Order 57, rule 9(3), may the Court set the registration aside on such terms as it thinks fit?
GIVEN `the Court is hearing my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court hearing an application under this Rule to set aside the registration?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 9(3), may the Court set the registration aside on such terms as it thinks fit` IS
    `o 57 r 9(3) the Court may order the registration to be set aside on such terms as it thinks fit` `the Court is hearing my application`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Whether an enforcement order can yet be issued against me (rule 10)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 57 r 10(1)
@export Under Order 57, rule 10(1), is an enforcement order barred against me because the period to apply to set aside has not yet expired?
GIVEN `there is a specified period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order for registration specify a period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration?
      `the date the period expires` IS A DATE @desc On what date does that period expire, as extended by the Court if it was?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 10(1), is an enforcement order barred against me because the period to apply to set aside has not yet expired` IS
    `o 57 r 10(1) an enforcement order cannot yet be issued because the specified period has not expired` `there is a specified period` `the date the period expires` `the date I am asking about`

@ref O 57 r 10(2)
@export Under Order 57, rule 10(2), is an enforcement order barred against me because my application to set aside has not yet been disposed of?
GIVEN `I applied to set aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made to set aside the registration?
      `it has been disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that application been disposed of?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 10(2), is an enforcement order barred against me because my application to set aside has not yet been disposed of` IS
    `o 57 r 10(2) an enforcement order cannot yet be issued because the application to set aside is not disposed of` `I applied to set aside` `it has been disposed of`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `An application for an order under section 48M(4) (rule 11)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 57 r 11(1)
@export Under Order 57, rule 11(1)(a), may the Commission apply against me for an order under section 48M(4) at this stage of its application to register?
GIVEN `the Commission has already applied to register the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Commission already applied to register the instrument made against you?
      `the Commission is applying for the order together with its application to register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Commission making its application for the order under section 48M(4) together with its application to register the instrument?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 11(1)(a), may the Commission apply against me for an order under section 48M(4) at this stage of its application to register` IS
    `o 57 r 11(1)(a) the application for an order specified in section 48M(4) may be made at this time` (IF `the Commission is applying for the order together with its application to register` THEN `o 57 r 11(1)(a) together with the application for registration` ELSE IF `the Commission has already applied to register the instrument` THEN `o 57 r 11(1)(a) at a time after the application for registration` ELSE `o 57 r 11(1)(a) before the application for registration`)

@ref O 57 r 11(2)
@export Under Order 57, rule 11(2), may the Commission make its application against me for an order under section 48M(4) without notice?
GIVEN `without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Commission want to make the application without notice to you?
      `urgent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the case one of urgency?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 11(2), may the Commission make its application against me for an order under section 48M(4) without notice` IS
    `o 57 r 11(2) the application may be made in this way` (IF `without notice` THEN `o 57 r 11(2) by summons supported by an affidavit, without notice` ELSE `o 57 r 11(2) by summons supported by an affidavit, with notice`) `urgent`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `A claim for relief under section 48O (rules 12 and 13)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 57 r 12
@export Under Order 57, rule 12, did I serve a copy of my originating claim or originating application on the Commission in time?
GIVEN `my claim is under section 48O(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim one for relief in civil proceedings under section 48O(1) of the Personal Data Protection Act?
      `the date I served the Commission` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve a copy of the originating claim or originating application on the Commission?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the 14 days after service on the defendant, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 12, did I serve a copy of my originating claim or originating application on the Commission in time` IS
    `o 57 r 12 the claimant serves a copy on the Commission in time` `my claim is under section 48O(1)` `the date I served the Commission` `the last day`

@ref O 57 r 12
@export Under Order 57, rule 12, must I serve the Commission with a copy of my originating claim or originating application?
GIVEN `my claim is under section 48O(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim one for relief in civil proceedings under section 48O(1) of the Personal Data Protection Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 12, must I serve the Commission with a copy of my originating claim or originating application` IS
    `o 57 r 12 the duty to serve a copy on the Commission arises` `my claim is under section 48O(1)`

@ref O 57 r 13
@export Under Order 57, rule 13, did I transmit a copy of the judgment or order to the Commission in time?
GIVEN `I was granted it under section 48O` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you granted the judgment or order by a Court pursuant to section 48O?
      `the date I transmitted it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you transmit a copy of the judgment or order to the Commission?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the 3 days after the date of the judgment or order, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 13, did I transmit a copy of the judgment or order to the Commission in time` IS
    `o 57 r 13 the person transmits a copy to the Commission in time` `I was granted it under section 48O` `the date I transmitted it` `the last day`

@ref O 57 r 13
@export Under Order 57, rule 13, must I transmit a copy of the judgment or order to the Commission?
GIVEN `I was granted it under section 48O` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you granted the judgment or order by a Court pursuant to section 48O of the Personal Data Protection Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 57, rule 13, must I transmit a copy of the judgment or order to the Commission` IS
    `o 57 r 13 the duty to transmit a copy to the Commission arises` `I was granted it under section 48O`

-- ===========================================================================
-- ORDER 58 -- HIRE-PURCHASE -- wiring
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `roc11 section of the Hire-Purchase Act` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 Hire-Purchase Act section 5(3)`
    `roc11 Hire-Purchase Act section 10`
    `roc11 Hire-Purchase Act section 32`
    `roc11 Hire-Purchase Act section 43`
    `roc11 Hire-Purchase Act section 44`
    `roc11 another section of the Hire-Purchase Act`

GIVEN section IS A `roc11 section of the Hire-Purchase Act`
GIVETH A `o 58 r 2 section of the Hire-Purchase Act`
`roc11 the section as Order 58 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER section
    WHEN `roc11 Hire-Purchase Act section 5(3)` THEN `o 58 r 2 section 5(3)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 Hire-Purchase Act section 10` THEN `o 58 r 2 section 10` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 Hire-Purchase Act section 32` THEN `o 58 r 2 section 32` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 Hire-Purchase Act section 43` THEN `o 58 r 2 section 43` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 Hire-Purchase Act section 44` THEN `o 58 r 2 section 44` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 another section of the Hire-Purchase Act` THEN `o 58 r 2 another section` -- input mapping

§ `Order 58 -- proceedings arising out of hire-purchase agreements -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Do these Rules apply to my proceedings (rule 1)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 58 r 1
@export Under Order 58, rule 1, do the Rules of Court on hire-purchase proceedings apply to my proceedings?
GIVEN `my proceedings are under the Hire-Purchase Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your proceedings proceedings under the Hire-Purchase Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 58, rule 1, do the Rules of Court on hire-purchase proceedings apply to my proceedings` IS
    `o 58 r 1 these Rules apply to the proceedings` `my proceedings are under the Hire-Purchase Act`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `How I make an application under the Hire-Purchase Act (rule 2)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 58 r 2
@export Under Order 58, rule 2, is my application under the Hire-Purchase Act made as the Rule requires?
GIVEN section IS A `roc11 section of the Hire-Purchase Act` @desc Under which section of the Hire-Purchase Act do you apply?
      `by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you apply by originating application?
      `supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application supported by an affidavit stating the grounds of the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 58, rule 2, is my application under the Hire-Purchase Act made as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 58 r 2 the application is made as the Rule requires` (`roc11 the section as Order 58 has it` section) (IF `by originating application` THEN `Originating application` ELSE Summons) `supported by an affidavit`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The particulars my statement of claim must give (rule 3)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 58 r 3
@export Under Order 58, rule 3, must my statement of claim give the hire-purchase particulars?
GIVEN `my claim is for the recovery of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for the recovery of money arising out of a hire-purchase agreement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 58, rule 3, must my statement of claim give the hire-purchase particulars` IS
    `o 58 r 3 the duty to give the particulars arises` `my claim is for the recovery of money`

@ref O 58 r 3
@export Under Order 58, rule 3, what hire-purchase particulars has my statement of claim not yet given?
GIVEN `date and parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement of claim give the date of the agreement and the parties to it?
      `goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the goods let under the agreement?
      `price` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the amount of the hire-purchase price?
      `amount paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the amount paid by or on behalf of the hirer?
      `an amount is due and unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim an amount as due and unpaid in respect of any instalment or instalments of the hire-purchase price?
      `states the amount due` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the statement of claim give that amount?
      `another claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make any other claim?
      `states the other claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the statement of claim give its amount and the circumstances in which it arises?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 58, rule 3, what hire-purchase particulars has my statement of claim not yet given` IS
    `o 58 r 3 the particulars still to be given` (`o 58 r 3 particulars given` OF `date and parties`, `goods`, `price`, `amount paid`, `an amount is due and unpaid`, `states the amount due`, `another claim`, `states the other claim`)

@ref O 58 r 3
@export Under Order 58, rule 3, does my statement of claim give the hire-purchase particulars the Rule requires?
GIVEN `my claim is for the recovery of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your claim for the recovery of money arising out of a hire-purchase agreement?
      `date and parties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the statement of claim give the date of the agreement and the parties to it?
      `goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the goods let under the agreement?
      `price` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the amount of the hire-purchase price?
      `amount paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it give the amount paid by or on behalf of the hirer?
      `an amount is due and unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you claim an amount as due and unpaid in respect of any instalment or instalments of the hire-purchase price?
      `states the amount due` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the statement of claim give that amount?
      `another claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you make any other claim?
      `states the other claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does the statement of claim give its amount and the circumstances in which it arises?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 58, rule 3, does my statement of claim give the hire-purchase particulars the Rule requires` IS
    `o 58 r 3 the statement of claim gives the particulars` `my claim is for the recovery of money` (`o 58 r 3 particulars given` OF `date and parties`, `goods`, `price`, `amount paid`, `an amount is due and unpaid`, `states the amount due`, `another claim`, `states the other claim`)

-- ===========================================================================
-- ORDER 59 -- PROCEEDINGS BY AND AGAINST GOVERNMENT -- wiring
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `roc11 the kind of thing the order is` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 a judgment`
    `roc11 a decree`
    `roc11 a rule of court`
    `roc11 an award`
    `roc11 a declaration`
    `roc11 something else`

GIVEN kind IS A `roc11 the kind of thing the order is`
GIVETH A `o 59 r 1(2) kind of thing`
`roc11 the kind of thing as Order 59 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `roc11 a judgment` THEN `o 59 r 1(2) a judgment` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a decree` THEN `o 59 r 1(2) a decree` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a rule of court` THEN `o 59 r 1(2) a rule` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an award` THEN `o 59 r 1(2) an award` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a declaration` THEN `o 59 r 1(2) a declaration` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 something else` THEN `o 59 r 1(2) another kind of thing` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 who makes the counterclaim or set-off` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 the Government, in proceedings against the Government`
    `roc11 I do, in proceedings by the Government`
    `roc11 someone else`

GIVEN who IS A `roc11 who makes the counterclaim or set-off`
GIVETH A `o 59 r 4(2) who makes it and in what proceedings`
`roc11 who makes it as Order 59 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `roc11 the Government, in proceedings against the Government` THEN `o 59 r 4(2) the Government in proceedings against the Government` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 I do, in proceedings by the Government` THEN `o 59 r 4(2) a person in proceedings by the Government` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 someone else` THEN `o 59 r 4(2) someone else` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 the name in which the Government is sued or sues` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 a Government department`
    `roc11 the Attorney-General`
    `roc11 another name`

GIVEN name IS A `roc11 the name in which the Government is sued or sues`
GIVETH A `o 59 r 4(2) in whose name the Government is sued or sues`
`roc11 the name as Order 59 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER name
    WHEN `roc11 a Government department` THEN `o 59 r 4(2) a Government department` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 the Attorney-General` THEN `o 59 r 4(2) the Attorney-General` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 another name` THEN `o 59 r 4(2) another name` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 who made the Government's affidavit` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 the solicitor acting for the Government`
    `roc11 an officer authorised by that solicitor`
    `roc11 an officer authorised by the department concerned`
    `roc11 another person`

GIVEN deponent IS A `roc11 who made the Government's affidavit`
GIVETH A `o 59 r 5(2) deponent`
`roc11 the deponent as Order 59 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER deponent
    WHEN `roc11 the solicitor acting for the Government` THEN `o 59 r 5(2)(a) the solicitor acting for the Government` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an officer authorised by that solicitor` THEN `o 59 r 5(2)(b) an officer duly authorised by the solicitor so acting` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an officer authorised by the department concerned` THEN `o 59 r 5(2)(b) an officer duly authorised by the department concerned` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 another person` THEN `o 59 r 5(2) someone else` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 the course in the section 21 application` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 further evidence is filed`
    `roc11 the Court decides on the affidavits`
    `roc11 the Court directs oral evidence`

GIVEN course IS A `roc11 the course in the section 21 application`
GIVETH A `o 59 r 6(5) course`
`roc11 the course as Order 59 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER course
    WHEN `roc11 further evidence is filed` THEN `o 59 r 6(5) further evidence is filed` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 the Court decides on the affidavits` THEN `o 59 r 6(5) the Court decides the matter upon the affidavits` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 the Court directs oral evidence` THEN `o 59 r 6(5) the Court directs that the matter be decided by oral evidence in Court` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 the kind of default` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 default of notice of intention to contest or not contest`
    `roc11 default of pleading`
    `roc11 another default`

GIVEN default IS A `roc11 the kind of default`
GIVETH A `o 59 r 7(1) kind of default`
`roc11 the default as Order 59 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER default
    WHEN `roc11 default of notice of intention to contest or not contest` THEN `o 59 r 7(1) default of notice of intention to contest or not contest` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 default of pleading` THEN `o 59 r 7(1) default of pleading` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 another default` THEN `o 59 r 7(1) another kind of default` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 the proceedings the default is in` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 my civil proceedings against the Government`
    `roc11 third party proceedings against the Government`
    `roc11 other proceedings`

GIVEN proceedings IS A `roc11 the proceedings the default is in`
GIVETH A `o 59 r 7(1) proceedings`
`roc11 the proceedings as Order 59 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER proceedings
    WHEN `roc11 my civil proceedings against the Government` THEN `o 59 r 7(1) civil proceedings against the Government` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 third party proceedings against the Government` THEN `o 59 r 7(1) third party proceedings against the Government` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 other proceedings` THEN `o 59 r 7(1) other proceedings` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 the order I seek against money due from the Government` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 an order for the attachment of debts under Order 22`
    `roc11 an order for the appointment of a receiver under Order 13, Rule 9`
    `roc11 an order of another kind`

GIVEN kind IS A `roc11 the order I seek against money due from the Government`
GIVETH A `o 59 r 12(1) kind of order`
`roc11 the kind of order as Order 59 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `roc11 an order for the attachment of debts under Order 22` THEN `o 59 r 12(1)(a) an order for the attachment of debts under Order 22` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an order for the appointment of a receiver under Order 13, Rule 9` THEN `o 59 r 12(1)(b) an order for the appointment of a receiver under Order 13, Rule 9` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an order of another kind` THEN `o 59 r 12(1) another kind of order` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 when I make the application` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 before the trial`
    `roc11 at the trial of the proceedings`
    `roc11 after the trial`

GIVEN when IS A `roc11 when I make the application`
GIVETH A `o 59 r 13(2) when the application is made`
`roc11 the time as Order 59 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER when
    WHEN `roc11 before the trial` THEN `o 59 r 13(2) before the trial` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 at the trial of the proceedings` THEN `o 59 r 13(2) at the trial of the proceedings` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 after the trial` THEN `o 59 r 13(2) after the trial` -- input mapping

§ `Order 59 -- proceedings by and against Government -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Application and definitions (rule 1)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 59 r 1(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 1, do the Rules of Court apply to my proceeding?
GIVEN `the Government is a party to my proceeding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Government a party to your civil proceeding?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 1, do the Rules of Court apply to my proceeding` IS
    `o 59 r 1(1) these Rules apply to the proceedings` `the Government is a party to my proceeding`

@ref O 59 r 1(2)
@export Under Order 59, rule 1, does a reference to a section in this Order mean a section of the Government Proceedings Act?
GIVEN `the reference is to a section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reference one to a section?
      `the reference names another Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the reference name another Act expressly?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 1, does a reference to a section in this Order mean a section of the Government Proceedings Act` IS
    `o 59 r 1(2) a reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act` `the reference is to a section` `the reference names another Act`

@ref O 59 r 1(2) "civil proceedings by or against the Government"
@export Under Order 59, rule 1, which part of the Government Proceedings Act says what civil proceedings by or against the Government mean?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 1, which part of the Government Proceedings Act says what civil proceedings by or against the Government mean` IS
    `o 59 r 1(2) "civil proceedings by or against the Government" the part of the Act that gives its meaning`

@ref O 59 r 1(2) "civil proceedings to which the Government is a party"
@export Under Order 59, rule 1, which provision of the Government Proceedings Act says what civil proceedings to which the Government is a party mean?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 1, which provision of the Government Proceedings Act says what civil proceedings to which the Government is a party mean` IS
    `o 59 r 1(2) "civil proceedings to which the Government is a party" the provision that gives its meaning`

@ref O 59 r 1(2) "order"
@export Under Order 59, rule 1, is this thing an order for the purposes of this Order?
GIVEN `the kind of thing` IS A `roc11 the kind of thing the order is` @desc Is it a judgment, a decree, a rule of court, an award, a declaration, or something else?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 1, is this thing an order for the purposes of this Order` IS
    `o 59 r 1(2) "order" the thing is within the term` (`roc11 the kind of thing as Order 59 has it` `the kind of thing`)

@ref O 59 r 1(2) "order against the Government"
@export Under Order 59, rule 1, is the order I hold an order against the Government?
GIVEN `made in civil proceedings by or against the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made in civil proceedings by or against the Government?
      `made in connection with an arbitration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it made in connection with an arbitration to which the Government is a party?
      `in my favour against the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in favour of a person against the Government, a Government department or an officer of the Government as such?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 1, is the order I hold an order against the Government` IS
    `o 59 r 1(2) "order against the Government" the order is an order against the Government` `made in civil proceedings by or against the Government` `made in connection with an arbitration` `in my favour against the Government`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Endorsement of claim (rule 2)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 59 r 2(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 2(1), what has my endorsement of claim left out that the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it states the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the endorsement state the circumstances in which the Government's liability is alleged to have arisen?
      `it states the department` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the Government department concerned?
      `it states the officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the officers of the Government concerned?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 2(1), what has my endorsement of claim left out that the Rule requires` IS
    `o 59 r 2(1) the matters the endorsement has not yet stated` (`o 59 r 2(1) endorsement of claim` OF `it states the circumstances`, `it states the department`, `it states the officers`)

@ref O 59 r 2(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 2(1), does my endorsement of claim state what the Rule requires?
GIVEN `my originating claim begins civil proceedings against the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your originating claim begin civil proceedings against the Government?
      `it states the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the endorsement state the circumstances in which the Government's liability is alleged to have arisen?
      `it states the department` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the Government department concerned?
      `it states the officers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the officers of the Government concerned?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 2(1), does my endorsement of claim state what the Rule requires` IS
    `o 59 r 2(1) the endorsement of claim states what the Rule requires` `my originating claim begins civil proceedings against the Government` (`o 59 r 2(1) endorsement of claim` OF `it states the circumstances`, `it states the department`, `it states the officers`)

@ref O 59 r 2(2)
@export Under Order 59, rule 2(2), may I as defendant apply to the claimant by notice for a further and better statement?
GIVEN `the proceedings are against the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are these civil proceedings against the Government?
      `I consider the statement insufficient` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you consider that the originating claim does not contain a sufficient statement as Rule 2 requires?
      `the date I apply` IS A DATE @desc On what date do you apply, or are you asking about?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for filing and serving a notice of intention to contest or not contest, counted as Order 6, Rule 6 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 2(2), may I as defendant apply to the claimant by notice for a further and better statement` IS
    `o 59 r 2(2) the defendant may apply to the claimant by notice for a further and better statement` `the proceedings are against the Government` `I consider the statement insufficient` `the date I apply` `the last day`

@ref O 59 r 2(3)
@export Under Order 59, rule 2(3), has the time for filing my notice of intention to contest or not contest not yet expired?
GIVEN `I gave a notice under Rule 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you give the claimant a notice for a further and better statement?
      `I was told the statement is satisfactory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you notify the claimant in writing that you are satisfied with the statement supplied?
      `the last day after my notification` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day of the 4 days after you notified the claimant, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it? (Give any date if not.)
      `the Court decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Court, on the claimant's application, decide that no further information is reasonably required?
      `the last day after the decision` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is the last day of the 4 days after the decision, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it? (Give any date if not.)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 2(3), has the time for filing my notice of intention to contest or not contest not yet expired` IS
    `o 59 r 2(3) the time for filing a notice of intention to contest or not contest cannot yet expire` `I gave a notice under Rule 2` (IF `I was told the statement is satisfactory` THEN JUST `the last day after my notification` ELSE NOTHING) (IF `the Court decided` THEN JUST `the last day after the decision` ELSE NOTHING) `the date I am asking about`

@ref O 59 r 2(3)
@export Under Order 59, rule 2(3), is the claimant's application to the Court made and served as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claimant's application made by summons?
      `served on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the summons served on you as defendant?
      `the date served` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it served?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for serving it, that is the last day that leaves at least 14 days before the return day, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 2(3), is the claimant's application to the Court made and served as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 59 r 2(3)(b) the claimant's application is made and served as the Rule requires` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`) `served on me` `the date served` `the last day`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Service on Government (rule 3)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 59 r 3(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 3(1), does Order 7, Order 8 or another provision on service out of Singapore apply to the service of the process by which I begin proceedings against the Government?
GIVEN `my process begins civil proceedings against the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a process by which civil proceedings against the Government are begun?
      `the provision is about service out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the provision Order 7, Order 8 or another provision relating to service out of Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 3(1), does Order 7, Order 8 or another provision on service out of Singapore apply to the service of the process by which I begin proceedings against the Government` IS
    `o 59 r 3(1) the provision applies to the service of the process` `my process begins civil proceedings against the Government` `the provision is about service out of Singapore`

@ref O 59 r 3(2)
@export Under Order 59, rule 3(2), must I serve a document on the Government personally?
GIVEN `the document is required to be served on the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document required to be served on the Government for the purpose of or in connection with civil proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 3(2), must I serve a document on the Government personally` IS
    `o 59 r 3(2) personal service on the Government is requisite` `the document is required to be served on the Government`

@ref O 59 r 3(2)
@export Under Order 59, rule 3(2), did I serve the Government as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the proceedings are by or against the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings by or against the Government?
      `I left it at the office` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you leave the document at the office of the person to be served in accordance with section 20, or of an agent that person nominated, with a member of the staff of that person or agent?
      `I posted it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you post it in a prepaid envelope addressed to that person or to such an agent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 3(2), did I serve the Government as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 59 r 3(2) service on the Government is effected as the Rule requires` `the proceedings are by or against the Government` `I left it at the office` `I posted it`

@ref O 59 r 3(3)
@export Under Order 59, rule 3(3), does a rule of Order 7 apply to my service of a document on the Government?
GIVEN `the document is required to be served on the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document required to be served on the Government for the purpose of or in connection with civil proceedings by or against the Government?
      `which rule` IS A STRING @desc Which rule of Order 7 do you ask about, written for example as "Order 7 rule 3"?
      `the service is under paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the service one made under Rule 3(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 3(3), does a rule of Order 7 apply to my service of a document on the Government` IS
    `o 59 r 3(3) the provision applies to the service` `the document is required to be served on the Government` `which rule` `the service is under paragraph (2)`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Counterclaim and set-off (rule 4)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 59 r 4(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 4(1), may I make a counterclaim or plead a set-off in proceedings by the Government?
GIVEN `the proceedings are by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings by the Government?
      `for the recovery of taxes, duties or penalties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings for the recovery of any taxes, duties or penalties?
      `it arises out of a claim to repayment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the counterclaim or set-off arise out of a right or claim to repayment in respect of any taxes, duties or penalties?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 4(1), may I make a counterclaim or plead a set-off in proceedings by the Government` IS
    `o 59 r 4(1) a person may make a counterclaim or plead a set-off` `the proceedings are by the Government` `for the recovery of taxes, duties or penalties` `it arises out of a claim to repayment`

@ref O 59 r 4(2)
@export Under Order 59, rule 4(2), is the Court's permission required for the counterclaim or set-off?
GIVEN `who makes it` IS A `roc11 who makes the counterclaim or set-off` @desc Does the Government make it in proceedings against the Government, do you make it in proceedings by the Government, or does someone else?
      `the name` IS A `roc11 the name in which the Government is sued or sues` @desc In what name is the Government sued or does it sue: a Government department, the Attorney-General, or another name?
      `the subject matter relates to that department` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the subject matter of the counterclaim or set-off relate to that department?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 4(2), is the Court's permission required for the counterclaim or set-off` IS
    `o 59 r 4(2) the permission of the Court is required for the counterclaim or set-off` (`roc11 who makes it as Order 59 has it` `who makes it`) (`roc11 the name as Order 59 has it` `the name`) `the subject matter relates to that department`

@ref O 59 r 4(2)
@export Under Order 59, rule 4(2), may the counterclaim be made or the set-off pleaded?
GIVEN `who makes it` IS A `roc11 who makes the counterclaim or set-off` @desc Does the Government make it in proceedings against the Government, do you make it in proceedings by the Government, or does someone else?
      `the name` IS A `roc11 the name in which the Government is sued or sues` @desc In what name is the Government sued or does it sue: a Government department, the Attorney-General, or another name?
      `the subject matter relates to that department` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the subject matter of the counterclaim or set-off relate to that department?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 4(2), may the counterclaim be made or the set-off pleaded` IS
    `o 59 r 4(2) the counterclaim may be made or the set-off pleaded` (`roc11 who makes it as Order 59 has it` `who makes it`) (`roc11 the name as Order 59 has it` `the name`) `the subject matter relates to that department` `the Court has given permission`

@ref O 59 r 4(3)
@export Under Order 59, rule 4(3), is my application for permission made as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it is an application for permission under Rule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for permission under Rule 4?
      `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by summons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 4(3), is my application for permission made as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 59 r 4(3) the application for permission is made as the Rule requires` `it is an application for permission under Rule 4` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Summary judgment (rule 5)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 59 r 5(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 5(1), may an application against the Government be made under a given provision of Order 9?
GIVEN `the proceedings are by the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings by the Government (answer no if they are against the Government)?
      `which provision` IS A STRING @desc Under which provision is the application made, written for example as "Order 9 rule 17" or "Order 9 rule 17(11)"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 5(1), may an application against the Government be made under a given provision of Order 9` IS
    `o 59 r 5(1) an application against the Government may be made under the provision` (IF `the proceedings are by the Government` THEN `o 59 r 5(1) proceedings by the Government` ELSE `o 59 r 5(1) proceedings against the Government`) `which provision`

@ref O 59 r 5(2)
@export Under Order 59, rule 5(2), is the affidavit supporting the Government's application against me made by a person the Rule allows?
GIVEN `the Government applies under Order 9` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one made by the Government under Order 9, Rule 17(1) or (11) or 19?
      `who made the affidavit` IS A `roc11 who made the Government's affidavit` @desc Who made the affidavit: the solicitor acting for the Government, an officer authorised by that solicitor, an officer authorised by the department concerned, or another person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 5(2), is the affidavit supporting the Government's application against me made by a person the Rule allows` IS
    `o 59 r 5(2) the affidavit in support is made by a person the Rule allows` `the Government applies under Order 9` (`roc11 the deponent as Order 59 has it` `who made the affidavit`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Summary applications to Court in certain revenue matters (rule 6)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 59 r 6(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 6(1), does this Rule apply to the application against me?
GIVEN `it is under section 21` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one under section 21 of the Government Proceedings Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 6(1), does this Rule apply to the application against me` IS
    `o 59 r 6(1) this Rule applies to the application` `it is under section 21`

@ref O 59 r 6(2)
@export Under Order 59, rule 6(2), is the application against me made by originating application as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `this Rule applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one to which Order 59, Rule 6 applies (an application under section 21)?
      `by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by originating application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 6(2), is the application against me made by originating application as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 59 r 6(2) the application is made as the Rule requires` `this Rule applies` (IF `by originating application` THEN `Originating application` ELSE Summons)

@ref O 59 r 6(3)
@export Under Order 59, rule 6(3), have I been made defendant to the application as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `I am the person claimed against` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an account, information or payment claimed from you, or are you required to produce books?
      `I am made defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been made defendant to the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 6(3), have I been made defendant to the application as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 59 r 6(3) the person is made defendant as the Rule requires` `I am the person claimed against` `I am made defendant`

@ref O 59 r 6(4)
@export Under Order 59, rule 6(4), what has the originating application against me left unsatisfied that the Rule requires?
GIVEN `entitled in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it entitled in the matter or matters out of which the need for the application arises?
      `entitled in the matter of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it entitled in the matter of the Government Proceedings Act?
      `refers to the written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it refer to the written law under which the account, information, payment or production of books is claimed?
      `information is claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is information claimed?
      `shows what information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If information is claimed, does it show (by appropriate questions or otherwise) what information is required?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 6(4), what has the originating application against me left unsatisfied that the Rule requires` IS
    `o 59 r 6(4) the matters the originating application has not yet satisfied` (`o 59 r 6(4) originating application` OF `entitled in the matter`, `entitled in the matter of the Act`, `refers to the written law`, `information is claimed`, `shows what information`)

@ref O 59 r 6(4)
@export Under Order 59, rule 6(4), is the originating application against me what the Rule requires?
GIVEN `this Rule applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one to which Order 59, Rule 6 applies?
      `entitled in the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it entitled in the matter or matters out of which the need for the application arises?
      `entitled in the matter of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it entitled in the matter of the Government Proceedings Act?
      `refers to the written law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it refer to the written law under which the account, information, payment or production of books is claimed?
      `information is claimed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is information claimed?
      `shows what information` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If information is claimed, does it show (by appropriate questions or otherwise) what information is required?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 6(4), is the originating application against me what the Rule requires` IS
    `o 59 r 6(4) the originating application is what the Rule requires` `this Rule applies` (`o 59 r 6(4) originating application` OF `entitled in the matter`, `entitled in the matter of the Act`, `refers to the written law`, `information is claimed`, `shows what information`)

@ref O 59 r 6(5)
@export Under Order 59, rule 6(5), is the Government officer's affidavit evidence of the facts it sets out?
GIVEN `this Rule applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one to which Order 59, Rule 6 applies?
      `by a duly authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the affidavit by a duly authorised officer of the Government department concerned?
      `sets out the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out the state of facts upon which the application is based?
      `states reason to think` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the officer has reason to think that those facts exist?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 6(5), is the Government officer's affidavit evidence of the facts it sets out` IS
    `o 59 r 6(5) the affidavit is evidence of those facts` `this Rule applies` `by a duly authorised officer` `sets out the facts` `states reason to think`

@ref O 59 r 6(5)
@export Under Order 59, rule 6(5), is this course open once evidence is filed disputing the facts?
GIVEN `the course` IS A `roc11 the course in the section 21 application` @desc Is the course that further evidence is filed, that the Court decides on the affidavits, or that the Court directs oral evidence?
      `evidence is filed disputing the facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has evidence been filed disputing any of the facts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 6(5), is this course open once evidence is filed disputing the facts` IS
    `o 59 r 6(5) the course is open` (`roc11 the course as Order 59 has it` `the course`) `evidence is filed disputing the facts`

@ref O 59 r 6(6)
@export Under Order 59, rule 6(6), must an order in favour of the Government against me name a time for compliance with each of its terms?
GIVEN `the order is in the Government's favour on a section 21 application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order one in favour of the Government on an application to which Order 59, Rule 6 applies?
      `the Court otherwise determines` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court otherwise determined?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 6(6), must an order in favour of the Government against me name a time for compliance with each of its terms` IS
    `o 59 r 6(6) the duty to name a time for compliance with each term arises` `the order is in the Government's favour on a section 21 application` `the Court otherwise determines`

@ref O 59 r 6(6)
@export Under Order 59, rule 6(6), does the order in favour of the Government name a time as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the order is in the Government's favour on a section 21 application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order one in favour of the Government on an application to which Order 59, Rule 6 applies?
      `the Court otherwise determines` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court otherwise determined?
      `it names a time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order name a time within which each of its terms is to be complied with?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 6(6), does the order in favour of the Government name a time as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 59 r 6(6) the order names a time as the Rule requires` `the order is in the Government's favour on a section 21 application` `the Court otherwise determines` `it names a time`

@ref O 59 r 6(7)
@export Under Order 59, rule 6(7), does Rule 6 require the Government to proceed by way of a section 21 application when it claims only money?
GIVEN `the only relief claimed is the payment of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only relief claimed by the Government the payment of money?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 6(7), does Rule 6 require the Government to proceed by way of a section 21 application when it claims only money` IS
    `o 59 r 6(7) this Rule requires the Government to proceed by way of an application under it` `the only relief claimed is the payment of money`

@ref O 59 r 6(7)
@export Under Order 59, rule 6(7), does Rule 6 prevent the Government from using another procedure open under these Rules when it claims only money?
GIVEN `the only relief claimed is the payment of money` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the only relief claimed by the Government the payment of money?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 6(7), does Rule 6 prevent the Government from using another procedure open under these Rules when it claims only money` IS
    `o 59 r 6(7) this Rule prevents the Government from availing itself of another procedure open under these Rules` `the only relief claimed is the payment of money`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Judgment in default (rule 7)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 59 r 7(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 7(1), is judgment in default against the Government barred without the Court's permission?
GIVEN `the default` IS A `roc11 the kind of default` @desc Is the default one of notice of intention to contest or not contest, of pleading, or another?
      `the proceedings` IS A `roc11 the proceedings the default is in` @desc Are the proceedings your civil proceedings against the Government, third party proceedings against the Government, or other proceedings?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 7(1), is judgment in default against the Government barred without the Court's permission` IS
    `o 59 r 7(1) judgment in default is barred without permission` (`roc11 the default as Order 59 has it` `the default`) (`roc11 the proceedings as Order 59 has it` `the proceedings`) `the Court has given permission`

@ref O 59 r 7(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 7(1), may judgment in default be entered against the Government?
GIVEN `the default` IS A `roc11 the kind of default` @desc Is the default one of notice of intention to contest or not contest, of pleading, or another?
      `the proceedings` IS A `roc11 the proceedings the default is in` @desc Are the proceedings your civil proceedings against the Government, third party proceedings against the Government, or other proceedings?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 7(1), may judgment in default be entered against the Government` IS
    `o 59 r 7(1) judgment in default may be entered against the Government` (`roc11 the default as Order 59 has it` `the default`) (`roc11 the proceedings as Order 59 has it` `the proceedings`) `the Court has given permission`

@ref O 59 r 7(2)
@export Under Order 59, rule 7(2), does Order 10, Rule 5(1)(a) apply in the third party proceedings against the Government?
GIVEN `the proceedings` IS A `roc11 the proceedings the default is in` @desc Are the proceedings your civil proceedings against the Government, third party proceedings against the Government, or other proceedings?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 7(2), does Order 10, Rule 5(1)(a) apply in the third party proceedings against the Government` IS
    `o 59 r 7(2) Order 10 rule 5(1)(a) applies` (`roc11 the proceedings as Order 59 has it` `the proceedings`) `the Court has given permission`

@ref O 59 r 7(3)
@export Under Order 59, rule 7(3), is my application for permission made and served as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it is an application for permission under Rule 7` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for permission under Rule 7?
      `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by summons?
      `the date I served the summons` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve the summons?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for serving it, that is the last day that leaves at least 14 days before the return day, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 7(3), is my application for permission made and served as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 59 r 7(3) the application for permission is made and served as the Rule requires` `it is an application for permission under Rule 7` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`) `the date I served the summons` `the last day`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Third party notice (rule 8)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 59 r 8(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 8(1), may I issue a third party notice for service on the Government?
GIVEN `the notice is for service on the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it a third party notice, including one issuable by virtue of Order 10, Rule 9, for service on the Government?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 8(1), may I issue a third party notice for service on the Government` IS
    `o 59 r 8(1) the third party notice may be issued` `the notice is for service on the Government` `the Court has given permission`

@ref O 59 r 8(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 8(1), is my application for permission to issue the notice made and served as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it is an application for permission to issue such a notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for permission to issue a third party notice for service on the Government?
      `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by summons?
      `served on the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the summons served on the claimant?
      `served on the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the summons served on the Government?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 8(1), is my application for permission to issue the notice made and served as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 59 r 8(1) the application for permission is made and served as the Rule requires` `it is an application for permission to issue such a notice` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`) `served on the claimant` `served on the Government`

@ref O 59 r 8(2)
@export Under Order 59, rule 8(2), may the Court grant me permission to issue the notice?
GIVEN `the Court is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court satisfied that the Government is in possession of all such information as it reasonably requires as to the circumstances in which it is alleged that its liability has arisen and as to the departments and officers of the Government concerned?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 8(2), may the Court grant me permission to issue the notice` IS
    `o 59 r 8(2) the Court may grant permission to issue the notice` `the Court is satisfied`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Production, evidence, enforcement (rules 9 to 11)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 59 r 9(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 9(1), does the order for production require disclosure of the document?
GIVEN `the Government is a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings civil proceedings to which the Government is a party?
      `the order is under section 34(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the order made under the powers conferred by section 34(1)?
      `withholding is authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the withholding of the document authorised or required under any other written law or rule of law on the ground that its disclosure would be injurious to the public interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 9(1), does the order for production require disclosure of the document` IS
    `o 59 r 9(1) the order requires disclosure of the document` `the Government is a party` `the order is under section 34(1)` `withholding is authorised`

@ref O 59 r 9(2)
@export Under Order 59, rule 9(2), is the affidavit verifying the Government's list of documents made by the officer the Court directed?
GIVEN `the Government is a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings civil proceedings to which the Government is a party?
      `the order directs verification by affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does an order direct that a list of documents made in answer to an order for production against the Government be verified by affidavit?
      `by the officer the Court directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the affidavit made by the officer of the Government whom the Court directed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 9(2), is the affidavit verifying the Government's list of documents made by the officer the Court directed` IS
    `o 59 r 9(2) the affidavit verifying the list is made by the officer the Court directed` `the Government is a party` `the order directs verification by affidavit` `by the officer the Court directed`

@ref O 59 r 10
@export Under Order 59, rule 10, may the Court take evidence in my proceeding with the Government as it does between subjects?
GIVEN `the proceedings are by or against the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings by or against the Government?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 10, may the Court take evidence in my proceeding with the Government as it does between subjects` IS
    `o 59 r 10 the Court's powers in regard to the taking of evidence are exercisable as between subjects` `the proceedings are by or against the Government`

@ref O 59 r 11(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 11(1), does a given Order apply in respect of the order against the Government that I hold?
GIVEN `it is an order against the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an order against the Government?
      `which provision` IS A STRING @desc Which provision do you ask about, written for example as "Order 22", "Order 23" or "Order 13 rule 9"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 11(1), does a given Order apply in respect of the order against the Government that I hold` IS
    `o 59 r 11(1) the provision applies in respect of the order` `it is an order against the Government` `which provision`

@ref O 59 r 11(2)
@export Under Order 59, rule 11(2), may I apply by summons without notice for a direction on a separate certificate for costs?
GIVEN `it is a proviso application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application under the proviso to section 31(1) for a direction that a separate certificate be issued with respect to the costs ordered to be paid to you?
      `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by summons?
      `without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made without notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 11(2), may I apply by summons without notice for a direction on a separate certificate for costs` IS
    `o 59 r 11(2) the application may be made in this way` `it is a proviso application` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`) `without notice`

@ref O 59 r 11(3)
@export Under Order 59, rule 11(3), which form must the certificate be in?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 11(3), which form must the certificate be in` IS
    `o 59 r 11(3) the form of the certificate`

@ref O 59 r 11(3)
@export Under Order 59, rule 11(3), is the certificate in the form the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it is in Form 87` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the certificate in Form 87?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 11(3), is the certificate in the form the Rule requires` IS
    `o 59 r 11(3) the certificate is in the form the Rule requires` `it is in Form 87`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Attachment of debts, etc. (rule 12) and applications under sections 19 and 35 (rule 13)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 59 r 12(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 12(1), may the order I seek be made in respect of money due from the Government?
GIVEN `the kind of order` IS A `roc11 the order I seek against money due from the Government` @desc Is it an order for the attachment of debts under Order 22, an order for the appointment of a receiver under Order 13, Rule 9, or an order of another kind?
      `it concerns money due from the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in respect of any money due or accruing due, or alleged to be due or accruing due, from the Government?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 12(1), may the order I seek be made in respect of money due from the Government` IS
    `o 59 r 12(1) the order may be made` (`roc11 the kind of order as Order 59 has it` `the kind of order`) `it concerns money due from the Government`

@ref O 59 r 12(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 12(1), would the order I seek have effect in respect of money due from the Government?
GIVEN `the kind of order` IS A `roc11 the order I seek against money due from the Government` @desc Is it an order for the attachment of debts under Order 22, an order for the appointment of a receiver under Order 13, Rule 9, or an order of another kind?
      `it concerns money due from the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it in respect of any money due or accruing due, or alleged to be due or accruing due, from the Government?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 12(1), would the order I seek have effect in respect of money due from the Government` IS
    `o 59 r 12(1) the order has effect` (`roc11 the kind of order as Order 59 has it` `the kind of order`) `it concerns money due from the Government`

@ref O 59 r 12(2)
@export Under Order 59, rule 12(2), is my application under section 33(1) made and served as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it is a section 33(1) application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application under section 33(1) restraining a person from receiving money payable to that person by the Government?
      `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by summons?
      `served on the Government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the summons served on the Government?
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that the person to be restrained need not be served?
      `served on the person to be restrained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it served on the person to be restrained or that person's solicitor?
      `the date of the later service` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the later of the services made?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for serving it, that is the last day that leaves at least 4 days before the return day, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
      `supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it supported by an affidavit setting out the facts giving rise to it and identifying the particular debt?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 12(2), is my application under section 33(1) made and served as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 59 r 12(2) the application is made and served as the Rule requires` `it is a section 33(1) application` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`) `served on the Government` `the Court otherwise orders` `served on the person to be restrained` `the date of the later service` `the last day` `supported by an affidavit`

@ref O 59 r 12(3)
@export Under Order 59, rule 12(3), does Order 22, Rule 10 apply to my application under section 33(1)?
GIVEN `it is an application mentioned in paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application mentioned in Rule 12(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 12(3), does Order 22, Rule 10 apply to my application under section 33(1)` IS
    `o 59 r 12(3) Order 22 rule 10 applies to the application` `it is an application mentioned in paragraph (2)`

@ref O 59 r 12(3)
@export Under Order 59, rule 12(3), may the Court order an enforcement order to be issued against the Government?
GIVEN `it is an application mentioned in paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application mentioned in Rule 12(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 12(3), may the Court order an enforcement order to be issued against the Government` IS
    `o 59 r 12(3) the Court has power to order an enforcement order to be issued against the Government` `it is an application mentioned in paragraph (2)`

@ref O 59 r 13(1)
@export Under Order 59, rule 13(1), is my application under section 19(4) made as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it is a section 19(4) application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application to the Court under section 19(4)?
      `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by summons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 13(1), is my application under section 19(4) made as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 59 r 13(1) the application is made as the Rule requires` `it is a section 19(4) application` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`)

@ref O 59 r 13(2)
@export Under Order 59, rule 13(2), may I make my section 35(2) application in this way and at this time?
GIVEN `it is a section 35(2) application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application such as is referred to in section 35(2)?
      `when` IS A `roc11 when I make the application` @desc Do you make it before the trial, at the trial of the proceedings, or after the trial?
      `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by summons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 59, rule 13(2), may I make my section 35(2) application in this way and at this time` IS
    `o 59 r 13(2) the application may be made in this way and at this time` `it is a section 35(2) application` (`roc11 the time as Order 59 has it` `when`) (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`)

-- ===========================================================================
-- ORDER 60 -- RECIPROCAL ENFORCEMENT OF JUDGMENTS -- wiring
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `roc11 who would exercise the power` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 a Judge sitting in chambers`
    `roc11 a Judge not sitting in chambers`
    `roc11 a District Judge`
    `roc11 the Registrar`

GIVEN who IS A `roc11 who would exercise the power`
GIVETH A `Decision maker`
`roc11 the decision maker as Order 60 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `roc11 a Judge sitting in chambers` THEN `A Judge` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a Judge not sitting in chambers` THEN `A Judge` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a District Judge` THEN `A District Judge` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 the Registrar` THEN `The Registrar` -- input mapping

GIVEN who IS A `roc11 who would exercise the power`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`roc11 the Judge sits in chambers` MEANS
    CONSIDER who
    WHEN `roc11 a Judge sitting in chambers` THEN TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a Judge not sitting in chambers` THEN FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a District Judge` THEN FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 the Registrar` THEN FALSE -- input mapping

§ `Order 60 -- registering a foreign judgment in the General Division, and getting certified copies of a General Division judgment -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Who may exercise the General Division's powers under the Act (rule 1A)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 60 r 1A
@export Under Order 60, rule 1A, may the person who would hear my matter exercise the General Division's powers under the Reciprocal Enforcement of Foreign Judgments Act?
GIVEN who IS A `roc11 who would exercise the power` @desc Who would exercise the power in my matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 1A, may the person who would hear my matter exercise the General Division's powers under the Act` IS
    `o 60 r 1A the power conferred on the General Division by the Act may be exercised by the person` (`roc11 the decision maker as Order 60 has it` who) (`roc11 the Judge sits in chambers` who)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `My application to register a foreign judgment (rules 2 to 4)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 60 r 2
@export Under Order 60, rule 2, is my application to register the foreign judgment made by originating application without notice, as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `my application is under section 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application one under section 4 of the Reciprocal Enforcement of Foreign Judgments Act to have a judgment registered in the General Division?
      `the judgment is one to which Part 1 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judgment one to which Part 1 of that Act applies?
      `I applied by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply by originating application?
      `I applied without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you apply without notice to the other side?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 2, is my application to register the foreign judgment made by originating application without notice` IS
    `o 60 r 2 the application for registration is made in the way the Rule requires` `my application is under section 4` `the judgment is one to which Part 1 applies` `I applied by originating application` `I applied without notice`

@ref O 60 r 3(1)
@export Under Order 60, rule 3(1), what has my affidavit supporting the application to register left out that the Rule requires?
GIVEN `exhibits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit exhibit the judgment, or a verified, certified or otherwise duly authenticated copy of it?
      `not in English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judgment in a language other than English?
      `translation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If it is not in English, does the affidavit exhibit a translation certified by a notary public or authenticated by affidavit? (No if it is in English.)
      `names and places` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state the names, trades or businesses and the usual or last known places of residence or business of the judgment creditor and the judgment debtor, so far as you know?
      `entitled to enforce` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state, to the best of your information or belief, that the judgment creditor is entitled to enforce the judgment?
      `not satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state that at the date of the application the judgment has not been satisfied?
      `amount unsatisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state the amount in respect of which the judgment remains unsatisfied?
      `enforceable and no ground to set aside` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state that at the date of the application the judgment can be enforced by an enforcement order in the country of the original court, and that no grounds exist for which its registration may or must be set aside under section 5?
      `interest due` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has interest become due under the judgment, by the law of the country of the original court, up to the time of registration?
      `interest amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit specify the amount of that interest?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 3(1), what has my affidavit supporting the application to register left out that the Rule requires` IS
    `o 60 r 3(1) the matters the affidavit has not yet stated` (`o 60 r 3(1) affidavit` OF `exhibits`, `not in English`, `translation`, `names and places`, `entitled to enforce`, `not satisfied`, `amount unsatisfied`, `enforceable and no ground to set aside`, `interest due`, `interest amount`)

@ref O 60 r 3(2)
@export Under Order 60, rule 3(2), must my affidavit state the provisions of the judgment that I want registered?
GIVEN `different matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judgment in respect of different matters?
      `some but not all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are some, but not all, of its provisions such that, had they been in separate judgments, those judgments could properly have been registered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 3(2), must my affidavit state the provisions of the judgment that I want registered` IS
    `o 60 r 3(2) the duty to state the provisions arises` `different matters` `some but not all`

@ref O 60 r 3(2)
@export Under Order 60, rule 3(2), does my affidavit state the provisions of the judgment that I want registered?
GIVEN `different matters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judgment in respect of different matters?
      `some but not all` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are some, but not all, of its provisions such that, had they been in separate judgments, those judgments could properly have been registered?
      `states the provisions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit state the provisions in respect of which you want the judgment registered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 3(2), does my affidavit state the provisions of the judgment that I want registered` IS
    `o 60 r 3(2) the affidavit states the provisions in respect of which registration is sought` `different matters` `some but not all` `states the provisions`

@ref O 60 r 3(3)
@export Under Order 60, rule 3(3), is my affidavit accompanied by the other evidence the Order extending the Act to the foreign country requires?
GIVEN `the other evidence is supplied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the affidavit accompanied by all the other evidence about the enforceability of the judgment in the country of the original court, and about the law of that country under which interest has become due, that the Order extending the Act to that country requires?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 3(3), is my affidavit accompanied by the other evidence the Order extending the Act requires` IS
    `o 60 r 3(3) the affidavit is accompanied by the other evidence the Rule requires` `the other evidence is supplied`

@ref O 60 r 4
@export Under Order 60, rule 4, may the Court order me, as judgment creditor, to give security for the costs of my application to register and of any proceedings to set the registration aside?
GIVEN `another Order provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a relevant Order under the Act (the Order extending the Act to the foreign country) provide otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 4, may the Court order me as judgment creditor to give security for costs` IS
    `o 60 r 4 the Court may order the judgment creditor to give security for costs` `another Order provides otherwise`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The order giving permission to register (rule 5)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 60 r 5(1)
@export Under Order 60, rule 5(1), was the order giving permission to register the judgment drawn up and served as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `in Form 88` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order in Form 88?
      `drawn up by the judgment creditor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it drawn up by, or on behalf of, the judgment creditor?
      `served on the judgment debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it served on the judgment debtor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 5(1), was the order giving permission to register the judgment drawn up and served as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 60 r 5(1) the order giving permission to register is drawn up and served as the Rule requires` `in Form 88` `drawn up by the judgment creditor` `served on the judgment debtor`

@ref O 60 r 5(2)
@export Under Order 60, rule 5(2), does the order state the period to apply to set aside and contain the notification the Rule requires?
GIVEN `states the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the order state the period within which an application may be made to set aside the registration?
      `contains the notification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it contain a notification that an enforcement order will not be issued until after the expiration of that period?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 5(2), does the order state the period to apply to set aside and contain the notification` IS
    `o 60 r 5(2) the order states the period and contains the notification` `states the period` `contains the notification`

@ref O 60 r 5(3)
@export Under Order 60, rule 5(3), may the Court extend the period for applying to set aside the registration on my application?
GIVEN `still competent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made at a time when it still remains competent for any party to apply to have the registration set aside?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 5(3), may the Court extend the period for applying to set aside the registration on my application` IS
    `o 60 r 5(3) the Court may extend the period for applying to set aside the registration` `still competent`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The notice of registration (rule 7)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 60 r 7(1)
@export Under Order 60, rule 7(1), was the notice of registration served on the judgment debtor as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `served on the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the notice of registration served on the judgment debtor?
      `served personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it served personally?
      `court ordered other service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that it be served in some way other than personally?
      `served as the court ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If the Court ordered another way, was it served that way?
      `served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it served outside Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 7(1), was the notice of registration served on the judgment debtor as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 60 r 7(1) the notice of registration is served as the Rule requires` `served on the debtor` `served personally` `court ordered other service` `served as the court ordered` `served out of Singapore`

@ref O 60 r 7(2)
@export Under Order 60, rule 7(2), do I need permission to serve the notice of registration outside Singapore?
GIVEN `served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will the notice of registration be served outside Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 7(2), do I need permission to serve the notice of registration outside Singapore` IS
    `o 60 r 7(2) permission is needed to serve the notice out of Singapore` `served out of Singapore`

@ref O 60 r 7(3)
@export Under Order 60, rule 7(3), what has the notice of registration left out that the Rule requires it to state?
GIVEN `particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the notice state full particulars of the judgment registered and the order for registration?
      `creditor's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the name and address of the judgment creditor, or of the judgment creditor's solicitor, on whom any summons issued by the judgment debtor may be served?
      `right to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the right of the judgment debtor to apply to have the registration set aside?
      `period to apply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the period within which an application to set aside the registration may be made?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 7(3), what has the notice of registration left out that the Rule requires it to state` IS
    `o 60 r 7(3) the matters the notice has not yet stated` (`o 60 r 7(3) notice of registration` OF `particulars`, `creditor's name and address`, `right to apply`, `period to apply`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Endorsement of service (rule 8)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 60 r 8(1)
@export Under Order 60, rule 8(1), was the notice of registration endorsed in time?
GIVEN `endorsed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the notice (or a copy) been endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date of service?
      `the date it was endorsed` IS A DATE @desc If it has been endorsed, on what date? (Give any date if it has not.)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the 3 days after service, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
      `a longer period was allowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court, in special circumstances, allowed a longer period?
      `the last day of the longer period` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is its last day? (Give any date if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 8(1), was the notice of registration endorsed in time` IS
    `o 60 r 8(1) the notice is endorsed in time` (IF `endorsed` THEN JUST `the date it was endorsed` ELSE NOTHING) `the date I am asking about` `the last day` (IF `a longer period was allowed` THEN JUST `the last day of the longer period` ELSE NOTHING)

@ref O 60 r 8(1)
@export Under Order 60, rule 8(1), may I, as judgment creditor, apply for an enforcement order without the Court's permission?
GIVEN `endorsed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the notice (or a copy) been endorsed by the person who served it with the day of the week and date of service?
      `the date it was endorsed` IS A DATE @desc If it has been endorsed, on what date? (Give any date if it has not.)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the 3 days after service, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
      `a longer period was allowed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court, in special circumstances, allowed a longer period?
      `the last day of the longer period` IS A DATE @desc If so, what is its last day? (Give any date if not.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 8(1), may I as judgment creditor apply for an enforcement order without the Court's permission` IS
    `o 60 r 8(1) the judgment creditor may apply for an enforcement order without the permission of the Court` (`o 60 r 8(1) the notice is endorsed in time` (IF `endorsed` THEN JUST `the date it was endorsed` ELSE NOTHING) `the date I am asking about` `the last day` (IF `a longer period was allowed` THEN JUST `the last day of the longer period` ELSE NOTHING))

@ref O 60 r 8(2)
@export Under Order 60, rule 8(2), does my affidavit of service state the date on which the notice was endorsed?
GIVEN `states the date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit of service state the date on which the notice was endorsed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 8(2), does my affidavit of service state the date on which the notice was endorsed` IS
    `o 60 r 8(2) the affidavit of service states the date of endorsement` `states the date`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Setting aside the registration (rule 9)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 60 r 9(1)
@export Under Order 60, rule 9(1), is my application to set aside the registration made by summons supported by an affidavit?
GIVEN `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you apply by summons?
      `supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application supported by an affidavit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 9(1), is my application to set aside the registration made by summons supported by an affidavit` IS
    `o 60 r 9(1) the application to set aside the registration is made as the Rule requires` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`) `supported by an affidavit`

@ref O 60 r 9(2)
@export Under Order 60, rule 9(2), may the Court order the issue between the judgment creditor and the judgment debtor to be tried as an issue in an action is tried?
GIVEN `the Court is hearing the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court hearing an application to set aside the registration?
      `between creditor and debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the issue one between the judgment creditor and the judgment debtor?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 9(2), may the Court order the issue between the judgment creditor and the judgment debtor to be tried as an issue in an action is tried` IS
    `o 60 r 9(2) the Court may order the issue to be tried as an issue in an action is tried` `the Court is hearing the application` `between creditor and debtor`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Whether an enforcement order can yet be issued (rule 10)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 60 r 10(1)
@export Under Order 60, rule 10(1), is an enforcement order barred because the period to apply to set aside the registration has not yet expired?
GIVEN `the judgment is registered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judgment registered under the Act?
      `the date the period expires` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the period specified in the order for registration expire, as extended by the Court if it was?
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 10(1), is an enforcement order barred because the period to apply to set aside the registration has not yet expired` IS
    `o 60 r 10(1) an enforcement order cannot yet be issued because the specified period has not expired` `the judgment is registered` `the date the period expires` `the date I am asking about`

@ref O 60 r 10(2)
@export Under Order 60, rule 10(2), is an enforcement order barred because an application to set aside the registration has not yet been finally determined?
GIVEN `an application was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has an application been made to set aside the registration?
      `finally determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has that application been finally determined?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 10(2), is an enforcement order barred because an application to set aside the registration has not yet been finally determined` IS
    `o 60 r 10(2) an enforcement order cannot yet be issued because the application to set aside is not finally determined` `an application was made` `finally determined`

@ref O 60 r 10(3)
@export Under Order 60, rule 10(3), have I produced to the Court what the Rule requires before applying for an enforcement order?
GIVEN `affidavit of service produced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you produced to the Court an affidavit of service of the notice of registration?
      `there is a court order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court made any order in relation to the judgment?
      `order produced` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you produced that order to the Court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 10(3), have I produced to the Court what the Rule requires before applying for an enforcement order` IS
    `o 60 r 10(3) the party applying for an enforcement order has produced what the Rule requires` `affidavit of service produced` `there is a court order` `order produced`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The Order extending the Act to the foreign country (rules 11 and 12)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 60 r 11
@export Under Order 60, rule 11, is my question about enforceability or interest decided in accordance with the Order extending the Act to the foreign country?
GIVEN `enforceability question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question whether the foreign judgment can be enforced by an enforcement order in the country of the original court?
      `interest question` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the question what interest is payable under the foreign judgment under the law of the original court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 11, is my question decided in accordance with the Order extending the Act to the foreign country` IS
    `o 60 r 11 the question is determined in accordance with the extending Order` `enforceability question` `interest question`

@ref O 60 r 12
@export Under Order 60, rule 12, does this Rule have effect subject to the provision of the Order extending the Act to the foreign country?
GIVEN `rule number` IS A STRING @desc Which rule of Order 60 are you asking about? (For example 5 or 1A.)
      `declared necessary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Order extending the Act to the foreign country declare the provision necessary for giving effect to the agreement between the Government and that country?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 12, does this Rule have effect subject to the provision of the Order extending the Act` IS
    `o 60 r 12 the rule has effect subject to the provision of the extending Order` `rule number` `declared necessary`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Certified copies of a General Division judgment (rule 13)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 60 r 13(1)
@export Under Order 60, rule 13(1), is my application for certified copies made by summons without notice to the Registrar, supported by an affidavit?
GIVEN `under section 13` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application one under section 13 of the Reciprocal Enforcement of Foreign Judgments Act for certified copies of the pleadings, order of court and written grounds of decision?
      `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you apply by summons?
      `without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you apply without notice to the Registrar?
      `supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application supported by an affidavit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 13(1), is my application for certified copies made by summons without notice to the Registrar supported by an affidavit` IS
    `o 60 r 13(1) the application for certified copies is made in the way the Rule requires` `under section 13` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`) `without notice` `supported by an affidavit`

@ref O 60 r 13(2)
@export Under Order 60, rule 13(2), what has my affidavit supporting the application for certified copies left out that the Rule requires?
GIVEN `particulars of the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit give particulars of the proceedings in which the judgment was obtained?
      `claim annexed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it annex a copy of the originating claim or originating application by which the proceedings were begun?
      `service or notice annexed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it annex the evidence of service of the originating claim or originating application on the defendant, or a notice of intention to contest or not contest by the defendant?
      `there are pleadings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were there any pleadings?
      `pleadings annexed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If there were pleadings, does it annex copies of them?
      `grounds annexed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it annex a statement of the grounds on which the judgment was based?
      `says whether objected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state whether the defendant did or did not object to the jurisdiction of the court in Singapore?
      `defendant objected` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the defendant object to the jurisdiction?
      `objection grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does it state on what grounds?
      `no stay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it show that the judgment is not subject to any stay of enforcement?
      `time for appealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the time for appealing has expired or the date on which it will expire?
      `appeal entered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state whether notice of appeal against the judgment has been entered?
      `interest rate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the rate at which the judgment carries interest?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 13(2), what has my affidavit supporting the application for certified copies left out that the Rule requires` IS
    `o 60 r 13(2) the matters the affidavit has not yet covered` (`o 60 r 13(2) affidavit` OF `particulars of the proceedings`, `claim annexed`, `service or notice annexed`, `there are pleadings`, `pleadings annexed`, `grounds annexed`, `says whether objected`, `defendant objected`, `objection grounds`, `no stay`, `time for appealing`, `appeal entered`, `interest rate`)

@ref O 60 r 13(3)
@export Under Order 60, rule 13(3), what do the certified copies and the Registrar's certificate I received still lack that the Rule requires?
GIVEN `sealed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the certified copies sealed with the seal of the Supreme Court?
      `claim annexed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they have a copy of the originating claim or originating application annexed?
      `form 90 certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they accompanied by a certificate in Form 90, signed by the Registrar, certifying that the judgment is a true copy of a judgment obtained in the General Division?
      `service stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the manner in which the originating claim or originating application was served, or that the defendant filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest?
      `there were objections` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were any objections made to the jurisdiction of the court in Singapore?
      `objections stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state what objections were made?
      `there were pleadings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were any pleadings served?
      `pleadings stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state what pleadings were served?
      `grounds stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the certificate state the grounds on which the judgment was based?
      `appeal time stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state that the time for appealing has expired or the date on which it will expire?
      `appeal entered stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state whether notice of appeal against the judgment has been entered?
      `other particulars stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state such other particulars as may be necessary to give to the court in the foreign country where you want to enforce the judgment?
      `interest rate stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the rate at which the judgment carries interest?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 60, rule 13(3), what do the certified copies and the Registrar's certificate I received still lack that the Rule requires` IS
    `o 60 r 13(3) the matters the copies and certificate have not yet satisfied` (`o 60 r 13(3) certified copies and certificate` OF `sealed`, `claim annexed`, `form 90 certificate`, `service stated`, `there were objections`, `objections stated`, `there were pleadings`, `pleadings stated`, `grounds stated`, `appeal time stated`, `appeal entered stated`, `other particulars stated`, `interest rate stated`)

-- ===========================================================================
-- ORDER 61 -- SECURITIES AND FUTURES ACT, CIVIL LIABILITY ACTIONS -- wiring
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `roc11 the section my proceeding is under` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 my proceeding is under section 234`
    `roc11 my proceeding is under section 235`
    `roc11 my proceeding is under section 236`
    `roc11 my proceeding is under section 236D`
    `roc11 my proceeding is under section 236G`
    `roc11 my proceeding is under section 236I`
    `roc11 my proceeding is under section 236J`
    `roc11 my proceeding is under section 236K`
    `roc11 my proceeding is under another section`

GIVEN section IS A `roc11 the section my proceeding is under`
GIVETH A `o 61 r 1 proceeding`
`roc11 the proceeding as Order 61 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER section
    WHEN `roc11 my proceeding is under section 234` THEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 234` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 my proceeding is under section 235` THEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 235` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 my proceeding is under section 236` THEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 my proceeding is under section 236D` THEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236D` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 my proceeding is under section 236G` THEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236G` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 my proceeding is under section 236I` THEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236I` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 my proceeding is under section 236J` THEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236J` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 my proceeding is under section 236K` THEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under section 236K` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 my proceeding is under another section` THEN `o 61 r 1 a proceeding under another section` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 the exhibit I want to attach` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 trade notes or slips`
    `roc11 statements of accounts for the relevant period`
    `roc11 copies of instructions given to a broker or remisier`
    `roc11 some other exhibit`

GIVEN exhibit IS A `roc11 the exhibit I want to attach`
GIVETH A `o 61 r 4(3) exhibit`
`roc11 the exhibit as Order 61 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER exhibit
    WHEN `roc11 trade notes or slips` THEN `o 61 r 4(3)(a) trade notes or slips` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 statements of accounts for the relevant period` THEN `o 61 r 4(3)(b) statements of accounts for the relevant period` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 copies of instructions given to a broker or remisier` THEN `o 61 r 4(3)(c) copies of instructions given to a broker or remisier` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 some other exhibit` THEN `o 61 r 4(3) another exhibit` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 the direction or order asked for` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 a direction for the filing of a further affidavit`
    `roc11 a direction on the manner in which proceedings are to be instituted by the claimants against the defendant`
    `roc11 an order that an issue between the claimants and the defendant be stated and tried`
    `roc11 an order that the matter be adjourned`
    `roc11 an order that further advertisements be made`
    `roc11 an order for the substitution of the claimant making the application with another claimant`
    `roc11 an order that the application be dismissed`
    `roc11 a direction or order of some other kind`

GIVEN kind IS A `roc11 the direction or order asked for`
GIVETH A `o 61 r 5(1) kind of direction or order`
`roc11 the kind of direction or order as Order 61 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `roc11 a direction for the filing of a further affidavit` THEN `o 61 r 5(1)(a) for the filing of such further affidavit as the Court considers necessary` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a direction on the manner in which proceedings are to be instituted by the claimants against the defendant` THEN `o 61 r 5(1)(b) on the manner in which proceedings are to be instituted by the claimants against the defendant` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an order that an issue between the claimants and the defendant be stated and tried` THEN `o 61 r 5(1)(c) that an issue between the claimants and the defendant be stated and tried` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an order that the matter be adjourned` THEN `o 61 r 5(1)(d) that the matter be adjourned` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an order that further advertisements be made` THEN `o 61 r 5(1)(e) that further advertisements be made in addition to that required under Rule 3(6)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an order for the substitution of the claimant making the application with another claimant` THEN `o 61 r 5(1)(f) for the substitution of the claimant making the application with another claimant` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an order that the application be dismissed` THEN `o 61 r 5(1)(g) that the application be dismissed` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a direction or order of some other kind` THEN `o 61 r 5(1) another kind of direction or order` -- input mapping

§ `Order 61 -- Securities and Futures Act, civil liability actions -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Who is the claimant and who is the contravening person in my proceeding (rule 1)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 61 r 1(1)
@export Under Order 61, rule 1, which section of the Securities and Futures Act says who is the claimant in my proceeding?
GIVEN section IS A `roc11 the section my proceeding is under` @desc Under which section of the Securities and Futures Act is your proceeding brought?
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 1, which section of the Securities and Futures Act says who is the claimant in my proceeding` IS
    `o 61 r 1(1) "claimant" the section that gives its meaning` (`roc11 the proceeding as Order 61 has it` section)

@ref O 61 r 1(1)
@export Under Order 61, rule 1, which section of the Securities and Futures Act says who is the contravening person in my proceeding?
GIVEN section IS A `roc11 the section my proceeding is under` @desc Under which section of the Securities and Futures Act is your proceeding brought?
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 1, which section of the Securities and Futures Act says who is the contravening person in my proceeding` IS
    `o 61 r 1(1) "contravening person" the section that gives its meaning` (`roc11 the proceeding as Order 61 has it` section)

@ref O 61 r 1(1)
@export Under Order 61, rule 1, am I a defendant individual?
GIVEN `I am an individual` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an individual (not a company or other organisation)?
      `liable under 236H` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you liable to an order for a civil penalty under section 236H of the Securities and Futures Act?
      `Part XII contravention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order in respect of a contravention of a provision of Part XII of the Act?
      `committed by an organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the contravention committed by a corporation, partnership, limited liability partnership or unincorporated association?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 1, am I a defendant individual` IS
    `o 61 r 1(1) "defendant individual" the person is a defendant individual` `I am an individual` `liable under 236H` `Part XII contravention` `committed by an organisation`

@ref O 61 r 1(2)
@export Under Order 61, rule 1, do the Rules of Court on civil liability actions apply to my proceeding?
GIVEN section IS A `roc11 the section my proceeding is under` @desc Under which section of the Securities and Futures Act is your proceeding brought?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 1, do the Rules of Court on civil liability actions apply to my proceeding` IS
    `o 61 r 1(2) these Rules apply to the proceeding` (`roc11 the proceeding as Order 61 has it` section)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Starting my action, or asking for permission (rule 2)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 61 r 2(1)
@export Under Order 61, rule 2, is my action commenced by originating claim as the Rule requires?
GIVEN section IS A `roc11 the section my proceeding is under` @desc Under which section of the Securities and Futures Act is your action brought?
      `by originating claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you commence the action by originating claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 2, is my action commenced by originating claim as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 61 r 2(1) the action is commenced as the Rule requires` (`roc11 the proceeding as Order 61 has it` section) (IF `by originating claim` THEN `Originating claim` ELSE `Originating application`)

@ref O 61 r 2(2)
@export Under Order 61, rule 2, is my application for permission to commence an action made by originating application naming the right defendant?
GIVEN `for permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application for permission of the Court under section 235(1) or 236J(1) or (3) to commence an action under section 234, 236D, 236G or 236I?
      `by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by originating application?
      `names the right defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it name as the defendant the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 2, is my application for permission to commence an action made by originating application naming the right defendant` IS
    `o 61 r 2(2) the application for permission is made as the Rule requires` `for permission` (IF `by originating application` THEN `Originating application` ELSE Summons) `names the right defendant`

@ref O 61 r 2(3)
@export Under Order 61, rule 2(3), does another Order apply to my originating application?
GIVEN `under rule 2` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application an originating application under rule 2 of Order 61?
      `which provision` IS A STRING @desc Which provision are you asking about? (For example: Order 6 rule 11, Order 9, Order 15 rule 7.)
      `rule 2 modifies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does rule 2 expressly modify that provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 2(3), does another Order apply to my originating application` IS
    `o 61 r 2(3) the provision applies to the originating application` `under rule 2` `which provision` `rule 2 modifies it`

@ref O 61 r 2(4)
@export Under Order 61, rule 2(4), what has my affidavit supporting the application for permission left out that the Rule requires?
GIVEN `securities particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit set out particulars of the securities, futures contract or contract or arrangement in connection with the leveraged foreign exchange trading transaction in question?
      `circumstances of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out the circumstances leading to the entering into of the transaction?
      `circumstances of the loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out the circumstances leading to the loss suffered?
      `particulars of the loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out particulars of the loss suffered?
      `grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out the grounds on which the application is made?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 2(4), what has my affidavit supporting the application for permission left out that the Rule requires` IS
    `o 61 r 2(4) the matters the affidavit has not yet set out` (`o 61 r 2(4) affidavit` OF `securities particulars`, `circumstances of the transaction`, `circumstances of the loss`, `particulars of the loss`, `grounds`)

@ref O 61 r 2(5)
@export Under Order 61, rule 2(5), did I serve my application for permission and affidavit as the Rule requires in the first instance?
GIVEN `served on the right person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve the application and affidavit on the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be?
      `served on anyone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve them on any other person?
      `court directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Court direct that they be served on that other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 2(5), did I serve my application for permission and affidavit as the Rule requires in the first instance` IS
    `o 61 r 2(5) the application is served as the Rule requires in the first instance` `served on the right person` `served on anyone else` `court directed`

@ref O 61 r 2(6)
@export Under Order 61, rule 2(6), is my application for permission to continue a stayed action made as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `to continue a stayed action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application for permission of the Court to continue an action under section 234, 236D, 236G or 236I that was stayed under section 235(2) or 236J(1) or (3)?
      `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by summons?
      `in the stayed action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made in the stayed action?
      `supported by an affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it supported by an affidavit stating the grounds of the application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 2(6), is my application for permission to continue a stayed action made as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 61 r 2(6) the application to continue the stayed action is made as the Rule requires` `to continue a stayed action` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`) `in the stayed action` `supported by an affidavit`

@ref O 61 r 2(7)
@export Under Order 61, rule 2(7), did I serve my application to continue the stayed action as the Rule requires in the first instance?
GIVEN `served on the defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve the application and affidavit on the defendant?
      `served on anyone else` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve them on any other person?
      `court directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Court direct that they be served on that other person?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 2(7), did I serve my application to continue the stayed action as the Rule requires in the first instance` IS
    `o 61 r 2(7) the application to continue is served as the Rule requires in the first instance` `served on the defendant` `served on anyone else` `court directed`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Asking the Court for directions on claims for compensation (rule 3)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 61 r 3(1)
@export Under Order 61, rule 3(1), may I apply to the Court for directions on claims for compensation?
GIVEN `I seek compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a claimant seeking compensation from the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual?
      `convicted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that person convicted for a contravention of any provision of Part XII of the Act?
      `civil penalty order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an order for a civil penalty made against that person under section 232, 236B, 236C, 236E, 236F or 236H?
      `default or consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, was the order made by way of a default judgment or a consent order?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 3(1), may I apply to the Court for directions on claims for compensation` IS
    `o 61 r 3(1) the claimant may apply for directions on claims for compensation` `I seek compensation` `convicted` `civil penalty order` `default or consent`

@ref O 61 r 3(1)
@export Under Order 61, rule 3(1), may the Court fix a return date for hearing my application for directions?
GIVEN `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an application for directions under rule 3(1)?
      `section 236 permits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 236(2) (or section 236K(2) read with section 236(2)) of the Act permit the Court to fix a return date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 3(1), may the Court fix a return date for hearing my application for directions` IS
    `o 61 r 3(1) the Court may fix a return date for hearing the application` `I have applied` `section 236 permits`

@ref O 61 r 3(2)
@export Under Order 61, rule 3(2), am I barred from making my application for directions because the conviction or order is not yet final?
GIVEN `under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application one under rule 3(1)?
      `final` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the conviction, or the order making the civil penalty, been made final in accordance with section 236(4) or (5) (or section 236K(2) read with section 236(4) or (5))?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 3(2), am I barred from making my application for directions because the conviction or order is not yet final` IS
    `o 61 r 3(2) an application cannot yet be made because the conviction or order is not yet final` `under paragraph (1)` `final`

@ref O 61 r 3(3)
@export Under Order 61, rule 3(3), is my application for directions made by originating application?
GIVEN `under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application one under rule 3(1)?
      `by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you apply by originating application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 3(3), is my application for directions made by originating application` IS
    `o 61 r 3(3) the application for directions is made as the Rule requires` `under paragraph (1)` (IF `by originating application` THEN `Originating application` ELSE Summons)

@ref O 61 r 3(4)
@export Under Order 61, rule 3(4), does another Order apply to my application for directions?
GIVEN `under rule 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application an originating application under rule 3 of Order 61?
      `which provision` IS A STRING @desc Which provision are you asking about? (For example: Order 6 rule 11, Order 9, Order 15 rule 7.)
      `rule 3 modifies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does rule 3 expressly modify that provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 3(4), does another Order apply to my application for directions` IS
    `o 61 r 3(4) the provision applies to the originating application` `under rule 3` `which provision` `rule 3 modifies it`

@ref O 61 r 3(5)
@export Under Order 61, rule 3(5), must I serve my application for directions personally at least 28 clear days before the return date?
GIVEN `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that the application need not be served in this way?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 3(5), must I serve my application for directions personally at least 28 clear days before the return date` IS
    `o 61 r 3(5) the duty to serve the application personally in time arises` `the Court otherwise orders`

@ref O 61 r 3(5)
@export Under Order 61, rule 3(5), did I serve my application for directions as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that the application need not be served personally and in this time?
      `served personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you serve it personally on the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual, as the case may be?
      `the date I served it` IS A DATE @desc On what date did you serve it?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for serving it, that is the last day that leaves at least 28 clear days (or any longer time the Court directed) before the return date, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 3(5), did I serve my application for directions as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 61 r 3(5) the application is served as the Rule requires` `the Court otherwise orders` `served personally` `the date I served it` `the last day`

@ref O 61 r 3(6)
@export Under Order 61, rule 3(6), did I advertise my application for directions as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `in Form 91` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the advertisement in Form 91?
      `in English and Chinese dailies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it appear at least once in one English and one Chinese local daily newspaper?
      `in the newspaper the Court directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Court direct another newspaper, and did it appear there?
      `the date it appeared` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it appear?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for advertising it, that is the last day that leaves at least 21 clear days (or any longer time the Court directed) before the return date, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 3(6), did I advertise my application for directions as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 61 r 3(6) the application is advertised as the Rule requires` `in Form 91` `in English and Chinese dailies` `in the newspaper the Court directed` `the date it appeared` `the last day`

@ref O 61 r 3(7)
@export Under Order 61, rule 3(7), what has my advertisement left out that the Rule requires it to state?
GIVEN `day filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement state the day on which the application was filed?
      `applicant's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the name and address of the applicant?
      `I have a solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the applicant have a solicitor?
      `solicitor's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does it state the name and address of the applicant's solicitor?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 3(7), what has my advertisement left out that the Rule requires it to state` IS
    `o 61 r 3(7) the matters the advertisement has not yet stated` (`o 61 r 3(7) advertisement` OF `day filed`, `applicant's name and address`, `I have a solicitor`, `solicitor's name and address`)

@ref O 61 r 3(8)
@export Under Order 61, rule 3(8), is my application for directions deemed dismissed?
GIVEN `I complied with paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you (or your solicitor) comply with paragraph (5), the personal service? (Yes if the Court ordered otherwise.)
      `I complied with paragraph (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you (or your solicitor) comply with paragraph (6), the advertisement?
      `I complied with paragraph (7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you (or your solicitor) comply with paragraph (7), the contents of the advertisement?
      `the Court otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court otherwise directed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 3(8), is my application for directions deemed dismissed` IS
    `o 61 r 3(8) the application is deemed dismissed` `I complied with paragraph (5)` `I complied with paragraph (6)` `I complied with paragraph (7)` `the Court otherwise directs`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Proving my claim (rule 4)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 61 r 4(1)
@export Under Order 61, rule 4(1), must I file an affidavit stating my claim?
GIVEN `I desire to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you desire to claim compensation against the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual under section 236 or 236K in respect of the same contravention for which that person was convicted or had a civil penalty order made against them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 4(1), must I file an affidavit stating my claim` IS
    `o 61 r 4(1) the duty to file an affidavit of claim arises` `I desire to claim`

@ref O 61 r 4(1)
@export Under Order 61, rule 4(1), did I file my affidavit stating my claim in time?
GIVEN `I desire to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you desire to claim compensation under section 236 or 236K in respect of the same contravention?
      `I have filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you filed the affidavit?
      `the date I filed` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Give any date if not.)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for filing it, that is the last day that leaves at least 7 clear days before the return date, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 4(1), did I file my affidavit stating my claim in time` IS
    `o 61 r 4(1) the claimant files the affidavit of claim in time` `I desire to claim` (IF `I have filed` THEN JUST `the date I filed` ELSE NOTHING) `the date I am asking about` `the last day`

@ref O 61 r 4(2)
@export Under Order 61, rule 4(2), what has my affidavit stating my claim left out that the Rule requires?
GIVEN `exhibits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the affidavit supported by the relevant exhibits?
      `grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it explain the grounds on which my claim is made?
      `securities particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include particulars of the securities, futures contract or contract or arrangement in connection with the leveraged foreign exchange trading transaction in question?
      `circumstances of the transaction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the circumstances leading to the entering into of the transaction?
      `circumstances of the loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the circumstances leading to the loss suffered?
      `particulars of the loss` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include particulars of the loss suffered?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 4(2), what has my affidavit stating my claim left out that the Rule requires` IS
    `o 61 r 4(2) the matters the affidavit has not yet covered` (`o 61 r 4(2) affidavit` OF `exhibits`, `grounds`, `securities particulars`, `circumstances of the transaction`, `circumstances of the loss`, `particulars of the loss`)

@ref O 61 r 4(3)
@export Under Order 61, rule 4(3), may my exhibits include this exhibit?
GIVEN exhibit IS A `roc11 the exhibit I want to attach` @desc Which exhibit do you want to attach?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 4(3), may my exhibits include this exhibit` IS
    `o 61 r 4(3) the exhibits may include` (`roc11 the exhibit as Order 61 has it` exhibit)

@ref O 61 r 4(4)
@export Under Order 61, rule 4(4), did I serve a copy of my affidavit on the subject in time?
GIVEN `I have served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you served a copy of the affidavit on the contravening person, the defendant corporation, the defendant partnership or the defendant individual (the subject)?
      `the date I served` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Give any date if not.)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the 3 days after the filing of the affidavit, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 4(4), did I serve a copy of my affidavit on the subject in time` IS
    `o 61 r 4(4) the claimant serves a copy of the affidavit on the subject in time` (IF `I have served` THEN JUST `the date I served` ELSE NOTHING) `the date I am asking about` `the last day`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `What the Court may do at the hearing (rule 5)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 61 r 5(1)
@export Under Order 61, rule 5(1), may the Court give directions or make orders on the hearing of the application?
GIVEN `hearing under rule 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court hearing an application made under rule 3(1)?
      `all served persons appear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the persons on whom the application has been served appear?
      `all claimants appear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all claimants who have filed their affidavits of claim appear?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 5(1), may the Court give directions or make orders on the hearing of the application` IS
    `o 61 r 5(1) the Court may give directions or make orders on the hearing` `hearing under rule 3(1)` `all served persons appear` `all claimants appear`

@ref O 61 r 5(1)
@export Under Order 61, rule 5(1), may the Court give this kind of direction or make this kind of order?
GIVEN kind IS A `roc11 the direction or order asked for` @desc What direction or order is asked for?
      `hearing under rule 3(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court hearing an application made under rule 3(1)?
      `all served persons appear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the persons on whom the application has been served appear?
      `all claimants appear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all claimants who have filed their affidavits of claim appear?
      `best adapted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Court think the direction or order best adapted to secure the just, expeditious and economical disposal of the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 5(1), may the Court give this kind of direction or make this kind of order` IS
    `o 61 r 5(1) the Court may give this kind of direction or make this kind of order` (`roc11 the kind of direction or order as Order 61 has it` kind) `hearing under rule 3(1)` `all served persons appear` `all claimants appear` `best adapted`

@ref O 61 r 5(2)
@export Under Order 61, rule 5(2), may the Court make an order against me as the contravening person?
GIVEN `I was duly served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you duly served with the application under rule 3?
      `I did not appear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not appear on the hearing of the application?
      `I appeared but did not comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you appear but fail or refuse to comply with an order made in the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 5(2), may the Court make an order against me as the contravening person` IS
    `o 61 r 5(2) the Court may make such order as it deems appropriate against the contravening person` `I was duly served` `I did not appear` `I appeared but did not comply`

@ref O 61 r 5(3)
@export Under Order 61, rule 5(3), may the Court declare me forever barred from bringing any claim?
GIVEN `I filed an affidavit of claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file an affidavit of claim under rule 4?
      `I did not appear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not appear on the hearing of the application?
      `I appeared but did not comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you appear but fail or refuse to comply with an order made in the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 5(3), may the Court declare me forever barred from bringing any claim` IS
    `o 61 r 5(3) the Court may declare the claimant forever barred` `I filed an affidavit of claim` `I did not appear` `I appeared but did not comply`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Costs, other matters and the trial of an issue (rules 6 and 7)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 61 r 6
@export Under Order 61, rule 6, may the Court make the order as to costs or any other matter that is asked for?
GIVEN `in or for the purposes of proceedings in this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order asked for in or for the purposes of proceedings under Order 61?
      `rules 1 to 5 provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of rules 1 to 5 of Order 61 provide otherwise on the matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 6, may the Court make the order as to costs or any other matter that is asked for` IS
    `o 61 r 6 the Court may make such order as to costs or any other matter as it thinks just` `in or for the purposes of proceedings in this Order` `rules 1 to 5 provide otherwise`

@ref O 61 r 7(1)
@export Under Order 61, rule 7(1), does Order 15 apply to the trial of the issue stated?
GIVEN `issue stated under 5(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trial of an issue stated under rule 5(1)(c)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 7(1), does Order 15 apply to the trial of the issue stated` IS
    `o 61 r 7(1) Order 15 applies to the trial of the issue` `issue stated under 5(1)(c)`

@ref O 61 r 7(2)
@export Under Order 61, rule 7(2), may the Court that tries the issue give judgment or make an order finally disposing of all questions?
GIVEN `the Court tries the issue stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court the one by which an issue stated is tried?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 61, rule 7(2), may the Court that tries the issue give judgment or make an order finally disposing of all questions` IS
    `o 61 r 7(2) the Court may give such judgment or make such order as finally to dispose of all questions` `the Court tries the issue stated`

-- ===========================================================================
-- ORDER 62 -- SECURITIES AND FUTURES ACT, CIVIL PENALTY ACTIONS -- wiring
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `roc11 the section the Authority sues under` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 the Authority sues under section 137ZD`
    `roc11 the Authority sues under section 232`
    `roc11 the Authority sues under section 236B(3)`
    `roc11 the Authority sues under section 236C`
    `roc11 the Authority sues under section 236E(3)`
    `roc11 the Authority sues under section 236F`
    `roc11 the Authority sues under section 236H`
    `roc11 the Authority sues under another section`

GIVEN section IS A `roc11 the section the Authority sues under`
GIVETH A `o 62 r 1 proceeding`
`roc11 the proceeding as Order 62 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER section
    WHEN `roc11 the Authority sues under section 137ZD` THEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 137ZD` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 the Authority sues under section 232` THEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 232` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 the Authority sues under section 236B(3)` THEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 236B(3)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 the Authority sues under section 236C` THEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 236C` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 the Authority sues under section 236E(3)` THEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 236E(3)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 the Authority sues under section 236F` THEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 236F` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 the Authority sues under section 236H` THEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under section 236H` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 the Authority sues under another section` THEN `o 62 r 1 a proceeding under another section` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 how the Authority sues` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 by a solicitor`
    `roc11 in person`
    `roc11 in another way`

GIVEN how IS A `roc11 how the Authority sues`
GIVETH A `o 62 r 2(4) how the Authority sues`
`roc11 how the Authority sues as Order 62 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `roc11 by a solicitor` THEN `o 62 r 2(4)(a) the Authority sues by a solicitor` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 in person` THEN `o 62 r 2(4)(b) the Authority sues in person` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 in another way` THEN `o 62 r 2(4) the Authority sues in another way` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 the course the Authority takes against the defendant in default` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 applying for judgment against the defendant in default and proceeding against the others`
    `roc11 setting down the action for judgment against the defendant in default with the others`

GIVEN course IS A `roc11 the course the Authority takes against the defendant in default`
GIVETH A `o 62 r 5(2) course`
`roc11 the course as Order 62 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER course
    WHEN `roc11 applying for judgment against the defendant in default and proceeding against the others` THEN `o 62 r 5(2)(a) apply for judgment against the defendant in default and proceed against the others` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 setting down the action for judgment against the defendant in default with the others` THEN `o 62 r 5(2)(b) set down the action for judgment against the defendant in default with the others` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 the document I ask the Authority to produce, first list` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 a book I voluntarily produced to the Authority`
    `roc11 a book produced to or seized by the Authority under section 163, 163A or 164`
    `roc11 the Authority's acknowledgment of receipt for such a book`
    `roc11 correspondence between the Authority or its solicitors and me or my agents or solicitors`
    `roc11 an examination requirement served on me under section 154`
    `roc11 a production requirement served on me under section 163`
    `roc11 a written notice or production requirement about my premises under section 163A`
    `roc11 a warrant about my premises under section 164`
    `roc11 a written record under section 158 of what I said to the Authority`
    `roc11 trading information relating to my trading which the Authority relies on`
    `roc11 another document which the Authority relies on`
    `roc11 a document of another kind in the first list`

GIVEN kind IS A `roc11 the document I ask the Authority to produce, first list`
GIVETH A `o 62 r 8(4) kind of document`
`roc11 the first-list document as Order 62 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `roc11 a book I voluntarily produced to the Authority` THEN `o 62 r 8(4)(a) a book voluntarily produced by the defendant or contravening person to the Authority` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a book produced to or seized by the Authority under section 163, 163A or 164` THEN `o 62 r 8(4)(b) a book produced by or seized from any person pursuant to section 163, 163A or 164` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 the Authority's acknowledgment of receipt for such a book` THEN `o 62 r 8(4)(c) an acknowledgment of receipt issued by the Authority for a book referred to in (a) or (b)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 correspondence between the Authority or its solicitors and me or my agents or solicitors` THEN `o 62 r 8(4)(d) correspondence between the Authority or its solicitors and the defendant or contravening person, or their agents or solicitors` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an examination requirement served on me under section 154` THEN `o 62 r 8(4)(e) an examination requirement served on the defendant or contravening person pursuant to section 154` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a production requirement served on me under section 163` THEN `o 62 r 8(4)(f) a production requirement served on the defendant or contravening person pursuant to section 163` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a written notice or production requirement about my premises under section 163A` THEN `o 62 r 8(4)(g) a written notice or written production requirement in respect of the premises pursuant to section 163A` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a warrant about my premises under section 164` THEN `o 62 r 8(4)(h) a warrant issued in respect of the premises pursuant to section 164` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a written record under section 158 of what I said to the Authority` THEN `o 62 r 8(4)(i) a written record made pursuant to section 158 of statements made to the Authority` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 trading information relating to my trading which the Authority relies on` THEN `o 62 r 8(4)(j) trading information relating to the trading activities which the Authority relies on or will rely on in the action` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 another document which the Authority relies on` THEN `o 62 r 8(4)(k) any other document which the Authority relies on or will rely on in the action` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a document of another kind in the first list` THEN `o 62 r 8(4) a document of another kind` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 the document I ask the Authority to produce, second list` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 a book I voluntarily produced to a Commercial Affairs Officer or a police officer`
    `roc11 a book or document produced to such an officer under section 20 of the Code`
    `roc11 a book or document seized by such an officer under section 35 of the Code`
    `roc11 a book or document placed in safe custody by such an officer under section 78 of the Code`
    `roc11 an acknowledgment of receipt for one of those four`
    `roc11 an acknowledgment of receipt for another thing produced under section 20 of the Code`
    `roc11 an acknowledgment of receipt for other property seized under section 35 of the Code`
    `roc11 an acknowledgment of receipt for another article placed in safe custody under section 78 of the Code`
    `roc11 a written order issued by such an officer under section 20 of the Code`
    `roc11 a written order issued to me by such an officer under section 21 of the Code`
    `roc11 a statement made by any person to such an officer under section 22 of the Code`
    `roc11 a statement made by me to such an officer under section 23 of the Code`
    `roc11 a search warrant about my premises under section 24 of the Code`
    `roc11 a document of another kind in the second list`

GIVEN kind IS A `roc11 the document I ask the Authority to produce, second list`
GIVETH A `o 62 r 8(5) kind of document`
`roc11 the second-list document as Order 62 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `roc11 a book I voluntarily produced to a Commercial Affairs Officer or a police officer` THEN `o 62 r 8(5)(a) a book voluntarily produced by the defendant or contravening person to a Commercial Affairs Officer or a police officer` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a book or document produced to such an officer under section 20 of the Code` THEN `o 62 r 8(5)(b) a book or document produced by any person to such an officer under section 20 of the Code` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a book or document seized by such an officer under section 35 of the Code` THEN `o 62 r 8(5)(c) a book or document seized by such an officer under section 35 of the Code` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a book or document placed in safe custody by such an officer under section 78 of the Code` THEN `o 62 r 8(5)(d) a book or document placed in safe custody by such an officer under section 78 of the Code` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an acknowledgment of receipt for one of those four` THEN `o 62 r 8(5)(e)(i) an acknowledgment of receipt for a book or document referred to in (a), (b), (c) or (d)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an acknowledgment of receipt for another thing produced under section 20 of the Code` THEN `o 62 r 8(5)(e)(ii) an acknowledgment of receipt for any other thing produced under section 20 of the Code` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an acknowledgment of receipt for other property seized under section 35 of the Code` THEN `o 62 r 8(5)(e)(iii) an acknowledgment of receipt for any other property seized under section 35 of the Code` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an acknowledgment of receipt for another article placed in safe custody under section 78 of the Code` THEN `o 62 r 8(5)(e)(iv) an acknowledgment of receipt for any other article placed in safe custody under section 78 of the Code` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a written order issued by such an officer under section 20 of the Code` THEN `o 62 r 8(5)(f) a written order issued by such an officer under section 20 of the Code` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a written order issued to me by such an officer under section 21 of the Code` THEN `o 62 r 8(5)(g) a written order issued to the defendant or contravening person by such an officer under section 21 of the Code` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a statement made by any person to such an officer under section 22 of the Code` THEN `o 62 r 8(5)(h) a statement made by any person to such an officer under section 22 of the Code` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a statement made by me to such an officer under section 23 of the Code` THEN `o 62 r 8(5)(i) a statement made by the defendant or contravening person to such an officer under section 23 of the Code` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a search warrant about my premises under section 24 of the Code` THEN `o 62 r 8(5)(j) a search warrant issued in respect of the premises under section 24 of the Code` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a document of another kind in the second list` THEN `o 62 r 8(5) a document of another kind` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 the description the document falls within` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 a supervisory document under a written law other than the Act`
    `roc11 a complaint or request to investigate, or a similar document`
    `roc11 the Authority's internal books`
    `roc11 correspondence with the Government or a statutory body`
    `roc11 a document the Authority sent to the Government or a statutory body, not provided under section 168B`
    `roc11 a document the Authority received from the Government or a statutory body, not referred to in paragraph (5)`
    `roc11 correspondence with an overseas regulatory authority`
    `roc11 correspondence with an exchange or clearing house`
    `roc11 correspondence with the complainant`
    `roc11 none of those descriptions`

GIVEN description IS A `roc11 the description the document falls within`
GIVETH A `o 62 r 8(6) description`
`roc11 the description as Order 62 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER description
    WHEN `roc11 a supervisory document under a written law other than the Act` THEN `o 62 r 8(6)(a) a document in the Authority's possession, custody or power as a result of its supervisory functions, duties or powers under a written law other than the Act` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a complaint or request to investigate, or a similar document` THEN `o 62 r 8(6)(b) a complaint or request received by the Authority to investigate or provide assistance on a possible or alleged contravention of the Act, or a similar document received by the Authority` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 the Authority's internal books` THEN `o 62 r 8(6)(c) the Authority's internal books` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 correspondence with the Government or a statutory body` THEN `o 62 r 8(6)(d) correspondence between the Authority and the Government or a statutory body` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a document the Authority sent to the Government or a statutory body, not provided under section 168B` THEN `o 62 r 8(6)(e) a document sent by the Authority to the Government or a statutory body but not provided under section 168B` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a document the Authority received from the Government or a statutory body, not referred to in paragraph (5)` THEN `o 62 r 8(6)(f) a document received by the Authority from the Government or a statutory body but not referred to in paragraph (5)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 correspondence with an overseas regulatory authority` THEN `o 62 r 8(6)(g)(i) correspondence between the Authority and an overseas regulatory authority` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 correspondence with an exchange or clearing house` THEN `o 62 r 8(6)(g)(ii) correspondence between the Authority and a securities exchange, futures exchange or clearing house` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 correspondence with the complainant` THEN `o 62 r 8(6)(g)(iii) correspondence between the Authority and the complainant` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 none of those descriptions` THEN `o 62 r 8(6) none of these descriptions` -- input mapping

§ `Order 62 -- Securities and Futures Act, civil penalty actions -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Definitions and application (rule 1)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 62 r 1(1) "civil penalty action"
@export Under Order 62, rule 1, is the Authority's proceeding against me a civil penalty action?
GIVEN `commenced by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the proceeding commenced by the Monetary Authority of Singapore?
      `the section` IS A `roc11 the section the Authority sues under` @desc Under which section of the Securities and Futures Act does the Authority sue: 137ZD, 232, 236B(3), 236C, 236E(3), 236F, 236H, or another?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 1, is the Authority's proceeding against me a civil penalty action` IS
    `o 62 r 1(1) "civil penalty action" the proceeding is a civil penalty action` `commenced by the Authority` (`roc11 the proceeding as Order 62 has it` `the section`)

@ref O 62 r 1(1)
@export Under Order 62, rule 1, does a reference to a section in this Order mean a section of the Securities and Futures Act?
GIVEN `the reference is to a section` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the reference one to a section?
      `the reference names another Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the reference name another Act expressly?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 1, does a reference to a section in this Order mean a section of the Securities and Futures Act` IS
    `o 62 r 1(1) a reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act` `the reference is to a section` `the reference names another Act`

@ref O 62 r 1(1) "Act"
@export Under Order 62, rule 1, which Act does this Order mean by the Act?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 1, which Act does this Order mean by the Act` IS
    `o 62 r 1(1) the Act`

@ref O 62 r 1(1) "Authority"
@export Under Order 62, rule 1, who is the Authority?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 1, who is the Authority` IS
    `o 62 r 1(1) "Authority" who it is`

@ref O 62 r 1(1) "Code"
@export Under Order 62, rule 1, which Code does this Order mean by the Code?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 1, which Code does this Order mean by the Code` IS
    `o 62 r 1(1) "Code" which Code`

@ref O 62 r 1(1) "Commercial Affairs Officer"
@export Under Order 62, rule 1, is the officer who dealt with me a Commercial Affairs Officer?
GIVEN `appointed under section 64 of the Police Force Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the officer appointed under section 64 of the Police Force Act as a Commercial Affairs Officer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 1, is the officer who dealt with me a Commercial Affairs Officer` IS
    `o 62 r 1(1) "Commercial Affairs Officer" the person is a Commercial Affairs Officer` `appointed under section 64 of the Police Force Act`

@ref O 62 r 1(1) "contravening person"
@export Under Order 62, rule 1, which section of the Securities and Futures Act says who is the contravening person in the Authority's proceeding against me?
GIVEN `the section` IS A `roc11 the section the Authority sues under` @desc Under which section of the Securities and Futures Act does the Authority sue: 137ZD, 232, 236B(3), 236C, 236E(3), 236F, 236H, or another?
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 1, which section of the Securities and Futures Act says who is the contravening person in the Authority's proceeding against me` IS
    `o 62 r 1(1) "contravening person" the section that gives its meaning` (`roc11 the proceeding as Order 62 has it` `the section`)

@ref O 62 r 1(1) "police officer"
@export Under Order 62, rule 1, is the officer who dealt with me a police officer?
GIVEN `in the Commercial Affairs Department` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the officer a member of the Singapore Police Force deployed in the Commercial Affairs Department of that Force?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 1, is the officer who dealt with me a police officer` IS
    `o 62 r 1(1) "police officer" the person is a police officer` `in the Commercial Affairs Department`

@ref O 62 r 1(2)
@export Under Order 62, rule 1, do the Rules of Court apply to the Authority's proceeding against me?
GIVEN `the section` IS A `roc11 the section the Authority sues under` @desc Under which section of the Securities and Futures Act does the Authority sue: 137ZD, 232, 236B(3), 236C, 236E(3), 236F, 236H, or another?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 1, do the Rules of Court apply to the Authority's proceeding against me` IS
    `o 62 r 1(2) these Rules apply to the proceeding` (`roc11 the proceeding as Order 62 has it` `the section`)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Commencement of civil penalty action, etc. (rule 2)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 62 r 2(1)
@export Under Order 62, rule 2(1), has the Authority commenced the civil penalty action against me as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a civil penalty action?
      `by originating claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it commenced by originating claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 2(1), has the Authority commenced the civil penalty action against me as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 62 r 2(1) the civil penalty action is commenced as the Rule requires` `it is a civil penalty action` (IF `by originating claim` THEN `Originating claim` ELSE `Originating application`)

@ref O 62 r 2(2)
@export Under Order 62, rule 2(2), does a given provision of Order 6 apply to the civil penalty action against me?
GIVEN `it is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a civil penalty action?
      `which provision` IS A STRING @desc Which provision do you ask about, written for example as "Order 6 rule 2" or "Order 6 rule 5(3)"?
      `rule 2 modifies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Rule 2 modify that provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 2(2), does a given provision of Order 6 apply to the civil penalty action against me` IS
    `o 62 r 2(2) the provision applies to the civil penalty action` `it is a civil penalty action` `which provision` `rule 2 modifies it`

@ref O 62 r 2(3)
@export Under Order 62, rule 2(3), what has the Authority's endorsement on the originating claim against me left out that the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the provision contravened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the provision of the Act contravened by the defendant or under which the defendant is liable for the payment of a civil penalty?
      `the Authority's address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the address of the Authority?
      `the Authority sues by a solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Authority sue by a solicitor?
      `the solicitor's details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does it state the solicitor's name or firm and a business address of the solicitor?
      `I am sued in a representative capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a defendant sued in a representative capacity?
      `the capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does it state the capacity in which the defendant is sued?
      `the number of days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the number of days within which a notice of intention to contest or not contest is to be filed and served under Order 6, Rule 6?
      `a statement of claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a statement of claim endorsed?
      `a concise statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not, is a concise statement of the nature of the claim made or the relief or remedy required endorsed?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 2(3), what has the Authority's endorsement on the originating claim against me left out that the Rule requires` IS
    `o 62 r 2(3) the matters the endorsement has not yet stated` (`o 62 r 2(3) endorsement` OF `the provision contravened`, `the Authority's address`, `the Authority sues by a solicitor`, `the solicitor's details`, `I am sued in a representative capacity`, `the capacity`, `the number of days`, `a statement of claim`, `a concise statement`)

@ref O 62 r 2(3)
@export Under Order 62, rule 2(3), does the Authority's endorsement on the originating claim against me state what the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a civil penalty action?
      `the provision contravened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the endorsement state the provision of the Act contravened by the defendant or under which the defendant is liable for the payment of a civil penalty?
      `the Authority's address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the address of the Authority?
      `the Authority sues by a solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Authority sue by a solicitor?
      `the solicitor's details` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does it state the solicitor's name or firm and a business address of the solicitor?
      `I am sued in a representative capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a defendant sued in a representative capacity?
      `the capacity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does it state the capacity in which the defendant is sued?
      `the number of days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the number of days within which a notice of intention to contest or not contest is to be filed and served under Order 6, Rule 6?
      `a statement of claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a statement of claim endorsed?
      `a concise statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not, is a concise statement of the nature of the claim made or the relief or remedy required endorsed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 2(3), does the Authority's endorsement on the originating claim against me state what the Rule requires` IS
    `o 62 r 2(3) the endorsement states what the Rule requires` `it is a civil penalty action` (`o 62 r 2(3) endorsement` OF `the provision contravened`, `the Authority's address`, `the Authority sues by a solicitor`, `the solicitor's details`, `I am sued in a representative capacity`, `the capacity`, `the number of days`, `a statement of claim`, `a concise statement`)

@ref O 62 r 2(4)
@export Under Order 62, rule 2(4), what is the Authority's address for service?
GIVEN how IS A `roc11 how the Authority sues` @desc Does the Authority sue by a solicitor, in person, or in another way?
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 2(4), what is the Authority's address for service` IS
    `o 62 r 2(4) the address for service of the Authority` (`roc11 how the Authority sues as Order 62 has it` how)

@ref O 62 r 2(5)
@export Under Order 62, rule 2(5), which provision of the Securities and Futures Act refers to the Public Prosecutor's consent in the Authority's proceeding against me?
GIVEN `the section` IS A `roc11 the section the Authority sues under` @desc Under which section of the Securities and Futures Act does the Authority sue: 137ZD, 232, 236B(3), 236C, 236E(3), 236F, 236H, or another?
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 2(5), which provision of the Securities and Futures Act refers to the Public Prosecutor's consent in the Authority's proceeding against me` IS
    `o 62 r 2(5) the provision that refers to the consent of the Public Prosecutor` (`roc11 the proceeding as Order 62 has it` `the section`)

@ref O 62 r 2(5)
@export Under Order 62, rule 2(5), must the Authority file the consent of the Public Prosecutor with the Registrar?
GIVEN `it presents the originating claim for sealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority presenting the originating claim for sealing?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 2(5), must the Authority file the consent of the Public Prosecutor with the Registrar` IS
    `o 62 r 2(5) the duty to file the consent of the Public Prosecutor arises` `it presents the originating claim for sealing`

@ref O 62 r 2(5)
@export Under Order 62, rule 2(5), did the Authority file the consent of the Public Prosecutor as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it presented the originating claim for sealing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Authority present the originating claim for sealing?
      `it filed the consent with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it file the consent of the Public Prosecutor with the Registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 2(5), did the Authority file the consent of the Public Prosecutor as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 62 r 2(5) the Authority files the consent as the Rule requires` `it presented the originating claim for sealing` `it filed the consent with the Registrar`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Provisions applicable to pleadings (rule 3)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 62 r 3(1)
@export Under Order 62, rule 3(1), does a given provision apply to the pleadings in the civil penalty action against me?
GIVEN `it is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a civil penalty action?
      `which provision` IS A STRING @desc Which provision do you ask about, written for example as "Order 6 rule 7(3)" or "Order 9 rule 14"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 3(1), does a given provision apply to the pleadings in the civil penalty action against me` IS
    `o 62 r 3(1) the provision applies to the pleadings in the civil penalty action` `it is a civil penalty action` `which provision`

@ref O 62 r 3(2)
@export Under Order 62, rule 3(2), does the defence of tender apply to the civil penalty action against me?
GIVEN `it is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a civil penalty action?
      `the defence is the defence of tender` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the defence you ask about the defence of tender?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 3(2), does the defence of tender apply to the civil penalty action against me` IS
    `o 62 r 3(2) the defence applies to the civil penalty action` `it is a civil penalty action` `the defence is the defence of tender`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Default of notice of intention to contest or not contest (rule 4)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 62 r 4(1)
@export Under Order 62, rule 4(1), may the Authority apply to the Court for judgment against me for not filing a notice of intention to contest or not contest?
GIVEN `only a penalty order is sought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority applied for no order apart from an order for a civil penalty against you in respect of the same contravention?
      `I failed to file and serve the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to file and serve a notice of intention to contest or not contest?
      `the date the Authority applies` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the Authority apply, or are you asking about?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for filing and serving the notice, counted as Order 6, Rule 6 and Order 3, Rule 3 count it?
      `an affidavit of service is filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority filed an affidavit proving due service of the originating claim on you?
      `the statement of claim was endorsed or served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement of claim endorsed on or served with the originating claim?
      `the statement of claim was served after` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not, has the Authority served a statement of claim on you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 4(1), may the Authority apply to the Court for judgment against me for not filing a notice of intention to contest or not contest` IS
    `o 62 r 4(1) the Authority may apply to the Court for judgment` `only a penalty order is sought` `I failed to file and serve the notice` `the date the Authority applies` `the last day` `an affidavit of service is filed` `the statement of claim was endorsed or served` `the statement of claim was served after`

@ref O 62 r 4(1)
@export Under Order 62, rule 4(1), must the Court give the Authority such judgment as it appears entitled to?
GIVEN `the application is being heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority's application for judgment being heard?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 4(1), must the Court give the Authority such judgment as it appears entitled to` IS
    `o 62 r 4(1) the Court must give such judgment as the Authority appears entitled to` `the application is being heard`

@ref O 62 r 4(2)
@export Under Order 62, rule 4(2), is the Authority's application for judgment made as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it is an application under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application under Rule 4(1)?
      `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by summons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 4(2), is the Authority's application for judgment made as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 62 r 4(2) the application is made as the Rule requires` `it is an application under paragraph (1)` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`)

@ref O 62 r 4(3)
@export Under Order 62, rule 4(3), may the Authority proceed with the civil penalty action as if I had filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest?
GIVEN `another order is also sought` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority applied for another order in addition to an order for a civil penalty against you in respect of the same contravention?
      `I failed to file and serve the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to file and serve a notice of intention to contest or not contest?
      `the date the Authority proceeds` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the Authority proceed, or are you asking about?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for filing and serving the notice, counted as Order 6, Rule 6 and Order 3, Rule 3 count it?
      `an affidavit of service is filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Authority filed an affidavit proving due service of the originating claim on you?
      `the statement of claim was endorsed or served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the statement of claim endorsed on or served with the originating claim?
      `the statement of claim was served after` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If not, has the Authority served a statement of claim on you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 4(3), may the Authority proceed with the civil penalty action as if I had filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest` IS
    `o 62 r 4(3) the Authority may proceed as if the defendant had filed and served a notice of intention to contest or not contest` `another order is also sought` `I failed to file and serve the notice` `the date the Authority proceeds` `the last day` `an affidavit of service is filed` `the statement of claim was endorsed or served` `the statement of claim was served after`

@ref O 62 r 4(4)
@export Under Order 62, rule 4(4), may the Authority enter judgment against me for costs?
GIVEN `it has become unnecessary to proceed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has it become unnecessary for the Authority to proceed with the civil penalty action because you satisfied the claim or complied with its demands or for any other like reason?
      `I failed to file and serve the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you fail to file and serve a notice of intention to contest or not contest?
      `the date the Authority enters judgment` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the Authority enter judgment, or are you asking about?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for filing and serving the notice, counted as Order 6, Rule 6 and Order 3, Rule 3 count it?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 4(4), may the Authority enter judgment against me for costs` IS
    `o 62 r 4(4) the Authority may enter judgment against the defendant for costs` `it has become unnecessary to proceed` `I failed to file and serve the notice` `the date the Authority enters judgment` `the last day` `the Court has given permission`

@ref O 62 r 4(5)
@export Under Order 62, rule 4(5), is the Authority's application for permission made as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it is an application for permission under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for permission under Rule 4(4)?
      `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by summons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 4(5), is the Authority's application for permission made as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 62 r 4(5) the application for permission is made as the Rule requires` `it is an application for permission under paragraph (4)` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`)

@ref O 62 r 4(5)
@export Under Order 62, rule 4(5), must the Authority serve the summons on me?
GIVEN `it is an application for permission under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for permission under Rule 4(4)?
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court otherwise ordered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 4(5), must the Authority serve the summons on me` IS
    `o 62 r 4(5) the duty to serve the summons on the defendant arises` `it is an application for permission under paragraph (4)` `the Court otherwise orders`

@ref O 62 r 4(5)
@export Under Order 62, rule 4(5), has the Authority served the summons on me as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it is an application for permission under paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for permission under Rule 4(4)?
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court otherwise ordered?
      `the summons was served on me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the summons served on you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 4(5), has the Authority served the summons on me as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 62 r 4(5) the summons is served on the defendant as the Rule requires` `it is an application for permission under paragraph (4)` `the Court otherwise orders` `the summons was served on me`

@ref O 62 r 4(6)
@export Under Order 62, rule 4(6), does a given provision apply to the civil penalty action against me?
GIVEN `it is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a civil penalty action?
      `which provision` IS A STRING @desc Which provision do you ask about, written for example as "Order 3 rule 2(9)" or "Order 6 rule 6(5)"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 4(6), does a given provision apply to the civil penalty action against me` IS
    `o 62 r 4(6) the provision applies to the civil penalty action` `it is a civil penalty action` `which provision`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Default of defence (rule 5)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 62 r 5(1)
@export Under Order 62, rule 5(1), may the Authority apply to the Court for judgment against me for not serving a defence?
GIVEN `no defence was served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the defendant, or all the defendants, fail to serve a defence on the Authority?
      `the date the Authority applies` IS A DATE @desc On what date does the Authority apply, or are you asking about?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the period fixed under the Rules for service of the defence, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 5(1), may the Authority apply to the Court for judgment against me for not serving a defence` IS
    `o 62 r 5(1) the Authority may apply to the Court for judgment` `no defence was served` `the date the Authority applies` `the last day`

@ref O 62 r 5(1)
@export Under Order 62, rule 5(1), must the Court give the Authority such judgment as it appears entitled to on the default of defence?
GIVEN `the application is being heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Authority's application for judgment being heard?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 5(1), must the Court give the Authority such judgment as it appears entitled to on the default of defence` IS
    `o 62 r 5(1) the Court must give such judgment as the Authority appears entitled to` `the application is being heard`

@ref O 62 r 5(2)
@export Under Order 62, rule 5(2), may the Authority take this course against a defendant in default?
GIVEN `the course` IS A `roc11 the course the Authority takes against the defendant in default` @desc Does the Authority apply for judgment against the defendant in default and proceed against the others, or set down the action for judgment against the defendant in default with the others?
      `more than one defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the action against more than one defendant?
      `one makes default` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of the defendants make default as mentioned in Rule 5(1)?
      `severable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the claim against the defendant in default severable from the claim against the other defendants?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 5(2), may the Authority take this course against a defendant in default` IS
    `o 62 r 5(2) the Authority may take the course` (`roc11 the course as Order 62 has it` `the course`) `more than one defendant` `one makes default` `severable`

@ref O 62 r 5(3)
@export Under Order 62, rule 5(3), is the Authority's application for judgment on the default of defence made as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it is an application under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application under Rule 5(1)?
      `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by summons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 5(3), is the Authority's application for judgment on the default of defence made as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 62 r 5(3) the application is made as the Rule requires` `it is an application under paragraph (1)` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`)

@ref O 62 r 5(4)
@export Under Order 62, rule 5(4), does a given provision apply to the civil penalty action against me?
GIVEN `it is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a civil penalty action?
      `which provision` IS A STRING @desc Which provision do you ask about, written for example as "Order 3 rule 2(10)" or "Order 6 rule 9(3)"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 5(4), does a given provision apply to the civil penalty action against me` IS
    `o 62 r 5(4) the provision applies to the civil penalty action` `it is a civil penalty action` `which provision`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Joinder and third party proceedings (rules 6 and 7)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 62 r 6
@export Under Order 62, rule 6, is the Authority required to make or add another person as a defendant to the civil penalty action?
GIVEN `it is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a civil penalty action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 6, is the Authority required to make or add another person as a defendant to the civil penalty action` IS
    `o 62 r 6 the Authority is required to make or add a person as a defendant` `it is a civil penalty action`

@ref O 62 r 7(1)
@export Under Order 62, rule 7(1), may I issue a third party notice in the civil penalty action against me?
GIVEN `it is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a civil penalty action?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court given permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 7(1), may I issue a third party notice in the civil penalty action against me` IS
    `o 62 r 7(1) the third party notice may be issued` `it is a civil penalty action` `the Court has given permission`

@ref O 62 r 7(2)
@export Under Order 62, rule 7(2), which form must my summons for permission be in?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 7(2), which form must my summons for permission be in` IS
    `o 62 r 7(2) the form of the summons`

@ref O 62 r 7(2)
@export Under Order 62, rule 7(2), is my application for permission made and served as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `it is an application for permission under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it an application for the grant of permission to issue a third party notice?
      `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it made by summons?
      `in Form 22` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the summons in Form 22?
      `served on the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the summons served on the Authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 7(2), is my application for permission made and served as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 62 r 7(2) the application for permission is made and served as the Rule requires` `it is an application for permission under paragraph (1)` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`) `in Form 22` `served on the Authority`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Production and inspection of documents (rule 8)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 62 r 8(1)
@export Under Order 62, rule 8(1), does Order 11 apply to the civil penalty action against me?
GIVEN `it is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a civil penalty action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 8(1), does Order 11 apply to the civil penalty action against me` IS
    `o 62 r 8(1) Order 11 applies to the civil penalty action` `it is a civil penalty action`

@ref O 62 r 8(2)
@export Under Order 62, rule 8(2), may the Court require the Authority to give production of documents or produce them for inspection?
GIVEN `it is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a civil penalty action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 8(2), may the Court require the Authority to give production of documents or produce them for inspection` IS
    `o 62 r 8(2) the Authority may be required to give production of documents or produce them for inspection` `it is a civil penalty action`

@ref O 62 r 8(3)
@export Under Order 62, rule 8(3), does an order under Order 11 require disclosure of a document whose withholding is authorised on the ground of the public interest?
GIVEN `the order was made under Order 11` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the order made under Order 11?
      `withholding is authorised` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the withholding of the document authorised or required under a written law or rule of law on the ground that its disclosure would be injurious to the public interest?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 8(3), does an order under Order 11 require disclosure of a document whose withholding is authorised on the ground of the public interest` IS
    `o 62 r 8(3) the order requires disclosure of the document` `the order was made under Order 11` `withholding is authorised`

@ref O 62 r 8(4)
@export Under Order 62, rule 8(4), may the Authority be ordered to give production of this document or produce it for inspection?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `roc11 the document I ask the Authority to produce, first list` @desc What kind of document is it, among those paragraph (4) lists?
      `held as a result of its functions under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it or was it in the Authority's possession, custody or power as a result of the performance or exercise by the Authority of any of its functions, duties or powers under the Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 8(4), may the Authority be ordered to give production of this document or produce it for inspection` IS
    `o 62 r 8(4) the Authority may be ordered to give production of the document or produce it for inspection` (`roc11 the first-list document as Order 62 has it` `the document`) `held as a result of its functions under the Act`

@ref O 62 r 8(5)
@export Under Order 62, rule 8(5), may the Authority also be ordered to give production of this document or produce it for inspection?
GIVEN `the document` IS A `roc11 the document I ask the Authority to produce, second list` @desc What kind of document is it, among those paragraph (5) lists?
      `provided under section 168C` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it or was it in the Authority's possession, custody or power as a result of being provided to the Authority under section 168C?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 8(5), may the Authority also be ordered to give production of this document or produce it for inspection` IS
    `o 62 r 8(5) the Authority may be ordered to give production of the document or produce it for inspection` (`roc11 the second-list document as Order 62 has it` `the document`) `provided under section 168C`

@ref O 62 r 8(6)
@export Under Order 62, rule 8(6), may an order be made for the Authority to give production of this document or produce it for inspection?
GIVEN `it is listed in paragraph (4) or (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the document one listed in Rule 8(4) or (5)?
      `strong and exceptional grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court of the opinion that there are strong and exceptional grounds to order the Authority to give production of the document or produce it for inspection?
      `the description` IS A `roc11 the description the document falls within` @desc Does the document fall within one of the descriptions in Rule 8(6)(a) to (g), and if so which?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 8(6), may an order be made for the Authority to give production of this document or produce it for inspection` IS
    `o 62 r 8(6) an order may be made for the Authority to give production of the document or produce it for inspection` `it is listed in paragraph (4) or (5)` `strong and exceptional grounds` (`roc11 the description as Order 62 has it` `the description`)

@ref O 62 r 8(7)
@export Under Order 62, rule 8(7), does paragraph (6) affect the operation of the Evidence Act?
GIVEN `the question is about the operation of the Evidence Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your question about the operation of the Evidence Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 8(7), does paragraph (6) affect the operation of the Evidence Act` IS
    `o 62 r 8(7) paragraph (6) affects the operation of the Evidence Act` `the question is about the operation of the Evidence Act`

@ref O 62 r 8(8) "book"
@export Under Order 62, rule 8(8), which provision of the Securities and Futures Act gives the meaning of book?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 8(8), which provision of the Securities and Futures Act gives the meaning of book` IS
    `o 62 r 8(8) "book" the provision that gives its meaning`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Directions, payment into Court, consent and costs (rules 9 to 12)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 62 r 9
@export Under Order 62, rule 9, does Order 9 apply to the civil penalty action against me?
GIVEN `it is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a civil penalty action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 9, does Order 9 apply to the civil penalty action against me` IS
    `o 62 r 9 Order 9 applies to the civil penalty action` `it is a civil penalty action`

@ref O 62 r 10
@export Under Order 62, rule 10, does a given Order apply to the civil penalty action against me?
GIVEN `it is a civil penalty action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the proceeding a civil penalty action?
      `which Order` IS A STRING @desc Which Order do you ask about, written for example as "Order 5" or "Order 14"?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 10, does a given Order apply to the civil penalty action against me` IS
    `o 62 r 10 the provision applies to the civil penalty action` `it is a civil penalty action` `which Order`

@ref O 62 r 11
@export Under Order 62, rule 11, must the Authority file the consent of the Public Prosecutor for the order it seeks?
GIVEN `the order is sought under one of those sections` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order sought under section 137ZD(3) or 232(4), or under section 232(4) read with section 236B(6), 236C(5), 236E(6), 236F(5) or 236H(4)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 11, must the Authority file the consent of the Public Prosecutor for the order it seeks` IS
    `o 62 r 11 the duty to file the consent of the Public Prosecutor arises` `the order is sought under one of those sections`

@ref O 62 r 11
@export Under Order 62, rule 11, did the Authority file the consent of the Public Prosecutor as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the order is sought under one of those sections` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order sought under section 137ZD(3) or 232(4), or under section 232(4) read with section 236B(6), 236C(5), 236E(6), 236F(5) or 236H(4)?
      `the Authority filed the consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Authority file the consent of the Public Prosecutor referred to in that provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 11, did the Authority file the consent of the Public Prosecutor as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 62 r 11 the Authority files the consent as the Rule requires` `the order is sought under one of those sections` `the Authority filed the consent`

@ref O 62 r 12(1)
@export Under Order 62, rule 12(1), may an order be made for my costs to be paid by the Authority?
GIVEN `the Authority discontinued or withdrew all claims against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Authority discontinue the civil penalty action or withdraw all claims made against you in it?
      `on one of those grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that on the ground of your death, bankruptcy or winding up, or the commencement of bankruptcy or winding up proceedings against you, after the commencement of the action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 12(1), may an order be made for my costs to be paid by the Authority` IS
    `o 62 r 12(1) an order may be made for the costs of the defendant to be paid by the Authority` `the Authority discontinued or withdrew all claims against me` `on one of those grounds`

@ref O 62 r 12(2)
@export Under Order 62, rule 12(2), may the Court make such order as to costs as it thinks just?
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings in this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the proceedings proceedings in Order 62?
      `a Rule in this Order limits the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a Rule in Order 62 limit the order sought?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 12(2), may the Court make such order as to costs as it thinks just` IS
    `o 62 r 12(2) the Court may make such order as to costs as it thinks just` `the proceedings are proceedings in this Order` `a Rule in this Order limits the order`

@ref O 62 r 12(3)
@export Under Order 62, rule 12(3), do the costs awarded to the Authority include this item?
GIVEN `a legal officer or State Counsel appears for the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does a legal officer of the Authority admitted as an advocate and solicitor under the Legal Profession Act, or a State Counsel, appear as an advocate on behalf of the Authority?
      `costs are awarded to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are costs awarded to the Authority?
      `the item is of that kind` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the item of a kind that would be included within the meaning of the word costs in any written law as though an advocate and solicitor with a practising certificate had appeared?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 12(3), do the costs awarded to the Authority include this item` IS
    `o 62 r 12(3) the costs include the item` `a legal officer or State Counsel appears for the Authority` `costs are awarded to the Authority` `the item is of that kind`

@ref O 62 r 12(4)
@export Under Order 62, rule 12(4), are the costs awarded to the Authority in accordance with the scale of fees?
GIVEN `they are costs under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they costs awarded to the Authority under Rule 12(3)?
      `in accordance with the scale` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they in accordance with the scale of fees prescribed from time to time to be chargeable by advocates and solicitors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 12(4), are the costs awarded to the Authority in accordance with the scale of fees` IS
    `o 62 r 12(4) the costs are in accordance with the scale of fees` `they are costs under paragraph (3)` `in accordance with the scale`

@ref O 62 r 12(4)
@export Under Order 62, rule 12(4), may the costs awarded to the Authority be assessed in accordance with Order 21?
GIVEN `they are costs under paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they costs awarded to the Authority under Rule 12(3)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 12(4), may the costs awarded to the Authority be assessed in accordance with Order 21` IS
    `o 62 r 12(4) the costs may be assessed in accordance with Order 21` `they are costs under paragraph (3)`

@ref O 62 r 12(5)
@export Under Order 62, rule 12(5), must the costs awarded to the Authority be paid to the Authority?
GIVEN `they are costs awarded in accordance with this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they costs awarded to the Authority in accordance with Order 62, Rule 12?
      `they have been recovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the costs been recovered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 12(5), must the costs awarded to the Authority be paid to the Authority` IS
    `o 62 r 12(5) the duty to pay the costs to the Authority arises` `they are costs awarded in accordance with this Rule` `they have been recovered`

@ref O 62 r 12(5)
@export Under Order 62, rule 12(5), have the costs recovered been paid to the Authority as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `they are costs awarded in accordance with this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they costs awarded to the Authority in accordance with Order 62, Rule 12?
      `they have been recovered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have the costs been recovered?
      `they have been paid to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have they been paid to the Authority?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 62, rule 12(5), have the costs recovered been paid to the Authority as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 62 r 12(5) the costs are paid to the Authority as the Rule requires` `they are costs awarded in accordance with this Rule` `they have been recovered` `they have been paid to the Authority`

-- ===========================================================================
-- ORDER 63 -- SECURITIES AND FUTURES ACT, ORDER FOR DISGORGEMENT AGAINST THIRD PARTY -- wiring
-- ===========================================================================

DECLARE `roc11 the stage the Court has reached` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 hearing the application for the order for disgorgement`
    `roc11 hearing the third party show cause`
    `roc11 hearing the application for directions on claims for compensation`
    `roc11 some other stage of the proceedings`

GIVEN stage IS A `roc11 the stage the Court has reached`
GIVETH A `o 63 r 5(1) hearing`
`roc11 the hearing as Order 63 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER stage
    WHEN `roc11 hearing the application for the order for disgorgement` THEN `o 63 r 5(1)(a) the hearing of an application under Rule 2(1)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 hearing the third party show cause` THEN `o 63 r 5(1)(b) the hearing of the third party under Rule 2(7)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 hearing the application for directions on claims for compensation` THEN `o 63 r 5(1)(c) the hearing of an application under Rule 3(1)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 some other stage of the proceedings` THEN `o 63 r 5(1) some other stage` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 the direction or order sought at the hearing` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 a direction for the filing of further affidavits`
    `roc11 a direction on the manner in which proceedings are to be instituted against the third party`
    `roc11 an order that an issue be stated and tried`
    `roc11 an order that the matter be adjourned`
    `roc11 an order that further advertisements be made`
    `roc11 an order for the substitution of the claimant making the application with another claimant`
    `roc11 an order that the application be dismissed`
    `roc11 a direction or order of another kind`

GIVEN kind IS A `roc11 the direction or order sought at the hearing`
GIVETH A `o 63 r 5(1) kind of direction or order`
`roc11 the kind of direction or order as Order 63 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `roc11 a direction for the filing of further affidavits` THEN `o 63 r 5(1)(d) for the filing of such further affidavits as the Court considers necessary` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a direction on the manner in which proceedings are to be instituted against the third party` THEN `o 63 r 5(1)(e) on the manner in which proceedings are to be instituted against the third party` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an order that an issue be stated and tried` THEN `o 63 r 5(1)(f) that an issue be stated and tried` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an order that the matter be adjourned` THEN `o 63 r 5(1)(g) that the matter be adjourned` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an order that further advertisements be made` THEN `o 63 r 5(1)(h) that further advertisements be made in addition to that required under Rule 3(4)` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an order for the substitution of the claimant making the application with another claimant` THEN `o 63 r 5(1)(i) for the substitution of the claimant making the application under Rule 2(1) or 3(1) with another claimant` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 an order that the application be dismissed` THEN `o 63 r 5(1)(j) that the application under Rule 2(1) or 3(1) be dismissed` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 a direction or order of another kind` THEN `o 63 r 5(1) another kind of direction or order` -- input mapping

DECLARE `roc11 the exhibit I plan to attach` IS ONE OF
    `roc11 trade notes or slips attached`
    `roc11 statements of accounts attached`
    `roc11 copies of instructions to a broker or remisier attached`
    `roc11 another exhibit attached`

GIVEN exhibit IS A `roc11 the exhibit I plan to attach`
GIVETH A `o 63 r 4(3) exhibit`
`roc11 the exhibit as Order 63 has it` MEANS
    CONSIDER exhibit
    WHEN `roc11 trade notes or slips attached` THEN `o 63 r 4(3)(a) trade notes or slips` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 statements of accounts attached` THEN `o 63 r 4(3)(b) statements of accounts for the relevant period` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 copies of instructions to a broker or remisier attached` THEN `o 63 r 4(3)(c) copies of instructions given to a broker or remisier` -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc11 another exhibit attached` THEN `o 63 r 4(3) another exhibit` -- input mapping

§ `Order 63 -- Securities and Futures Act, order for disgorgement against a third party -- my questions`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Definitions and application (rule 1)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 63 r 1(1)
@export Under Order 63, rule 1, is this an order for disgorgement?
GIVEN `applied for under 236L(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order one applied for under section 236L(1) of the Securities and Futures Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 1, is this an order for disgorgement` IS
    `o 63 r 1(1) "order for disgorgement" the order is an order for disgorgement` `applied for under 236L(1)`

@ref O 63 r 1(1)
@export Under Order 63, rule 1, which section of the Securities and Futures Act says who is a claimant in these proceedings?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 1, which section of the Securities and Futures Act says who is a claimant in these proceedings` IS
    `o 63 r 1(1) "claimant" the section that gives its meaning`

@ref O 63 r 1(1)
@export Under Order 63, rule 1, which section of the Securities and Futures Act says who is the third party in these proceedings?
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 1, which section of the Securities and Futures Act says who is the third party in these proceedings` IS
    `o 63 r 1(1) "third party" the section that gives its meaning`

@ref O 63 r 1(2)
@export Under Order 63, rule 1, do the Rules of Court on disgorgement against a third party apply to my proceeding?
GIVEN `under section 236L` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your proceeding one under section 236L of the Securities and Futures Act?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 1, do the Rules of Court on disgorgement against a third party apply to my proceeding` IS
    `o 63 r 1(2) these Rules apply to the proceeding` `under section 236L`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `The application for an order for disgorgement (rule 2)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 63 r 2(1)
@export Under Order 63, rule 2, may I make my application for an order for disgorgement by originating application naming the third party as defendant?
GIVEN `for disgorgement under 236L` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application one for an order for disgorgement under section 236L?
      `by originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you apply by originating application?
      `names the third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you name the third party as the defendant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 2, may I make my application for an order for disgorgement by originating application naming the third party as defendant` IS
    `o 63 r 2(1) the application for an order for disgorgement may be made in this way` `for disgorgement under 236L` (IF `by originating application` THEN `Originating application` ELSE Summons) `names the third party`

@ref O 63 r 2(2)
@export Under Order 63, rule 2(2), does another Order apply to the originating application for disgorgement?
GIVEN `the originating application of rule 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application the originating application of rule 2(1) of Order 63?
      `which provision` IS A STRING @desc Which provision are you asking about? (For example: Order 6 rule 11, Order 9, Order 15 rule 7.)
      `rule 2 modifies it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does rule 2 expressly modify that provision?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 2(2), does another Order apply to the originating application for disgorgement` IS
    `o 63 r 2(2) the provision applies to the originating application` `the originating application of rule 2(1)` `which provision` `rule 2 modifies it`

@ref O 63 r 2(3)
@export Under Order 63, rule 2(3), what has my supporting affidavit left out that the Rule requires?
GIVEN `grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the affidavit set out the grounds on which the application is made?
      `contravention particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out particulars of the contravention of the relevant provision of Part XII of the Act?
      `trades circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out the circumstances leading to the trades carried out for the third party in question?
      `benefit circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out the circumstances leading to the third party receiving the whole or any part of the benefit of the contravention?
      `benefit particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it set out particulars of the benefit received by the third party?
      `I am a claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application made by a claimant?
      `transaction particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does it set out particulars of the securities transaction, futures contract, or contract or arrangement in respect of which the claimant suffered a loss?
      `transaction circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does it set out the circumstances leading to the entering into of the transaction?
      `loss circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does it set out the circumstances leading to the loss suffered?
      `loss particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does it set out particulars of the loss suffered?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 2(3), what has my supporting affidavit left out that the Rule requires` IS
    `o 63 r 2(3) the matters the affidavit has not yet set out` (`o 63 r 2(3) affidavit` OF `grounds`, `contravention particulars`, `trades circumstances`, `benefit circumstances`, `benefit particulars`, `I am a claimant`, `transaction particulars`, `transaction circumstances`, `loss circumstances`, `loss particulars`)

@ref O 63 r 2(4)
@export Under Order 63, rule 2(4), must the application and affidavit be served personally at least 28 clear days before the hearing?
GIVEN `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that they need not be served in this way?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 2(4), must the application and affidavit be served personally at least 28 clear days before the hearing` IS
    `o 63 r 2(4) the duty to serve the application personally in time arises` `the Court otherwise orders`

@ref O 63 r 2(4)
@export Under Order 63, rule 2(4), were the application and affidavit served on the third party as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that they need not be served personally and in this time?
      `served on the third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were they served personally on the third party?
      `court directed another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court directed service on another person appearing to be interested?
      `served on that other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, were they served personally on that person?
      `the date served` IS A DATE @desc On what date were they served?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for serving them, that is the last day that leaves at least 28 clear days (or any longer time the Court directed) before the hearing of the application, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 2(4), were the application and affidavit served on the third party as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 63 r 2(4) the application and affidavit are served as the Rule requires` `the Court otherwise orders` `served on the third party` `court directed another` `served on that other` `the date served` `the last day`

@ref O 63 r 2(5)
@export Under Order 63, rule 2(5), is the application for an order for disgorgement deemed dismissed?
GIVEN `complied with paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the applicant (or the applicant's solicitor) comply with paragraph (4)? (Yes if the Court ordered otherwise.)
      `the Court otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court otherwise directed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 2(5), is the application for an order for disgorgement deemed dismissed` IS
    `o 63 r 2(5) the application is deemed dismissed` `complied with paragraph (4)` `the Court otherwise directs`

@ref O 63 r 2(6)
@export Under Order 63, rule 2(6), may the Court direct the applicant to serve a notice on me to show cause why an order for disgorgement should not be made against me?
GIVEN `heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court heard the application for an order for disgorgement?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 2(6), may the Court direct the applicant to serve a notice on me to show cause` IS
    `o 63 r 2(6) the Court may direct the applicant to serve a notice to show cause on the third party` `heard`

@ref O 63 r 2(7)
@export Under Order 63, rule 2(7), may I show cause by affidavit or otherwise?
GIVEN `I am the third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the third party?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 2(7), may I show cause by affidavit or otherwise` IS
    `o 63 r 2(7) the person may show cause by affidavit or otherwise to the satisfaction of the Court` `I am the third party`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Asking for directions on claims for compensation (rule 3)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 63 r 3(1)
@export Under Order 63, rule 3(1), may I apply for directions on claims for compensation out of the sum under the order?
GIVEN `final` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the order for disgorgement been made final in accordance with section 236L(11)?
      `applicant or claimant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the applicant for the order, or a claimant?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 3(1), may I apply for directions on claims for compensation out of the sum under the order` IS
    `o 63 r 3(1) the person may apply for directions on claims for compensation` `final` `applicant or claimant`

@ref O 63 r 3(1)
@export Under Order 63, rule 3(1), may the Court fix a return date for hearing my application for directions?
GIVEN `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you made an application for directions under rule 3(1)?
      `section 236L(6) permits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 236L(6) of the Act permit the Court to fix a return date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 3(1), may the Court fix a return date for hearing my application for directions` IS
    `o 63 r 3(1) the Court may fix a return date for hearing the application` `I have applied` `section 236L(6) permits`

@ref O 63 r 3(2)
@export Under Order 63, rule 3(2), is my application for directions made by summons?
GIVEN `under paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your application one under rule 3(1)?
      `by summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you apply by summons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 3(2), is my application for directions made by summons` IS
    `o 63 r 3(2) the application for directions is made as the Rule requires` `under paragraph (1)` (IF `by summons` THEN Summons ELSE `Originating application`)

@ref O 63 r 3(3)
@export Under Order 63, rule 3(3), must my application for directions be served personally at least 28 clear days before the return date?
GIVEN `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that the application need not be served in this way?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 3(3), must my application for directions be served personally at least 28 clear days before the return date` IS
    `o 63 r 3(3) the duty to serve the application personally in time arises` `the Court otherwise orders`

@ref O 63 r 3(3)
@export Under Order 63, rule 3(3), was my application for directions served as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court ordered that the application need not be served personally and in this time?
      `served on the third party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it served personally on the third party?
      `court directed another` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court directed service on another person appearing to be interested?
      `served on that other` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, was it served personally on that person?
      `the date served` IS A DATE @desc On what date was it served?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for serving it, that is the last day that leaves at least 28 clear days (or any longer time the Court directed) before the return date, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 3(3), was my application for directions served as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 63 r 3(3) the application is served as the Rule requires` `the Court otherwise orders` `served on the third party` `court directed another` `served on that other` `the date served` `the last day`

@ref O 63 r 3(4)
@export Under Order 63, rule 3(4), did I advertise my application for directions as the Rule requires?
GIVEN `in Form 93` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the advertisement in Form 93?
      `in English and Chinese dailies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did it appear at least once in one English and one Chinese local daily newspaper?
      `in the newspaper the Court directed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Court direct another newspaper, and did it appear there?
      `the date it appeared` IS A DATE @desc On what date did it appear?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for advertising it, that is the last day that leaves at least 21 clear days (or any longer time the Court directed) before the return date, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 3(4), did I advertise my application for directions as the Rule requires` IS
    `o 63 r 3(4) the application is advertised as the Rule requires` `in Form 93` `in English and Chinese dailies` `in the newspaper the Court directed` `the date it appeared` `the last day`

@ref O 63 r 3(5)
@export Under Order 63, rule 3(5), what has my advertisement left out that the Rule requires it to state?
GIVEN `day filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the advertisement state the day on which the application was filed?
      `applicant's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it state the name and address of the applicant for directions?
      `I have a solicitor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the applicant have a solicitor?
      `solicitor's name and address` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, does it state the name and address of the applicant's solicitor?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 3(5), what has my advertisement left out that the Rule requires it to state` IS
    `o 63 r 3(5) the matters the advertisement has not yet stated` (`o 63 r 3(5) advertisement` OF `day filed`, `applicant's name and address`, `I have a solicitor`, `solicitor's name and address`)

@ref O 63 r 3(6)
@export Under Order 63, rule 3(6), is my application for directions deemed dismissed?
GIVEN `I complied with paragraph (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you (or your solicitor) comply with paragraph (3), the personal service? (Yes if the Court ordered otherwise.)
      `I complied with paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you (or your solicitor) comply with paragraph (4), the advertisement?
      `I complied with paragraph (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you (or your solicitor) comply with paragraph (5), the contents of the advertisement?
      `the Court otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Court otherwise directed?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 3(6), is my application for directions deemed dismissed` IS
    `o 63 r 3(6) the application is deemed dismissed` `I complied with paragraph (3)` `I complied with paragraph (4)` `I complied with paragraph (5)` `the Court otherwise directs`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Proving my claim (rule 4)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 63 r 4(1)
@export Under Order 63, rule 4(1), must I file an affidavit stating my claim?
GIVEN `I desire to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you desire to file a claim for compensation under section 236L(6)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 4(1), must I file an affidavit stating my claim` IS
    `o 63 r 4(1) the duty to file an affidavit of claim arises` `I desire to claim`

@ref O 63 r 4(1)
@export Under Order 63, rule 4(1), did I file my affidavit stating my claim in time?
GIVEN `I desire to claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you desire to file a claim for compensation under section 236L(6)?
      `I have filed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you filed the affidavit?
      `the date I filed` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Give any date if not.)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for filing it, that is the last day that leaves at least 7 clear days before the return date, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 4(1), did I file my affidavit stating my claim in time` IS
    `o 63 r 4(1) the claimant files the affidavit of claim in time` `I desire to claim` (IF `I have filed` THEN JUST `the date I filed` ELSE NOTHING) `the date I am asking about` `the last day`

@ref O 63 r 4(2)
@export Under Order 63, rule 4(2), what has my affidavit stating my claim left out that the Rule requires?
GIVEN `exhibits` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the affidavit supported by the relevant exhibits?
      `grounds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it explain the grounds on which my claim is made?
      `transaction particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include particulars of the securities transaction, futures contract, or contract or arrangement in respect of which I suffered a loss?
      `transaction circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the circumstances leading to the entering into of the transaction?
      `loss circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include the circumstances leading to the loss suffered?
      `loss particulars` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does it include particulars of the loss suffered?
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 4(2), what has my affidavit stating my claim left out that the Rule requires` IS
    `o 63 r 4(2) the matters the affidavit has not yet covered` (`o 63 r 4(2) affidavit` OF `exhibits`, `grounds`, `transaction particulars`, `transaction circumstances`, `loss circumstances`, `loss particulars`)

@ref O 63 r 4(3)
@export Under Order 63, rule 4(3), may my exhibits include this exhibit?
GIVEN exhibit IS A `roc11 the exhibit I plan to attach` @desc Which exhibit do you plan to attach?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 4(3), may my exhibits include this exhibit` IS
    `o 63 r 4(3) the exhibits may include` (`roc11 the exhibit as Order 63 has it` exhibit)

@ref O 63 r 4(4)
@export Under Order 63, rule 4(4), did I serve a copy of my affidavit on the third party in time?
GIVEN `I have served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you served a copy of the affidavit on the third party?
      `the date I served` IS A DATE @desc If so, on what date? (Give any date if not.)
      `the date I am asking about` IS A DATE @desc On what date are you asking?
      `the last day` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day of the 3 days after the filing of the affidavit, counted as Order 3, Rule 3 counts them?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 4(4), did I serve a copy of my affidavit on the third party in time` IS
    `o 63 r 4(4) the claimant serves a copy of the affidavit on the third party in time` (IF `I have served` THEN JUST `the date I served` ELSE NOTHING) `the date I am asking about` `the last day`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `What the Court may do (rule 5)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 63 r 5(1)
@export Under Order 63, rule 5(1), may the Court give directions or make orders after the hearing it has reached?
GIVEN stage IS A `roc11 the stage the Court has reached` @desc At what stage has the Court reached?
      `everyone appears` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the persons on whom the application has been served, and all claimants who have filed their affidavits of claim, appear?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 5(1), may the Court give directions or make orders after the hearing it has reached` IS
    `o 63 r 5(1) the Court may give directions or make orders after the hearing` (`roc11 the hearing as Order 63 has it` stage) `everyone appears`

@ref O 63 r 5(1)
@export Under Order 63, rule 5(1), may the Court give this kind of direction or make this kind of order?
GIVEN kind IS A `roc11 the direction or order sought at the hearing` @desc What direction or order is sought?
      stage IS A `roc11 the stage the Court has reached` @desc At what stage has the Court reached?
      `everyone appears` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do all the persons on whom the application has been served, and all claimants who have filed their affidavits of claim, appear?
      `best adapted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Court think the direction or order best adapted to secure the just, expeditious and economical disposal of the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 5(1), may the Court give this kind of direction or make this kind of order` IS
    `o 63 r 5(1) the Court may give this kind of direction or make this kind of order` (`roc11 the kind of direction or order as Order 63 has it` kind) (`roc11 the hearing as Order 63 has it` stage) `everyone appears` `best adapted`

@ref O 63 r 5(2)
@export Under Order 63, rule 5(2), may the Court make an order against me as the third party?
GIVEN `I am the third party or an interested party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you the third party, or another interested party referred to in rule 3(3)(b)?
      `served with the notice to show cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you duly served with a notice to show cause under rule 2(6)?
      `did not appear at that hearing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not appear at the hearing for the notice?
      `served with the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you duly served with the application under rule 3(1)?
      `did not appear on the application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not appear on the hearing of the application?
      `appeared but did not comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you appear but fail or refuse to comply with an order made in the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 5(2), may the Court make an order against me as the third party` IS
    `o 63 r 5(2) the Court may make such order as it deems appropriate` `I am the third party or an interested party` `served with the notice to show cause` `did not appear at that hearing` `served with the application` `did not appear on the application` `appeared but did not comply`

@ref O 63 r 5(3)
@export Under Order 63, rule 5(3), may the Court declare me forever barred from bringing any claim against the third party?
GIVEN `I filed an affidavit of claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you file an affidavit of claim under rule 4?
      `I did not appear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you not appear on the hearing of the application under rule 4?
      `I appeared but did not comply` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did you appear but fail or refuse to comply with an order made in the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 5(3), may the Court declare me forever barred from bringing any claim against the third party` IS
    `o 63 r 5(3) the Court may declare the claimant forever barred` `I filed an affidavit of claim` `I did not appear` `I appeared but did not comply`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Costs, other matters, the trial of an issue and the Authority's application (rules 6 to 8)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@ref O 63 r 6
@export Under Order 63, rule 6, may the Court make the order as to costs or any other matter that is asked for?
GIVEN `in or for the purposes of proceedings in this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the order asked for in or for the purposes of proceedings under Order 63?
      `rules 1 to 5 provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does one of rules 1 to 5 of Order 63 provide otherwise on the matter?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 6, may the Court make the order as to costs or any other matter that is asked for` IS
    `o 63 r 6 the Court may make such order as to costs or any other matter as it thinks just` `in or for the purposes of proceedings in this Order` `rules 1 to 5 provide otherwise`

@ref O 63 r 7(1)
@export Under Order 63, rule 7(1), does Order 15 apply to the trial of the issue stated?
GIVEN `issue stated under 5(1)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trial of an issue stated under rule 5(1)(f)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 7(1), does Order 15 apply to the trial of the issue stated` IS
    `o 63 r 7(1) Order 15 applies to the trial of the issue` `issue stated under 5(1)(f)`

@ref O 63 r 7(2)
@export Under Order 63, rule 7(2), may the Court that tries the issue give judgment or make an order finally disposing of all questions?
GIVEN `the Court tries the issue stated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Court the one by which an issue stated is tried?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 7(2), may the Court that tries the issue give judgment or make an order finally disposing of all questions` IS
    `o 63 r 7(2) the Court may give such judgment or make such order as finally to dispose of all questions` `the Court tries the issue stated`

@ref O 63 r 8(1)
@export Under Order 63, rule 8(1), does a rule of Order 62 apply to the Authority's application for disgorgement against me?
GIVEN `the application is one by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the application one by the Monetary Authority of Singapore under Order 63?
      `rule number` IS A STRING @desc Which rule of Order 62 are you asking about? (For example 6, 7, 8, 10 or 12.)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 8(1), does a rule of Order 62 apply to the Authority's application for disgorgement against me` IS
    `o 63 r 8(1) a rule of Order 62 applies to the application` `the application is one by the Authority` `rule number`

@ref O 63 r 8(2)
@export Under Order 63, rule 8(2), whom does "the defendant" in Order 62, rule 8 mean when that rule is applied to the Authority's application?
GIVEN `the reference is to the defendant in Order 62 rule 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you asking about a reference to "the defendant" in Order 62, rule 8?
      `for paragraph (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the rule being applied to an application by the Authority under Order 63?
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `Under Order 63, rule 8(2), whom does the defendant in Order 62 rule 8 mean when that rule is applied to the Authority's application` IS
    `o 63 r 8(2) a reference to the defendant in Order 62 rule 8 is a reference to` `the reference is to the defendant in Order 62 rule 8` `for paragraph (1)`

-- ============================================================
-- roc12: this part's seat text, unchanged (merged by concatenation)
-- ============================================================
-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026
-- (Orders 64 to 70 and the First to Fourth Schedules, lines 7400 to 8829 of the source file) -- THE SEAT LAYER.
-- The source is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- SEAT: a party to a civil action in the Singapore courts (a claimant, a defendant, a third party or an appellant),
-- asking on facts they can state what they must file or serve, by when, how, at what cost,
-- what the court may order, and what follows if they do not.
-- This layer phrases the rules of the modules imported above as the questions that person would ask.
-- Nothing here is new law: every question calls one layer-1 rule (or a layer-1 rule that a layer-1 rule calls), and restates none.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, a number, a date, a text, or a choice from a list --
-- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded as the person would be asked.
-- The MAYBE values the layer-1 rules take are built in each question from those answers, and the SAME layer-1 rule is then called.
--   * A fact the person may not know about another part of the Rules (Order 6, rule 5 and Order 8, rule 4A(7) are the two cases) is asked as "Yes / No / I am not sure";
--     "I am not sure" becomes NOTHING, and a rule that cannot answer without it answers NOTHING.
--   * A date that has not happened yet is asked as "has this happened yet" and a date; "no" becomes NOTHING.
--   * An amount the person does not know is asked as 0 where the rule allows NOTHING for it.
--   * The days that Order 3, rule 3 counts ("the last day for doing the act", "the first day on which the act may be done") are the
--     seams with the part that encodes Order 3; here the person gives the day they have counted, and the @desc says how it is counted.
--   * Order 64, rule 3 asks whether Rules 2, 4 and 4A apply; those are conclusions the person takes from the questions under rules 2(1), 4(1) and 4A(1), and they are asked as yes/no.
--     They are not wired automatically: those rules answer MAYBE BOOLEAN, the layer-1 rule 3 takes BOOLEAN, and turning NOTHING into FALSE is what the Rules do not allow.
--   * The Fourth Schedule asks for the court system, the court level and the value of the claim; the Schedule's column follows from them.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Rules themselves give; NOTHING means the Rules do not answer on these facts
-- (see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").  Never read NOTHING as no.
--
-- Provisions that address only an official (the Minister, the Registrar, the Court, the process server) are in layer 1;
-- a question below is asked only where the provision means something to the party: a duty on the party, a right the party may use, a bar on the party,
-- or a time or a fee that the party meets.  There is no seat for an official.

DECLARE `roc12 seat my answer` IS ONE OF
    `roc12 seat answer yes`
    `roc12 seat answer no`
    `roc12 seat answer I am not sure`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Wiring: the person's answers become the modules' inputs.  Not questions.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- An answer of yes, no or "I am not sure" as a MAYBE BOOLEAN.
GIVEN answer IS A `roc12 seat my answer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`roc12 seat what I say, as a fact` MEANS
    CONSIDER answer
    WHEN `roc12 seat answer yes` THEN JUST TRUE -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc12 seat answer no` THEN JUST FALSE -- input mapping
    WHEN `roc12 seat answer I am not sure` THEN NOTHING -- input mapping

-- A date that may not have happened yet.
GIVEN happened IS A BOOLEAN
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`roc12 seat a date if it has happened` MEANS
    IF happened THEN JUST day ELSE NOTHING -- input mapping

-- An amount that the person gives as 0 when there is none or they do not know it.
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`roc12 seat an amount if I know it` MEANS
    IF amount EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST amount -- input mapping

-- Whether the person who gave permission is a Judge (Order 1, rule 3(1)): the court and the decision-maker are asked, and the keel decides.
GIVEN level IS A `Court level`
      decider IS A `Decision maker`
      appropriate IS A BOOLEAN
      empowered IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`roc12 seat the person who gave permission is a Judge` MEANS
    `o 1 r 3(1) a person sitting in a court is a Judge` (Sitting WITH
        `sitting court level` IS level
        `sitting decision maker` IS decider) appropriate empowered -- input mapping

§ `Rules of Court 2021, Orders 64 to 70 and the Schedules -- my questions as a party to a civil action`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 64 -- Service of foreign process`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 64, rule 2(1), does the rule on serving foreign process on a letter of request received by the Minister apply to this process?
GIVEN `the process is required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the process is required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country?
      `a letter of request from such a tribunal requests service on a person in Singapore of the process sent with the letter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a letter of request from such a tribunal requests service on a person in Singapore of the process sent with the letter?
      `the letter of request is received by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the letter of request is received by the Minister?
      `the Minister sends it to the Supreme Court with an intimation that it is desirable that effect should be given to the request` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Minister sends it to the Supreme Court with an intimation that it is desirable that effect should be given to the request?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 64, rule 2(1), does the rule on serving foreign process on a letter of request received by the Minister apply to this process` IS
    `o 64 r 2(1) this Rule applies to the service` `the process is required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country` `a letter of request from such a tribunal requests service on a person in Singapore of the process sent with the letter` `the letter of request is received by the Minister` `the Minister sends it to the Supreme Court with an intimation that it is desirable that effect should be given to the request`

@export Under Order 64, rule 2(2), is the letter of request accompanied by what the rule requires?
GIVEN `the letter of request is accompanied by a translation of the letter in English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the letter of request is accompanied by a translation of the letter in English?
      `the number of copies of the process to be served that accompany the letter of request` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of copies of the process to be served that accompany the letter of request?
      `the number of copies of the translation of the process in English that accompany the letter of request` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of copies of the translation of the process in English that accompany the letter of request?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 64, rule 2(2), is the letter of request accompanied by what the rule requires` IS
    `o 64 r 2(2) the letter of request is accompanied as the Rule requires` `the letter of request is accompanied by a translation of the letter in English` `the number of copies of the process to be served that accompany the letter of request` `the number of copies of the translation of the process in English that accompany the letter of request`

@export Under Order 64, rule 3, does the rule on serving foreign process otherwise than on a letter of request apply to this process?
GIVEN `the process is required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the process is required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country?
      `Rule 2 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Rule 2 apply to this process? (take the answer from the question under Order 64, rule 2(1); answer No if it is not Yes)
      `Rule 2 is invoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has Rule 2 been invoked, that is, has a letter of request been received by the Minister?
      `Rule 4 applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Rule 4 apply to this process? (take the answer from the question under Order 64, rule 4(1); answer No if it is not Yes)
      `Rule 4A applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does Rule 4A apply to this process? (take the answer from the question under Order 64, rule 4A(1); answer No if it is not Yes)
      `Rule 4A is invoked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has Rule 4A been invoked, that is, has a request for service under Article 5 of the Hague Service Convention been made to the Minister?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 64, rule 3, does the rule on serving foreign process otherwise than on a letter of request apply to this process` IS
    `o 64 r 3 this Rule applies to the service` `the process is required in connection with civil proceedings pending before a court or other tribunal of a foreign country` `Rule 2 applies` `Rule 2 is invoked` `Rule 4 applies` `Rule 4A applies` `Rule 4A is invoked`

@export Under Order 64, rule 4(1), does the rule on serving foreign process under a Civil Procedure Convention apply to this document?
GIVEN `the process or other court document is required in connection with civil proceedings instituted in a court or other tribunal of a foreign country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the process or other court document is required in connection with civil proceedings instituted in a court or other tribunal of a foreign country?
      `which instrument the foreign tribunal relies on` IS A `sch 3 convention` @desc Which instrument does the foreign tribunal rely on? (choose the item of the Third Schedule, or another instrument)
      `the instrument is a convention, treaty or agreement between different States relating to civil procedure in the Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the instrument is a convention, treaty or agreement between different States relating to civil procedure in the Court?
      `the instrument is the Hague Service Convention as defined in Order 8, Rule 4A(7)` IS A `roc12 seat my answer` @desc Is it the case that the instrument is the Hague Service Convention as defined in Order 8, Rule 4A(7)? (Yes, No, or I am not sure)
      `the Convention provides for service in Singapore of process or other court document of the tribunals of that country` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Convention provides for service in Singapore of process or other court document of the tribunals of that country?
      `a letter of request from a consular or other authority of that country requesting service on a person in Singapore of such process or other court document sent with the letter is received by the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a letter of request from a consular or other authority of that country requesting service on a person in Singapore of such process or other court document sent with the letter is received by the Registrar?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 64, rule 4(1), does the rule on serving foreign process under a Civil Procedure Convention apply to this document` IS
    `o 64 r 4(1) this Rule applies to the service` `the process or other court document is required in connection with civil proceedings instituted in a court or other tribunal of a foreign country` (`o 1 r 3(1) an instrument is a Civil Procedure Convention` (`sch 3 the convention is set out in the Third Schedule` `which instrument the foreign tribunal relies on`) `the instrument is a convention, treaty or agreement between different States relating to civil procedure in the Court`) (`o 64 r 4A(13) an instrument is the Hague Service Convention` (`roc12 seat what I say, as a fact` `the instrument is the Hague Service Convention as defined in Order 8, Rule 4A(7)`)) `the Convention provides for service in Singapore of process or other court document of the tribunals of that country` `a letter of request from a consular or other authority of that country requesting service on a person in Singapore of such process or other court document sent with the letter is received by the Registrar`

@export Under Order 64, rule 4A(1), does the rule on serving a document under Article 5 of the Hague Service Convention apply?
GIVEN `the process or other court document is required in connection with civil proceedings in respect of a civil or commercial matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the process or other court document is required in connection with civil proceedings in respect of a civil or commercial matter?
      `the proceedings are instituted in a court or tribunal of a Contracting State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceedings are instituted in a court or tribunal of a Contracting State?
      `the service is under Article 5 of the Hague Service Convention` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the service is under Article 5 of the Hague Service Convention?
      `the service is on a person in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the service is on a person in Singapore?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 64, rule 4A(1), does the rule on serving a document under Article 5 of the Hague Service Convention apply` IS
    `o 64 r 4A(1) this Rule applies to the service` `the process or other court document is required in connection with civil proceedings in respect of a civil or commercial matter` `the proceedings are instituted in a court or tribunal of a Contracting State` `the service is under Article 5 of the Hague Service Convention` `the service is on a person in Singapore`

@export Under Order 64, rule 4A(4), is my request for service made and accompanied as the rule requires?
GIVEN `the request is made by an applicant to the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the request is made by an applicant to the Minister?
      `the request is in the current version of Part 1 of the Model Form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the request is in the current version of Part 1 of the Model Form?
      `the request is accompanied by the document to be served` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the request is accompanied by the document to be served?
      `the request is accompanied by a summary of the document to be served, in accordance with Part 3 of the Model Form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the request is accompanied by a summary of the document to be served, in accordance with Part 3 of the Model Form?
      `the documents mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) and (b) are in English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the documents mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) and (b) are in English?
      `the request is accompanied by a translation of those documents in English` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the request is accompanied by a translation of those documents in English?
      `the request is accompanied by a copy each of the request and of the documents mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a), (b) and (c)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the request is accompanied by a copy each of the request and of the documents mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a), (b) and (c)?
      `the number of addresses for service` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of addresses for service?
      `the sum that accompanies the request` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the sum that accompanies the request?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 64, rule 4A(4), is my request for service made and accompanied as the rule requires` IS
    `o 64 r 4A(4) the request for service is made and accompanied as the Rule requires` `the request is made by an applicant to the Minister` `the request is in the current version of Part 1 of the Model Form` `the request is accompanied by the document to be served` `the request is accompanied by a summary of the document to be served, in accordance with Part 3 of the Model Form` `the documents mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a) and (b) are in English` `the request is accompanied by a translation of those documents in English` `the request is accompanied by a copy each of the request and of the documents mentioned in sub-paragraphs (a), (b) and (c)` `the number of addresses for service` `the sum that accompanies the request`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 65 -- Simplified process in the Magistrate's Court or the District Court`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 65, rule 1(1), does the simplified process of Order 65 apply to my proceedings?
GIVEN `the document that began the proceedings` IS A `Document kind` @desc What kind of document began the proceedings?
      `o 6 r 5 the document commences an action in Court as described` IS A `roc12 seat my answer` @desc Does the document commence an action in Court as Order 6, rule 5 describes? (Yes, No, or I am not sure)
      `the court before which the proceedings are` IS A `Court level` @desc In which court are the proceedings?
      `all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 65, rule 1(1), does the simplified process of Order 65 apply to my proceedings` IS
    `o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` `the document that began the proceedings` (`roc12 seat what I say, as a fact` `o 6 r 5 the document commences an action in Court as described`) `the court before which the proceedings are` `all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings`

@export Under Order 65, rule 2(1), is my pleading accompanied by the list and copies of documents the rule requires?
GIVEN `the document that began the proceedings` IS A `Document kind` @desc What kind of document began the proceedings?
      `o 6 r 5 the document commences an action in Court as described` IS A `roc12 seat my answer` @desc Does the document commence an action in Court as Order 6, rule 5 describes? (Yes, No, or I am not sure)
      `the court before which the proceedings are` IS A `Court level` @desc In which court are the proceedings?
      `all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings?
      `the pleading is accompanied by a list of all documents falling within the categories of documents set out in Order 11, Rule 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the pleading is accompanied by a list of all documents falling within the categories of documents set out in Order 11, Rule 2(1)?
      `the pleading is accompanied by a copy of all documents falling within the categories of documents set out in Order 11, Rule 2(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the pleading is accompanied by a copy of all documents falling within the categories of documents set out in Order 11, Rule 2(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 65, rule 2(1), is my pleading accompanied by the list and copies of documents the rule requires` IS
    `o 65 r 2(1) the pleading is accompanied as the Rule requires` (`o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` `the document that began the proceedings` (`roc12 seat what I say, as a fact` `o 6 r 5 the document commences an action in Court as described`) `the court before which the proceedings are` `all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings`) `the pleading is accompanied by a list of all documents falling within the categories of documents set out in Order 11, Rule 2(1)` `the pleading is accompanied by a copy of all documents falling within the categories of documents set out in Order 11, Rule 2(1)`

@export Under Order 65, rule 2(3), does the duty to list and produce documents apply to my amended pleading?
GIVEN `the amended pleading is filed and served by a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the amended pleading is filed and served by a party?
      `the amended pleading pleads any additional fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the amended pleading pleads any additional fact?
      `the amended pleading refers to any document that was not referred to in any other pleading filed by that party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the amended pleading refers to any document that was not referred to in any other pleading filed by you?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 65, rule 2(3), does the duty to list and produce documents apply to my amended pleading` IS
    `o 65 r 2(3) this Rule applies to the amended pleading` `the amended pleading is filed and served by a party` `the amended pleading pleads any additional fact` `the amended pleading refers to any document that was not referred to in any other pleading filed by that party`

@export Under Order 65, rule 2(3), must I disclose again a document I already disclosed in the same proceedings, by reason only of my amendments?
GIVEN `the document was previously disclosed in the same proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document was previously disclosed in the same proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 65, rule 2(3), must I disclose again a document I already disclosed in the same proceedings, by reason only of my amendments` IS
    `o 65 r 2(3) a previously disclosed document needs to be disclosed by reason only of the amendments` `the document was previously disclosed in the same proceedings`

@export Under Order 65, rule 2(4), may I rely on this document?
GIVEN `the document that began the proceedings` IS A `Document kind` @desc What kind of document began the proceedings?
      `o 6 r 5 the document commences an action in Court as described` IS A `roc12 seat my answer` @desc Does the document commence an action in Court as Order 6, rule 5 describes? (Yes, No, or I am not sure)
      `the court before which the proceedings are` IS A `Court level` @desc In which court are the proceedings?
      `all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings?
      `the document was produced in accordance with this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document was produced in accordance with this Order?
      `the Court has ordered or permitted the party to rely on the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has ordered or permitted you to rely on the document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 65, rule 2(4), may I rely on this document` IS
    `o 65 r 2(4) the party may rely on the document` (`o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` `the document that began the proceedings` (`roc12 seat what I say, as a fact` `o 6 r 5 the document commences an action in Court as described`) `the court before which the proceedings are` `all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings`) `the document was produced in accordance with this Order` `the Court has ordered or permitted the party to rely on the document`

@export Under Order 65, rule 2(4), am I barred from relying on this document?
GIVEN `the document that began the proceedings` IS A `Document kind` @desc What kind of document began the proceedings?
      `o 6 r 5 the document commences an action in Court as described` IS A `roc12 seat my answer` @desc Does the document commence an action in Court as Order 6, rule 5 describes? (Yes, No, or I am not sure)
      `the court before which the proceedings are` IS A `Court level` @desc In which court are the proceedings?
      `all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings?
      `the document was produced in accordance with this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document was produced in accordance with this Order?
      `the Court has ordered or permitted the party to rely on the document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has ordered or permitted you to rely on the document?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 65, rule 2(4), am I barred from relying on this document` IS
    `o 65 r 2(4) reliance on the document is barred` (`o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` `the document that began the proceedings` (`roc12 seat what I say, as a fact` `o 6 r 5 the document commences an action in Court as described`) `the court before which the proceedings are` `all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings`) `the document was produced in accordance with this Order` `the Court has ordered or permitted the party to rely on the document`

@export Under Order 65, rule 3, may I make this application?
GIVEN `the document that began the proceedings` IS A `Document kind` @desc What kind of document began the proceedings?
      `o 6 r 5 the document commences an action in Court as described` IS A `roc12 seat my answer` @desc Does the document commence an action in Court as Order 6, rule 5 describes? (Yes, No, or I am not sure)
      `the court before which the proceedings are` IS A `Court level` @desc In which court are the proceedings?
      `all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings?
      `kind` IS A `o 65 r 3 kind of application` @desc Which application do you want to make?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 65, rule 3, may I make this application` IS
    `o 65 r 3 the application may be made` (`o 65 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceedings` `the document that began the proceedings` (`roc12 seat what I say, as a fact` `o 6 r 5 the document commences an action in Court as described`) `the court before which the proceedings are` `all parties to those proceedings have filed their consent for this Order to apply to those proceedings`) `kind`

@export Under Order 65, rule 4(3), is the time I have taken within the time limit for the simplified trial?
GIVEN `stage` IS A `o 65 r 4(3) stage of the simplified trial` @desc Which stage of the simplified trial is it?
      `the minutes taken, per witness or per party` IS A NUMBER @desc How many minutes have you taken, per witness for examination or cross-examination, or in all for your closing submissions?
      `the time limit as extended by the Court under paragraph (4), if the Court extended it` IS A NUMBER @desc If the Court extended the time limit, to how many minutes? (0 if it did not)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 65, rule 4(3), is the time I have taken within the time limit for the simplified trial` IS
    `o 65 r 4(3) the time taken is within the time limit` `stage` `the minutes taken, per witness or per party` (`roc12 seat an amount if I know it` `the time limit as extended by the Court under paragraph (4), if the Court extended it`)


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 66 -- Summary proceedings for possession of land`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 66, rule 1, may I bring my claim for possession of land by originating application under this Order?
GIVEN `a person claims possession of land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a person claims possession of land?
      `the person alleges that the land is occupied solely by a person or persons who entered into or remained in occupation without the person's licence or consent or that of any predecessor in title` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that you allege that the land is occupied solely by a person or persons who entered into or remained in occupation without your licence or consent or that of any predecessor in title?
      `any of those occupiers is a tenant holding over after the termination of the tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that any of those occupiers is a tenant holding over after the termination of the tenancy?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 66, rule 1, may I bring my claim for possession of land by originating application under this Order` IS
    `o 66 r 1 the proceedings may be brought by originating application under this Order` `a person claims possession of land` `the person alleges that the land is occupied solely by a person or persons who entered into or remained in occupation without the person's licence or consent or that of any predecessor in title` `any of those occupiers is a tenant holding over after the termination of the tenancy`

@export Under Order 66, rule 4(1), have I filed the supporting affidavit that the rule requires?
GIVEN `the originating application is filed under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the originating application is filed under this Order?
      `a supporting affidavit is filed at the time of the filing of the originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a supporting affidavit is filed at the time of the filing of the originating application?
      `the affidavit states the claimant's interest in the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the affidavit states your interest in the land?
      `the affidavit states the circumstances in which the land has been occupied without licence or consent and in which the claim to possession arises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the affidavit states the circumstances in which the land has been occupied without licence or consent and in which the claim to possession arises?
      `the affidavit states that the claimant does not know the name of any person occupying the land who is not named in the summons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the affidavit states that you do not know the name of any person occupying the land who is not named in the summons?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 66, rule 4(1), have I filed the supporting affidavit that the rule requires` IS
    `o 66 r 4(1) the claimant has filed the supporting affidavit as the Rule requires` `the originating application is filed under this Order` `a supporting affidavit is filed at the time of the filing of the originating application` `the affidavit states the claimant's interest in the land` `the affidavit states the circumstances in which the land has been occupied without licence or consent and in which the claim to possession arises` `the affidavit states that the claimant does not know the name of any person occupying the land who is not named in the summons`

@export Under Order 66, rule 5(1), must I serve a person in occupation of the land who is named in my originating application?
GIVEN `a person in occupation of the land is named in the originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a person in occupation of the land is named in the originating application?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 66, rule 5(1), must I serve a person in occupation of the land who is named in my originating application` IS
    `o 66 r 5(1) the duty to serve the named occupier arises` `a person in occupation of the land is named in the originating application`

@export Under Order 66, rule 5(1), have I served the named occupier in a way the rule allows?
GIVEN `a person in occupation of the land is named in the originating application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a person in occupation of the land is named in the originating application?
      `manner` IS A `o 66 r 5(1) manner of service` @desc How did you serve the named occupier?
      `the Court has directed the manner used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has directed the manner used?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 66, rule 5(1), have I served the named occupier in a way the rule allows` IS
    `o 66 r 5(1) the named occupier has been served in a manner the Rule allows` `a person in occupation of the land is named in the originating application` `manner` `the Court has directed the manner used`

@export Under Order 66, rule 6, may I apply to be joined as a defendant?
GIVEN `the person is not named as a defendant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that you are not named as a defendant?
      `the person is in occupation of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that you are in occupation of the land?
      `the person wishes to be heard on the question whether an order for possession should be made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that you wish to be heard on the question whether an order for possession should be made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 66, rule 6, may I apply to be joined as a defendant` IS
    `o 66 r 6 the person may apply at any stage of the proceedings to be joined as a defendant` `the person is not named as a defendant` `the person is in occupation of the land` `the person wishes to be heard on the question whether an order for possession should be made`

@export Under Order 66, rule 7(1), may the Court make the final order for possession on this date?
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceedings are proceedings under this Order?
      `the date the final order for possession is made` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the final order for possession is made?
      `the first day on which the act may be done, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day on which the final order for possession may be made, counted as Order 3, rule 3 counts it (14 days after service)?
      `it is a case of emergency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is a case of emergency?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has given permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 66, rule 7(1), may the Court make the final order for possession on this date` IS
    `o 66 r 7(1) the final order for possession may be made` `the proceedings are proceedings under this Order` `the date the final order for possession is made` `the first day on which the act may be done, counted under Order 3, rule 3` `it is a case of emergency` `the Court has given permission`

@export Under Order 66, rule 7(1), is a final order for possession made on this date barred?
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceedings are proceedings under this Order?
      `the date the final order for possession is made` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the final order for possession is made?
      `the first day on which the act may be done, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the first day on which the final order for possession may be made, counted as Order 3, rule 3 counts it (14 days after service)?
      `it is a case of emergency` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is a case of emergency?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has given permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 66, rule 7(1), is a final order for possession made on this date barred` IS
    `o 66 r 7(1) a final order made on that date is barred` `the proceedings are proceedings under this Order` `the date the final order for possession is made` `the first day on which the act may be done, counted under Order 3, rule 3` `it is a case of emergency` `the Court has given permission`

@export Under Order 66, rule 7(1), what is the earliest date on which the Court may make the final order for possession?
GIVEN `the date of service of the originating application` IS A DATE @desc On what date was the originating application served on the person in occupation? (the earliest date is 14 days after it; if you count the 14 days differently under Order 3, rule 3, use the questions that take the first day as an input)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under Order 66, rule 7(1), what is the earliest date on which the Court may make the final order for possession` IS
    `o 66 r 7(1) the earliest date for a final order for possession` `the date of service of the originating application`

@export Under Order 66, rule 8(1), may I file my application for an enforcement order on this date?
GIVEN `the application for an enforcement order is to enforce an order for possession under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application for an enforcement order is to enforce an order for possession under this Order?
      `the date the application is filed` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the application is filed?
      `the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for filing the application without the Court's permission, counted as Order 3, rule 3 counts it (3 months after the order for possession)?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has given permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 66, rule 8(1), may I file my application for an enforcement order on this date` IS
    `o 66 r 8(1) the party may file the application for an enforcement order` `the application for an enforcement order is to enforce an order for possession under this Order` `the date the application is filed` `the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, rule 3` `the Court has given permission`

@export Under Order 66, rule 8(1), am I barred from filing my application for an enforcement order on this date without permission?
GIVEN `the application for an enforcement order is to enforce an order for possession under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application for an enforcement order is to enforce an order for possession under this Order?
      `the date the application is filed` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the application is filed?
      `the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for filing the application without the Court's permission, counted as Order 3, rule 3 counts it (3 months after the order for possession)?
      `the Court has given permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court has given permission?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 66, rule 8(1), am I barred from filing my application for an enforcement order on this date without permission` IS
    `o 66 r 8(1) a filing on that date without permission is barred` `the application for an enforcement order is to enforce an order for possession under this Order` `the date the application is filed` `the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, rule 3` `the Court has given permission`


-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 67 -- Terrorism (Suppression of Financing) Act`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@export Under Order 67, rule 2(1), is my application made as the rule requires?
GIVEN `kind` IS A `o 67 r 2(1) kind of application` @desc Which application are you making?
      `the application is made without notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is made without notice?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 67, rule 2(1), is my application made as the rule requires` IS
    `o 67 r 2(1) the application is made as the Rule requires` `kind` `the application is made without notice`

@export Under Order 67, rule 3(2), did I file and serve my application to revoke or vary within the period?
GIVEN `the application is to revoke or vary a warrant issued under section 11(1)(a) or an order issued under section 11(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is to revoke or vary a warrant issued under section 11(1)(a) or an order issued under section 11(1)(b)?
      `the date by which the application and affidavit were filed and served on every person in (a) and (b) (has this happened yet)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the date by which the application and affidavit were filed and served on every person in (a) and (b)?
      `the date by which the application and affidavit were filed and served on every person in (a) and (b)` IS A DATE @desc On what date did this happen: the date by which the application and affidavit were filed and served on every person in (a) and (b)? (give any date if it has not happened yet)
      `the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this, counted as Order 3, rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 67, rule 3(2), did I file and serve my application to revoke or vary within the period` IS
    `o 67 r 3(2) the application and affidavit are filed and served within the period` `the application is to revoke or vary a warrant issued under section 11(1)(a) or an order issued under section 11(1)(b)` (`roc12 seat a date if it has happened` `the date by which the application and affidavit were filed and served on every person in (a) and (b) (has this happened yet)` `the date by which the application and affidavit were filed and served on every person in (a) and (b)`) `the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

@export Under Order 67, rule 4, did I file and serve my application and affidavit in time?
GIVEN `the application is under section 19(1) by a person who has an interest in the property seized under a warrant of search and seizure under section 11(1)(a) or in respect of which a restraint order was issued under section 11(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is under section 19(1) by a person who has an interest in the property seized under a warrant of search and seizure under section 11(1)(a) or in respect of which a restraint order was issued under section 11(1)(b)?
      `the application is for an order under section 19(4) or for permission to examine the property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is for an order under section 19(4) or for permission to examine the property?
      `the date by which the application and an affidavit in support were filed and served on every person in (c), (d) and (e) (has this happened yet)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the date by which the application and an affidavit in support were filed and served on every person in (c), (d) and (e)?
      `the date by which the application and an affidavit in support were filed and served on every person in (c), (d) and (e)` IS A DATE @desc On what date did this happen: the date by which the application and an affidavit in support were filed and served on every person in (c), (d) and (e)? (give any date if it has not happened yet)
      `the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this, counted as Order 3, rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 67, rule 4, did I file and serve my application and affidavit in time` IS
    `o 67 r 4 the application and affidavit are filed and served in time` `the application is under section 19(1) by a person who has an interest in the property seized under a warrant of search and seizure under section 11(1)(a) or in respect of which a restraint order was issued under section 11(1)(b)` `the application is for an order under section 19(4) or for permission to examine the property` (`roc12 seat a date if it has happened` `the date by which the application and an affidavit in support were filed and served on every person in (c), (d) and (e) (has this happened yet)` `the date by which the application and an affidavit in support were filed and served on every person in (c), (d) and (e)`) `the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

@export Under Order 67, rule 9, did I file and serve my application and affidavit within the period?
GIVEN `the application is under section 27(1) to vary or set aside a forfeiture order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is under section 27(1) to vary or set aside a forfeiture order?
      `the date by which the application and supporting affidavit were filed and served on the Public Prosecutor and on every person appointed under section 15(1) (has this happened yet)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has this happened yet: the date by which the application and supporting affidavit were filed and served on the Public Prosecutor and on every person appointed under section 15(1)?
      `the date by which the application and supporting affidavit were filed and served on the Public Prosecutor and on every person appointed under section 15(1)` IS A DATE @desc On what date did this happen: the date by which the application and supporting affidavit were filed and served on the Public Prosecutor and on every person appointed under section 15(1)? (give any date if it has not happened yet)
      `the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for doing this, counted as Order 3, rule 3 counts it?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 67, rule 9, did I file and serve my application and affidavit within the period` IS
    `o 67 r 9 the application and affidavit are filed and served within the period` `the application is under section 27(1) to vary or set aside a forfeiture order` (`roc12 seat a date if it has happened` `the date by which the application and supporting affidavit were filed and served on the Public Prosecutor and on every person appointed under section 15(1) (has this happened yet)` `the date by which the application and supporting affidavit were filed and served on the Public Prosecutor and on every person appointed under section 15(1)`) `the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

@export Under Order 67, rule 10, may I inspect or take a copy of this document?
GIVEN `the document was filed under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document was filed under this Order?
      `the permission of a Judge has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the permission of a Judge has been given?
      `the court in which the person who gave permission sat` IS A `Court level` @desc In which court did the person who gave permission sit?
      `who the person who gave permission was` IS A `Decision maker` @desc Who gave permission?
      `it is appropriate for a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is appropriate for a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal to act?
      `the Magistrate or the Registrar is empowered to act in the case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Magistrate or the Registrar is empowered to act in the case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 67, rule 10, may I inspect or take a copy of this document` IS
    `o 67 r 10 the person may inspect or take a copy of the document` `the document was filed under this Order` `the permission of a Judge has been given` (`roc12 seat the person who gave permission is a Judge` `the court in which the person who gave permission sat` `who the person who gave permission was` `it is appropriate for a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal to act` `the Magistrate or the Registrar is empowered to act in the case`)

@export Under Order 67, rule 10, am I barred from inspecting or taking a copy of this document?
GIVEN `the document was filed under this Order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the document was filed under this Order?
      `the permission of a Judge has been given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the permission of a Judge has been given?
      `the court in which the person who gave permission sat` IS A `Court level` @desc In which court did the person who gave permission sit?
      `who the person who gave permission was` IS A `Decision maker` @desc Who gave permission?
      `it is appropriate for a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal to act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that it is appropriate for a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal to act?
      `the Magistrate or the Registrar is empowered to act in the case` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Magistrate or the Registrar is empowered to act in the case?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 67, rule 10, am I barred from inspecting or taking a copy of this document` IS
    `o 67 r 10 inspecting or taking a copy of the document is barred` `the document was filed under this Order` `the permission of a Judge has been given` (`roc12 seat the person who gave permission is a Judge` `the court in which the person who gave permission sat` `who the person who gave permission was` `it is appropriate for a judge sitting in the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal to act` `the Magistrate or the Registrar is empowered to act in the case`)


