@export Under Order 69, rule 2, is my application for a civil restraint order heard in open court as the rule requires?
GIVEN `the application is for a civil restraint order, or for an order mentioned in section 73A(2), (3), (5) or (6)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is for a civil restraint order, or for an order mentioned in section 73A(2), (3), (5) or (6)?
      `the application is heard in open court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is heard in open court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 69, rule 2, is my application for a civil restraint order heard in open court as the rule requires` IS
    `o 69 r 2 the application is heard in open court as the Rule requires` `the application is for a civil restraint order, or for an order mentioned in section 73A(2), (3), (5) or (6)` `the application is heard in open court`

@export Under Order 69, rule 3(2), has the civil restraint order been extracted and served as the rule requires?
GIVEN `the order is a civil restraint order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the order is a civil restraint order?
      `the order has been extracted by the person that applies for the order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you extracted the order, as the person who applied for it?
      `the order has been served on all other parties to the legal proceedings in respect of which the order was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the order has been served on all other parties to the legal proceedings in respect of which the order was made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 69, rule 3(2), has the civil restraint order been extracted and served as the rule requires` IS
    `o 69 r 3(2) the order is extracted and served as the Rule requires` `the order is a civil restraint order` `the order has been extracted by the person that applies for the order` `the order has been served on all other parties to the legal proceedings in respect of which the order was made`

@export Under Order 69, rule 4(1), must I serve my application for permission to commence an action, with the affidavit, on the persons the rule names?
GIVEN `a civil restraint order is in force against the party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a civil restraint order is in force against you?
      `kind` IS A `o 69 r 1 kind of civil restraint order` @desc What kind of civil restraint order is in force against you?
      `the application is by that party for permission to commence an action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is by you for permission to commence an action?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 69, rule 4(1), must I serve my application for permission to commence an action, with the affidavit, on the persons the rule names` IS
    `o 69 r 4(1) the duty to serve the application and affidavit arises` `a civil restraint order is in force against the party` `kind` `the application is by that party for permission to commence an action`

@export Under Order 69, rule 4(1), have I served my application and affidavit as the rule requires?
GIVEN `a civil restraint order is in force against the party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a civil restraint order is in force against you?
      `kind` IS A `o 69 r 1 kind of civil restraint order` @desc What kind of civil restraint order is in force against you?
      `the application is by that party for permission to commence an action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application is by you for permission to commence an action?
      `the order was made on the application of the Attorney-General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the order was made on the application of the Attorney-General?
      `the application and affidavit have been served on every intended defendant to the action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application and affidavit have been served on every intended defendant to the action?
      `the application and affidavit have been served on the Attorney-General` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the application and affidavit have been served on the Attorney-General?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 69, rule 4(1), have I served my application and affidavit as the rule requires` IS
    `o 69 r 4(1) the application and affidavit are served as the Rule requires` (`o 69 r 4(1) the duty to serve the application and affidavit arises` `a civil restraint order is in force against the party` `kind` `the application is by that party for permission to commence an action`) `the order was made on the application of the Attorney-General` `the application and affidavit have been served on every intended defendant to the action` `the application and affidavit have been served on the Attorney-General`

@export Under Order 69, rule 4(4), may I file and serve my affidavit in reply on this date?
GIVEN `the person was served with an application for permission mentioned in paragraph (1), (2) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that you were served with an application for permission mentioned in paragraph (1), (2) or (3)?
      `the date on which the affidavit in reply is filed and served` IS A DATE @desc What is the date on which the affidavit in reply is filed and served?
      `the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, rule 3` IS A DATE @desc What is the last day for filing and serving the affidavit in reply, counted as Order 3, rule 3 counts it (14 days after the application is served)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 69, rule 4(4), may I file and serve my affidavit in reply on this date` IS
    `o 69 r 4(4) the person may file and serve the affidavit in reply` `the person was served with an application for permission mentioned in paragraph (1), (2) or (3)` `the date on which the affidavit in reply is filed and served` `the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

@export Under Order 69, rule 5(1)(a), may I inform the Registrar in writing that the other party has commenced an action without permission?
GIVEN `an extended civil restraint order or a general civil restraint order is in force against the party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an extended or a general civil restraint order in force against the other party?
      `the party commences an action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other party commenced an action?
      `that was done without the permission of the Court under section 73C(2)(a) or 73D(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that done without the Court's permission under section 73C(2)(a) or 73D(2)(a)?
      `the person is any other party to the action, or to the application pursuant to which that civil restraint order was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you another party to the action, or to the application under which that civil restraint order was made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 69, rule 5(1)(a), may I inform the Registrar in writing that the other party has commenced an action without permission` IS
    `o 69 r 5(1)(a) the person may inform the Registrar in writing` (`o 69 r 5(1) this paragraph applies` `an extended civil restraint order or a general civil restraint order is in force against the party` `the party commences an action` `that was done without the permission of the Court under section 73C(2)(a) or 73D(2)(a)`) `the person is any other party to the action, or to the application pursuant to which that civil restraint order was made`


