DECIDE `Under Order 70, rule 5, did I file and serve the order and the process within the period` IS
    `o 70 r 5 the order and the process are filed and served within the period` `the person is given permission under section 74(1) to institute or continue legal proceedings` (`roc12 seat a date if it has happened` `the date the order, and the process or document, were filed and served on every other party (has this happened yet)` `the date the order, and the process or document, were filed and served on every other party`) `the last day for doing the act, counted under Order 3, rule 3`

@export Under Order 70, rule 6(a), may I apply for the other party's legal proceedings to be struck out?
GIVEN `an order under section 74(1) is in force against the person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is an order under section 74(1) in force against the other party?
      `the person institutes legal proceedings, or continues legal proceedings instituted before the making of that order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the other party instituted legal proceedings, or continued proceedings instituted before that order was made?
      `that was done without the permission of the General Division under section 74(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was that done without the General Division's permission under section 74(1)?
      `the person is another party to those legal proceedings, or to the application pursuant to which that order was made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you another party to those legal proceedings, or to the application under which that order was made?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under Order 70, rule 6(a), may I apply for the other party's legal proceedings to be struck out` IS
    `o 70 r 6(a) the person may apply for those legal proceedings to be struck out` (`o 70 r 6 this Rule applies` `an order under section 74(1) is in force against the person` `the person institutes legal proceedings, or continues legal proceedings instituted before the making of that order` `that was done without the permission of the General Division under section 74(1)`) `the person is another party to those legal proceedings, or to the application pursuant to which that order was made`


