@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 1, do the revoked Rules of Court continue to apply to my proceedings?
GIVEN `kind` IS A `sch 1 para 1 kind of proceedings` @desc Which kind of proceedings are they?
      `the date the proceedings were commenced, or the appeal or originating summons was filed` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the proceedings were commenced, or the appeal or originating summons was filed?
      `the Court otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the Court otherwise directs?
      `a written law provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that a written law provides otherwise?
      `the proceedings have been disposed of by the General Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceedings have been disposed of by the General Division?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 1, do the revoked Rules of Court continue to apply to my proceedings` IS
    `sch 1 para 1 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings` `kind` `the date the proceedings were commenced, or the appeal or originating summons was filed` `the Court otherwise directs` `a written law provides otherwise` `the proceedings have been disposed of by the General Division`

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 2, do the revoked Rules of Court continue to apply to proceedings in the lower Court following my appeal?
GIVEN `the proceedings are proceedings in the lower Court following an appeal before the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division under these Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the proceedings are proceedings in the lower Court following an appeal before the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division under these Rules?
      `the judgment or order of the lower Court appealed against was given or made in proceedings governed by the revoked Rules, whether pursuant to this Schedule or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the judgment or order of the lower Court appealed against was given or made in proceedings governed by the revoked Rules, whether pursuant to this Schedule or otherwise?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 2, do the revoked Rules of Court continue to apply to proceedings in the lower Court following my appeal` IS
    `sch 1 para 2 the revoked Rules continue to apply to the proceedings in the lower Court` `the proceedings are proceedings in the lower Court following an appeal before the Court of Appeal or the Appellate Division under these Rules` `the judgment or order of the lower Court appealed against was given or made in proceedings governed by the revoked Rules, whether pursuant to this Schedule or otherwise`

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 3, is my caveat against arrest deemed to be a caveat issued under Order 33, rule 5?
GIVEN `the caveat against arrest was entered in the record of caveats under Order 70, Rule 5 of the revoked Rules` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the caveat against arrest was entered in the record of caveats under Order 70, Rule 5 of the revoked Rules?
      `the caveat is in force immediately before the relevant date` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it the case that the caveat is in force immediately before the relevant date?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 3, is my caveat against arrest deemed to be a caveat issued under Order 33, rule 5` IS
    `sch 1 para 3 the caveat is deemed to be a caveat against arrest issued under Order 33, Rule 5` `the caveat against arrest was entered in the record of caveats under Order 70, Rule 5 of the revoked Rules` `the caveat is in force immediately before the relevant date`

@export Under schedule 1 paragraph 3, until what date does my caveat against arrest remain in force?
GIVEN `the date the caveat would have expired but for the revocation of the revoked Rules` IS A DATE @desc What is the date the caveat would have expired but for the revocation of the revoked Rules?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Under schedule 1 paragraph 3, until what date does my caveat against arrest remain in force` IS
    `sch 1 para 3 the date of expiry of the caveat` `the date the caveat would have expired but for the revocation of the revoked Rules`


