DECIDE `Under schedule 4 part 1 item 44, what court fee do I pay on filing an affidavit of this many pages` IS
    `sch 4 the fee for this document in the proceedings` 1 "44" `the court system the proceedings are in` `the court level the proceedings are in` `the value of the claim, in dollars` `the number of pages of the affidavit` 0 1 0

@export Under schedule 4, what court fee does the Schedule set for this item of this Part?
GIVEN `the Part of the Fourth Schedule (1 to 5)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the Part of the Fourth Schedule (1 to 5)?
      `the item in that Part, written as the Schedule writes it (for example 7(k)(v), 44A or table 1 item 1)` IS A STRING @desc What is the item in that Part, written as the Schedule writes it (for example 7(k)(v), 44A or table 1 item 1)?
      `the court system the proceedings are in` IS A `Court system` @desc Are the proceedings in the Supreme Court or the State Courts?
      `the court level the proceedings are in` IS A `Court level` @desc In which court are the proceedings? (General Division, District Court or Magistrate's Court; for the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal choose that court)
      `the value of the claim, in dollars` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the claim, in dollars? (0 if it has none or you do not know)
      `the number the fee is charged on` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number the fee is charged on? It depends on the kind of row. For a fee per page: the pages charged (for the stepped fee for pages over a limit, only the pages over the limit). For a fee for each person, party, witness, exhibit, document, address, attempt, request, book or search term: how many there are. For a fee for each hour, half day or day: how many, counting part of one as one. For the late-filing fee (Part 1 item 9): the court days the document has remained unfiled. For a hearing fee in Part 2 (Table 1, Table 3, Table 4 and the Appellate Division and Court of Appeal fee): the number of days the hearing lasts, counting any part of a day as a day. Table 1 and the Appellate fee charge from the second day, so a one-day hearing owes 0. Tables 3 and 4 charge from the fourth day, so a hearing of 3 days or fewer owes 0, and a row for one day or a band of days, such as table 3 item 1 (the fourth day), shows its sum only when the hearing lasts at least to that day: give 4 or more for it, not 1. To ask what is charged for one day of a hearing, use the question about that day under Table 3 or Table 4. For a fee that is a single sum or a percentage: 1.
      `the amount the fee is a percentage of, in dollars (0 if none)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount the fee is a percentage of, in dollars (0 if none)?
      `the number of documents the fee is charged on, or 1` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the number of documents the fee is charged on, or 1?
      `the fee payable for the last application, in dollars (0 if none)` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the fee payable for the last application, in dollars (0 if none)?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `Under schedule 4, what court fee does the Schedule set for this item of this Part` IS
    `sch 4 the fee for this document in the proceedings` `the Part of the Fourth Schedule (1 to 5)` `the item in that Part, written as the Schedule writes it (for example 7(k)(v), 44A or table 1 item 1)` `the court system the proceedings are in` `the court level the proceedings are in` `the value of the claim, in dollars` `the number the fee is charged on` `the amount the fee is a percentage of, in dollars (0 if none)` `the number of documents the fee is charged on, or 1` `the fee payable for the last application, in dollars (0 if none)`

